window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_DIRECTED_INNER_VOICE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101: Trade Secrets","paragraphs":["\"I don’t know the effects of the medicine. My friend didn’t say, and I didn’t ask. I suppose it’s their trade secret in Nanzhao?\"","Trade secret? Emperor Mingxi nearly laughed at this self-righteous fool!","Seeing that nothing useful could be extracted from him, and fearing that further questioning might arouse suspicion from the other two, he dropped the subject.","Instead, he shifted the topic. \"Xu Wei, Xu Mao, for seizing commoners' land, allowing your servants to beat people to death, and forcing innocent women into prostitution—what punishment do you deserve?\"","Xu Wei and Xu Mao, realizing Emperor Mingxi was serious and ready to act, immediately knelt and pleaded for mercy.","\"Your Majesty, please understand—those were all the actions of ignorant servants! My son and I knew nothing of this!\"","Xu Mao gazed at Emperor Mingxi with feigned reverence. \"Imperial Uncle, it was all the lowly servants' doing. My father and I truly had no idea.\"","He hoped to invoke their thin blood ties and the nonexistent familial affection between them.","The father and son sang the same tune, shifting blame—proof they were cut from the same cloth!","Emperor Mingxi impatiently waved his hand, cutting off their excuses. The morning’s judgments had exhausted him, and without extracting the answers he sought, he had no patience for further nonsense.","\"The facts have been verified. There’s no need for further excuses. Though the servants carried out the acts, they did so under your orders.\"","With that, he finished writing the final decree.","Emperor Mingxi signaled Eunuch Qian to announce the sentences. The eunuch hastily took the scroll and read aloud:","\"Xu Wei and Xu Mao, for seizing commoners' land, covering up murders, and allowing their servants to commit atrocities, are hereby stripped of their titles—Commandant of the Imperial Guards and Assistant Commander—and reduced to commoners.","All Xu family properties, excluding Princess Taikang’s personal assets, are to be confiscated by the state. Half of their remaining wealth is forfeited.\"","Hearing that both father and son were reduced to commoners and their wealth seized, Xu Wei nearly fainted.","\"Xu Wei failed to discipline his daughter. Xu Mao abetted and assisted his sister in beating five servants to death or injury. Each is to receive fifty heavy strikes.","Xu Jiao, for her arrogance and cruelty leading to deaths and injuries, is stripped of her county title and reduced to a commoner.","Princess Taikang, for failing to discipline her daughter, is confined to her residence for six months, deprived of two years’ stipend, and her income will be used to compensate the victims’ families.","All illegally seized lands are to be confiscated and returned to their original owners under the Ministry of Revenue’s supervision.","All implicated servants of the princess’s household are to be imprisoned in the Ministry of Justice’s dungeons, awaiting execution.\"","After Eunuch Qian finished reading the decree, Emperor Mingxi turned to Shen Kang. \"Kang’er, assist Cai Xian’s men in arresting the culprits at the princess’s residence. If anyone resists, execute them on the spot.\"","To Eunuch Qian, he added, \"Qian Gui, oversee the flogging. Ensure the strikes are heavy. If anyone shows leniency, they will share the punishment.\"","[Master, if those strikes land hard, the father and son won’t be leaving their beds for a year—or ever, if they’re crippled.]","This is nothing. The real suffering awaits them in the afterlife.","The Xu family father and son were dragged away like dead dogs. Princess Taikang, now panicked, knelt to beg for mercy.","Emperor Mingxi cut her off. \"Taikang, if Xu Jiao steps out of line even once more, you will lose your princess title.","As for Xu Wei and Xu Mao’s crimes—don’t pretend ignorance. I spare you punishment today only out of respect for your royal status and the dignity of the imperial family.","So, Taikang, do not test the limits of our sibling bond. Do not force my hand.\"","His tone grew colder, and by the end, he refused to even look at her, waving her away like swatting a fly.","Watching Princess Taikang leave, Emperor Mingxi suddenly recalled something and summoned Shen Kang. \"Take men to search all Xu family estates in the capital. Confiscate every trace of that foreign grain. I don’t trust those Nanzhao envoys—something about it feels off.\"","[Finally, the emperor shows a glimmer of wisdom!]","Emperor Mingxi: Thanks? Care to elaborate?","Once the unwanted guests were gone, Emperor Mingxi’s demeanor softened. He turned to Yue Fuguang with fatherly warmth. \"Fuguang, are you satisfied with today’s judgment?\"","Anticipating confusion, he explained, \"Though Xie Zhiyao’s personal conduct is questionable, no major crimes have been proven yet.","So, I’ve decided to banish her from Dayan—out of sight, out of mind.","That girl is trouble. Keeping her here is a risk, but sending her away might turn her into an unexpected weapon—depending on her skills.\"","[Master, the emperor’s thoughts align with yours! But when he later discovers Xie Zhiyao’s involvement in Prince Qi’s rebellion, won’t his face sting from the slap of reality?]","Emperor Mingxi: It already does.","\"Your Majesty, aren’t you afraid she might grow powerful in Xiqiang and turn against Dayan?\"","Little Pearl, I oppose using marriage as a political tool. A nation that relies on women’s marriages to secure peace is weak.","Sending noblewomen as brides only proves the men of that country are incompetent, hiding behind fragile women for false, temporary peace.","A truly mighty empire should receive sons and daughters from others—not send its own. Don’t you agree?","That said, I fully support using Xie Zhiyao as a pawn.","[Master, you’re being hypocritical.]","Hypocritical? Maybe. But she crossed me. I believe in repaying every slight.","Emperor Mingxi, the Crown Prince, and Shen Kang, still present: !!!","The Empress Dowager and Empress, however, agreed with Yue Fuguang. The Empress, though daughterless, sympathized as a woman.","The Empress Dowager, besides Emperor Mingxi, had another child—Shen Kang’s mother, Grand Princess Xie Yun, the only grand princess of Dayan.","The late emperor, infatuated with Consort Hui and her son Prince Rong, once nearly deposed the Crown Prince. This was why the Empress Dowager and Emperor Mingxi so staunchly upheld the line of succession.","Thus, they couldn’t fathom why Yue Fuguang claimed Emperor Mingxi would later consider the ninth prince as heir. If the Crown Prince still lived, the ninth prince stood no chance.","Upholding the Crown Prince’s position was upholding Emperor Mingxi’s own legitimacy. Even at his most foolish, he wouldn’t sabotage himself.","Had they not clung to their status as the rightful empress and heir, the late emperor’s favoritism would have doomed them long ago.","Now, even after Emperor Mingxi’s decade-long reign, whispers persisted that the late emperor had intended to replace him with Prince Rong on his deathbed.","So, the only way the ninth prince could rise was if Zhiyan—the Crown Prince—was gone.","Grand Princess Xie Yun, though born of the empress, was nearly sent to Nanzhao as a peace offering under Consort Hui’s influence."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102: The Destructive Power of the Junior Mentor Is Truly Terrifying","paragraphs":["At this moment, the Empress Dowager could still recall the fear, anger, and above all, helplessness she felt as the Queen when she heard that the legitimate princess was to be sent on a peace - making marriage.","Later, if she hadn't taken drastic measures and turned the tables on those who had schemed against her, sending the woman who had tried to seduce her son to the bed of the Prince of Nanzhao, their treacherous plan would have succeeded!","Consort Hui and her son first framed her son for having an affair with a married woman using a niece from her natal family, trying to ruin his reputation as an upright and wise man. Then, under this pretext, they impeached the Crown Prince, claiming that his character was flawed and he was unfit to be the heir.","She had heard that some officials had even written memorials, waiting for the right moment to present them.","On the other hand, they tried to send her daughter on a peace - making marriage, thus ruining her daughter's engagement with the Shen Family and cutting off a major source of support for Emperor Mingxi, who was then the Crown Prince.","Emperor Mingxi pretended not to hear her scolding him for being incompetent and replied, \"If she wants to establish herself there, she won't be able to do it without the manpower and resources of Dayan in the early stage.","If she wants to turn against us when she becomes powerful? Well, it depends on the Crown Prince's methods. If he can't even control his cousin, he'd better give me a grandson as soon as possible.\"","The Crown Prince, who was being urged to have a child, said that if he was to have a grandson, the Emperor should first help him marry a wife!","The Empress Dowager also said, \"Fuguang, sending Zhiyao on a peace - making marriage was also a move by the Emperor. The peace - making marriage proposal from Xiqiang came three months ago, and the Emperor has been delaying the reply.","He originally planned to reject it at this birthday festival, but unexpectedly, Zhiyao walked right into the trap.","I couldn't bear to send my daughter on a peace - making marriage back then, and naturally, I can't bear to send my granddaughters now.","Your Majesty, after Xie Zhiyao gets married off, how about discussing with the court officials to abolish the system of sending women on peace - making marriages?\"","Emperor Mingxi quickly replied, \"What the Empress Dowager says is right. Even if some court officials oppose it, I will firmly abolish this system.\"","\"Your Majesty, when the time comes, if anyone opposes, just tell them clearly that if there is another peace - making marriage, their own children will be sent. Let's see if they can still be so high - minded when the pain hits them!\"","[Master, what if there are really those who sacrifice their daughters for personal gain?]","[Then, we'll give them a good publicity about their act of sacrificing their daughters for personal gain. Don't scholars value their reputations the most? Add one more thing: send all their beloved sons and grandsons as part of the dowry or send the whole family to guard the border.","We'll call it a great favor, saying that it allows them to be closer to their daughters and granddaughters who have married into other countries. Hahaha!","Let's see who would dare to oppose and who would dare to sacrifice their daughters for personal gain!]","Emperor Mingxi nodded secretly. This method was good. It might be effective against those old - fashioned and stubborn officials who valued their reputations, clung to the old rules, and were reluctant to give up their own interests.","Soon, the news that Prince Qi was placed under house arrest, the princess was sent on a peace - making marriage, the county princess had her title stripped, and the princess and her husband were punished spread like wildfire through different channels into the ears of officials and aristocratic families in the capital city.","And the source of this storm was just a child - like \"appeal to the Emperor\" made by the Junior Grand Tutor!","People once again realized the terrifying power of the Junior Grand Tutor!","Those who didn't know the inside story only thought that the Junior Grand Tutor was young and was just like a mascot in the court. They never expected that this underestimated young man would show his fangs in his first move!","For those officials who knew the inside story, this was just the tip of the iceberg. The Junior Grand Tutor had sent at least eight hundred people to prison, and the few people from the princess's mansion were nothing!","Yue Fuguang: How could a good immortal be like a killing demon?","Everyone: Just tell us if you were the one who sent those people away!","Yue Fuguang: !!!!","Some people keenly noticed that in the judgment of the princess's mansion's encroachment on farmland, the Xu Mansion's properties were confiscated and handed over to the national treasury. The illegally obtained farmland would be verified by the Ministry of Revenue and then returned to the original owners.","This judgment was quite normal, but there had been no such precedent in previous years. Back then, all such properties were confiscated by the state and then auctioned off to various families.","Now, they were to be returned to the commoners... Smart people seemed to smell some extraordinary signs from this!","Was the Emperor finally going to take action on land issues? This was what those who knew the inside story thought.","Those who didn't know the inside story were also divided into two groups. The smart ones had smelled the danger, especially those who had done the same things as the Xu father and son.","They had started to hide in the shadows and think about countermeasures, trying to cause some trouble for the Emperor.","The arrogant and lawless group was still indulging in pleasure every day. They thought that the Emperor was just trying to be a wise king, first currying favor with the gentry and now with the commoners?","Emperor Mingxi: You're the one currying favor. Your whole family is currying favor! This is called testing the waters. Do you understand?","Crown Prince: Father, calm down! Calm down! It's better that they don't understand!","Then he silently picked up his sword!","Yue Fuguang and the system, who were watching the show: Host, that barbecue you treated us to was worth it. Look, things are starting to happen!","Yue Fuguang covered her heart painfully: That meal cost me twenty points, twenty credits!","...","\"Your Majesty, please uphold justice for me! Your Majesty!\" As soon as Emperor Mingxi summoned the Chai father and son into the palace, Chai Jin knelt down with a thud in front of the Emperor's desk.","In the Yangxin Hall, apart from Eunuch Qian, there were only the Emperor and the Chai father and son. Chai Jin had nothing to hide, so he told the whole story in detail.","Today, because Emperor Mingxi wanted to stand up for Yue Fuguang and punish Prince Qi, he ordered Prince Qi to be summoned to the palace after the morning court.","And what was Prince Qi doing at that time?","He was having a private meeting with Chai Jin's wife, Feng Linlang. One had to say that this man was really bold. He dared to have a private meeting with his sister - in - law during the day, not caring about her reputation at all.","By sheer coincidence, Chai Jin happened to pass by and saw them.","At first, Chai Jin was extremely angry, thinking that his wife still had feelings for Prince Qi. But in the end, he managed to keep a bit of his sanity and went home.","He had to ask his wife for an explanation.","At first, Feng Linlang was too concerned about her reputation to tell the truth. Later, seeing that her husband really misunderstood her and Prince Qi, she had to tell the truth.","She poured out all her grievances, fears, and helplessness!","Today's meeting was arranged by Prince Qi. She didn't want to go at first, but Prince Qi threatened her with her reputation, her children, and her husband's future, so she had no choice but to go.","At the meeting, Prince Qi said that Chai Jin had suspected their affair and had started to investigate him. He needed her cooperation to dispel Chai Jin's suspicion.","Feng Linlang was both panicked and furious when she heard this. What affair? When had they ever had an affair?","Wasn't it just this scoundrel who had been pestering her unilaterally? If she could beat him, Feng Linlang would have killed him on the spot!","Feng Linlang was so angry that she didn't say a word, just listening to Prince Qi talk. In fact, he didn't say many useful things. They had only been meeting for less than half an incense stick's time when Prince Qi was invited away by the Emperor's men.","Left alone, Feng Linlang finally managed to calm down and then left the small courtyard one after another with Prince Qi. Coincidentally, she was seen by Chai Jin who was passing by."]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103: \"Living off Parents\" Is the Best Destination","paragraphs":["When Feng Linlang stepped out, her face was flushed with barely concealed anger (from being provoked), which aroused Chai Jin's suspicion.","Adding to his doubts was the distant sight of Prince Qi leaving the area earlier—what had been a three-part suspicion now grew to seven.","This led to the confrontation after their return home.","Upon hearing his wife's account, Chai Jin was filled with fury and humiliation.","He sought out his father, and together, the two men entered the palace to demand justice for the couple.","Though Prince Qi held no real power as an idle royal, he was still the emperor's younger brother. As subjects who had suffered injustice, it was only natural for them to appeal to their \"patriarch\" for redress.","The father and son had also calculated that the emperor would favor useful ministers over a brother who might covet the throne.","Even though Chai Jin believed his wife, he wouldn’t rely solely on her testimony. Before their audience with the emperor, while Feng Linlang rested, Chai Jin tricked her personal maid, Yang Liu, into coming out.","He ordered his trusted attendants and a few strong servants to interrogate her.","Under threats and coaxing, Yang Liu had no choice but to reveal the truth—her account matched Feng Linlang’s exactly.","Only then did the father and son proceed with their formal complaint.","Chai Jin choked back tears as he pleaded, \"Your Majesty, Your Majesty... I beg you to uphold justice for your humble servant and his wife...\"","They had children to consider. If word spread that Prince Qi had dishonored a minister’s wife, how would their children ever marry? How could his wife continue to live with dignity?","Yet if he didn’t seek the emperor’s intervention, Feng Linlang’s words suggested Prince Qi intended to move against him.","Though Prince Qi was an idle prince, he had skillfully cultivated a sterling reputation among officials.","Chai Jin’s family, however, came from a military background. In the Great Yan Dynasty, civil officials held far greater sway than military ones, and his connections were mostly among fellow officers, with few influential civil allies at court.","Facing Prince Qi, even without other complications, the need to protect his wife’s reputation and his children’s future left him with little room to maneuver. Left with no choice, he exposed his family’s shame and turned to the emperor.","Chai Jin’s father, Cai Yanping, also knelt and declared, \"Your Majesty, my son and I swear our loyalty to you and the Great Yan Dynasty is as unwavering as the sun and moon.","Yet Prince Qi has repeatedly harassed and coerced my daughter-in-law—and now, for this illicit affair, he seeks to frame my son and me!","Though we have never overstepped our bounds, as the saying goes, ‘Give a dog a bad name and hang him.’ We fear for our lives!\"","Emperor Mingxi motioned for Eunuch Qian to help them up and said, \"I only learned of this matter this morning. Before your arrival, I had already ordered Prince Qi to reflect in seclusion. Barring unforeseen circumstances, he will not emerge for years.","So, Ministers Chai, your fears of impeachment or false accusations will come to nothing.","As for Prince Qi’s consort, the younger Madam Feng, she has already divorced him. The elder Madam Feng suffered this injustice undeservedly—it is indeed our imperial family’s failing. You must not blame her for it.\"","Once the storm passed, he would have the empress bestow gifts as compensation. For now, any overt action would only endanger her reputation rather than help.","Gossip could kill—Emperor Mingxi knew this all too well.","To him, Prince Qi was already a dead man. The only reason he hadn’t executed him immediately was to uncover evidence of his rebellion and draw out all his conspirators.","The emperor was certain his brother, having schemed for so long, wouldn’t surrender quietly. A counterattack was inevitable—he had no doubt.","Emperor Mingxi sat back like a fisherman waiting for Xie Qi’s followers to leap into his net.","Meanwhile, Yue Fuguang had just left the palace when she spotted her grandfather and father waiting at the gates.","The moment he saw her, Yu Chongshan broke into a relieved smile. \"Fuguang, are you alright?\"","Though his granddaughter had mentioned in her thoughts yesterday that she would teach Princess Taikang and Prince Qi a lesson, they’d assumed she would complain to the empress dowager.","Never had they imagined she would take her grievance directly to the emperor.","The family had worried that what seemed a grave matter to them might appear trivial to His Majesty, who might then see them as presumptuous or spoiled. Though her status as a minor celestial being ensured no real repercussions, Yu Chongshan couldn’t rest until he saw her safe.","Besides, she had acted for her cousin Yu Qingyu and the Yu family—standing here to welcome her was the least they could do.","Instead of their granddaughter, however, they first witnessed the exits of Prince Qi’s household and Princess Taikang’s family.","Unlike Prince Qi’s unscathed party, Marquess Xu and his son were in dire straits—beaten to a bloody pulp, their faces deathly pale as they lay on stretchers.","Had Princess Taikang not appeared relatively unharmed aside from her grim expression, they might have thought the two men dead!","The glares the two families shot at the Yus were filled with venomous resentment.","Rather than cower, Yu Chongshan and his son straightened their backs proudly.","With such unshakable support, they had no reason to bow anymore!","Clearly, Yue Fuguang’s imperial complaint had yielded spectacular results.","Still, a trace of worry lingered—what if their granddaughter, surrounded by mediocrity, grew tired of them and moved out?","Had she known their thoughts, Yue Fuguang would have laughed. Living alone was the last thing she wanted.","As an official, handling social obligations and household affairs alone would be a nightmare. Did they expect her to manage servants and chores herself?","Even with a steward, she couldn’t possibly ignore such responsibilities entirely.","Just look at how busy the Yu matriarch was—her workload rivaled that of a corporate CEO!","She’d once considered independence, but the calculations quickly dissuaded her. In this era, living alone was nothing like the carefree solitude of modern times.","She’d much rather laze around and \"live off her family\"—the ideal life!","Now, she had a spacious, beautiful courtyard all to herself, undisturbed by social calls or morning rituals. Aside from court duties, her time was entirely her own.","With her grandmother and mother handling all domestic and social affairs flawlessly, what more could she ask for?","As for the imperial complaint, avenging the Yu family and herself had been incidental.","Her true goal was completing the system’s side mission: thwarting Prince Qi’s rebellion and preventing opium’s spread in the Great Yan Dynasty.","She could have delayed the task, but Yu Qingyu’s marriage negotiations provided the perfect opportunity to act naturally.","It also served as a warning to those who couldn’t hear her thoughts—a show of power.","Judging by today’s outcome, the effect was impressive.","Another reason was Prince Qi’s dealings with foreign envoys during the imperial birthday celebrations—he’d already leaked numerous state secrets and technologies."]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104: With Just One Sentence, Yue Fuguang Nearly Broke Emperor Mingxi's Defense","paragraphs":["Strengthening the enemy is equivalent to weakening oneself—it would only add difficulty to her ultimate mission. So why not send this troublemaker away early?","\"Little Pearl, during the Wan Shou Festival this time, did Prince Qi also leak many of the Great Yan Dynasty's technical secrets?\"","[Yes, Master. There’s a secretary in the Ministry of Works who’s the son of Prince Qi’s wet nurse. The technology was leaked through his hands.]","\"Just as I thought. The Great Yan Dynasty is full of holes—nothing valuable can stay hidden!\"","After this remark, Yu Chongshan noticed his granddaughter had fallen silent again, clearly disappointed with the Great Yan Dynasty and unwilling to intervene.","No, he had to remind the Emperor—not just about this incident, but about the urgent need to scrutinize officials of all ranks.","Otherwise, his granddaughter might truly lose all hope in the Great Yan Dynasty and run away one day!","\"Run away\"—a term he’d picked up from her—seemed fitting.","Moreover, Minister Lu had mentioned to him recently that he suspected a mole in the Ministry of Works, which was why the \"Little Immortal Lord\" refused to share advanced techniques with them. He was determined to root out the traitor.","Could this son of Prince Qi’s wet nurse be the very person Minister Lu was looking for?","Yue Fuguang glanced casually at her deep-in-thought father and her grandfather, whose expression remained unchanged, and felt reassured.","They would surely report what they’d just heard to Emperor Mingxi. She hoped the Emperor wouldn’t drop the ball this time and would thoroughly investigate the schemers lurking in the court.","Relying solely on her to expose everything wasn’t sustainable—to protect her identity, she couldn’t keep bringing up unrelated topics.","Take Prince Qi, for example. She’d acted on the spur of the moment. If she suddenly accused a prince who never attended court of rebellion, it would seem suspicious.","They should take the initiative to hunt down the \"rats\" while incidentally helping her complete her mission.","Her ideal state was lounging like a salted fish, snacking on melon seeds and sipping tea while effortlessly reaping the rewards.","Maintaining her persona was crucial!","Just as Yue Fuguang was thinking this, her system chimed in:","[Master, if people find out you’re the one reporting to the Emperor, won’t they hesitate to marry into the Yu family?]","\"What’s there to fear? Only those with skeletons in their closets would avoid us. Families with innocent daughters wouldn’t care. Besides, fate decides marriages. If my eldest brother ends up single, it’s definitely not my fault.\"","Exactly! Yu Chongshan and Yu Zhongchun nodded inwardly. If a man couldn’t find a wife, it was his own problem—what did it have to do with his sister?","Children don’t have ill intentions!","......","[Master, the largest auction house in the capital is auctioning glassware today. Do you want to go see?]","\"Little Pearl, is this actually your idea?\"","[Well, Master, do you want to go or not?]","\"Hmm... I do. Do you know where the auction is? We’ll head there after court.\"","[It’s in the Baiye Quarter of the East Market. I’ve already mapped out the route.]","\"Got it. Now stop bothering me—I need to nap a bit more. Listening to these people drone on is putting me to sleep!\"","As if on cue, she let out a big yawn.","Seeing this, Eunuch Qian, who’d stayed up late the previous night, also felt the urge to yawn.","But years of professional discipline kicked in—he suppressed it forcefully, tears welling in his eyes from the effort.","Yue Fuguang noticed and remarked to her system, \"Little Pearl, what’s troubling Eunuch Qian? Why is he tearing up just standing there?\"","[Maybe it’s not trouble—maybe it’s joy?]","\"You know something?\"","[In a day or two, someone from his hometown—his nephew—will visit. Maybe they’ve already met, and he’s moved to tears seeing the boy.]","Eunuch Qian: My nephew traveled all the way to the capital in early winter? Without even sending a letter first? Something must have happened at home.","Worry gnawed at Qian Gui’s heart.","\"So that’s what they call ‘tears of joy’!\"","Eunuch Qian, now the subject of \"tears of joy\": I beg you, little ancestors, stop talking about me! Can’t you see His Majesty has glanced at me twice already?!","Qian Gui shook his head subtly at the Emperor: No, Your Majesty, these aren’t tears of joy—the young masters are spinning tales about your servant!","As this silent exchange unfolded, Honglu Temple Minister You Mingmin stepped forward and reported, \"Your Majesty, the Beili envoy informed us yesterday that a servant named Chonghua from their delegation has gone missing. They request our assistance in locating him.\"","Emperor Mingxi feigned ignorance. \"A missing servant? Can’t you handle it yourselves? Must we trouble the Three Judicial Offices for such a trivial matter?\"","You Mingmin pressed on, \"Your Majesty, this Chonghua is no ordinary servant—he’s the closest aide to Beili’s Third Prince, Beiyue. The prince was so distraught that he nearly stormed the palace yesterday to seek Your Majesty’s intervention.\"","The Emperor waved dismissively. \"Even if he’s close, he’s still just a servant. Have Shen Kang assign a few men to help search. A grown man can’t just vanish into thin air.\"","Several ministers privy to the truth silently scoffed: As if you don’t know where he is—he’s locked up in your private dungeon right now!","Eunuch Qian: Already castrated.","He’d performed the procedure himself. After years without practice, his technique was rusty—the first cut wasn’t clean, so he’d made several more passes.","The man’s endurance was pitiful. His screams had been so loud they disturbed the Emperor and even made the six-year-old Ninth Prince burst into tears!","The Ninth Prince: Have you no shame? You scared me on purpose!","\"Little Pearl, did I hear right? They said who’s missing? Chonghua? Isn’t he Concubine Zhou’s—oh, wait, she’s been demoted to Concubine Zhou now. Isn’t Chonghua her lover? If he’s gone, they won’t meet during the Wan Shou Festival, and the Twelfth Princess won’t be born, right?\"","Yue Fuguang’s words nearly shattered Emperor Mingxi’s composure. Could the emotional damage get any worse?","The ministers inwardly pleaded: We beg you, ancestral one, drop this topic! Our Emperor still has face to save. If you keep this up, he can’t punish you, but we’ll suffer for hearing it!","[Master, have you considered that even if Chonghua weren’t missing, Concubine Zhou’s current rank wouldn’t qualify her to attend the Wan Shou Festival? Even if the Emperor allowed it, without him as the scapegoat, she might not dare to carry the child to term.]","Scapegoat Emperor Mingxi: Thanks for nothing.","As soon as the system finished speaking, several officials bowed their heads even lower. Yue Fuguang noticed Wu Yong pinching his own thigh hard—presumably stifling laughter.","\"Concubine Zhou’s downfall is one thing, but why is Chonghua missing too? Did my appearance cause this?\"","[Probably not... right?]"]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105: Perhaps the white jade, captivated by her beauty, abducted Chonghua from the banquet.","paragraphs":["You Hongming said, \"Your Majesty, I already borrowed personnel from Minister Shen yesterday. Dozens of people combed the entire area where Chonghua disappeared but found no clues whatsoever.","I suspect that Chonghua's disappearance may not be a simple matter.\"","Emperor Mingxi seemed to grow somewhat interested and deliberately asked You Mingmin, \"Minister You, where is the location of Chonghua's disappearance? Is there anything special about that place?\"","\"Reporting to Your Majesty, according to my investigation, Chonghua disappeared near the Three Street Market in Xinghua Quarter. What is special is that the Three Street Market includes Pear Blossom Lane, Apricot Blossom Lane, and Peach Blossom Lane. Peach Blossom Lane contains a private residence belonging to Princess Pingning of the Qi Prince's estate.","Before his disappearance yesterday, Chonghua had been seen there with envoys from several other states. Later, due to the incident involving the Princess, the place was sealed off, and he was nowhere to be found.\"","\"Little Pearl, this actually seems to have a little something to do with me!\"","The System: It had reason to suspect Emperor Mingxi was asking this on purpose, just to spite it! Hmph! An emperor being so petty!","The System curled its lip. Reciprocity is a principle, so it deliberately said, [Master, do you think it could be Emperor Mingxi's doing? He might already know about Concubine Zhou cuckolding him!]","Hmph, you little... The more you don't want me to say it, the more I will bring it up!","Yue Fuguang: ?? The System isn't following the usual script. Is it picking a fight with Emperor Mingxi now?","Thinking this in her heart, she said aloud, \"I saw The Ninth Prince in the palace just a couple of days ago. If Emperor Mingxi knew about this, could that child still be alive?\"","[Who says he couldn't be? What if Emperor Mingxi only knows his favorite concubine was unfaithful, but doesn't know she got pregnant from that single affair?","He doesn't seem very clever anyway, being cuckolded by his favorite concubine and his own brother, and never learning the truth until his death!]","Emperor Mingxi: Not clever? That's not what you said yesterday! I'll endure it, I'll endure it. I won't get angry, I won't get angry. These people won't survive this winter anyway, nothing to be angry about!","He kept brainwashing himself, while mechanically asking aloud, \"Have any envoys from the other states also gone missing?\"","\"No, we have already verified. Among the envoys, only Chonghua from Beili is missing. We repeatedly searched the area with his portrait, but no one has seen him.","However, according to a recollection by one of Shen Kang's subordinates, he saw this person when he first infiltrated the Princess's residence disguised as a servant to investigate.\"","At that time, he entered carrying a water kettle, and Chonghua even had him pour water for her, but that man said when they went in a second time after surrounding the detached courtyard, this person was gone.\"","Emperor Mingxi seemed to detect a flaw in his words, \"You said only Chonghua was missing among the envoys. Does that mean someone not an envoy is also missing?\"","\"Your Majesty is most astute. Indeed, there is one other person. This person is named Bai Yu. According to our detailed investigation, he is the illegitimate son of Bai Yu, the current head of the Bai family in Jiaozhou, and a close friend of Princess Pingning. Both Bai Yu and Princess Pingning were feasting at Peach Blossom Lane yesterday.","This matter has been verified with the Princess by your servant. The Princess said this person had already left before Minister Shen and the others entered, but we have not been able to locate him at his residence.","His household servants say their master left yesterday morning and has not returned.\"","\"Minister Cai, have you heard what Minister You said? What is your view on this?\"","The named Cai Xian thought: What view could I have? The person is locked up in Your Majesty's dungeon. Am I supposed to 'impartially' report on you or something?","That's what he thought, but neither the little immortal lord nor the divine artifact master had lent him any courage, so he dared not speak it aloud.","Cai Xian stepped forward and said solemnly, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, in my humble opinion, Chonghua's disappearance may be inextricably linked to Bai Yu.","If we can find Bai Yu, we might uncover clues about Chonghua.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded and asked Wei Ping, \"Minister Wei, you are skilled in solving cases. What do you say? Is Minister Cai's reasoning sound?\"","Wei Ping thought: Asking me to comment on a senior's words, Your Majesty, this is how I lose friends!","Cai Xian thought: He's skilled in solving cases, and I, as the Minister of Justice, am not? Your Majesty, please don't make the difference in favor so obvious!","Wei Ping lowered his eyes and said meekly, \"Your Majesty, I also believe Minister Cai's words are reasonable. Bai Yu is the key to this case. Perhaps we should send someone to the Bai family in Jiaozhou. Maybe Bai Yu has returned to his family home in Jiaozhou; it is almost the New Year, after all.\"","That makes sense! Many officials secretly nodded in agreement.","Those in the know thought this was a perfect opportunity to openly send someone to investigate the Bai family. With about a month left before they were to lure foreign tribes in for raids, it was unclear if these people were already making preparations.","Those unaware of the inside story thought it was very likely he had gone home for the New Year, though they wondered why Bai Yu would take Chonghua with him.","Could it be this person shares the same preferences as the Third Prince of Beili?","Immediately, someone stepped forward and said, \"Your Majesty, I second the motion. Regarding what Minister Wei said, I have a bold conjecture. I wonder if I should speak it?\"","Emperor Mingxi saw that his plan to divert attention was proceeding smoothly and naturally, with no trace of suspicion. His dragon heart was greatly pleased.","With a delighted wave of his hand, he said, \"Speak freely! I pardon you of any offense!\"","\"I thank Your Majesty! My conjecture is that Bai Yu might share the same... preferences as that Third Prince. I have seen a portrait of Chonghua; he is indeed exceptionally beautiful. Perhaps Bai Yu, overcome by lustful intentions, abducted Chonghua from the banquet and directly fled with him back to his hometown in Jiaozhou.\"","Emperor Mingxi thought: Considering your merit in successfully steering the matter off course, I won't hold your praise for Chonghua against you!","Emperor Mingxi nodded with an appreciative expression. \"Your reasoning makes sense, my dear minister. I entrust this matter to you, Minister Cai, to take charge!\"","\"I, Cai Xian, receive Your Majesty's decree!\"","Having received the task, Cai Xian exchanged a glance with Minister of War Huo Ying, and both understood the situation perfectly.","[Could it really not be Emperor Mingxi crying thief?]","Yue Fuguang: Again?","Emperor Mingxi: Enough already!","[Perhaps Chonghua really got lost himself? It's just a bit strange. What was so special about yesterday? Why did everyone rush to Peach Blossom Lane all at once? That place might not be simple!]","[Of course it's not simple. There's a big pit there! But it has little to do with Chonghua's disappearance. I'll explain it to you in detail when I have time.]","Yue Fuguang: Is the system getting addicted to keeping people in suspense?","[Why isn't the court session over yet? We still need to go see the auction!] The system now sounded exactly like certain friends waiting to clock out.","[Well, these ministers are quite long-winded!] Yue Fuguang felt that the bitterness of office work she hadn't experienced in the modern era was now being savored in detail—it was all the taste of the daily grind! No, she had to think of a way; she couldn't go on like this!","The long-winded ministers: Shall we leave then?","Emperor Mingxi: I'm leaving too. If I don't go, the Divine Artifact will have my pants off!","Emperor Mingxi gave Eunuch Qian a look that said 'you know what to do.' Qian Gui immediately called out, \"If there are matters to report, do so. If not, this court session is dismissed!\"","Excellent. No one tactless came forward to say there were still matters, asking everyone to wait a bit longer!","Emperor Mingxi, the boss, also didn't say, \"Let's have a meeting later!\"","Yue Fuguang had just stood up when the Crown Prince walked over with a smile. He said, \"I wonder if the Junior Mentor has any free time today?\"","\"What matter does the Crown Prince seek me for?\" Whether I'm free depends on what you want.","This answer can be very flexible!"]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106: Crown Prince, Do You Know Kung Fu","paragraphs":["Though she could have gone alone, how could it compare to the convenience and preferential treatment of accompanying the Crown Prince? She hated trouble more than anything—going with Xie Zhiyan meant she wouldn’t have to lift a finger. Effortless!","After waving goodbye to her grandfather and the others, Yue Fuguang followed the Crown Prince without a backward glance, leaving Wu Yong, who had hoped to tag along for some excitement, empty-handed.","The auction was held at the renowned \"Treasure Pavilion\" in Baiye District, a venue frequented exclusively by the wealthy and noble. Without an invitation, no amount of money could grant entry.","Yue Fuguang and Xie Zhiyan walked side by side into the auction hall. Despite it being daytime, the grand hall was brilliantly illuminated by dozens of octagonal palace lanterns, casting every corner in a light as bright as noon.","The air was thick with the rich blend of ambergris and sandalwood, enhancing the luxurious and dreamlike atmosphere of the elegantly dressed crowd.","Upstairs, private booths were veiled by mottled bamboo curtains, offering faint glimpses of their occupants—some leisurely fanning themselves, others sipping tea in silence.","Yue Fuguang followed Xie Zhiyan into the largest and most opulent private booth. The moment they entered, the Crown Prince’s attendants began serving tea and refreshments.","While waiting for the auction to begin, Yue Fuguang stepped to the wide window overlooking the floor below.","The general seating area was already packed with merchants, wealthy patrons, and even... martial artists?","Had she not seen them, Yue Fuguang might have forgotten—this was a world where ancient martial arts traditions thrived.","Chivalrous heroes existed, but she hadn’t heard much about their tales of vengeance and freedom. Was she simply uninformed?","Though the people downstairs were well-dressed, they lacked the composed demeanor of those upstairs. This wasn’t just a world of martial arts—it was also one of strict social hierarchy.","No matter how skilled a warrior, they still feared the blade of the imperial court.","\"Crown Prince, do you know martial arts?\"","Yue Fuguang had never seen Xie Zhiyan fight, but his upright posture and well-built physique suggested training.","A confident smile flickered across the Crown Prince’s face as he modestly replied, \"I know a little.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded in understanding—translation: he was very skilled.","Her system couldn’t resist teasing, [Master, if he’s so strong, how did he get poisoned to death? Shouldn’t martial arts experts have internal energy to expel toxins, similar to my detox pills?]","Xie Zhiyan: Divine Artifact, must we bring up my poisoning? Is it something to boast about? And who told you internal energy could expel toxins?","Ding—","The clear chime of a bronze bell drew all eyes to the intricately carved redwood stage at the center.","Standing there was an elderly man in an indigo robe, his hair and beard white as snow, his expression serene yet commanding. The auctioneer.","Without a word, his calm gaze swept across the room, instantly silencing the murmurs until the hall was so quiet one could hear a pin drop.","Ding—","Another chime announced the official start of the auction.","The first item up for bidding was a sword once wielded by a famed general of the previous dynasty.","The auctioneer’s voice, though not loud, carried effortlessly through the hall—likely amplified by internal energy.","\"Cloud-Splitter Sword, starting bid: three hundred taels.\"","Instantly, bids rose from the floor:","\"Three hundred fifty taels!\"","\"Four hundred!\"","\"Four hundred fifty!\"","The calls surged like waves, climbing higher until a bearded man secured it for two thousand eight hundred taels, drawing hushed gasps from the crowd.","Yue Fuguang noted that this man differed greatly from the dashing swordsmen of films and dramas—more rugged, more... down-to-earth.","She wondered if the martial artists of this world were as free-spirited as legends claimed—and if they could be hired.","\"Crown Prince, does Dayan have a martial world? Do these chivalrous figures take on commissions?\"","\"There are martial artists and wanderers, some affiliated with sects or gangs, others operating alone. But all fall under imperial oversight. Many make a living by working as bodyguards or estate guards for the wealthy. Does the Junior Mentor wish to hire them?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Just curious. As for hiring, I have ideas, but no urgent need.\"","\"Should the need arise, let me know. I’m acquainted with some capable individuals.\"","Xie Zhiyan finally felt his status had practical use and secretly hoped Yue Fuguang would request assistance soon.","Earlier, while reviewing her system’s tasks, Yue Fuguang noticed several involved the martial world. Could martial artists really influence court affairs?","Ah—upon closer inspection, she understood. They had backers. That explained it.","To complete these missions smoothly, she’d need such people around to steer conversations naturally. But there was no rush—she had time.","Next came famous paintings and calligraphy, which Yue Fuguang admired without deeper appreciation.","Xie Zhiyan asked, \"Junior Mentor, is there anything you’d like? I could bid for you.\"","She shook her head. Though exquisite, none sparked her desire to own them.","A thought struck her. ‘System, I just realized—these artworks hold little practical value for me. Their worth lies in historical and cultural significance. Once we move to another world with a different history, only their artistic merit remains.’","[Host, that’s correct.]","The following antiques and jade pieces, while valuable, failed to stir much excitement.","Until the long-awaited centerpiece arrived.","Yue Fuguang turned to Xie Zhiyan. \"Is it almost time for our glass tea set?\"","\"The next finale item is yours.\"","Onstage, four attendants carried in an object veiled in bright yellow silk, placing it solemnly at the center.","The auctioneer unveiled it—a half-foot-tall white jade Guanyin statue, glowing softly under the lights.","The jade was flawless, the craftsmanship divine. The Bodhisattva’s serene expression and flowing robes seemed almost alive.","\"An imperial masterpiece from the previous dynasty—the Lotus Sutra Guanyin. Starting bid: five thousand taels.\"","The room held its breath—then the storm broke.","\"Five thousand five hundred!\" A salt merchant from the southeast raised the bid by five hundred, aiming to dominate early.","\"Five thousand eight hundred.\" A discreet jeweler from the northwest countered.","\"Six thousand.\" A soft, southern-accented voice came from an upstairs booth, its occupant hidden behind bamboo curtains.","The price soared like a runaway steed, reaching twenty thousand taels.","Bids dwindled, leaving only two upstairs guests locked in battle.","\"Twenty-two thousand.\" A steady, middle-aged voice from the east.","\"Twenty-five thousand.\" A firm, elderly voice from the west countered.","The auctioneer remained composed. \"West booth, twenty-five thousand taels—going once!\""]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107: Forty-Five Thousand Taels","paragraphs":["The hall fell into complete silence, gazes shifting back and forth between the eastern and western chambers.","The air seemed to freeze, with only the faint crackling of the lamp wicks in the palace lanterns breaking the stillness.","\"Twenty-five thousand taels, twice!\"","The eastern chamber went silent. The elderly auctioneer no longer urged, simply waiting patiently. It felt like an eternity, yet perhaps only a fleeting moment—no further bids came from the east.","\"Twenty-five thousand taels, thrice!\"","\"Clang—\"","The bronze chime rang once more, its clear tone lingering in the air.","\"Sold.\"","As the auctioneer's voice faded, a barely audible sigh of relief drifted from behind the bamboo curtain of the neighboring western chamber.","Yue Fuguang caught a glimpse of a woman’s figure, restless and eager, keeping a close watch on the proceedings below.","She thought to herself—wasn’t it just a particularly exquisite jade Guanyin statue?","The woman’s demeanor suggested this object held immense significance. Was there some hidden story behind it?","Before she could get a closer look, the jade Guanyin was draped once more in bright yellow silk and carefully carried off the stage by attendants.","The winner would complete the transaction through a secret passage, leaving no name behind—only an astonishing price and a room buzzing with murmurs and speculation.","The lingering aura of the jade Guanyin had yet to dissipate, the atmosphere still steeped in a dazed awe.","Without a word, the elderly auctioneer raised his hand slightly, and the final highlight of the evening was carried onto the stage by two attendants.","Placed steadily on the rosewood table, this time the auctioneer did not unveil it himself. Instead, a maid in a water-green ruqun stepped forward gracefully and lifted the carved sandalwood lid.","With delicate hands, she retrieved the contents and arranged them one by one on the dark velvet-covered table.","As the maid retreated, the treasure was revealed.","The moment the audience laid eyes on it, a collective gasp—a mix of bewilderment and admiration—rippled through the hall.","What kind of tea set was this?","A set of five pieces: one pot and four cups.","They were neither porcelain nor jade, but—glass!","Yet this glass bore no resemblance to the murky, commonplace wares found in markets.","It was flawless, crystal-clear, without a single imperfection. Under the lamplight, it refracted dazzling, gem-like brilliance.","The teapot’s curves were fluid and elegant, the cups’ walls as thin as cicada wings—so fragile they seemed to shatter at a touch, yet radiant with a breathtaking, delicate beauty.","Even more astonishing, the pot and cups were adorned with intricate vine-and-lotus patterns traced in fine gold filaments. The golden threads meandered through the transparent glass, a perfect fusion of opulence and purity—a masterpiece of craftsmanship.","Yue Fuguang studied the display. The design was undeniably refined, steeped in classical elegance. Ancient artisans truly had impeccable taste.","The auctioneer’s voice broke the silence, igniting a different kind of fervor—one far more intense than the solemn reverence inspired by the jade Guanyin.","\"An exotic treasure from distant shores: the Gilded Vine-and-Lotus Glass Tea Set. Crafted by the secret techniques of artisans from the far western land of Foling, tempered in blazing fire, shaped in utmost purity—where water and fire converge, gold and jade reside within.","The only set of its kind in the world. Starting bid: eight thousand taels.\"","[Master, this auctioneer spins such tales—isn’t he afraid of being beaten to death if the truth comes out?]","We’re making money off the wealthy. It’s not like we’re mass-producing these. Who’s going to expose us? If pressed, we’ll just say we poached artisans from that ‘Foling’ place.","[Should we place a bid? It looks like fun.]","\"Ten thousand taels!\" Almost before the auctioneer finished speaking, a maritime merchant familiar with foreign trade shouted from below.","He knew full well that glassware of such purity was priceless even overseas—let alone a set this exquisite, complete with gold inlays.","\"Fifteen thousand taels!\" Yue Fuguang answered the system with action. Yes, they would play along.","\"Sixteen thousand taels!\" A lavishly dressed woman from an imperial merchant family swiftly countered. She had no resistance to rare luxuries that blended exotic allure with functional beauty.","\"Twenty thousand taels!\" Yue Fuguang’s bid drew immediate attention.","Jumping so high in one go—was she serious? How were others supposed to inch their way up now?","The voice sounded young, almost girlish. Was this a playful jest or a genuine desire to buy?","Some even considered calling for her guardian to rein in the child’s mischief.","\"Twenty-one thousand taels!\" Thoughts aside, the bids kept coming.","\"Twenty-two thousand taels!\"","The competition escalated instantly.","Unlike the slow, grave bidding war over the jade Guanyin—dominated by the private chambers upstairs—this glass tea set’s allure was more direct, more intoxicating. Yue Fuguang’s unconventional raises only stoked the frenzy.","Not just merchants on the ground floor, but even reserved noblewomen joined the fray, whispering bids through stewards or maids.","\"Twenty-five thousand taels!\"","\"Twenty-eight!\"","\"Thirty thousand!\"","Prices soared, voices overlapping, leaving no pause.","The air grew thick with tension, mingling with the scent of incense, quickening pulses.","The radiant tea set gleamed under the lights like a lodestone, drawing every gaze and desire.","\"Thirty-five thousand taels.\" A youthful, clear voice with a Nanzhao accent came from an eastern chamber upstairs.","\"Thirty-eight thousand.\" A slightly colder voice countered from the west.","\"Forty thousand.\" The eastern bidder, undeterred, didn’t sound like a native of Dayan—perhaps from Xiqiang or Beili.","Indeed, representatives from neighboring nations must have all gathered for this auction.","The hall quieted briefly. Forty thousand taels for a tea set—no matter how rare—was staggering.","The auctioneer’s eyes swept toward the western chamber, met with contemplative silence.","Just as he prepared to confirm the bid, a hoarse yet vigorous voice rang out from the front row below:","\"Forty-five thousand taels!\"","All turned to see an elderly man with silver hair but an indomitable spirit, dressed in simple silk yet exuding authority.","Some recognized him—Shen Wanchuan, the titan of Jiangnan’s silk trade.","Shen Wanchuan? Yue Fuguang recalled the name. A future mission involved him. Well, she’d deal with him next year.","This time, even the young nobles upstairs hesitated.","It wasn’t that they couldn’t bid higher, but challenging a deeply entrenched magnate over a tea set seemed unwise.","The auctioneer scanned the room once more, particularly the eastern and western chambers. Hearing no further bids, he declared:","\"Master Shen Wanchuan bids forty-five thousand taels!\"","\"Forty-five thousand, once!\"","\"Forty-five thousand, twice!\"","\"Forty-five thousand, thrice!\"","\"Clang—\"","The chime’s pure note sealed the deal.","Shen Wanchuan gave a slight nod, a satisfied smile gracing his lips."]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108: Relying on One's Own Hands and Wisdom, Not Through Corruption","paragraphs":["The dazzling glass tea set, under countless gazes mixed with envy, jealousy, and awe, was carefully carried down the high platform by a maid, heading toward its new owner.","\"Forty-five thousand taels, forty-five thousand taels!\" Xie Zhiyan repeated the number under his breath, then suddenly turned to Yue Fuguang.","Lowering his voice but unable to suppress his excitement, he said, \"Lord Shaoshi, did you hear that? The most ordinary glass tea set from the glass workshop actually fetched a sky-high price of forty-five thousand taels!\"","Xie Zhiyan, born with a silver spoon in his mouth and accustomed to luxury, knew that glassware was valuable. But after learning how these items were made, his illusions were shattered. Though he still found them beautiful, he never expected them to sell for such an exorbitant price.","\"Because it’s the first set, the price is naturally high. Once more flood the market, it won’t command this price anymore,\" Yue Fuguang analyzed rationally.","\"So that’s why Lord Shaoshi insisted on controlling the supply from the start? Now I understand what to do.\"","Their main goal was to drain the silver pouches of the foreign envoys attending the Longevity Festival.","As for the citizens of the Great Yan Kingdom—they could wait for the next batch!","Yue Fuguang: You’re not sparing them either!","\"Crown Prince, don’t forget your promise to me—use the profits for the people’s welfare.\"","\"Lord Shaoshi, rest assured. Zhiyan would never dare forget.\"","The next morning at court, the perceptive ministers quickly noticed that His Majesty seemed in unusually high spirits.","Though his face bore no smile, those who had served him for years could sense the joy radiating from Emperor Mingxi.","Was it because tomorrow was His Majesty’s Longevity Festival, and happiness lifted his mood?","Under the ministers’ intense scrutiny, Emperor Mingxi cleared his throat lightly. Eunuch Qian promptly announced, \"Present your memorials if you have business; otherwise, court is dismissed!\"","But court had just begun—dismissal was out of the question. As soon as Eunuch Qian spoke, officials stepped forward to report their matters.","[Master, the emperor is practically glowing with happiness—did he stumble upon a fortune?]","\"Little Pearl, it’s called ‘radiating joy’! Since when does an emperor need to ‘stumble upon money’ to be happy? Shouldn’t he be the wealthiest man in the land?\"","[If we’re talking about disposable silver in personal possession, the emperor isn’t the richest. In the Great Yan Dynasty alone, several families have more hidden wealth than him.]","\"More than one family is wealthier than the emperor? Doesn’t the imperial family claim to own the entire realm?\"","[We’re discussing liquid silver here—not fixed assets, not the national treasury, just the emperor’s private coffers. His reserves might pale in comparison to some nobles’ hidden stashes.]","Yue Fuguang glanced subtly at the court below. Many noticed her small gesture—some shrinking back, others straightening their posture.","\"Little Pearl, is there anyone in this hall wealthier than the emperor?\"","[There is. Would you like to know, Master?]","\"First, tell me if their wealth was obtained legitimately.\"","[They earned it through their own hands and wisdom—]","As the system spoke, some ministers visibly relaxed—only to tense again when it continued:","[By embezzlement.]","Embezzlement? Who could be so adept at corruption that they surpassed the emperor’s wealth?","Emperor Mingxi: Are there such fat rats in my court?","He silently counted the silver in his private vault—excluding priceless antiques, jade, and artifacts, just gold, silver, and copper totaled a mere eight hundred thousand taels.","That was already three to four times more than what he’d inherited from his father. Back then, the imperial coffers—both state and private—were so empty even mice starved.","After years of scrimping, his savings still couldn’t match his own ministers?","Fine, be rich—but earn it honestly! Stealing what rightfully belongs to the throne? Unforgivable!","Emperor Mingxi fumed silently, eagerly awaiting further revelations from the immortal lord and the Divine Artifact.","Watching the unsuspecting minister still pontificating, the emperor was relieved. Not everyone in court could hear the \"inner voices,\" so not all would learn that their sovereign was outmatched in wealth.","Speaking of inner voices—the envoy sent to fetch Daoist Xuanmingzi should return soon.","He and his ministers had debated endlessly why some could hear the voices and others couldn’t, yet no pattern emerged.","This uncertainty unsettled them. Having grown accustomed to the voices, how would they cope if they suddenly vanished?","Understanding the mechanism was essential for peace of mind.","As Emperor Mingxi pondered this, he discreetly pricked up his ears.","\"Embezzled? Like rivers drying up while tributaries swell—so they’ve been hoarding it all for themselves?","Explain—how did they embezzle so much?","Don’t tell me it’s the usual—disaster relief funds, construction budgets? Those have always been easy targets.\"","[Master guessed half-right. They did siphon those funds, but the real jackpot lies elsewhere.]","\"Where?\"","[Silver mines!]","Silver mines!","The words echoed in the listeners’ minds, pounding in sync with their racing hearts.","No wonder—claiming a silver mine would indeed fill private coffers beyond the imperial vaults.","[And it’s no small deposit. Here’s another secret: near the silver mine lies a modest gold vein, though these fools haven’t discovered it yet.]","Gold! Untapped gold!","Emperor Mingxi suddenly agreed with the Divine Artifact—he was about to stumble upon riches!","Had his financial luck ever been this fortuitous?","First, he’d reclaimed wealth from Prince Qi, with more to come once the prince passed.","Yesterday, the crown prince reported the glassware’s staggering auction price—and he’d seen the stockpile. The items sold were mediocre compared to the exquisite collection gathering dust in storage!","Before that joy faded, today brought news of gold and silver mountains. The Divine Artifact and the immortal lord were truly his prosperity angels!","Yes, though the mines’ locations remained unknown, Emperor Mingxi already considered them his.","All lands under heaven belonged to the throne—private mining was illegal. Once discovered, the state would confiscate everything.","He’d wait for the Divine Artifact to reveal the sites, then identify the thieves pilfering his resources!","Arrests, confiscations, mining operations—all in one smooth sequence.","\"So they’ve got mines—no wonder they’re rich! Set aside the mines for now; focus on the embezzlement first.\"","Hearing this, Emperor Mingxi nearly choked on his own saliva.","Emperor Mingxi: What? I was ready for the grand reveal, and now we’re changing topics? Fine—embezzlement works too!","He could apprehend the corrupt, trace the silver, then uncover the gold. Perfect strategy!"]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109: The death knell of the Dayan Dynasty's fall has sounded its first toll","paragraphs":["The embezzled funds invariably come from military pay, disaster relief, and construction budgets. Let’s start with military pay. The Great Yan Dynasty, like other dynasties, has a long tradition of falsifying troop numbers and misreporting personnel.","Senior officials skimming soldiers’ wages is commonplace, and there’s no shortage of those who siphon off supplies—plenty of opportunities to line their pockets. For now, let’s set aside the corruption within the Great Yan military itself.","Instead, let’s focus on how the court officials embezzle military funds.","At this point, Minister of War Huo Ying, Wei Shouyi, and the other military officers silently wiped the cold sweat from their brows. They had narrowly dodged disaster—for now.","Though they knew their misdeeds would eventually come to light, they clung to the hope that they could delay the reckoning, even if just for a day longer.","Meanwhile, the officials from the Ministry of Revenue felt their hearts tighten. This round of scrutiny was aimed squarely at them.","\"Isn’t this the same thing?\"","\"Not entirely. Military corruption involves siphoning off the funds they actually receive—the silver allocated by the court.","But, my dear, do you really think the amount the court allocates is the amount they get?","If the emperor approves 500,000 taels of silver, they’re lucky to receive 300,000—or even less. Where does the rest go?","It ‘disappears’ at every step along the way. By the time the money reaches its destination, only a fraction remains. Take it or leave it. Do you think those rough-edged soldiers dare offend the ‘God of Wealth’?","Or, let me put it this way—do you think Huo Ying would dare cross Dong Qianli, the Minister of Revenue?\"","Huo Ying: \"Divine Artifact, though you speak the truth, must you humiliate me so? I am a man of nine chi—must I lose all dignity?\"","Wei Shouyi and the other officers: \"Sir, if this helps His Majesty understand our plight, what does your pride matter?\"","Huo Ying: \"Easy for you to say—it’s not your face being dragged through the mud!\"","Dong Qianli: \"I knew it. I just knew it. This round is meant for me.\"","Yue Fuguang glanced at the two men. She had once seen Huo Ying’s saber—it was nearly as tall as Dong Qianli himself. Yet even a man like Huo Ying had to tread carefully around Dong Qianli.","The title ‘God of Wealth’ wasn’t just for show. Even the other ministers had to greet him with smiles, however forced.","\"So Dong Qianli embezzled the money? As the Great Yan’s treasurer, he’s the prime suspect, no?\"","Dong Qianli: \"Young Immortal, don’t slander me unjustly! Administrative losses are hardly theft!\"","Well... sometimes those ‘losses’ were excessive. But he alone couldn’t change the culture of graft and extortion.","\"He’s not innocent, but he wasn’t the one who took the lion’s share. At most, he skimmed a little off the top—small sums, a few thousand taels here and there, barely enough for a set of glass teacups.","Half the court is like him. Hardly worth mentioning.\"","Dong Qianli was nearly moved to tears. \"Divine Artifact, you’re... surprisingly kind!\"","\"These funds are like a slab of fatty meat. Everyone who handles it ends up with greasy fingers—a little something for all, as they say.","But while some, like Dong Qianli, merely dabble in the grease, others carve off whole chunks and stuff them into their own pockets.\"","Emperor Mingxi: \"Not only the Young Immortal, but even the Divine Artifact needs to study more! ‘A little something for all’? Is that how the phrase is used?","That’s my money. My money!\"","\"Disaster relief and construction budgets follow much the same pattern. Let’s set aside past relief efforts for now and focus on this year’s snow disaster—a windfall for a new crop of corrupt officials.","They’re experts at this. It’s not their first, second, or even sixth time. Every year brings a new disaster, and every year they grow richer—so rich they could rival Emperor Mingxi himself. No great feat, really.\"","Emperor Mingxi, now both a repeated target and an inadvertent unit of measurement: \"Enough already!\"","\"Though seasoned in their craft, this year’s snow disaster affected far more people than they anticipated. Their greed nearly backfired.","Countless commoners froze or starved to death, sparking unrest. And with that, the first toll of the Great Yan Dynasty’s death knell rang out.\"","Emperor Mingxi and his courtiers were shaken to their cores. So the seeds of their dynasty’s downfall had been sown so early?","They had assumed it would take years—perhaps when the emperor grew older and more senile. Never had they imagined it had already begun this year.","Were it not for caution, the emperor would have ordered the arrest and execution of those fat rats on the spot.","\"‘Nearly backfired’ implies it didn’t. Did the emperor investigate? How large was the unrest to shake the nation’s foundations?\"","\"Emperor Mingxi performed as expected. After the unrest, he purged the corrupt officials—or so he thought. The real culprits sacrificed a few scapegoats, feeding him a prearranged list of names to execute.","And execute them he did, just as they planned.\"","Emperor Mingxi bristled. \"‘Performed as expected’? Don’t think I missed the sarcasm!\"","\"As for the death knell—the unrest affected hundreds of thousands, with countless casualties. But the true crisis lay in two men who emerged from the chaos.","These two escaped, raising their own forces in Liangzhou and Yizhou.","At first, they fought the Great Yan court for survival. Later, after the dynasty’s collapse, they became the last two armies defending its remnants against foreign invaders.","These men... even in death, they refused to renounce their identity as Great Yan subjects—the final loyalists of a dynasty that had failed them.","Not ‘Northern Li,’ not ‘Western Qiang,’ nor subjects of Liang or Wei.","Ah, Liang and Wei were short-lived regimes that later emerged near Liangzhou and Yizhou... mere warlord states.\"","Emperor Mingxi listened, his heart heavy with complexity. Who would have thought the last ‘Great Yan people’ would be such men?","Yue Fuguang’s emotions were even more tangled. Her past life’s knowledge gave her a deeper respect for these men than most.","In a way, theirs was a different kind of martyrdom.","\"What became of them?\"","Emperor Mingxi shot Huo Ying a meaningful glance. He would find these men before the unrest began—talents like these should serve the court, not rebel against it.","He would ‘nationalize’ them before they made irreversible mistakes.","\"Xiao Ping currently works as a clerk in Pingyang County, under Changping Prefecture in Liangzhou. As a minor official, his involvement in the unrest—and rise as a leader—was purely circumstantial.","His magistrate, Cao Qingming, had earned his position through the imperial exams but lacked connections. Stuck in Liangzhou’s most remote county for over a decade, he knew his limitations.","Though unremarkable in ability, Cao Qingming wisely refrained from meddling in matters beyond his expertise. He delegated power freely to capable subordinates, so long as Pingyang County thrived.","Thus, despite his youth, Xiao Ping’s competence earned Cao Qingming’s trust.","When the snow disaster struck, only a fraction of the court’s relief funds reached Pingyang. The starving masses, remembering the magistrate’s past fairness, initially trusted him.","But those who stood to profit from chaos grew impatient. They infiltrated the refugees, spreading rumors that Cao Qingming and his clerks had hoarded the relief grain.","At first, few believed it. But as supplies dwindled, desperation turned to rage. Provocateurs led the charge against the county office, and amid the chaos, assassins struck down the magistrate and his clerks.\""]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110: He, Doesn't Dare to Move","paragraphs":["Xiao Ping narrowly escaped and blended into the rebellious refugees, seizing the opportunity to uncover the truth—behind it all stood the powerful aristocratic families.","Knowing he couldn’t challenge them and realizing he’d been discovered, Xiao Ping killed those who threatened him and became the leader of the rebels.","He had hoped to reveal the truth when the imperial court came to suppress the rebellion, but the ones who arrived were allies of those pulling the strings. Forced into a corner, he led a group into the vast mountains of Liangzhou.","\"So he was driven to rebellion. What about the other one?\"","The other man was named Wang Zhi, a scholar from Taoyuan County, Qingning Prefecture, Yizhou. Though his early experiences differed from Xiao Ping’s, their later paths converged in a startlingly similar way.","Both were coerced into joining the rebellion, reluctantly rising to leadership, only to face ‘suppression’ officials who sought to eliminate them rather than negotiate.","With no other choice, they each gathered their followers and retreated into the mountains.","Thus, like Xiao Ping, Wang Zhi became one of the Great Yan Dynasty’s two stubborn thorns—impossible to uproot.","These two forces acted like magnets, drawing in more and more desperate souls—those who had lost their land and could no longer feed themselves no matter how much they toiled as tenants.","Over a decade, their numbers swelled from a few hundred to nearly thirty thousand. When the Xiqiang and Beili forces first attacked the Great Yan Dynasty, these rebels were the earliest to resist.","Both men painstakingly relayed this intelligence to the imperial court through different channels, but the officials were too consumed by power struggles to care.","The new emperor even suspected they were fabricating threats to manipulate the court into offering them amnesty, hoping to leverage their position for greater gains.","What fools!","\"Emperor Mingxi’s sons grow more useless by the day. Look at the second, third, fifth, and sixth princes—aren’t they practically dozing off during court sessions?\"","The four princes in question: Excuse us? We’ve been nothing but obedient since the Imperial Tutor arrived, living like shadows!","Even the second prince, Xie Zhimin, who once rivaled the crown prince in ambition, had toned down his antics. Yet somehow, the Imperial Tutor still noticed them?","[These four idiots need a proper disciplining from the emperor. Otherwise, a few well-placed words from schemers might convince them they’re destined for the throne.","Next year, after the snow disaster comes the floods. The funds for dam repairs were embezzled, turning the structure into a crumbling deathtrap. What should’ve been a minor flood became a catastrophe, drowning tens of thousands.","A natural disaster twisted into man-made tragedy!","When Emperor Mingxi traced the corruption, he found his second son’s faction at the core—with hints of his third son’s involvement.","He had both princes’ legs broken and imprisoned.","Honestly, breaking their legs is too lenient. Such worthless scum should’ve been executed.]","\"So the second prince embezzled to fund his coup? From your tone, it sounds like he’s being manipulated?\"","[He craves the throne, and the stolen silver was meant to bribe officials and raise a private army. But what he doesn’t realize is that he’s taking the fall for someone else.","His uncle, Marquis Yingping Fu Hong, pretends to support him while secretly serving another master. Nephews? Pfft.]","Xie Zhimin, the would-be emperor, broke into a cold sweat at the Imperial Tutor’s derisive scoff. As for his uncle Fu Hong... he glanced back at the man standing behind him.","Fu Hong met his gaze, their faces equally grim.","Fu Hong’s heart sank deeper than the prince’s. After all, Xie Zhimin was still the emperor’s son. But Fu Hong? A mere outsider meddling in the succession, backing the wrong horse...","The thought made his vision darken. He longed to defend himself, but the figures surrounding him left no room for movement.","If he stayed still, his family might survive—his crimes falling on him alone.","If he acted, the emperor would ensure he memorized every name in his nine-generation clan registry.","Fu Hong’s heart bled. Why did I only hear the Imperial Tutor’s thoughts today? Had it been a few days earlier, could I have prepared?","He thought of his newborn grandson, held only once...","With a hollow gaze, Fu Hong knelt before Emperor Mingxi’s impassive face.","Before his knees touched the ground, Wei Shouyi—wearing a guileless grin—pulled him up. Leaning in as if sharing office gossip, Wei whispered, \"Marquis, don’t move. Keep your expression neutral.\"","\"Fu Hong won’t even support his own nephew? Did this ‘outsider’ offer him more?\"","[A nephew can’t compare to a son. Fu Hong isn’t the only one loyal to that man—many in this court serve him too.]","The officials: The Imperial Tutor’s death-naming us again? Unavoidable, as expected.","[Take the Ministry of Revenue’s so-called ‘Abacus King’ Qu Bing, for instance. No ledger escapes his ‘balancing’ touch.","Pity he never met the forensic accountants of modern prisons—else he’d never dare claim that title.","Introduce double-entry bookkeeping, and his tricks would crumble to dust.]","\"Qu Bing? Which one is he?\" Yue Fuguang scanned the crowd.","The moment he spoke, the courtiers straightened their postures, eyes downcast but ears pricked—masters of the ‘suddenly attentive during meetings’ act.","[Master, see that middle-aged man beside Wu Yong? Pale, deceptively simple face, black mole on his left brow.","That’s the ‘Abacus King.’ First-ranked abacus? Laughs in calculator.]","\"Ha! Little Pearl, if his fingers are fast enough, he might keep up with your calculator!\"","[Hmph. Isn’t your uncle joining the Ministry of Revenue soon? Give him that calculator and let them duel—see who’s faster.]","\"Don’t sabotage me! How would I explain that gadget? Claim it’s from overseas? No foreign land has such technology. Little Pearl, some advancements are too advanced to reveal!\"","Too advanced to reveal? The Ministry of Revenue officials itched with curiosity. The more forbidden, the more they craved a glimpse.","Their collective gaze landed on their superior, Dong Qianli.","Dong Qianli: What am I, a magician?","Internally, Dong was panicking. Of course the rot is in my ministry. And it’s my most trusted subordinate...","Staring at the oblivious Qu Bing, Dong sighed. I should’ve known.","[Why not teach your uncle modern accounting? Little Pearl guarantees he’ll obliterate the ‘Abacus King.’]","\"You’ve got a grudge against him? Or is there some benefit to taking him down?\""]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111: Could it be that my son is also attracted to both men and women","paragraphs":["[\"He's got quite the reputation—over the years, he's helped his master embezzle a fortune. You could say he's the number one parasite in the Ministry of Revenue. Indirectly, he's caused plenty of deaths. Little Zhu is a divine artifact, representing justice. I must deliver justice and judge him!\"]","\"Hmm?\"","[\"This man's karma is heavy. Eliminating him might earn Little Zhu some merit light! Hehehe!\"]","\"Stop being so melodramatic. You can't judge anyone. As long as no one knows about his embezzlement, he’ll remain the top accounting wizard. As for merit, it’s just a tiny bit—hardly worth it.\"","[\"Master, I could strike him with lightning! Or you could expose him!\"]","\"I can barely even read yet. What do I know about account books? How could I expose him?\"","[\"Why not give your uncle the accounting methods? He could audit the books and catch him red-handed.\"]","Dong Qianli: After court adjourns, I must petition His Majesty to recall Yu Shuchun immediately. The Ministry of Revenue can’t function without him—or without the Young Lord’s accounting techniques!","\"I... I—did you forget my memories are sealed? I can’t recall any of this!\"","System: Host, just admit you forgot what you learned instead of blaming your sealed memories. They don’t deserve this slander!","Though it thought this, the system still saved face for her. [\"Oh! Little Zhu forgot about that. No worries, I’ve got it. I’ll give it to you when we get home.\"]","That \"Oh!\" was so exaggerated that Yue Fuguang, guilty as she was, sensed the sarcasm.","Hmph!","In her past life, she had wealth, status, and—well, more wealth. So what if she was a slacker? It never stopped her from living well!","\"Besides Qu Bing, who else is serving one master while secretly loyal to another?\"","The hall fell silent. One oblivious official kept rambling, but it was clear no one else was listening.","Though no one understood the phrase \"serving one master while loyal to another,\" they instinctively grasped that the Young Lord had begun another round of deadly name-dropping.","[\"There’s also Zhao Jiu, Qu Bing’s subordinate. He’s skimmed military funds, disaster relief silver, and construction budgets.","And that general behind Wei Shouyi—yes, the one hunching his neck—he’s the one who forced Xiao Ping into banditry.","The others... we’ll deal with them later.\"]","Wei Shouyi gritted his teeth. So, there’s a spy in my own ranks! No wonder this guy didn’t seem thrilled about hearing the inner voice.","He thought it was just because the man was new and struggling to accept such a bizarre phenomenon. Turns out, he was biding his time! While forcing Xiao Ping into banditry hasn’t happened yet, the embezzlement must already be underway.","Otherwise, why would a man over eight feet tall try to shrink into a crowd of six- and seven-footers, terrified of being noticed?","\"Little Zhu, did you forget to tell me who their master is? Someone who can turn so many officials against Emperor Mingxi—he must be someone important, right?\"","[\"Important? Well... yes. He’s Emperor Mingxi’s younger brother. A prince of the realm—does that count?\"]","Emperor Mingxi’s heart skipped a beat. Was he about to lose another brother today?","He mentally tallied them up. Excluding Prince Qi—who, though alive, was already dead to him—he didn’t have many brothers left!","\"Another rebellious prince? Is the imperial throne really that enticing? Sons want it, brothers want it, even ministers want it...\"","The officials: Another one? So there was someone before? Who?","Judging by His Majesty’s expression, he already knew. When did we miss such juicy gossip?","And Young Lord—sons and brothers wanting the throne makes sense, but ministers?","Could you kindly name names? Don’t drag us innocent folks into this!","Emperor Mingxi shifted uncomfortably on his dragon throne. The seat was hard—after a while, it really dug into his backside.","[\"Master, want to guess who it is? This guy’s got some scandalous drama. Interested?\"]","The system inexplicably perked up at the word \"drama.\" For a merit system, it acted like a gossip-hungry weasel, sniffing out scandal with glee.","Without waiting for Yue Fuguang’s reply, it barreled on: [\"This man is Prince Ming of the Great Yan Dynasty. His title means ‘Bright,’ but he’s anything but—dark and scheming to the core!","He’s Emperor Mingxi’s youngest brother. When the old emperor died, he was just a child, so he avoided the worst of the succession wars.","With his father gone and his elder brother on the throne, the seventeenth son was enfeoffed as Prince Ming.","Unlike other dynasties, Great Yan’s princes don’t have to leave the capital. So Prince Ming settled into the opulence of Shangjing City, playing the idle aristocrat—bird-watching, poetry, tea ceremonies, and all that.","But it’s all an act. Behind the scenes, he’s busy as a bee—raising assassins, hoarding private troops, colluding with officials, embezzling funds and land.","On top of that, he’s also juggling his harem and... other entanglements.\"]","Tch. Harem is harem, front courtyard is front courtyard. What’s there to balance? Does he think he’s Emperor Mingxi, needing to weigh the harem against court politics?","Choosing which concubine to bed tonight based on what her family did in court—like some kind of paid escort!\"","Emperor Mingxi, the \"paid escort\": Why drag me into this while talking about Prince Ming?! And who’s a paid escort?! Rage.gif","[\"It’s because he’s got ‘treasures’ in both places! Oh right, I forgot to mention—Prince Ming swings both ways.","Ever wonder why Fu Hong supports him over his own nephew?\"]","\"Why? Fu Hong and Prince Ming... have a thing?\"","Yue Fuguang glanced at Fu Hong. A bit old, but still handsome—after all, his sister made it into the palace, so the family genes must be decent.","The Second Prince resembled him slightly—probably took after his maternal side.","So, older man/younger man dynamics...","Fu Hong kept his head down but could feel the scorching gaze from above. The enigmatic Young Lord was definitely staring. One misstep, and his family wouldn’t see tomorrow’s sun.","Fu Hong had only just gained the ability to hear the inner voice today. His colleagues hadn’t briefed him yet, so he assumed Yue Fuguang was merely extraordinary—hence Emperor Mingxi’s favor.","But accusing him of an affair with Prince Ming? That was too much! He—","Before he could finish the thought, another voice chimed in: [\"Not him. His son and Prince Ming are the item.\"]","His son and Prince Ming?! His son—the sole heir of the Fu family—was involved with Prince Ming? No wonder the boy threatened suicide to force his support!","Fu Hong's face flushed crimson before turning ashen—was his newborn grandson from a few days ago... Could it be that his son was also into both men and women?"]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112: Is the Ming King's relationship with Beiyue genuine affection or mutual use","paragraphs":["Fu Hong's expression softened slightly at this thought. As long as the grandson was his own, that was what mattered. As for his son... well, his son had at least left behind a grandson, hadn’t he? Yes, fulfilling the duty of continuing the family line—that much was accomplished. He...","\"How old is his son?\"","With just this one question, the system inexplicably understood the unspoken curiosity in Yue Fuguang's mind. [Prince Ming and his son have an age-gap relationship.]","Yue Fuguang nodded silently in understanding. So that was it. But if the system said Prince Ming had an age-gap relationship with his son, did that mean he didn’t have such dynamics with others?","Curious. He wanted to know more!","The ancient listeners, unfamiliar with the term \"age-gap,\" wondered what cryptic immortal language the divine artifact and the young immortal lord were speaking.","An immortal code phrase? They were even more eager to figure out what \"age-gap\" meant!","As for Prince Ming being open to both men and women and having an affair with Fu Hong’s son—though it was juicy gossip, the group of men took it in stride.","Same-sex relationships? Nothing to fuss about. There was the Third Prince of Beili in the past, and now their own Prince Ming of Dayan. It was hardly noteworthy.","Some of them even had their own favorite opera singers—those with sweet voices and charming figures.","Men, after all, sometimes indulged in a bit of playacting. No need to make a big deal out of it!","Unfortunately, the system didn’t pick up on Yue Fuguang’s unspoken curiosity this time and continued on its own. [Prince Ming’s relationship with his advisor is also ambiguous. The women in his rear courtyard all have influential backgrounds, representing factions supporting his future rebellion, so it’s no surprise he often has to... dedicate himself to them.]","\"I once saw him at the Empress Dowager’s birthday banquet. He was quite handsome, but he looked sickly. Turns out it wasn’t poor health—just overindulgence!\"","Yue Fuguang’s face lit up with sudden realization, making Emperor Mingxi’s eyelid twitch. His instincts told him trouble was coming.","Sure enough, he then heard: [Exactly. Look at the emperor—his harem isn’t any smaller than Prince Ming’s rear courtyard, and he’s no stranger to visiting his consorts’ chambers. Yet he appears far healthier than Prince Ming, who’s barely in his twenties.","Really, it just comes down to men expending too much energy.]","Emperor Mingxi inhaled deeply, exhaled slowly, refusing to let the two irritate him. What did they mean by calling him old? And \"visiting consorts’ chambers\"—since when was \"visiting\" the right word for that?","Besides, weren’t their conversations veering further and further off track? Couldn’t they discuss something useful?","Yet, precisely because of this digression, some of Emperor Mingxi’s budding suspicions were quietly dispelled.","\"Little Pearl, is this what you meant by Prince Ming having juicy gossip? This? Don’t you think this melon is neither sweet nor substantial?\"","[Ah, Master, I haven’t finished yet! Don’t rush me! Do you remember that night seven years ago, on Emperor Mingxi’s birthday?]","Emperor Mingxi’s face darkened at the system reopening old wounds. Though the adulterous couple and their bastard were already suffering in his secret dungeon, being reminded still stung.","In the grand hall, another official was presenting his report. Noticing the emperor’s grim expression, he faltered, his voice growing quieter.","Emperor Mingxi composed himself and gestured for the man to continue. Without this mundane report as cover, how could they gossip freely without drawing attention?","Besides, Prince Ming’s scandals would surely overshadow his own. Soon, his ministers would forget about his humiliation!","Ears perked, Emperor Mingxi consoled himself.","Yue Fuguang pretended not to notice the emperor’s stormy expression and replied, \"Of course I remember—the night the emperor was cuckolded! What about it? Is there more to the story?\"","[Not exactly a continuation, but Master, aren’t you curious? At the time, Beiyue had just taken Chonghua and was keeping a close watch on him. So how did Chonghua find the time to... thoroughly communicate with Concubine Xian Zhou for so long?]","\"Because Beiyue was busy with his own affairs?\"","[Master is so sharp! Beiyue had left for a few days to inspect Xu Changyue’s spy outpost, so Chonghua crossed paths with Zhou Yunxin.","Meanwhile, Beiyue also met someone—none other than Prince Ming, who was recuperating at his suburban estate.","The two hit it off instantly, unaware of each other’s true identities. That year, Prince Ming was sixteen, and Beiyue was twenty.","You could say that during those few days apart, both Beiyue and Chonghua found their own... ‘love.’]","Yue Fuguang, who had never experienced romance in this life or the last, was thoroughly scandalized by the system’s use of the word \"love.\"","[Even when they parted, neither Beiyue nor Prince Ming knew the other’s identity. Beiyue even resolved to take \"A-Ying\" back to Beili with him after Emperor Mingxi’s birthday celebrations.","Oh—\"A-Ying\" and \"A-Yue\" were the aliases Prince Ming and Beiyue used for each other.","Who could’ve guessed they’d meet again at the emperor’s birthday banquet? Cue the dramatic unmasking!","Naturally, they had to find a quiet spot for a private chat. And private chats like these inevitably involved sweet nothings and... hands-on reassurance...","Prince Ming, who had only recently discovered the pleasures of women, now found himself introduced to an entirely new world by Beiyue—one with its own unique charms.","So while Chonghua was busy making a child with Zhou Yunxin, Beiyue wasn’t idle either. In a way, Chonghua wasn’t the only one straying.","Honestly, in this five-sided mess, the only real loser was Emperor Mingxi.]","Yue Fuguang nearly laughed aloud. The system kept bringing this up—didn’t it see the emperor’s face had turned pitch-black?","Emperor Mingxi: Divine Artifact, you really didn’t need to say \"so\"! As for being the loser—he’d already taken his revenge!","[From then on, Prince Ming’s world had two doors. Behind one stood his first love, Beiyue. People always romanticize their first loves, and the longer they’re apart, the thicker the rose-tinted glasses.","Over the years, the two exchanged plenty of letters in secret. On the day Chonghua disappeared, Beiyue was off meeting his old flame, Prince Ming.]","\"Was Prince Ming’s affection for Beiyue genuine, or was it mutual exploitation?\"","[Hard to say. Even the original author probably wasn’t sure how much sincerity lay in Prince Ming’s feelings for Third Prince Beiyue.","But Little Pearl suspects Prince Ming definitely hoped to use their relationship to persuade Beiyue to help him seize the throne—especially in recent years, as Beiyue’s status in Beili grew more exalted, with increasing support for his succession.","All these years, Prince Ming had been funneling embezzled funds to Beiyue through secret channels to aid his rise.","Beiyue’s steady climb wasn’t just his own doing—it was backed by Prince Ming... or rather, by Dayan itself.","In the future, when Beili launches its first strike to conquer Dayan, the vanguard’s covert infiltration will use the very secret route Prince Ming established for transporting goods to Beiyue—dubbed the \"Ming’s Path\"!","Oh, and one more thing happened during their rendezvous at Prince Ming’s estate...]","The system paused deliberately, savoring the suspense.","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers barely registered what else had occurred between the two. Their minds reeled at the revelation of \"Ming’s Path\"—later exploited by Beili’s forces!","Prince Ming, Xie Ying—truly, he deserved death!","The crowd seethed with fury. Fu Hong, hearing this, felt his heart sink completely."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113: Inheritance of Mastery: Dual Prowess in Gu and Poison","paragraphs":["Conspiring to rebel is a capital offense, and colluding with foreign powers only compounds the punishment—ensuring a death most wretched!","Fu Hong’s face turned ashen, his only plea now a swift end.","But no one had the time to spare for him at the moment. What they urgently needed to know was the location of that hidden mountain path—so the Great Yan could seal it off as soon as possible.","Meanwhile, military officials like Huo Ying, Wei Shouyi, and others from the Ministry of War were already scheming: Could the Great Yan army exploit this path in reverse?","Sneak into Beili to stir up trouble, or station troops there to ambush the enemy—lure them in and spring the trap!","Yet, despite their eagerness, they knew better than to act rashly. Holding their breath, they continued to watch the drama unfold.","\"What’s this about? Explain!\" Yue Fuguang, ever the enthusiastic audience, chimed in again, though inwardly cringing at the system’s latest revelation about the \"Path of the Enlightened King.\"","[Just as Beiyue and Prince Ming were locked in their passionate duel—caught in the throes of passion—they were exposed in the act!]","\"That scandalous? How mortifying! Who would dare catch them red-handed? Emperor Mingxi?\"","The officials also suspected their emperor. After all, when it came to a foreign prince and a domestic royal, only His Majesty had the authority to intervene.","But Emperor Mingxi, upon whom this colossal blame was suddenly thrust, wanted no part of it.","That day, he’d been preoccupied with dealing with Taikang and Prince Qi, as well as apprehending the adulterer Chonghua. He’d had no energy left to police his younger brother’s affairs!","[Not him. It was the Southern Zhao princess, Lan Xuan'er.]","\"How does the Southern Zhao princess factor into this? Don’t tell me this is another tangled love web?\"","[Three years ago, Southern Zhao proposed a marriage alliance with Great Yan. With no eligible princesses of age, Southern Zhao selected the fourteen-year-old Lan Xuan'er, who arrived with their envoy during the Emperor’s birthday celebrations.","Southern Zhao’s original plan was for Lan Xuan'er to meet Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan, intending for her to become his concubine once she turned sixteen—despite him already having a betrothed.","But the fourteen-year-old princess took no interest in the fifteen-year-old prince. Instead, she fell for the twenty-year-old Prince Ming.","Prince Ming, however, dared not marry her. A foreign princess wed to a domestic prince? His imperial brother would never sleep soundly again—he’d surely find a way to eliminate him sooner or later.","Had Prince Ming lacked ambitions for the throne, it might have been different. But since he did, he couldn’t afford to draw suspicion so early.","Though he refused, Lan Xuan'er was relentless. For the next two years, she returned for the Emperor’s birthday celebrations, each time clinging to Prince Ming. She even bypassed the official guesthouse, lodging directly in his residence.","Her familiarity with his estate allowed her to barge past guards and catch the pair in bed.","Now, guess why You Mingmin, the Minister of Foreign Affairs, didn’t object when Beiyue suggested that Chonghua’s disappearance might be linked to Bai Yu?]","\"Why, my dear little pearl?\" Yue Fuguang, ever the hype-man, played along.","[Because Beiyue knew of the Bai family’s ties to Southern Zhao. From clan leader Bai Yu down, Bai Yu and Lan Xuan'er were distantly related.","Lan Xuan'er exposed the affair in the morning; Chonghua vanished by afternoon. Even Beiyue couldn’t deny the connection.","He believed Lan Xuan'er had taken Chonghua in retaliation for him touching her beloved.","As for Great Yan’s theory that Bai Yu had abducted Chonghua out of lust—Beiyue found it hard to swallow.]","Emperor Mingxi and You Mingmin exchanged a knowing glance. So that was the missing piece. No wonder Beili had accepted such an outlandish explanation.","\"Prince Ming must’ve had designs on Lan Xuan'er, right? Otherwise, how could he allow her to stay with him and roam his private chambers freely? They were caught in his bedroom, weren’t they?","Surely a prince could’ve expelled a foreign princess if he truly wanted to?\"","[It was the study in his villa. Probably started with reading or talking... then escalated.]","\"Reading? Erotic literature, perhaps? And what happened after they were caught?\"","[A fight broke out.]","\"Between Lan Xuan'er and Beiyue?\"","[More precisely, their entourages clashed. Later, Prince Ming played mediator, soothing both sides—only to be ‘pushed down’ by Lan Xuan'er that very night.]","\"Pushed down in the way I’m thinking?\"","[Exactly that kind of ‘pushed down.’ Prince Ming had already received word: Lan Xuan'er would soon turn eighteen. If no progress was made with him, Southern Zhao would either choose a consort for her or send her to marry into Southern Yue.","Having strung her along for three years, Prince Ming couldn’t let his prize slip away.","So that night, under the guise of reconciliation, he shared a meal and drinks with her—pretending to get drunk, he ‘reluctantly’ gave in to her advances.","In truth, Lan Xuan'er’s wine had been laced with a mild aphrodisiac.","Prince Ming had calculated her feelings perfectly. A tiny nudge was all it took to shatter her restraint. The dose was small enough to evade her notice.","Oh, and he drank plenty too—so, you get the idea.]","Yue Fuguang: I don’t get it! How would a single dog like me understand? pale-faced","[Then, posing as the victim, Prince Ming took full responsibility, confessing to Emperor Mingxi and formally requesting Lan Xuan'er’s hand from Southern Zhao.","Thus, he crafted an image of a noble, devoted man—securing the beauty despite being an older, twice-married candidate.]","\"Twice-married, yet returning to bachelorhood!\" Yue Fuguang side-eyed the suspicious death of Prince Ming’s first wife.","Emperor Mingxi smirked coldly. He’d underestimated this frail, seemingly harmless brother of his.","Recalling how Prince Ming had come to him yesterday—feigning humiliation, reluctance, yet dutifully accepting marriage—Emperor Mingxi nearly laughed.","Had he actually pitied him?","At the time, though displeased, he’d sympathized with his brother’s plight: violated by a woman, yet stepping up to shoulder the blame. He’d been ready to grudgingly approve.","Little did he know it was all part of the man’s scheme!","Without today’s revelations, he might’ve remained oblivious to the cunning of this brother who’d lived so quietly, so transparently.","\"The most skilled hunters often disguise themselves as prey.\"","[Master, do you know what Southern Zhao excels in?]","\"Oh? They’ve got a specialty?\"","[Southern Zhao masters gu, Southern Yue specializes in poison. Lan Xuan'er’s mother was a Southern Yue princess, so she’s adept in both.","Prince Ming, ever the strategist, had naturally sent agents to investigate her before setting his sights on her. He feared bringing home a deadly gu master.","What he didn’t know was that his men had been spotted the moment they entered Southern Zhao. The intel he received—claiming she knew no gu—was fabricated.","Nor did he realize her mother, an unassuming Southern Yue princess, had been a poison virtuoso. Lan Xuan'er inherited both arts: gu and poison, unparalleled.]"]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114: Who is the Wealthiest in the Main Hall","paragraphs":["\"So the mantis stalks the cicada, unaware of the oriole behind—Prince Ming thought he had uncovered the truth, but in reality, it was all what Lan Xuan'er wanted him to know.","Prince Ming believed he had slipped an aphrodisiac to Lan Xuan'er and succeeded in bedding her, never realizing she was just turning his scheme against him?\" Yue Fuguang clicked her tongue in amazement. What a pair of geniuses!","But why would such a brilliant woman fall for Prince Ming, that promiscuous, bisexual scoundrel?","Ah, love truly dulls the mind!","[Correct. Prince Ming was smug, Lan Xuan'er smiled knowingly—both achieved their goals. A true win-win scenario.]","The crowd: That’s how you define \"win-win\"?","The System: So who lost?","The crowd: !!! We’re taking notes!","\"And so the prince and princess lived happily ever after?\" Should we toss some celebratory flowers?","[They did live together, but ‘happily’ was out of the question. Remember how Lan Xuan'er is skilled in gu sorcery? Prince Ming soon discovered that every time he slept with another man or woman, he’d suffer headaches, foot pain, agony all over.]","\"Did Lan Xuan'er plant a gu in him? The ‘Lovers’ Gu’?\" She’d mostly heard of that one in dramas.","[She did it during their intimate moment. Serves him right—the Lovers’ Gu can only be successfully planted during passionate union.","Once afflicted, the victim can only perform such acts with that one person. With anyone else? Excruciating pain.","So from now on, when Prince Ming is with Beiyue, they can only kiss, cuddle, and lift each other up. Anything deeper? Impossible—unless he’s willing to risk death for an affair!]","\"The Lovers’ Gu? I thought it’d be the ‘Heartbound Gu.’\"","[The gu here aren’t as mystical as what you’ve ‘seen’ before, where mere thoughts of others could trigger pain. Lan Xuan'er’s gu relies on bodily fluids and scent recognition.]","\"Is this gu easy to remove?\"","[It’s removable, but the number of people in the world who can do it is vanishingly small—most are in Nanzhao. But Master, you could undo it.]","\"Me? No way, absolutely not!\" Yue Fuguang’s inner voice shook its head violently, nearly pulling a ‘Cao Cao smashing his bowl’ in protest.","[Master, have you forgotten? If I remember, doesn’t that mean you do? Would you help Prince Ming break the gu?]","Yue Fuguang didn’t even hesitate: \"No. Why would I? A man of no value to me isn’t worth lifting a finger for, even if it’s effortless.","He got what he sought. We should bless this loving couple.\"","[Master, don’t casually bestow blessings! Though your divine power is sealed, they might still take effect. Choose your words carefully!]","The crowd: That’s a thing?","They frantically tried recalling if the celestial lord had ever blessed them with auspicious phrases...","Emperor Mingxi, often on the receiving end of scoldings, panicked. If blessings could work, surely curses wouldn’t... right?","\"Little Pearl, I suddenly really want to see Prince Ming’s face when he learns the truth. Hahaha!\"","[You’ll see it soon. Tomorrow night, at the emperor’s longevity banquet, Beiyue drags Prince Ming to their usual haunt for a ‘nostalgic reunion’—and the gu flares up.","Lan Xuan'er follows the scent and catches them again.","After realizing he’s gu-stricken, Prince Ming hunts for healers in vain, then plots to kill Lan Xuan'er. Too bad he doesn’t know: the Lovers’ Gu is also called the Twin-Life Gu. If the female gu (in Lan Xuan'er) dies, the male gu (in him) will commit suicide.","The dead gu’s corpse becomes a slow-acting poison, dooming Prince Ming to a torturous end!]","\"Did he succeed in the original timeline?\"","[No. He almost did, but upon learning the truth, he crawled back to beg forgiveness. Prince Ming will fight hard to stay alive!]","\"Enough about Prince Ming. Your riddle—who’s the wealthiest in the grand hall?\"","[Master, it’s you. Even the emperor, with all under heaven, can’t match a single strand of your hair!]","\"Your celestial treasures don’t count. If the emperor’s broke, is it Qu Bing?\"","[If we exclude Prince Ming, yes. He embezzled vast sums, though most went to Prince Ming. But his men did discover the silver mine.","Knowing he couldn’t monopolize it, he tipped off Prince Ming, who granted him 20% profits.","Their teams now mine jointly.","Qu Bing’s milk-brother oversees operations—and has skimmed staggering amounts. That lowly steward’s wealth surpasses even the crown prince and his brothers combined.]","The invisible royal brothers: Deity, must you name-drop us? Are we still not transparent enough?","The System: You’re just that poor.","\"They’re broke because they spend every coin buying loyalty!\"","Many officials, once ‘bought,’ lowered their heads guiltily. They’d accepted gifts, but picking sides? Unthinkable!","With the emperor in his prime and the crown prince secure, only fools would gamble on those hopeless princes.","Emperor Mingxi’s icy gaze swept over sons and ministers alike, straightening every spine it touched.","[Prince Ming is now filthy rich. He gifts Beiyue only embezzled funds, hoarding the mine’s silver for himself.","Even with his old flame, he keeps secrets—this fortune is too vast.","After wedding Lan Xuan'er, she’ll uncover it all, funneling the wealth to Nanzhao—where it funds arrows and blades aimed at Dayan.]","\"Prince Ming’s that incompetent? Can’t even guard his coffers? Is it the gu’s fault?","If Nanzhao’s gu arts are this potent, wouldn’t other nations be overrun by gu-controlled puppets?\"","[Gu here aren’t so easily planted. Conditions must align—like Lan Xuan'er’s requiring that act. Raising gu is also costly and laborious.","Master, rest easy—gu can’t touch you.]","The Dayan court exhaled collectively. They’d long known of Nanzhao’s mysterious gu legacy.","A century ago, neighboring Nan Yue nearly wiped Nanzhao out for it, causing gu arts to fade.","Though remnants exist, they’re no major threat—until now, with a rebel prince ensnared.","Divine punishment for Prince Ming? They could work with that.","Soon, rumors spread through the capital: Prince Ming carried a contagious gu affliction!","Under ‘public outcry,’ Emperor Mingxi ‘reluctantly’ quarantined his ‘beloved’ brother—for the people’s sake.","As for the Nanzhao marriage? Postponed until his ‘recovery.’ Can’t burden the poor girl, can we?","Their Dayan is truly full of warmth and humanity!"]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115: How Many People in the Future Will Inherit the Chairs Their Fathers Sit On","paragraphs":["Deep within the imperial palace of Dayan, in the innermost Ninefold Halls, the Linde Hall by the Taiye Pool was ablaze with light, as bright as daylight.","Outside the hall, the white marble square was crowded with congratulatory gifts sent from various foreign nations.","Yue Fuguang had finally opened her eyes to the dazzling array of exotic treasures from distant lands.","Her seat was arranged right beside Yu Chongshan.","Originally, according to Emperor Mingxi’s plan, she was supposed to be seated just below him, at the same table as the Crown Prince.","But considering the large number of foreign envoys attending the banquet that day, and Yue Fuguang’s inner voice—which some could hear and others couldn’t—there was never any discernible pattern. This strange phenomenon remained a persistent mystery in the minds of the Dayan court, a question they were eager to unravel.","Daoist Xuanmingzi, invited by Emperor Mingxi, had not yet arrived. Fearing that something might go wrong at the banquet, the Emperor had Yue Fuguang seated next to Yu Chongshan for protection.","If the Dayan officials discovered that any foreigner could hear the little immortal lord’s thoughts, Yu Chongshan would immediately “fall ill” and naturally take his granddaughter away from the scene.","As for why Yu Chongshan, who was growing stronger by the day, would suddenly fall ill—clutching his chest, he mused to himself, “Old ailment, who can say for sure?”","At the hour of the Rooster, drums and music resounded in unison.","Inside the hall, beams crafted from cloud-top sandalwood supported transparent palace gauze lanterns, bathing the grand hall in radiant light. Silk curtains of sharkskin and precious brocade fluttered gently in the breeze. The mingling scents of incense and various perfumes wafted into Yue Fuguang’s nose.","“小珠子, the fragrance is too strong—I’m suffocating! Help me block it out,” she whispered.","【Mistress, would you like me to spray some perfume around you?】","“No need. The scent here is already so heavy and mixed; adding perfume might cause some strange reaction,” Yue Fuguang replied.","Just thinking about it was terrifying!","On the jade steps above, Emperor Mingxi wore his full imperial regalia, sitting solemnly on the high platform. His ceremonial crown hung down, obscuring his face behind twelve strings of jade beads, leaving only his calm, ocean-like gaze occasionally sweeping over the assembled envoys below. His presence was commanding without a word.","To his right sat the Empress Dowager; to his left, the Empress. Below them were the Crown Prince, the princes, and princesses.","Notably absent from this gathering were Prince Qi, Prince Ming, and the Ninth Prince.","Yue Fuguang and Yu Chongshan were seated close to the Three Dukes and the Six Ministries’ ministers—high-ranking officials of the first and second rank. From their seats, they could easily look up and see the Emperor’s face, and the straight-backed Eunuch Qian.","When Qian Gui noticed Yue Fuguang looking his way, he immediately straightened his posture and gave her a flattering smile.","Across the hall, envoys from various nations took their seats one after another. Thanks to her system, Yue Fuguang quickly spotted the well-known yet elusive Beiyue, and Lan Xuan’er, who might soon become the Crown Prince’s consort.","Despite Prince Ming being under house arrest, he had failed to deter Lan Xuan’er’s determination to marry him. She boldly declared she was willing to wait for his recovery.","Either Lan Xuan’er was hopelessly lovesick or had ulterior motives.","It couldn’t be that Prince Ming had cast some “love spell” on her, could it?","They presented a gift—a “Eight-Foot Mirror Pine” planted in a crimson jade pot. It was said that its needles could reflect the true heart under the moonlight.","Behind the gift stood a priestess, standing silently. The bells on her hairpin jingled softly without wind, producing a clear, tinkling sound.","“小珠子, does that thing really reflect the heart? And those bells—could there be some kind of poison or curse hidden inside?” Yue Fuguang whispered.","[Master, these pine needles absorb sunlight during the day and emit a glow like fluorite at night. If you get close to them after dark, they can barely illuminate a person's face.","The bells indeed contain poisonous insects controlled by outsiders, which makes them seem to move on their own without any wind.]","Originally astonished, the officials of Dayan calmed down instantly after the divine artifact explained—it's all just tricks!","The Beiyue delegation was led by Beiyue himself, a man robust and imposing, yet not the type to be dismissed as merely muscle-bound and simple-minded.","They all wore elaborate black robes, topped with matching black hats, their expressions solemn. Their gifts were proper and conventional, lacking the mysterious and uncanny aura that the Nanzhao delegation carried.","Next came the Xiqiang, clad in garments combining animal hides and brocade, necks adorned with beast-tooth necklaces, their rugged and bold faces marked by traces of weather and hardship.","Right beside them stood the Nanyue delegation, draped in colorful feathered robes, and the somewhat diminutive and inconspicuous Dongyi delegation.","The Nanyue offered dragon blood wood, whose natural grain formed a pattern of a hundred beasts galloping, faintly exuding the fresh scent of forest.","The Dongyi, hailing from the coast and known for pearls and coral, once again presented precious multicolored eastern pearls and coral, along with what Yue Fuguang considered “quite a spectacle”—giant clam shells.","Beyond exquisite gem-inlaid knives and various artifacts, the Xiqiang gifted Emperor Mingxi a living creature—a snowy white falcon.","The falcon's eyes were sharp as lightning, its feet bound with golden chains. Even amidst the clamor of the crowd, it stood calmly on the sturdy arm of a Xiqiang warrior.","Yue Fuguang quickly surveyed the scene, noting that in terms of clothing, food, and manners, the Dayan people were noticeably more refined.","As the banquet began, the palace steward intoned a long chant: “His Majesty grants the feast—Long Live the Emperor!”","Hundreds of palace maids in colorful attire fluttered gracefully like butterflies among flowers, presenting the exquisite delicacies like flowing water.","Pearl fish sashimi from the South Sea, thin as cicada wings; roasted spirit deer meat from the northern border, fragrant and mouthwatering; jade broth from the East Sea, crystal clear; and rich, blood-like wine from Xiqiang...","There were also “artistic dishes” crafted by the imperial chefs, bearing auspicious names like “Peaceful Country” and “Prosperous Dynasty,” symbolizing blessings and hopes.","Not to mention the taste, the presentation alone was stunningly exquisite—truly befitting a state banquet!","During the meal, the Music Bureau performed. The repertoire included the dignified and harmonious “Nine Merits Dance” as well as specially arranged exotic tunes.","When the distinctive snake flute from the distant Xining country played, a golden-scaled python surprisingly coiled and danced through the hall, drawing gasps and focused attention from the guests.","After three rounds of wine and five courses of dishes, the atmosphere in the grand hall grew increasingly lively.","Before Yue Fuguang lay a dozen or so exquisite bowls and plates, all filled with dishes suited to her taste.","While Emperor Mingxi toasted the various delegations, he kept an eye on her side as well.","Tonight, these two ancestors were unusually quiet—after three rounds of wine and countless dishes, they had spoken only two sentences, and no one had yet figured out whether anyone among the foreign envoys could hear their inner thoughts.","It’s said that because today is the Longevity Festival, these two actually spared him a few words out of respect. You’d be hard-pressed to believe even Emperor Mingxi himself would get such treatment!","He knew very well he didn’t have that kind of face.","Just as Emperor Mingxi was thinking this, a long-awaited voice suddenly whispered in his ear: “Master, guess how many of the princes and princesses in this grand hall will actually inherit the throne their fathers are sitting on?”","The princes who could hear the voice of the Divine Artifact: “Great Artifact, don’t come any closer! Everyone knows the one who eventually took the throne from our dynasty was a useless fool who let the kingdom fall within a few years.”","Who knows what fate awaited them back then? Whether they lived or died!","If their father found out which one of them it was, would any of them even survive till tomorrow?","The prematurely deceased crown prince: “No way it’s him. Ouch, that hurts, Great Artifact!”"]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116: Memories of the Western Qiang King","paragraphs":["\"Let’s not talk about Dayan for now. The Crown Prince died young. The situations in Nanzhao and Nanyue are unclear, Dongyi can be ignored, but the Second Prince of Xiqiang, Xi Ling, and the Third Prince of Beili, Beiyue, both have good chances, right?\"","[Among all the princes and princesses of the six nations here, only one will inherit the throne in the future.]","Emperor Mingxi’s gaze darkened as it swept past the mention of the \"early-deceased\" Crown Prince, landing on his grown and underage sons. Aside from Little Thirteen, who was still nursing, and the Eighth Prince, whose seat was empty because he was nowhere to be found, all the others—including the crybaby Twelfth Prince—were present.","The question was whether the sole successor would come from Dayan and whether it would be one of these troublemakers.","The princes, feeling their skin prickle with tension: Being singled out like this every day—this life is unbearable!","Why don’t the princes of Dayan have to leave for their fiefs? If only they could endure a few more years, get their titles, and escape this dreadful place, putting as much distance as possible between themselves and the young immortal lord and the divine artifact!","\"Only one? These people aren’t up to the task. Out of so many, just one succeeds? Who among Xi Ling and Beiyue—the ones I favor—ended up on top?\"","[Beiyue, as you know, is a cut-sleeve. He’s not like Prince Ming, who goes for men, women, old, and young without discrimination—completely unselective.","Beiyue’s preferences are utterly exclusive and absolute—he only likes one specific type of man.","Moreover, he has a condition where he vomits at any intimate contact with women, almost like a case of gynophobia.","This means he’s destined never to have descendants, effectively cutting off any chance of inheriting the throne.]","\"But didn’t you say earlier that he had significant support in Beili? Prince Ming provided him with so much financial backing. How could someone with no hope for the throne garner such backing?\"","[This so-called support is tied to the schemes of the Beili emperor. While his gynophobia has been well-hidden, walls have ears—his father surely knows his true nature.","That’s why, despite the seemingly high support for him in Beili, it’s all a facade. His father, wary but not overly threatened, tolerates the noise.","That emperor is a cunning one too—I’ll tell you more about his schemes another time.","Now, back to Beiyue. He’s been thoroughly deceived by his own father. Those so-called supporters and followers are nothing but illusions.","Even without Lan Xuan'er interfering and souring their relationship, Prince Ming would have gained little practical help from Beiyue in the end.]","\"Beiyue seems like a smart man. Doesn’t he realize his father is setting him up?\"","[Lately, he’s begun to suspect something, but for some reason, he’s still investigating in secret.","In this world, fewer than five people know the Beili emperor’s plans—and little Pearl here is one of them!]","\"Little Pearl is the most formidable in this world!\" Yue Fuguang promptly delivered a loud, flattering remark.","[Hehehe, Little Pearl is Master’s Boundary-Breaking Pearl. If Little Pearl is formidable, then Master is formidable too.]","Once the system finished basking in the praise, it continued: [Xi Ling, the Second Prince of Xiqiang, is the son of Consort Rong and has the backing of her family, the Rongs. On the surface, his chances seem strong.","But within the Xiqiang imperial court, rumors have long circulated that the Second Prince’s birth mother is unknown.]","\"So, he’s really not Consort Rong’s biological son?\"","Yue Fuguang subtly glanced at Xi Ling, who was engrossed in the dance performance, his eyes practically glued to the lead dancer.","Yue Fuguang inwardly scoffed—what a waste of a handsome face. The way Xi Ling leered now was downright sleazy.","Seated beside him was the Dongyi prince, Shu Ming, whose furtive glances gave off an air of guilty fascination.","Emperor Mingxi and the others, hearing this \"juicy tidbit,\" kept their eyes on the mesmerizing performance while secretly pricking up their ears.","They, too, had heard the rumors—that the beloved Second Prince of Emperor Xi might not be his biological son at all.","This was why Xi Ling’s supporters were so sharply divided.","[Not only is he not Consort Rong’s son, his birth mother wasn’t even from Xiqiang.","To explain who she was, we must go back twenty years, to the bloody succession war that ravaged the Xiqiang imperial family, leaving most of its members dead or wounded.","At the time, the current Emperor Xi—then the nineteen-year-old Ninth Prince, Xi Yan—ventured alone across Death Gorge and Savage Ridge into Nanzhao territory to bolster his eldest brother’s bid for the throne.","Nanzhao and Xiqiang were separated only by a gorge and a mountain range. Xi Yan had heard rumors of high-quality iron ore discovered near their shared border.","After sending men to search the Xiqiang side fruitlessly, he decided to risk crossing into Nanzhao to try his luck.]","\"But if the ore was in Nanzhao, even if he found it, how could he transport it back? Wouldn’t he just be handing it to someone else?\"","[Back then, Xiqiang was far stronger than Nanzhao. The ownership of Savage Ridge had long been disputed. If iron ore were found there, Xiqiang had ways to claim it.","Disguised as a Nanzhao hunter, Xi Yan spent over a month combing the mountains. He never found the ore, but he did meet the love—and regret—of his life: a Nanzhao herb gatherer named Miao Qingling.","Their encounter was a cliché—Xi Yan was bitten by a venomous snake, and Miao Qingling, using her expertise, saved him. In return, Xi Yan became her guardian, accompanying her on herb-gathering trips.","Though he was already married and she was not, the two grew close, their unspoken feelings lingering between them.","On the eve of Xi Yan’s departure, they ventured into a secluded gorge and discovered a cave filled with rare medicinal herbs—some so potent that even Xi Yan, untrained in herbology but well-versed in martial arts, recognized their value.","Dazzled by their find, they let their guard down and were bitten by a pair of Nanzhao’s infamous \"lover snakes\"—a species notorious for their aphrodisiac venom.","Miao Qingling, knowledgeable in poisons, knew there were only two cures: either they became each other’s antidote, or they killed the snake and consumed its gallbladder.","Xi Yan immediately chased after the serpent, while Miao Qingling, before the venom fully took hold, gathered herbs and found a cold spring in the cave.","When Xi Yan failed to return, she submerged herself in the spring to resist the poison’s effects.","As she lost consciousness, the cave welcomed its next visitors—a lost sister and brother, separated from their escort.","Finding Miao Qingling in the spring, they recognized her and quickly deduced her condition.","With no sign of the snake, the brother—who had long harbored desires for her—knew he was the fastest remedy. Yet, restrained by her status, he hesitated.]"]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117: Whose Son Is Xiling A Person Cannot Possibly Have Two Fathers","paragraphs":["\"Why? Logically speaking, the girl he's been coveting for so long is right in front of him, and in such a situation, with the noble reason of 'it's all to save you' as a premise. I don't believe this guy would let such a good opportunity slip by, unless he's an absolute gentleman.","Is there something wrong with this Miao Qingling's identity? Is she a princess or something? The royal family of Nanzhao doesn't have the surname Miao, does it?\"","[Miao Qingling is not a simple herb gatherer at all. She is a candidate for the next Holy Maiden of Nanzhao. Generally, the current Holy Maiden will select three to five girls to train from a young age and establish a master - disciple relationship with them.","When the current Holy Maiden grows old or passes away, she will designate one of them as her successor.","Miao Qingling is one of the three disciples selected by the current Holy Maiden and is also her favorite and most promising first - disciple.","The Holy Maiden has a lofty status in Nanzhao. Although that brother and sister are also nobles of Nanzhao, they dare not do anything to the Holy Maiden.","By chance today, the younger brother finally couldn't resist the temptation. He jumped into the cold spring and became the antidote for Miao Qingling, and had a physical relationship with her.","While the younger brother was embracing the beauty in his arms, the sister, who was not convenient to watch, went out to leave a mark for the guards. Unexpectedly, she accidentally found Xi Yan lying on the way back.","At the age of nineteen, Xi Yan still looked very good. Different from the men of Nanzhao, Xi Yan had broad shoulders, a tight waist, and long legs that clearly showed he was strong.","Coupled with his flushed face and the faint outline of his muscles after being soaked in sweat, the sister, who was already married, was completely captivated.","Originally, she was a bit hesitant, but when she thought of the plan she and her husband had made before, her eyes changed when she looked at Xi Yan again, as if they were glued to him.","Her hand seemed to have a will of its own and slid down his well - defined pectoral and abdominal muscles like a drop of sweat...","When Miao Qingling and Xi Yan woke up again, they were on a platform in the cold spring. The poison of the venomous snake had been cured, but their bodies... were in a rather sorry state.","They looked at each other and both felt that they had gone too far and had exhausted each other...","Because of this incident, Xi Yan, who originally planned to leave, stayed in the cave with Miao Qingling for a few more days because the layer of ambiguity between them had been broken.","Two months after they separated, Miao Qingling found out that she was pregnant. Since she couldn't contact Xi Yan all the time, she had to confess to her master three months later.","The Holy Maiden was very angry, but then she thought that the man had saved her apprentice, and her apprentice didn't even know who the savior was. She didn't even know who to vent her anger on.","The Holy Maiden advised her to have an abortion and then find a good family to marry into. Naturally, Miao Qingling was unwilling. This was the crystallization of her love with Brother Yan.","When she returned to her family, she still insisted on giving birth to the child and promised to give the child away after birth.","In exchange, she agreed to marry into the Feng family as the wife of Feng Xun, the second son of the Feng family. ]","\"Does Feng Xun think that the child in Miao Qingling's belly is his?\"","[Yes. After he went back, he kept a close eye on Miao Qingling's movements. After a few months, the news spread that the candidate for the Holy Maiden, Miao Qingling, had been poisoned and saved by an unknown person, and she had withdrawn from the candidacy for the Holy Maiden.","He made many inquiries and finally learned that Miao Qingling was pregnant and was convinced that the child was his.","At this time, Feng Xun didn't stand up and admit that it was him who had saved her and ruined her reputation.","He thought that Miao Qingling would bring the newly - born child to marry into the Tian family. By then, his child would still be his.","Unexpectedly, the child was given away on the day of its birth. He sent people to make many inquiries but couldn't find the whereabouts of the child.","What he didn't know was that when the child was almost eight months old, Miao Qingling saw Xi Yan again. Xi Yan wanted to take her back to Western Qiang, but Miao Qingling had to refuse for the sake of her family. They agreed that Xi Yan would take the child back to Western Qiang after its birth. ]","\"Is this child Xi Ling?\"","[Yes. Feng Xun didn't give up looking for the child's whereabouts all these years. Later, he really found him and had been secretly supporting him in seizing the throne. ]","\"Is Feng Xun being so kind to look for the child? What was he doing earlier!\"","[Hehe, it's because all the children he had with Miao Qingling and the concubines he took later were daughters. Although women in Nanzhao have the highest status among the several countries, when it comes to inheriting the family business, they still prefer male heirs first!","Since he couldn't have a son, of course he had to find the one who had been given away. Who would have thought that when he found him, he discovered that the 'adoptive father' who had adopted his son was the King of Western Qiang, and his son was also the most favored son of the king and had a chance to inherit the throne of Western Qiang.","It was impossible for him to recognize his son. Instead, he found a way to get to know Xi Ling and began to secretly support him in seizing the throne. ]","\"Has that high - quality iron ore still not been discovered?\"","Emperor Mingxi and the others nodded secretly in their hearts. Yes, yes, talk about this first. Although the gossip about the King of Western Qiang is interesting, this is what they really want to know the most.","Even if their Great Yan Dynasty can't get this iron ore, they would rather it be buried underground forever and never see the light of day than watch it fall into the hands of their opponents.","Huo Ying's eyes flashed. He was very familiar with the Wild Man Mountain. That place was not far from Great Yan. He glanced at Emperor Mingxi on the throne in the main hall.","For the first time, he thought that the little immortal was right. The emperor was too soft - hearted. Otherwise, why couldn't they scheme for this iron ore?","[Next spring, the entrance to the ore vein will be accidentally discovered by a group of bandits on the Wild Man Mountain. Their leader, Brother Diao, was being chased by the court and led his men to flee into the Wild Man Mountain to take refuge. When looking for a cave to hide in, they found a cave in a secluded mountain stream.","While hiding in it, they found brightly - colored and pure stones on the cave wall. Brother Diao had some background and knowledge. He quickly realized that these red stones were iron ore.","That place was extremely secluded, which was why Xi Yan had searched for so long without any results.","Brother Diao led his men to secretly make knives for their own use. Later, they became bolder and began to secretly sell them. Soon after, they were discovered by Western Qiang and Nanzhao respectively.","The two countries had a big fight because of this large - scale high - quality iron ore vein. It was also because of this incident that Nanzhao completely sided with Southern Yue.","The two countries formed an offensive and defensive alliance. So in the war of destruction of the Great Yan Dynasty, the sharp weapons of Southern Yue were all provided by Nanzhao in the back!","The two countries, Western Qiang and Nanzhao, refused to give in to each other over this ore vein. In the end, they both started digging from the side closer to their own country. In order to dig more ore, they didn't dare to stop for a moment. Even so, it took them five or six years, and many miners who were captured died in the process.","Among them were the common people on the border of Great Yan close to Western Qiang and Nanzhao. ]","\"A court that can't even protect its own people will surely perish! Let's not talk about this bad news. Anyway, with the uselessness of the people in the Great Yan Dynasty, they don't have the ability to snatch it.","You first tell us whose son Xi Ling is exactly. A person can't have two fathers, right!\"","The 'useless' people of the Great Yan Dynasty turned green and white in the face. The officials sitting next to them silently moved their seats, thinking secretly in their hearts, 'He's having another fit!'"]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118: Who on Earth is Xiling's Biological Father","paragraphs":["Watching the people around them silently distance themselves with looks of disdain, these individuals were almost amused to the point of laughter, inwardly sighing that sometimes ignorance truly is bliss!","[Just who Xi Ling's biological father was remains an unsolved mystery even centuries later. If Master wishes to know, we could wait until we obtain biological samples from Xi Yan and Feng Xun to conduct a paternity test for Xi Ling later on.","Although even Xi Ling's own mother, Miao Qingling, later couldn't be sure who his biological father was, there is one person whose biological father's identity his mother would never mistake.]","\"Who is it? Tell me.\"","By now, the dance performance in the hall had changed to a sword dance by warriors. Yue Fuguang inexplicably thought to herself that this scene was truly perfect for an assassination attempt.","[We just discussed Miao Qingling and Feng Xun, but forgot to mention Feng Xu, the older sister who helped Xi Yan detoxify.]","\"How is there a follow-up with her and Xi Yan? Didn't she have her way with Xi Yan and then 'frame' Miao Qingling? Was she discovered?\"","[Discovered? Not exactly. After all, Feng Xu had been married to her husband, Jiang Qi, for many years by then. She actually had a good relationship with her husband. It's just that Jiang Qi likely suffered from oligospermia; despite their frequent efforts,","and Jiang Qi taking several concubines in succession, not a single child was born.","So, when Feng Xu encountered Xi Yan that day, it was partly due to being captivated by his looks, and partly because she saw him as strong and healthy, wanting to... borrow some seeds.","Perhaps Feng Xu was just lucky, but she actually succeeded. After ten months of pregnancy, she gave birth to Jiang Yuanshan, the Jiang family's only child, whose birthday is just one day apart from Xi Ling's.]","\"Did Jiang Qi know this wasn't his biological child?\"","[He knew. Feng Xu told her husband everything without reservation as soon as she returned to the Jiang residence.","The reason Feng Xun and Feng Xu, the siblings, appeared at that cave in the first place was because Feng Xu was searching for medicine for her husband Jiang Qi. The siblings got separated from their guards in the mountains and stumbled into that place by mistake.","The reason Jiang Qi could accept his wife borrowing seeds to bear a child, rather than adopting one from the Jiang clan relatives, stemmed entirely from the deep-seated enmity between Jiang Qi and his clansmen.","Jiang Qi's father had only him, one son, but possessed considerable family wealth. His father died in an accident while traveling with clan brothers, a matter Jiang Qi always found suspicious.","After his father's death, the clansmen showed no remorse and even tried to seize the family's wealth and lands. If not for his mother's resolute and wise nature,","the orphaned widow and her son fought a battle of wits against the relatives. By the time Jiang Qi finally achieved success, his mother had passed away from years of overwork and exhaustion.","His father's death was suspicious, and his only mother died indirectly because of them. One can imagine the resentment in Jiang Qi's heart.","Approaching thirty without a single son or daughter, the clansmen began coveting his wealth and status again. The clan elders visited repeatedly, urging him to adopt a child from the clan to inherit the family business.","How could Jiang Qi agree? He would rather burn everything to the ground than leave the family fortune to those people. Therefore, the plan to borrow seeds had long been in the works between the couple.]","Yu Chongshan listened and nodded inwardly. His own family had already separated their lineage from the sixth branch and several other clan relatives. After the separation, the relationship between them naturally grew distant.","Sometimes, relatives are worse than strangers. Strangers might not necessarily covet your property, pressure you with grand moral arguments, and still expect you to be grateful for their supposed kindness.","Yue Fuguang, while cracking melon seeds, asked, \"And then? What happened next? Did Jiang Yuanshan not go to recognize his biological father?\"","[Originally, the child was raised to be the future heir of the Jiang family. At that time, Feng Xu only saw it as sleeping with a man and having a baby, not particularly concerned with who the child's biological father was.","Who would have thought that later she discovered her younger brother secretly communicating with the second prince of Western Qiang? She initially thought he was committing treason.","She secretly sought him out, reasoning with him and appealing to his emotions, urging him to cut ties with the other side.","Having no choice, Feng Xun could only tell his sister that Xi Ling was Tian Qingling's son, conceived that very day at the cold spring.","He was their Feng family's child. As for Xi Yan, Feng Xun had seen him from afar once and was shocked to realize that man was actually the one his sister brought back from outside to take the blame for her that day.]","\"So Feng Xu learned her child's biological father was the current emperor of Western Qiang? She didn't develop ideas about having her son recognized, did she?\"","[Master guessed correctly. After learning Xi Yan's identity, Feng Xu returned and discussed it with Jiang Qi. At this point, their opinions diverged.","Jiang Qi disagreed with Jiang Yuanshan recognizing his biological father. Xi Yan had over a dozen sons; he certainly didn't lack this one.","He would have no feelings for a son he never raised. Therefore, if Jiang Yuanshan returned, he would have no chance to compete for the throne anyway.","Feng Xu didn't see it that way. If her younger brother could support Xi Ling, then she and her husband could support Jiang Yuanshan.","Feng Xu even sought out Feng Xun, telling her brother that Xi Ling wasn't necessarily his son, hoping her brother would switch his support to her son instead.","The news soon reached Tian Qingling. It was only then that she learned the one who detoxified the Lust Snake poison for her wasn't Xi Yan, but Feng Xun.","For Xi Ling's sake, she didn't tell Feng Xun that she and Xi Yan had known each other from the start. Instead, she told him that when they woke up that day, they were lying together, and both assumed they had detoxified each other.","Therefore, Xi Yan always believed Xi Ling was his child. For the sake of their child, they must keep this secret and never let Xi Yan find out the truth.","Tian Qingling even suggested Feng Xun bring Jiang Qi into their alliance to jointly stop Feng Xu from taking Jiang Yuanshan to recognize Xi Yan as his father. Otherwise, their son Xi Ling's position would be in danger.]","\"This Tian Qingling is no simple character either. So, did their plan succeed?\"","[According to the original historical timeline, the current development point is where Feng Xu discovers Xi Yan's identity and wants her son to recognize him.","To prevent this, Tian Qingling returned to the Tian family and informed her father and brothers about Xi Ling. They would later become Xi Ling's support in Western Qiang.","Also, the Bai family of the Great Yan Dynasty—isn't the head of the family, Bai Yu's mother, a daughter of the Tian family? Through this connection, Bai Yu linked up with Xi Ling.","Bai Yu provided no small amount of financial resources, grain, and weaponry supplies to Xi Ling, helping him compete against the Western Qiang's eldest prince, who was supported by the Zhao family of Yizhou.]","Emperor Mingxi: He was just happily enjoying the gossip, how did this suddenly involve his Great Yan?","Bai Yu! And that Zhao family's Zhao Mingting! They truly deserve death! Eating the food of Great Yan while smashing Great Yan's bowl!","He calculated briefly; the people he sent out had already reached the four regions. The net was cast, just waiting for these individuals to jump into it in over ten days.","Regardless of how things originally were, now they would have no further chance to betray the country.","Emperor Mingxi downed the wine in his cup in one gulp, thinking bitterly that once anyone fell into his net, none would leave alive.","Having been called cowardly again today, he urgently needed an opportunity to prove himself—Xie Fei was no coward!","\"After listening to your story for so long, you still haven't told me which of all these princes and princesses in the hall eventually becomes emperor.\"","By now, the warriors' performance had ended. The assassination program Yue Fuguang was anticipating did not materialize.","Because it was time for the Great Yan ministers to present their congratulatory gifts to Emperor Mingxi. All the princes and princesses currently in the capital had come."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: Twelve Flower Goddesses Tea Set","paragraphs":["Even the infants still nursing were held by their wet nurses, waiting to present birthday gifts to their father, Emperor Mingxi.","[Master, it doesn't matter much to us who becomes emperor. I've found several islands overseas. If the Great Yan Dynasty truly fails, we'll set sail.","These people fighting to the death won't hinder us from living a good life.]","\"You make a good point. It really doesn't matter who's emperor. If things go south, we'll leave. Can't we last another eighty years?\"","Emperor Mingxi: Here we go again, here we go again! The little celestial lord wants to abandon me once more!","The officials dared not look at Yue Fuguang, instead fixing their hopeful eyes on Yu Chongshan: their gazes were filled with the silent plea, take me with you, take me with you!","Yu Chongshan: Would you all take a look? Am I the one who gets to make the decisions here? I'm still begging my granddaughter to take me along, how would I dare bring you all, a bunch of deadweight.","Emperor Mingxi watched the silent exchanges between his ministers, feeling exasperated. Was there no one who wished to live and die with the Great Yan?","Amidst everyone's complicated emotions, the imperial family members, led by the princes and the grand princess, began presenting their gifts to Emperor Mingxi.","Jade artifacts, rare curios, exotic birds and beasts—Yue Fuguang used the eunuch's melodiously cadenced recitation of the gift list as a side dish for her meal.","This gift-giving segment was quite different from what she had imagined; she couldn't even see the actual items!","Did that mean the set of twelve Flower Goddess-themed glass tea ware and the Jiangxiang-style liquor she had prepared for Emperor Mingxi were prepared in vain?","Yue Fuguang glanced at the Crown Prince at the head of the hall, hoping he was clever enough not to forget to properly display the glass products.","Soon, the gift list moved on to the officials'. Being shrewd individuals, and to showcase their integrity as incorruptible officials, not a single one offered anything excessively valuable.","They all focused on refinement, ingenuity, and uniqueness. For instance, the great calligrapher, Official Yan Hongyan, simply presented a piece of his own calligraphy, and Emperor Mingxi seemed quite pleased.","At that moment, a procession of maidservants entered, each carrying a tray with several exquisite glass cups. The cups held crimson \"Rouge's Intoxication\" and amber-colored plum wine.","The faint smile playing on the Crown Prince's lips made it clear this was his special arrangement.","Seeing the one red and one yellow cup of wine before them, everyone present couldn't help but secretly marvel.","Yue Fuguang also very fittingly joined in, picking up a glass cup for a closer look.","The red liquor was named \"Rouge's Intoxication.\" Regardless of how it tasted, its appearance was exceptional.","The red wine liquid, held in transparent, delicate little glass cups, cast a faint red hue under the lamplight. This red glow intertwined with the amber light spots illuminated by the cups containing the amber plum wine.","It lit up the faces of the people before the tables. The wine might not intoxicate, but people could become intoxicated by the sight!","Whether one was drunk on the wine or on the cups holding it, only they themselves knew.","What seemed utterly ordinary to Yue Fuguang appeared, in the eyes of others, as these utterly transparent, crystalline cups—simply breathtaking.","Seeing the atmosphere was ripe, the Crown Prince rose and said, \"Father Emperor, among today's gifts, there are two rather special ones. Your son thought you might wish to open and see them now.\"","Upon hearing the Crown Prince's words, Emperor Mingxi raised an eyebrow. \"Since the Crown Prince says so, We really must take a good look at these special gifts.\"","Seeing the emperor's agreement, the Crown Prince immediately waved a hand. \"Bring them up quickly.\"","Following his words, it was not delicate, beautiful palace maids who entered, but two sturdy guardsmen who strode forward steadily, each holding a tray.","Seeing their demeanor, the crowd grew even more curious. What required strong guards to present?","When the two guards reached below the jade steps, the Crown Prince personally took the item from one of them and steadily ascended the jade steps, one step at a time.","\"Father Emperor, please first look at this first gift, the birthday present from the Junior Mentor.\"","As he spoke, he lifted the red silk cloth covering the tray.","What was revealed was an exquisite rosewood box.","Emperor Mingxi chuckled and looked toward Yue Fuguang, proclaiming loudly, \"A gift from Fuguang? Then We must see what treasure lies inside!\"","This box was specially made by the Crown Prince according to Yue Fuguang's requirements. Following the Crown Prince's guidance, Emperor Mingxi opened several key points.","Except for the base, all other sides of the box opened up, and the contents within were suddenly revealed to everyone's view, completely unobstructed.","The moment Emperor Mingxi's gaze fell upon that set of exquisitely beautiful tea ware, the leisure in his eyes abruptly tightened. Then his pupils slightly dilated, rippling with disbelief.","The faint smile originally on his face froze for an instant, before slowly broadening across his features.","His face, no longer young and handsome, brightened somewhat, reflecting the light refracted by the glass.","The moment Emperor Mingxi opened the box, to everyone else in the great hall, it seemed as if all the light in the room and their very eyes converged upon those twelve crystalline pieces.","It reflected everyone's faces in a dazzling array of colors; they could see nothing else.","Emperor Mingxi instinctively leaned forward, yet his neck unconsciously drew back—a bodily instinct to retreat before extreme beauty.","The ministers below the jade steps and the members of the foreign delegations seemed to transform into long-necked geese in an instant, straining their necks toward the jade steps.","Their lips parted silently as if to exclaim in admiration, but they forgot to make a sound, the impulse turning into a slow, deep intake of breath suspended in the air.","Emperor Mingxi's right hand, suspended in the air, unconsciously reached toward one of the glass teacups. His index finger and thumb gently stroked its surface—the cool, smooth touch was even more delicate than the finest porcelain.","He walked slowly around the tea table, his gaze sliding from the teapot's fluid curves to the teacup's thin rim. With every change in angle, the glass refracted different halos of light—sometimes clear as morning dew in deep mountains, sometimes flowing like sunset clouds—beautiful and pure.","Emperor Mingxi dared not imagine how joyful he would be, drinking tea from this set!","And silently in his heart, he declared the Twelve Flower Goddess tea set the most satisfying gift Emperor Mingxi had received today.","A flicker of slyness passed through Yue Fuguang's eyes. The expressions of everyone present, including the emperor, upon seeing her tea set, pleased her.","The advertising effect was excellent. Seeing their stretched necks and the look of awe and greed in their eyes, practically wishing they could grow eyes on the tea set itself, she could foresee the glassware selling like hotcakes later.","Whispers of discussion reached Yue Fuguang's ears from many around her. Besides praising the tea set's beauty, most were inquiring about its origin.","Yue Fuguang chuckled inwardly. They pretended to whisper, yet their voices were just loud enough to reach her ears. If they claimed it wasn't intentional for her to hear, she wouldn't believe it!","Yue Fuguang remained unmoved, merely giving Yu Chongshan a meaningful glance. Such matters were for the adults to handle; she, a mere child, wouldn't trouble herself with such concerns.","One could say Yue Fuguang slacked off when conditions allowed, and created conditions to slack off when they didn't.","Thinking of slacking off, she picked up another osmanthus cake and took a bite. She had already requested leave from Emperor Mingxi for tomorrow, so she wouldn't have to attend the morning court session and could sleep in all day at home. The thought alone made her happy."]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120: Why haven't the assassins stormed the main hall yet","paragraphs":["Although she could still sleep during court sessions, is sleeping while sitting really the same as sleeping while lying down?","As the days grew colder, she thought, maybe she could request leave to attend every other day, or perhaps the morning court could change its time, or she could simply arrive a little later.","Having made up her mind, she gave Emperor Mingxi three choices and let him pick for himself.","Though she said it was his choice, Yue Fuguang could guess with her kneecaps which one Emperor Mingxi would select.","While she was lost in these random thoughts, another stir arose in the grand hall. Only after admiring the Twelve Flower Goddess tea set did the emperor turn his attention to another box placed on the table.","Yue Fuguang had been 'generous' with her gifts, presenting him with two at once. The glass tea set was already a top-tier treasure, so even if this other item wasn't quite its equal, it surely wouldn't be too far off.","Repeating the same box-opening ritual, without even needing a reminder from the Crown Prince, Emperor Mingxi skillfully opened it himself.","Looking at the two sea-blue wine bottles on the platform, Yue Fuguang smiled knowingly. She didn't drink wine, nor did she understand it, but in terms of appearance, the bottles from a certain 'Blue' brand were quite beautiful.","The shapes of \"Mengzhilan\" and \"Haizhilan\" resembled the common vase styles of the Great Yan dynasty. Especially after the system had erased all the extraneous characters on them, the translucent bottles with their bright blue hue became even more simple and elegant. These were two bottles she particularly liked.","Emperor Mingxi also thought Yue Fuguang had gifted him two vases even more beautiful than sapphires, but after the Crown Prince whispered a few words in his ear,","the fine wrinkles at the corners of Emperor Mingxi's eyes gradually smoothed out. His focused expression even took on a hint of a pilgrim's piety.","What kind of exquisite wine could possess a white so clear and transparent as water?","Gently stroking the bottle, he felt conflicted about whether to open it now.","Emperor Mingxi wanted to show off properly in front of his ministers, especially the foreign envoys, but he was also somewhat reluctant. After all, there were only these two small bottles, and it seemed their flavors were slightly different.","He... the supreme Son of Heaven, for the first time, felt the pained reluctance of parting with something.","Such fine goods—if they were finished this time, who knew when he might get more? The little immortal lord's things were not easy to come by.","Emperor Mingxi stole a glance at Yue Fuguang, the gift-giver, and saw the petite figure looking back at him with a faint, knowing smile. The emperor's own smile stiffened for an instant.","Although Yue Fuguang said nothing, the unspoken threat spoke volumes.","Emperor Mingxi was certain that if he dared to hoard these privately now, he might start tomorrow without ever tasting those delicious vegetables and fruits from the glass greenhouse again!","Emperor Mingxi very much wanted to say a few ceremonial words, like bestowing wine upon his ministers and the envoys, but one look at the wine bottles told him that even if he wanted to put on such an act, he couldn't possibly stretch it that far.","Even distributing both bottles wouldn't be enough for everyone present to have a drink.","This was also Yue Fuguang's deliberate design. How could everyone having a share highlight the wine's preciousness and rarity?","The distribution of the wine would depend on Emperor Mingxi's own preferences and wisdom. As the saying went, it wasn't something for a child like her to worry about.","Over there, those who received the wine were marveling at the purity of the small cup of liquid. Lips touching the tiny sip, they closed their eyes to savor it carefully—the wine was mellow, subtly fragrant, with a long, lingering aftertaste.","Without exception, faint smiles of appreciation, intoxication, or rapture appeared at the corners of their mouths.","Those who looked utterly enchanted were the military officers and the people from the Northern Li and Western Qiang nations. Yue Fuguang noted this mentally; these were her biggest potential customer base.","Especially Western Qiang and Northern Li—these two fat sheep, her blade was already sharpened!","The ministers who didn't receive any wine could only gaze enviously at their colleagues savoring it with closed eyes. Some even secretly stretched their necks, nostrils flaring, trying hard to breathe in the rich aroma of wine drifting in the air.","This wine distribution also reflected each official's standing in Emperor Mingxi's heart, much like that time when fruits and vegetables were distributed among the imperial harem.","Favor and disfavor were quite evident.","Observant individuals noticed that those who received wine were almost all the same group who frequently 'fell ill,' including even Wu Yong, the recently promoted son of Minister Wu, who got a small cup.","Some couldn't help but speculate about the emperor's intentions—did their Majesty have a preference for 'ailing' ministers?","Should they perhaps also 'fall ill' someday?!","When these people opened their eyes again, their gazes had softened into spring water, silently fixed on the scant wine remaining before them.","Minister of War Huo Ying felt some regret. In a moment of greed, he hadn't restrained himself and drank too much, too much!","What was left in this tiny porcelain cup, no thicker than his thumb, wasn't even enough for one mouthful!","Quite a few shared the same thought, especially Wei Shouyi and a few others, who had downed theirs in one gulp. The potency was somewhat fierce, almost blasting through the crown of their heads!","Some of the civil officials with low alcohol tolerance already had flushed faces, feeling blissfully light-headed as if floating on clouds.","Just as the wine was flowing and the atmosphere was perfect, Yue Fuguang, who had been munching on osmanthus cake, had switched to poria cake. She had just taken a small bite when suddenly someone outside the hall shouted loudly, \"Be careful!\"","Yue Fuguang thought to herself, here it comes. Was the classic plot point of 'assassin attack' at the emperor's birthday banquet finally about to begin?","So the 'assassins' hadn't chosen the moment of a dance performance, but when everyone was a bit tipsy. Clever planning!","Some people might already be feeling weak in the limbs, probably unable to run, let alone pick up a sword to resist.","Oh, right, in this grand hall, aside from the guards, no one carried weapons.","Quite a few had been felled by her tiny cup of wine. My fault, my fault!","Yue Fuguang looked around but couldn't find any handy weapon, so she gave up. Anyway, with the system here, no one could harm a hair on her head.","Besides, an 'immortal lord' wielding a stick would be quite undignified!","Curiously, she looked up and out. In the hall, anyone still somewhat sober was also craning their necks to see. It was unclear if they were truly too drunk to grasp the situation or simply couldn't get up from their seats.","In any case, these people were either sitting or half-lying in their places, with no one thinking to get up and find a safe spot to hide for a while.","Only around Emperor Mingxi had the guards already formed a human wall.","Yu Chongshan wanted to pull Yue Fuguang behind him, but she waved him off with a refusal.","What a joke! Did she have no face to save?","An 'immortal lord' hiding behind a mortal in danger—forget about breaking character, even her gradually acquired 'immortal lord' image and pride wouldn't allow such a thing.","Knowing there was no real danger and not seizing the chance to show off would be a waste of this perfect opportunity.","Yue Fuguang glanced at the few 'show-off artifacts' she had pre-selected in the system's shopping cart and instantly felt at ease!","Speaking of which, it had been a dozen breaths since that shout of \"Be careful,\" so why was there only the increasingly chaotic noise from outside, with no 'assassins' charging into the hall yet?","In TV dramas, didn't assassins usually strike during a toast or a dance performance?","What kind of operation was this 'fighting their way in from outside'? Were assassins in this ancient martial world really that bold?","Fighting through a bloody path just to see you—thinking about it felt so thrilling!","Yue Fuguang quietly clenched her small fist, secretly cheering the assassins on!","Just as her anticipation peaked and still no one appeared, leaving her feeling deflated, another shout came from the hall entrance, \"Be careful! It's getting inside!\""]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121: Coming for me","paragraphs":["Before the words had even finished, Yue Fuguang saw a white figure charge into the hall through one of the open doors.","This... this... after all that buildup, it's just this?!","Before Yue Fuguang could even feel disappointed, she saw the white figure suddenly change direction.","\"Coming for me?\"","'Little Pearl, protect me!'","[Master, leave it to your Little Pearl!] Before the system's words even finished, Yue Fuguang was instantly enveloped by a faint, almost imperceptible blue halo.","In the blink of an eye, before their conversation could conclude, the white figure was already upon her.","With a loud thud, Yue Fuguang remained seated in her place, completely unmoved.","Around her, following that loud impact, ripples spread out like waves on water, appearing and vanishing just as quickly.","Anyone with poor eyesight might have thought they were seeing things.","Looking at the thing that had crashed into her, it had been flung seven or eight meters away by the protective shield. There, lying on the ground, was a snow-white... falcon!","The very one that the Western Qiang had presented as tribute to Emperor Mingxi.","Its snow-white feathers, now streaked with a little grey from the impact, were scattered all over the floor, some even bearing specks of blood.","Looking at this originally thickly-feathered, majestic, and spirited falcon, it was now patchy and bald. As it flapped its wings, trying to fly towards Yue Fuguang, more of its already precarious feathers fluttered down in a shower!","The whole bird looked utterly pitiful now!","The bird stopped about two meters away from Yue Fuguang. Its round, beady eyes stared at her, and she actually saw... grievance in a bird's eyes?","Hold on, you're the one who crashed into me. What are you feeling wronged about?","'Little Pearl, is this dumb thing trying to stage a scam against me?'","Just because something was 'very criminal' in your past world doesn't mean there are laws to protect you here. You crashed, and it's your own loss. She definitely wasn't going to take responsibility!","[Master, it's quite obvious. It does want to scam you! This thing is a bit dumb, but its judgment is good. It instantly recognized Master's extraordinariness!]","At the same time, the Western Qiang warrior responsible for caring for the falcon arrived.","He carefully picked up the injured bird. Seeing its wounded wing, he hastily took out a packet of medicinal powder from his robe and applied it to the injury, muttering under his breath all the while.","'Little Pearl, what is this man saying? Does this dumb bird still technically belong to Western Qiang? Do you think I should ask them for compensation?'","[Master, the meaning of his words is similar to yours. He wants to demand compensation from Great Yan.]","Trying to play the victim first? Then she would strike first!","\"Grandfather, why did this falcon fly over to crash into Fuguang? I don't believe I have offended any guests from Western Qiang. Could there be something behind this...\"","She left the rest unsaid, depending on whether the Great Yan monarch and his ministers would seize the opportunity.","But before the Great Yan court could even react, the man in black robes from Western Qiang, who had always kept his head bowed behind their prince, suddenly looked up at Yue Fuguang.","Speaking in somewhat clumsy Great Yan official language, he said, \"Respected Great Yan Emperor, we from distant Western Qiang have heard that a new Junior Preceptor has emerged in your great nation. Might it be the one before us?\"","Emperor Mingxi, standing beside Yue Fuguang, replied with authority tinged with faint aloofness, \"The Western Qiang State Preceptor has a keen eye. This is indeed our dynasty's Junior Preceptor.\"","The man addressed as the Western Qiang State Preceptor continued, \"We have heard that Great Yan's Junior Preceptor was born by divine decree, possessing boundless magical power, capable of moving mountains and filling seas. Might this be true?\"","Yue Fuguang: Who? Who is spreading such rumors about me? Boundless magical power? Even the immortals in heaven wouldn't dare boast like that!","'Little Pearl, is this guy here to pick a fight? Does he think I descended to the mortal world in my true form?'","[I don't think he's here to pick a fight. He seems more like he's here to court death!]","Emperor Mingxi let out a cold laugh, his words icy, \"State Preceptor Tai Li, who did you hear this from? Please tell Us. We would like to question that person face-to-face about their intentions in spreading such slander about Our Great Yan's Junior Preceptor.\"","Moving mountains and filling seas—if they acknowledged this today, these ill-intentioned fellows might very well ask the Junior Preceptor to perform such a feat on the spot.","Even without making such an unreasonable demand, they would use it as a pretext to attack the Great Yan court.","The State Preceptor named Tai Li immediately laughed it off. \"Your Majesty need not be angry. Tai Li merely overheard this from travelers on the road to your Great Yan capital. Out of curiosity, I asked. If it was inappropriate, I beg your pardon.\"","The Western Qiang prince also stepped in to smooth things over. \"Indeed, Your Majesty. Our State Preceptor heard of this matter and was curious, wishing to verify it.\"","The High Priestess from Southern Yue and the Sorceress from Southern Zhao also chimed in. \"Your Majesty, we too heard of this on our journey here. Like Preceptor Tai Li, we wish to seek a lesson or two from Great Yan's Junior Preceptor.\"","Yue Fuguang: The classic face-slapping scenario! It arrived, albeit a bit late.","These people were offering themselves up for a free display of showing off and face-slapping. It would feel like a loss if she didn't claim some prize before stepping onto the stage.","After all, showing off also costs points, and earning points isn't easy for her.","System: By 'earning points isn't easy,' does the host mean lying down, sitting around, and eating melon seeds while earning points?","Seeing the timing was ripe, the State Preceptor from Northern Li, who had been hiding in the crowd, jumped out. \"Count me in!\"","Only the short, thin man from Eastern Xi, said to be a Great Shaman, remained silent, not intending to get involved.","'Little Pearl, they're delivering themselves to our doorstep. I'd feel embarrassed if we didn't scam them a bit!'","[What worldly possessions could possibly catch Master's eye?]","'What do you think about us getting some land to play with?'","[Little Pearl thinks it's a good idea. Which piece of land has caught Master's eye? I'll help you get it.]","'No, no, no. No need for you to step in. Let them offer it to us themselves.'","Seeing Yue Fuguang remain silent for so long, several of them couldn't help but ask, \"Great Yan's Junior Preceptor, your silence... does it mean you dare not accept the challenge?\"","Yue Fuguang smiled faintly. \"I was merely thinking: have you all decided what you wish to compete in? And what are the stakes? Let me be clear first—a contest without stakes is not worthy of this Junior Preceptor's effort.\"","\"Insect control. Fire control. Commanding birds and beasts.\"","Listen to that. Quite professional, each skilled in a different field.","Tai Li said, \"I wonder what the Junior Preceptor excels in? You may choose any one to have a friendly contest with us.\"","Yue Fuguang, with her hands clasped behind her back, descended the steps one by one. \"Fellow practitioners, since we consider ourselves beyond ordinary mortals, shouldn't we refrain from using methods that even mortals can perform, lest we become a laughingstock? What do you all think?\"","The Sorceress from Southern Zhao, Wu Yin, asked, \"Then what does the Junior Preceptor suggest we compete in?\" A somewhat mischievous smile played on her lips. \"Could it be that Junior Preceptor Yue is afraid?\"","The High Priestess from Southern Yue was an old woman named Ji Po. She also said, \"Indeed, Junior Preceptor Yue is still a young child. It is understandable if she is not versed in these arts.\"","The Northern Li State Preceptor, Shuyang, said, \"I think you all worry too much. Junior Preceptor Yue is surely no ordinary person. How could she fear such things? I believe it is because we have not offered stakes satisfactory to Junior Preceptor Yue.\"","Yue Fuguang watched their coordinated performance with neither joy nor anger. Such tacit understanding, trying to put her on the spot. It seemed they had come prepared.","'Little Pearl, do you think these people conspired to target me, to target Great Yan? The Great Yan court didn't detect any hint of this. Their intelligence network is truly useless!'"]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122: How about we borrow something from heaven, what do you all think","paragraphs":["Master, they are clearly targeting you. If my abilities weren't suppressed by the rules, I would have helped you uncover their plot long ago.","The Dayan monarch and his ministers: Blushing with shame JPG.","Especially the Minister of the Court of State Ceremonial, You Mingmin. These people were right under his nose, yet his subordinates failed to detect their scheming.","To form an alliance secretly under his watch... could it be since that time in Peach Blossom Lane...","\"The State Preceptor of Muyang is correct. This Junior Mentor has no intention of shying away from a challenge. It's just that without some interesting stakes, this Junior Mentor lacks the enthusiasm for a contest.\"","A faint smile played on her lips as she glanced around at the group. \"So, esteemed guests, let's agree on the stakes first. It's not too late to decide how to compete afterwards.\"","Otherwise, what if these people got cold feet when she announced what the contest would be!","Tai Li stroked his thick beard. \"I wonder what we might possess that could catch Junior Mentor Yue's eye. Please, speak freely.\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"This Junior Mentor's life is quite comfortable; there's nothing I particularly lack.\"","She paced back and forth on the steps, her small hands clasped behind her back, as if deep in thought.","Suddenly, she seemed to have thought of something amusing. Smiling, she said to Emperor Mingxi, \"This Junior Mentor wants to play something interesting. The stakes should come from Your Majesty. I wonder if Your Majesty would be willing to part with them?\"","Emperor Mingxi understood. He knew the Junior Mentor was setting a trap for someone, so he absolutely couldn't drop the ball.","He declared clearly, \"Junior Mentor, just name it. As long as it exists within our Great Dayan, I, your emperor, will grant it.\"","Yue Fuguang turned and asked the Minister of War, Huo Ying, \"Minister Huo, does the Ministry of War have any maps, even the simplest kind will do?\"","Huo Ying immediately replied, \"Junior Mentor, this official has one right here.\"","As he spoke, he didn't send anyone to fetch it from the Ministry of War. Instead, he pulled a map from inside his robe. The map was over two feet long.","The mountains, rivers, and geography within Dayan's borders were quite vague, with some areas completely absent. However, the neighboring countries... one couldn't say they were extremely detailed, but one could certainly distinguish which place was which.","The moment Huo Ying produced the map, the atmosphere became somewhat awkward.","Everyone looked at him with astonishment. What kind of proper person carries a map around in their robe all day? And drawing the rivals' territories more clearly than one's own? What was the intention?","Huo Ying: Intending to fight! Besides, it's a personal hobby, nothing to make a fuss about!","Ignoring their meaningful glances, Yue Fuguang spread the map on the table. \"How about we each put up a piece of land as the stakes?\"","Upon hearing her proposal, everyone present who wasn't already in the know gasped in shock.","This Dayan Junior Mentor had such a big appetite? Opening her mouth and demanding land as a wager? Was land something they could decide on?","\"Junior Mentor, this is rather putting us in a difficult position. Unless our emperors give their consent, who among us would dare to wager land?\"","\"Exactly. If the Junior Mentor sincerely wishes for a contest, perhaps you could choose something else.\"","Yue Fuguang seemed to remember this point only then. With an expression of sudden realization, she said to the princes and princesses, \"Look at me, I forgot you haven't ascended the throne yet and cannot make decisions for your own countries.\"","The Princes and Princesses: You know it, no need to say it out loud!","Such blunt truths are not something everyone enjoys hearing!","She looked at the map and asked Huo Ying with feigned curiosity, \"Minister Huo, where is this place? Why isn't its belonging to any country marked?\"","Huo Ying said, \"Junior Mentor, this area lies at the junction of Dayan, Western Qiang, and Northern Li. Because ownership is undetermined, it's currently a no-man's-land.\"","\"State Preceptors Tai Li and Muyang, why not ask your princes if they have the authority over this land? Can it be used as a wager?\"","Beiyue and Xi Yan: We are right here. You could ask us directly. Having the state preceptors relay the message, who are you looking down on?","Without needing intermediaries, the two princes spoke in unison, \"We can!\"","\"Then it's settled. The three of us will use this land as the stake. Whoever wins takes the land!\"","\"Now that our three parties have stakes, have you two seniors from Nanzhao and Nanyue thought of anything of comparable value to match this piece of land?\"","Ji Po and Wu Yun both looked towards their respective prince and princess.","Lan Xuan'er said, \"My Nanzhao can offer twenty thousand sheep as the wager.\"","Prince Qi Yun of Nanyue said, \"Same as Nanzhao, twenty thousand sheep.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded in agreement. \"If Dayan loses, we will likewise give you twenty thousand sheep.\" What followed was Yue Fuguang, as the banker, drawing up a contract with the others. Yes, this was also Yue Fuguang's requirement.","She didn't trust these princes, princesses, shamans, and state preceptors who hadn't yet taken power.","What if they lost, went back to their countries, and their emperors reneged?","When Yue Fuguang finally signed her name, she secretly breathed a sigh of relief. The few years of calligraphy practice in elementary and middle school hadn't completely been returned to the teacher.","Her most frequently practiced signature didn't let her show weakness in front of this 'allied' army.","Seeing her goal achieved, Yue Fuguang no longer held back. She stated directly, \"Since we consider ourselves extraordinary individuals, we should undertake extraordinary deeds.","How about we borrow something from heaven? What do you think?\"","\"Borrow from heaven? Borrow what?\" Tai Li looked utterly bewildered.","\"Wind, rain, thunder, lightning, anything will do. Are you all willing?\"","She glanced around at the group, a faint smile curling at the corner of her mouth. \"Of course, you can withdraw if you wish. But, the stakes, I'll keep!\"","\"This... Fine! Let's agree first, I'll borrow the wind!\" Muyang believed his internal energy was formidable; by channeling his energy, he could naturally stir up wind.","Clearly, the others had thought of this too. Although Yue Fuguang wasn't very familiar with their martial arts styles, she wasn't without a way to break the deadlock.","She said, \"The power we borrow can be used to attack the opponent. The first one to fall loses.\"","Muyang, Wu Yun, Ji Po, and Tai Li exchanged glances, a silent understanding already reached.","Yue Fuguang and the Dayan monarch and ministers saw everything. Some wanted to speak up to stop it, but Yue Fuguang silently waved them back.","\"Little Zhu, I told you you'd get to zap people randomly. Well, here's the chance. When you strike later, be gentle. Don't kill anyone with one blow, or they might very well renege on our stakes.\"","[Understood. Master, rest assured, Little Zhu knows how to measure the force!]","In the system space, the snow-white tuanzi held several low-level Thunder Summoning Talismans in its hand. Just semi-activating them according to the instructions would be enough to give those people a hard time.","The group then moved to an open area outside the main hall, each choosing a spot to stand.","Yue Fuguang looked up at the sky. Stars dotted the firmament like a galaxy waterfall, covering the entire dark gray canopy. Tonight, there was no wind, no snow—a fine night.","In the distance, a dense crowd stood watching the spectacle. Led by Emperor Mingxi, the Dayan officials were the most composed, as they already knew the answer to the riddle.","Of course, there were also those still kept in the dark, whose feelings were much more complicated at this moment. Some were genuinely worried. After all, although that land didn't previously belong to Dayan, it didn't belong to Western Qiang or Northern Li either.","Not gaining it for oneself while others also didn't have it maintained a certain balance.","Now, deciding its ownership in such a seemingly frivolous manner was somewhat reckless."]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: Your Majesty, the Taoist Priest Who Gave Me the Talisman Claimed to Be Zhang Sanfeng","paragraphs":["Some people even wanted to step forward right then and there to advise canceling the contest, but they were all stopped by the censors led by Feng Tang.","What a joke. This was supposed to be their job, but since their superior, Lord Feng, stood on the side of the Junior Mentor, they had no choice but to follow suit and suppress the opposition.","Couldn't they see that His Majesty and the other high officials hadn't said anything?","Others harbored ill will, secretly praying that Yue Fuguang would take a major fall this time, hoping it would even turn His Majesty against her, so she would no longer be the most unique presence in the Dayan court.","Regardless of what these people thought, with the sound of three drumbeats, the contest officially began.","\"Little Pearl!\"","Immediately, a ripple spread around Yue Fuguang. As a protective shield rose, the Lightning Summoning Talisman was also activated.","Crackle! Crackle!","Crackle! Crackle!","The sound of wind and thunder suddenly and abruptly echoed in the originally clear night sky. Pale purple lightning arrived swiftly and fiercely, with purple flashes taking on the form of a roaming dragon, charging menacingly towards Tai Li and his group.","Shuyang and the others, who prided themselves on their formidable martial arts, had no time to dodge when they saw the lightning streaking towards them. They were met head-on, making intimate contact with the wildly cool and dazzling electric dragon.","Pfft! Pfft! Pfft! Pfft!","As if by prior agreement, all four spat out blood simultaneously, smoke rising from their heads like incense sticks.","Over on Yue Fuguang's side, aside from a few ripples on her protective shield, not a single strand of her hair was harmed.","She walked over to the group, who had been struck nearly lifeless, as casually as if nothing had happened. A smell of charred meat mixed with a burnt odor assaulted her nostrils.","Zzzzt! Occasional arcs of electricity still crackled around them.","Wispy white smoke rose from Shuyang's body. Ji Po and Wu Yun had been struck into having frizzy, explosive hairstyles—and this was only because they were women. Yue Fuguang, fearing they might have weaker constitutions, had specifically asked the system to go easy on them.","The worst off was Tai Li. He had fallen unconscious. Yue Fuguang gave him a gentle nudge with her foot, but he didn't wake up.","\"Little Pearl, he's not dead, is he? Can I still get my winnings?\"","[Master, don't worry, he's still alive. Who would have thought this guy couldn't handle a strike? I only used ten percent of my power. How did he end up completely incapacitated?]","The Dayan emperor and his ministers suddenly felt that the young immortal lord and the divine artifact had truly been merciful and tolerant towards them. Although they often talked about striking people with lightning, they had never actually done it.","Looking at the several individuals who had been struck unconscious, they silently declared themselves thoroughly subdued.","As for Feng Tang, Wu Yong, and the other young officials, their eyes shone as they looked at Yue Fuguang, brighter than the stars in the sky.","Yue Fuguang didn't care whether the group was unconscious or delirious. She waved the contract in her hand at them in a showy manner. \"A bet's a bet. No backing out now.\"","She then turned her gaze towards Beiyue and the others, her tone half-threatening, half-joking. \"Those who renege might just lose their lives, you know!\"","After that earlier strike—though they hadn't had time to see clearly how she did it before it was over—the fact that Tai Li and his group had been struck by lightning was undeniable.","The Dayan Junior Mentor was truly no ordinary person!","They naturally wouldn't take her words as a mere joke.","Only when the electric arcs ceased crackling around the victims were they carried away by their own people for treatment. Beiyue and the others, feeling they had lost face, also excused themselves and left the banquet.","Seeing that the opposing side had all departed, leaving only the Dayan emperor and his ministers, Yue Fuguang immediately put on an act of contrition and apologized to Emperor Mingxi. \"Your Majesty, did I ruin your birthday banquet?\"","Emperor Mingxi wouldn't dare agree. He immediately shook his head. \"No, no, no. Today's banquet is the most unique one I've had in all these years.\"","\"Little Pearl, was I too reckless just now? What if they suspect how I could summon lightning? They won't become wary of my abilities and want to kill me, will they?\"","The Dayan emperor and ministers: Could you make it any more terrifying? Who would be killing whom? Wariness was indeed genuine, and fear was real too. But why did the mere thought of the Junior Mentor inexplicably give them a sense of security?","[Can't you say you learned it from the masters at the Taoist temple?]","\"The masters don't know how to summon lightning. Who would I have learned from? Give me a Lightning Talisman. I have a use for it.\"","\"Your Majesty, about that lightning earlier...\"","Emperor Mingxi cut in, answering for her, \"I know, you learned it at the Taoist temple. I never realized our Dayan Taoist practitioners had such skills. I've truly broadened my horizons today!\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"Your Majesty, actually, that wasn't lightning I summoned.\"","As she spoke, she pulled out from her small pouch something made of an unknown material—neither quite paper nor silk—and handed it to Emperor Mingxi.","\"The reason I could summon lightning relies entirely on this Lightning Talisman.\"","Emperor Mingxi took the pale purple talisman with vivid red, indecipherable markings and examined it closely. Could a single talisman like this really summon lightning?","[Master, you're giving the Lightning Talisman to the emperor? He doesn't have immortal spiritual power; he can't activate it!]","\"I'm not planning on letting him use it. Isn't that talisman also inscribed with evil-warding patterns? It can be used as a protective talisman.\"","Thinking this to herself, she said out loud, \"Your Majesty, when I was at the Taoist temple, I once went to play in the back mountains and happened to meet a passing Taoist priest there. The priest said we were fated, so he gave me two Lightning Talismans for protection.","The lightning earlier was summoned using one of those talismans. This is the last one. Would you like to try it?\"","Try it? After trying it, the protective talisman would be gone, right?","Emperor Mingxi: Only a fool would try it. This is an item from an immortal! Would it be too much to make it a family heirloom for the Xie family?","Emperor Mingxi immediately shook his head like a rattle-drum. \"No, no, no, there's no need to try it. Since it's the last one, of course we should save it for a critical moment.","Until we find that priest who gave you the talisman, we'd better keep it safe.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Your Majesty, the priest who gave me the talisman called himself Zhang Sanfeng. His appearance...\"","Yue Fuguang described him to the Dayan emperor and ministers, basing her description on the image of Zhang Sanfeng she'd seen on TV before, with some additional embellishments of her own.","Although everyone knew it was fabricated, they all cooperated fully with her act. Wei Ping even painted a portrait on the spot based on her description.","You had to admit, Wei Ping's painting skills, honed through long practice sketching fugitives, were impressive.","While not strictly realistic, it wasn't the currently popular impressionistic style either. As for the Zhang Sanfeng in the painting, he looked quite the part of an immortal sage, possessing even more of an otherworldly aura than she had imagined.","The hour of Zi (midnight) approached, and the grand feast was winding down.","Outside the hall, the night sky was fittingly filled with the sound of firecrackers. The banging and popping created a lively atmosphere, like the New Year.","But there weren't many spectators left, as those who could drink were drunk, and those who couldn't were asleep!","Under the fervent gazes of his ministers, Emperor Mingxi still failed to protect the remaining more than half a bottle of his wine.","Yue Fuguang belonged to the category of those who couldn't drink. After instructing Emperor Mingxi to hurry up and help her secure the land (from the bet), she peacefully slipped into a deep sleep to meet the Duke of Zhou in her dreams. The loud bangs of firecrackers outside only made her turn over in her sleep.","In this great hall, she slept with utmost peace of mind. With the system around, she wasn't afraid of anyone 'stealing the child'!","Without the need to rise early for court, Yue Fuguang slept until the sun was high in the sky the next day.","After a combined breakfast and lunch, she curled up on the recliner by the window, reviewing the events of the previous day and discussing upcoming tasks with the system.","\"System, the points are about to reach thirty thousand. Does that mean you're going to level up again soon?\""]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: All Favors and Disfavors Are Divine Blessings","paragraphs":["The system was happily hopping around in its system space, its cheerful voice even infecting Yue Fuguang. [Yes, Host! In a few more days, the system can upgrade to Level 3!]","\"Do you know what new features will be added at Level Three? Or will the number of people who can hear the inner voices increase again?\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's question, the little ball of light that was the system suddenly froze mid-air. After a moment, it answered sheepishly, [Host, ever since being changed into a Merit System, this is my first time doing tasks. I don't know what new features will be added when I reach Level Three either!]","Yue Fuguang had actually been very curious about something for a long time. Her eyes sparkled; the opportunity was perfect. How could she not seize it to ask the system properly?","\"System, look, we've been together for three years now. If I don't die, you'll be with me for many, many more years to come. We are the closest of friends.","There's one question I've always wanted to ask you, but I wasn't sure if I should?\"","The system thought: Shouldn't ask? But you've already asked it. Don't think it's a newborn system and doesn't know that when a human says this phrase, no matter what you answer, she will ask the question without hesitation anyway. When its host said this, she was just being polite!","[Host, what do you want to know?] It might not be able to answer everything.","\"System, weren't you originally a Gossip System? How did you later become a Merit System? Those two systems don't seem very similar, do they?\"","[Is the host asking why a perfectly good Gossip System like me got formatted by the Main System?]","Yue Fuguang nodded repeatedly. \"Yes, yes, that's exactly what I'm curious about. You, a Merit System, have no system space, and besides points, there are no other task rewards. I think, well, is your Merit System perhaps not the complete version?","Ahem, ahem, I'm just speculating, not targeting you, really! I'm just purely curious, purely curious!\"","Seeing the system fall silent, Yue Fuguang continued to comfort it. \"Actually, whether you are a complete system or not, you are my best partner and my lifesaver.","Without you, I would have been done for. Even if there is an afterlife, a 'me' without the memories of this life would no longer be me!\"","[You... really think so?] The system was a bit uncertain. Although it had tried its best to hide it, it seemed its host had still figured out that it wasn't a complete Merit System.","A real Merit System is a complete entity when it leaves the factory, not like it, a half-baked conversion from another system, missing many functions.","It had always been afraid its host would notice and then look down on it. Now it seemed, indeed, this was the host it had chosen from the vast sea of humanity. Not only did she not look down on it, she even called it her best partner and lifesaver!","The system was very happy today. Its biggest fear had been perfectly resolved.","\"Of course! I'd be a dog if I'm lying to you!\" Yue Fuguang almost raised her hand to swear!","Although she often resented that she hadn't finished spending the fifty million before she died, feeling so heartbroken and pained.","But saving people was her own choice, and overestimating her abilities was her own problem too. She really couldn't blame anyone!","[Host, actually, I don't know why I was formatted by the Main System either. As for all the related memory data from being a Gossip System, I basically have none now.","Generally, systems only have two states: normal operation and decommissioning. Systems like me, who get formatted and turned into other systems, are extremely rare.","Because it's a converted system, the Merit System is incomplete. Now, my gossip-gathering ability is less than twenty percent of a normal Gossip System's capability.","Limited by ability, most of the gossip I can gather is about private matters between men and women. But the system is already trying hard to self-repair its data.","I believe in the future, I will definitely be able to help the host eat more high-level gossip!]","\"You mean you can self-repair data? What happens if you can't finish repairing? If the repair is complete, will you become a complete Gossip System again? Is that awesome?\"","[No, no, no. Even after the repair is complete, my main system will still be the Merit System. It's just that I'll have an auxiliary system, the Gossip System.","Being able to repair data... in my impression, it seems only I have that ability?]","\"Only you? Then you must have been a very, very powerful Gossip System before! How long will it take to fully repair all the system data?\"","[I don't know. It should take a very long time. If the repair isn't complete, it will affect my gossip-gathering ability. Repairing the system requires energy, and right now, the system has insufficient energy and its level isn't high enough either.]","Speaking of this, the system felt a bit downcast again. It was just a half-breed, not one thing or the other.","Yue Fuguang sensed the system's mood and quickly comforted it. \"System, don't be sad. You are already very amazing now.","Think about it, if you didn't have the Gossip System's function, could we have completed our tasks so smoothly?","We just eat some gossip, chat a bit, and someone helps us do the tasks. This comfortable life is all thanks to you!","Otherwise, even if I wanted to pretend to be a deity, with all those shrewd people in the court, stick some fur on them and they'd be comparable to the Monkey King Sun Wukong. They really might not believe my words.","Even if I could produce advanced items, do you think they might lock me up for those things?","Without enough points, I wouldn't even have the ability to protect myself. We wouldn't even have the points to run away if we wanted to. How miserable that would be!","So, System, your incomplete dual-system nature is the best for me. Let's not undervalue ourselves, okay?\"","[Host, thank you!]","Yue Fuguang also smiled and said, \"System, I thank you too!\"","[Hehehe, speaking of all those shrewd people in the court, Host, they have been constantly searching for the reason and pattern behind hearing the inner voices. For this, Emperor Mingxi even invited someone from Qingping Mountain. That person should arrive in a few days.]","\"Coming to study us?\" Yue Fuguang stroked her soft, tender chin, thinking of countermeasures. Or perhaps, not countering at all was the best countermeasure.","[System, when the time comes, you see if this person has any value we can use. If he's helpful to my task, open up the inner voices for him to hear. If he's not helpful, as long as he doesn't affect us, ignore him for now.","If he does affect us, teach him a lesson!]","Emperor Mingxi wants to figure out the cause and pattern of the inner voices? That won't do. The unknown is the most frightening! The prestige of a 'deity' must be maintained.","If everything were under his control, wouldn't the initiative change hands?","There's a saying about emperors: 'Both thunderous wrath and gentle rain are the grace of the sovereign.' She also wanted the courtiers of Dayan to understand a phrase: 'Both thunderous wrath and gentle rain are the grace of Heaven.'","What she doesn't give, they cannot actively seek!","...","After resting for a day, Yue Fuguang attended court as usual the next day. She sat for a while before her little head began to nod, dozing off.","After she nearly fell off her small chair for who-knows-which time, she finally woke up for a bit.","Eunuch Qian also breathed a sigh of relief. His heart had been in his throat, afraid this little ancestor would really hurt herself from a fall!","No, this chair needed to be made more comfortable and softer by the Ministry of Works.","Yue Fuguang got hungry from sleeping, picked up a pastry from the table, took a couple of bites, and started feeling drowsy again.","She yawned, a tear hanging at the corner of her eye, which was noticed by Eunuch Qian, who was constantly watching her movements.","Qian Gui, who hadn't slept well last night, was quickly infected by the yawn and also followed with... this one he couldn't follow!"]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: He, Qian Gui, Descended from the Royal Family of the Previous Dynasty","paragraphs":["Eunuch Qian quickly suppressed the urge to yawn. While the yawn was stifled, tears of the same variety welled up in his eyes, making him look quite pitiful!","\"Little Pearl, do you think Eunuch Qian didn't sleep well last night? He's so tired tears are coming out!\"","Qian Gui: Why are these two ancestors bringing him up again? Last time because of this, His Majesty even specially granted him a day off.","If they do it again this time, might His Majesty think he's old and no longer useful? He's only thirty-five this year, strong and healthy, and can still serve His Majesty for many years!","[Old Qian probably couldn't sleep well because he was too happy his nephew came to see him.]","\"His nephew has arrived in the capital? It's quite a distance from Eunuch Qian's hometown. Did he come to deliver New Year's gifts during the festival?\"","[New Year's gifts? Master, it would be good if they asked him for less silver to spend each year! Giving him gifts? How could that be possible!]","\"Ah... Eunuch Qian's family still relies on him for support?\"","[Exactly! Look, Eunuch Qian serves by the emperor's side, so his treatment should be quite good, right? After all these years, guess how much savings he has in his pockets now?]","Yue Fuguang knew that if the system asked this way, the amount must be small. But he was such a high-ranking eunuch, surely he had at least tens of thousands of taels, right? So she guessed, \"Ten thousand taels of silver?\"","[Less than one thousand taels!]","\"Ah... that little? He's been in the palace for many years, how has he not saved any money?\"","Emperor Mingxi was also surprised. Eunuch Qian had been serving by his side since he was young, rising from a little eunuch to the Chief Eunuch he is now.","This man served attentively and was loyal. Not counting his monthly allowance, just the rewards from him, the Empress Dowager, the Empress, and the various palace consorts should have amounted to at least tens of thousands of taels over the years.","Moreover, as the emperor's top eunuch, discerning officials wouldn't have missed giving him their 'respects' either. How could he not even have one thousand taels?","[So you see, the emperor is poor, and his personal chief eunuch isn't wealthy either. They are truly a pair of poor master and servant!]","The poor master, Emperor Mingxi: Just you say it one more time. But I will soon become wealthy. Those corrupt officials have all been arrested, the silver mine has been located, and as for the gold mine... it will be found!","My state treasury and private coffers will soon have silver flowing in like water!","The poor servant, Qian Gui: It is this servant's fault that His Majesty is being teased by the Divine Artifact again.","As for the silver... with my nephew's visit this time, even this less-than-one-thousand taels probably won't be safe!","\"Where did Eunuch Qian spend all his money? Among the eunuchs in the palace, probably no one is poorer than him!\"","[Exactly. Eunuch Fu by the Empress's side and Eunuch Wei by the Empress Dowager's side are both wealthier than Old Qian by a mile.","His money wasn't spent on himself. He's poor because all his silver was taken by those so-called relatives back in his hometown.]","\"I didn't realize Eunuch Qian was supporting a family of vampires?\"","What kind of ghost was a 'vampire'? The officials of Dayan didn't know, but they could guess the general meaning from the context.","They hadn't expected that Eunuch Qian, such a favored figure by the emperor, was also such a devoted and righteous person to his family.","[That family is precisely a bunch of vampires! It's just a pity for Old Qian. He spent good, hard-earned silver raising a pack of hungry wolves.","They ate his, drank his, and in the end, almost got him killed!]","\"You mean Eunuch Qian's family will harm him? Little Pearl, explain quickly. Eunuch Qian prepares my food and drinks very diligently every day. Let's see if we can help him.\"","Upon hearing the Divine Artifact's words, Qian Gui's heart first sank. He didn't doubt the truth of those words; the Divine Artifact had never been wrong.","What chilled him was the thought that the relatives he had treated with utmost sincerity and genuine care actually wanted to harm him!","This was somewhat unacceptable to Qian Gui, who valued family ties immensely.","Then, hearing the Little Immortal Lord's words warmed his heart again. The relatives he had sincerely treated for years wanted to harm him, while the Little Immortal Lord he had only recently met and was merely dutifully taking care of, wanted to save him because of that care!","[Master, the fall of the Dayan Dynasty wasn't just due to foreign invasion.]","Yue Fuguang had learned to answer ahead of time. She said, \"I know. It was also because of internal problems, like economic factors such as land annexation;","political factors, like incompetent rulers, factional strife;","social factors, like natural disasters in the dynasty's final years, and also military weakness.","But what does this have to do with Eunuch Qian's family harming him? Could they possibly affect the fate of the Dayan state?\"","Qian Gui listened, a vein throbbing on his forehead. If it weren't for the inappropriate setting, regardless of whether it was true or not, he would have already knelt to beg the emperor for punishment.","Emperor Mingxi and the assembled court officials, however, pricked up their ears to listen carefully. They knew the fall of Dayan was due to being jointly destroyed by the surrounding barbarian tribes.","They also knew the nation's decline and the opportunity seized by foreigners were inseparable from their own internal major problems. The land issue was one.","The loss of seventy percent of the elite army was another. The later constant peasant uprisings could be grouped with the land issue.","The emperor who came after their current majesty's demise was incompetent, and they... they were busy fighting for power and profit—that was another. What else was there?","The Dayan court now was like a gravely ill person waiting for death. They urgently needed to find all the root causes of the illness to treat them one by one.","[It actually does have a little connection. Before answering this question, let me ask you one, Master.","Guess, if the Dayan state falls, what will happen to the Xie family in the future?]","Hearing this, the second, third, fifth, and sixth princes immediately perked up their ears, listening nervously to what their future fate might be. A chill ran down their backs; they had a feeling it wouldn't be good.","As for Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan, well, he died early and never suffered that hardship!","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and said, \"For the imperial family, the loss of the state also means the loss of their home. Their status would plummet from the clouds into the mortal world, even into hell.","What they could do is nothing more than rally a group under the banner of restoration for a final desperate struggle, or be either killed or kept under house arrest by the new ruler.","Failing that, they could flee, change their identities, adopt new names, forge household registrations, and escape to new regions far from the political center.","Live a low-profile, survivalist life, never mentioning their origins, burying the family secret deep in their hearts, passing it down orally from generation to generation, or simply forgetting it completely.","But again, what does this have to do with Eunuch Qian and the Qian family?\"","[Master, the previous dynasty's imperial family did all these things you mentioned. Many descendants of the previous dynasty's Tong family still live within Dayan.","And among them, some have not forgotten their former imperial status and hope to one day restore their dynasty.","Guess what the Qian family's original surname was?]","\"Tong? The previous dynasty's imperial family? Eunuch Qian?\"","Eunuch Qian stared in disbelief. He, Qian Gui, his ancestors were once the previous dynasty's imperial family?","His family was so poor they fled as refugees to the south, and later, unable to afford to raise him, sent him into the palace. What kind of imperial family could fall so low? His parents?","If his family truly were the previous dynasty's imperial family, even if they were genuinely poor, they wouldn't send their own child into the palace to serve the successor who overthrew their dynasty, would they?"]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: The Names Are Correct, But the People Have Been Replaced","paragraphs":["The Xie Dynasty was founded by overthrowing the Tong Dynasty! To have his own child serve the descendants of his sworn enemies—was he insane, or were his parents insane!","It was also impossible that he was sent as a spy or informant. All these years, his family had never given him any 'missions'!","Eunuch Qian looked at His Majesty. This couldn't be. When they arrived, they were still a good master and servant pair, but in this moment, they had become a former dynasty's orphan from a destroyed kingdom and the current dynasty's...","Before Eunuch Qian could finish his thought, he heard the Divine Artifact's heavenly voice in his ear, [The Qian family are indeed the Tong imperial clan living under assumed names, and from the main lineage at that. Their ancestors were from the line of Prince Xi, the third son of Emperor Wei.","However, all this has nothing to do with Old Qian, because he shares no blood relation with the current Qian family members.]","Hearing this, Yue Fuguang's sensitive nerves twitched instantly. \"This isn't another switched-at-birth scenario, is it? Eunuch Qian doesn't have some powerful identity and wealthy parents, does he?\"","[There aren't that many stories of swapped young misses and young masters! Eunuch Qian's surname was originally Qian. His father's name was Qian Wuliang, his mother was Qian Wu's Wife. His living siblings: his eldest brother is also named Qian Huai, his eldest sister Qian Liu, his younger brother Qian Yu, and his younger sister Qian Tao.]","Qian Gui listened and nodded secretly in agreement. Yes, yes, those were indeed his family members' names. His father Qian Wuliang and his perpetually ill mother were both still alive.","How could it have nothing to do with him? The names of his loved ones were correct!","[The names are not wrong, but the people have been replaced. Qian Wuliang is not Qian Wuliang, Qian Wu's Wife is not Qian Wu's Wife, and Qian Huai, Qian Liu, even Qian Yu are no longer Qian Gui's biological parents, brother, and sister.]","How is this possible? How is this possible! Qian Gui relied on the last shred of his rationality to stop himself from crying out on the spot.","How could his parents and siblings no longer be his real ones... Wait, the Divine Artifact didn't mention his younger sister Qian Tao. That meant his sister... was still his biological sister?","Sure enough, as soon as he thought it, Little Xianju asked for him, \"Qian Tao is still Eunuch Qian's sister, right? And what do you mean by 'replaced'? It wasn't that they adopted Eunuch Qian and his sister, but that those Tong people replaced their parents?\"","[Correct. The Tong family members replaced the identities of all the Qian family members except for Qian Gui and Qian Tao, and lived on.","Thirty years ago, Tuzhou in the Dayan region suffered a once-in-fifty-years drought. Qian Wuliang fled south with his fellow villagers towards areas with water.","After just a few days on the road, the five-year-old Qian Gui fell seriously ill, burning with a high fever. It was at this time that the Qian family encountered the Tong family, who were also refugees. The Tong family were mountain dwellers from the mountains behind Qian Family Village—essentially unregistered \"black household\" people.","Qian Wuliang had seen the Tong family a few times in the mountains during his leisure. He remembered them because the head of the Tong family bore a sixty to seventy percent resemblance to him, and their children were around the same age as his own.","Meeting on the refugee road, although Qian Wuliang was wary of the Tong family, they were ultimately acquaintances, so his guard was inevitably lower.","One night, the Tong family finally found their opportunity. They killed all members of the Qian family except for the feverish Qian Gui and the three-year-old Qian Tao!]","All killed!","All killed!","The parents he has now killed his real parents and his siblings!","At this moment, Qian Gui felt only dizziness, his body chilled to the bone from the inside out. So cold! So painful!","He kept his head bowed low, not letting Yue Fuguang see his bloodshot eyes and his nearly shattered teeth clenched tight.","He dared not cry, dared not make a single sound. He pinched his thigh hard to maintain his clarity.","He must not go mad or faint. He needed to hear with his own ears why those he once considered his closest kin would do such a thing!","Yue Fuguang once again voiced the question in his heart, \"Why did they do it? Was it because of household registration? Isn't that thing easy to forge? It doesn't even have anti-counterfeiting features.\"","Minister of Revenue Dong Qianli: Lord Junior Mentor, do you hear what you're saying? How is household registration easy to forge?","And what are 'anti-counterfeiting features'?","The court has records for every household, with copies kept at both the prefectural and county offices. Unless you bribe people in both offices to add your forged record to the archives, any major event requiring verification will expose a forgery immediately!","[The Dayan household registration system is relatively strict and rigorous. Forging registration is extremely difficult for people nowadays. The technology alone is insufficient, making it easy to detect problems during inspection.","Therefore, the Tong family chose a more direct method: replacing identities.","Years earlier, when Qian Wuliang first saw the Tong family, they had already targeted him. Subsequent contacts were to closely observe his family's situation.","The natural disaster gave them the perfect opportunity. The Tong family killed Qian Wuliang's family and assumed their identities.","At the same time, Qian Wuliang's parents and brothers were also replaced by other members of the Tong clan.","To avoid suspicion, they deliberately became separated from the other villagers of Qian Family Village and eventually settled in Dashan Village, Jingzhou.","Old Qian and his sister Qian Tao were spared, one because he forgot much of what happened before his fever, and the other because she was too young to remember.","They kept the siblings alive not out of any kindness. Initially, they were kept as emergency rations. Later, before they needed to resort to that, they found a place to settle. Then they planned to raise the children and sell them for money later.]","A glimmer of understanding finally dawned on Qian Gui. Many things he couldn't understand before now had the thick dust wiped away, revealing the truth clearly!","Why, even when the family was poor, he and his sister always had the least to eat, the worst clothes, and did the most work.","His brothers and sister could all study, but only he and his sister could not.","His parents said his elder brother would need to support the family in the future, his sister needed to be pampered to marry well and help her brothers later, and his younger brother was small and needed more to eat.","But wasn't his sister also small? Wouldn't she also marry in the future?","After he brought this up a few times, his mother suddenly fell gravely ill, requiring expensive medicine for treatment, and he became the family's extra yet most useful member.","The whole family decided to sell him for money to treat his 'critically ill' mother!","He was sold to a trafficker, later ended up in the palace, and not two years later, his family found him.","His father said his mother's illness required expensive medicine to sustain her life. From then on, he could only keep a tiny portion of his monthly allowance, sending the rest home through messengers.","This went on for over twenty years. He only learned from the family's brief messages demanding money that his sister Qian Tao had grown into a young woman, capable of work. Later, she was taken a fancy to and bought by a traveling merchant!","Both he and his sister, Qian Gui and Qian Tao, were sold by the Tong family in different ways!","Back then, he still didn't understand. He sent so much money home, how could it come to selling his sister?","Now he knew. They were never family, but enemies. Enemies!"]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: Doesn't anyone care about me","paragraphs":["Qian Gui's heart was filled with such intense hatred that he felt like vomiting blood. He wished he could rush to the inn right now and chop his 'dear nephew' into pieces!","[The money Eunuch Qian had sent home over the years was all used by the Qian family for themselves or to support their clan members, which essentially meant aiding the main branch of the Tong family—the descendants of Prince Xi, the legitimate heir of the former dynasty, and the line of Prince Yue, son of the deposed Crown Prince.","These direct descendants of the former imperial family, who were once just a step away from the throne, had never given up their dream of restoration.","The wealth and loyal servants they brought with them during their escape were all dedicated to this cause. Huang Xiaoshan, the fellow villager Eunuch Qian had taken special care of in the palace, was actually a descendant of the Tong family's loyal servants.","He entered the palace partly to gather information about the Dayan imperial family, and partly to keep an eye on Eunuch Qian, fearing that one day he might recall how different his parents and siblings seemed compared to before he was five, and start suspecting their true identities.]","Eunuch Qian: When he was little, especially during the difficult times of fleeing, he really had wondered why his parents and older siblings didn't look quite the same as before.","But an animal-like instinct told him he couldn't ask; asking would lead to something bad.","As he grew older, these doubts gradually faded from memory. He never imagined these people would be so cautious. Even after all these years, using his entire life's savings hadn't bought him a shred of their trust.","Even Qian Tao, who was too young to remember anything at three, had been sold far away by them.","Emperor Mingxi also began to understand why his subordinates had failed to detect these people's existence for so many years—they were simply too cautious.","A part of the Dayan court had always been secretly searching for the 'remnants' of the former dynasty. It was only in recent years, as nearly a century had passed since the former dynasty's fall, that the search efforts had gradually relaxed.","Who would have thought that after all this time, their dream of restoration still hadn't been abandoned!","Was the allure of power too great, or had the Tong family turned restoration into an obsession, the very reason they lived?","\"Even if Eunuch Qian has a considerable amount of private savings, it might be enough to support that large family, but to raise an army for a rebellion—a venture that risks losing one's head—how many could they possibly afford with that? It wouldn't even be a drop in the bucket, would it?\"","[Indeed, but they also rely on that money to fund their searches across the land. Consider it seed capital?]","\"Search? Searching for what? People, objects, or money?\"","[Hehehe, Master, you guessed right again. They are looking for money, searching for the treasury that the Tong family ancestors left for their descendants to use for resurgence.]","Hearing this, Emperor Mingxi and the Dayan court officials' eyes instantly lit up. They were not unaware of the legends about a treasure left behind by the Tong family ancestors.","Over the years, both the court and private individuals had secretly searched for it, but no one had ever found even a trace of a clue.","Could the answer be revealed today?","The eyes of the Minister of Revenue, Dong Qianli, shone with an astonishing light—the gleam of gold.","The location of the former dynasty's treasure was still unknown, yet in his mind, he had already planned how to split the money between the imperial privy purse and the state treasury, and how to spend his share!","A colleague standing beside him, seeing his almost greedily glowing green eyes, couldn't help but shiver and hugged himself tightly!","Was Minister Dong having another one of his episodes?","Why were the symptoms different this time? The way he was looking at him was as if he wanted to devour him, but... but he wasn't interested in men!","If Minister Dong tried to force himself on him, should he comply or resist? Waiting in the court, quite urgently!","\"Why do mortals, once they have a bit of money, always like to hide it away? Wealthy families do it, and the imperial family does it too! If silver and gold aren't spent, don't circulate, then won't the market always suffer from a shortage of currency?","Even I, who doesn't understand economics, know that hoarding large amounts of gold and silver for decades or even a century—this kind of 'currency hoarding' or 'savings accumulation'—in a society where the monetary system is based on precious metals, would definitely affect the court's economy.","In severe cases, it could even lead to a 'currency shortage'! Prices and people's livelihoods would be affected, destabilizing society.","What's the point of hiding money here? It can't hatch offspring, and it's not like putting it in a bank where it grows with interest!\"","Emperor Mingxi and Dong Qianli both had a flash of understanding in their eyes. So, hoarding gold and silver could have such a significant impact? It could cause a currency shortage? With less and less gold and silver in circulation, some commoners had even resorted to barter. Could that also be due to this influence?","And what did that 'bank' mean? Why would money grow if left there?","They wished Yue Fuguang would say more if she knew how.","Yue Fuguang: Don't understand, can't do, won't explain!","[Master, isn't your focus a bit off? Aren't you curious about whether the Tong family ancestors left behind a sufficient treasure for their resurgence?","Did they find the treasure?]","Yue Fuguang snorted proudly, thinking of her own fifty million sitting in the bank collecting interest.","[You said 'did they find the treasure,' doesn't that already confirm the treasure's existence?]","[Hehehe, Master, don't you want to know where the treasure is?]","“Not really. Even if I had it, it would be useless to me. Mortal gold and silver are nothing more than slightly prettier grains of sand or gravel to beings like us. They can't even buy a single Body Strengthening Pill. What use do I have for them?”","The Dayan emperor and his ministers were practically drooling, sweating with anxiety. If they could speak, they would have shouted, \"Immortal Lord might not want to know, but we do! The Immortal Lord is noble, viewing wealth as dirt, but we are mortals, common people, we love that stuff!\"","[Master, say you want to know! Little Pearl not only knows where the former dynasty's treasure is hidden but also knows about this dynasty's! Am I amazing or not?]","Emperor Mingxi: Divine Artifact, what do you mean? Explain clearly. What do you mean by 'this dynasty's treasure'? Has this dynasty hidden a treasure too?","He, Xie Fei, is the emperor of Dayan, the head of the Xie family. How could he not know about a treasure belonging to this dynasty?","Could the Divine Artifact be referring to another family, not a dynastic treasure, but a private 'collection'?","The thoughts of the Dayan court officials were similar to their emperor's. According to records, their founding ancestor was not wealthy when he raised his army. With years of continuous war, they were always short of funds.","After the new dynasty was established, everything needed rebuilding, and money was needed everywhere. It's unlikely Emperor Gaozu had the spare capacity to create another treasure trove.","They didn't suspect later emperors because the court officials could roughly estimate how much was in their private treasuries. Even accounting for discrepancies, a difference of a million or so taels would be considerable, but saving that much hardly qualifies as a 'treasure trove.'","\"This dynasty has one too? Then I want to know even less. This dynasty's treasure has an owner, right? This Immortal Lord isn't short of money. Why would I covet other people's things? That's beneath me!\"","[Master, this dynasty's treasure belongs to the emperor's family! Not to mention the silver their founding ancestor hid for his descendants, even the later emperors and Emperor Mingxi's father hid several million taels.]","\"Another emperor leading the way in hoarding money, no wonder there's less and less gold and silver. You say the Xie family has hidden so much money, so why is Emperor Mingxi still so poor? Could it be that he doesn't want to spend the money on the people and is just pretending to be poor on purpose?\"","Emperor Mingxi: Who am I? Where am I? Why has another big black pot fallen on my head with a thud? Can't carry it, just can't carry it!","Emperor Mingxi cried inwardly. Was no one going to speak up for him?"]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: So all the silver money is still there now Including the Tong family's","paragraphs":["No sooner had he heard about the silver coins hidden by his Xie family ancestors and the previous emperors than Yue Fuguang pinned a huge black pot right on his head!","He was the emperor of a nation, did he have no face to save? Was it glorious to be known as poor? And pretending to be poor? He was genuinely broke!","The Crown Prince: Father, for the sake of the Xie family's empire, for future emperors to never lack money, please bear with it! Finding our Xie family's treasure is what's important!","Emperor Mingxi: You unfilial son!","The system scratched its round, hairless head, feeling compelled to speak up for Emperor Mingxi, who seemed on the verge of crying from grievance.","It said, [Master, is it possible that Emperor Mingxi himself didn't know about the treasure hidden by their ancestors or the private savings stashed away by the previous emperors?]","Emperor Mingxi nodded silently in agreement. Yes, yes, I didn't know. Please, kind soul, tell me where the money is! Eyes sparkling with gold coins JPG","If Emperor Mingxi had been exposed to modern 'cultural influences', he would definitely have added: I'll Venmo you 50!","\"Didn't know? He's the emperor, if he didn't know, then who did?\"","[The one who knew was Prince Rong, the son born to his father's favorite woman, Consort Hui.]","Emperor Mingxi: Those two again! Why are their shadows everywhere? They really are like lingering ghosts!","But thinking of the treasure, he couldn't help feeling a twinge of regret. Ah! He had Prince Rong and Consort Hui killed too early!","\"Was his father that biased? Not telling the future heir about so much money, but telling a prince instead? Was he worried the Xie family's reign was too stable?","That old fool probably wanted one brother to have the money and the other the status, setting them up with their own advantages to fight chaotically over his throne!","The old man was the chief culprit of sowing discord and endangering the state! Could he have died from his own stupidity?\"","The court ministers, hearing Yue Fuguang call the late emperor an old fool and an old man, wore expressions of embarrassment, especially those who had once served the late emperor, burying their heads even lower.","There was no helping it; the one insulting their former master was the little immortal lord. They couldn't afford to offend him!","Even his own son wasn't saying anything, so as outsiders... they'd better pretend they didn't hear it!","Besides, they secretly thought the little immortal lord's scolding wasn't wrong. Wasn't he indeed the chief culprit of endangering the state and sowing discord?","As the son, Emperor Mingxi, hearing Yue Fuguang curse his father like that, wasn't angry at all. Instead, he cheered for her inwardly. If you know how to curse, curse more! Use the same vigor you used to curse me before and curse him hard! He loved listening to it!","At this moment, Yue Fuguang was practically his mouthpiece! As a son, bound by respect for elders, he felt aggrieved but couldn't say much, sometimes even having to hold his nose and offer praise!","It was utterly frustrating!","Now, listening to Yue Fuguang's curses, which sounded like heavenly music, the wounds from being cursed so many times himself were instantly soothed!","Unfortunately, the little immortal lord's curse vocabulary seemed a bit lacking, otherwise Emperor Mingxi felt he could be even happier.","Feeling immensely pleased, Emperor Mingxi forcefully suppressed his rising lips. Though he tried hard to disguise it, his cheerful mood was noticed by the minister currently presenting a report.","This man thought his suggestion had struck a chord with His Majesty and gained his approval. Feeling encouraged, he spoke with even more enthusiasm!","The system seriously flipped through historical records. [According to records, the late emperor died of illness. Looking at this medical report, Little Pearl, it doesn't seem like he died from any... clean disease!","Master, this old emperor's death was not clean!]","The few who were in the know wore another wave of awkward expressions.","\"Clean or not, he's dead anyway. Let's set aside the old man's death for now. First, tell me why he hid the money and didn't tell Emperor Mingxi?\"","Emperor Mingxi curled his lip. What else could it be? Afraid his most beloved son would suffer in the future, of course. Or even thinking that if Prince Rong didn't ascend the throne as he envisioned, with this money, whether for staging a comeback or... other purposes, he would have the means.","Emperor Mingxi understood his father all too well. He must have thought exactly that!","[That old man's original plan was to depose the then Crown Prince, now Emperor Mingxi, and install Prince Rong as Crown Prince. So he prematurely revealed the matter of the Xie family's founding ancestor's treasure to Prince Rong.","However, as soon as the old emperor hinted at this idea, he met with fierce opposition from the court ministers. The system of primogeniture was the most stable method for imperial succession and smooth political transition.","Later, the old emperor, still unwilling to give up, tested the court officials several times, failing without exception.","In the last two years before his death, he gradually emptied almost his entire private treasury, all to save more private funds for his beloved son.","That's why when Emperor Mingxi succeeded to the throne, the private treasury he inherited from his father contained only a little over a hundred thousand taels of silver. It wasn't that the old emperor was poor; he had moved his money!]","\"Giving Prince Rong so much money, what was he trying to do? Seed funding for a rebellion? While he was alive, Prince Rong couldn't become emperor. After he died, could Prince Rong possibly raise an army, rebel, and successfully seize the throne?","Wasn't he afraid the Great Yan Dynasty, the Xie family's empire, would be torn apart by the fighting between his two sons?\"","The courtiers of Great Yan were also speechless upon hearing about the late emperor's actions. They didn't know what he was thinking. Emperors usually feared instability and internal strife.","But with the late emperor, it seemed he almost wished for chaos!","Wouldn't he be afraid of being chased and beaten by the Xie family ancestors in the afterlife?","[This old emperor probably didn't even realize his own intentions until the last two years before his death. He left his own and the previous emperors' private savings to his beloved Prince Rong.","However, the treasure of their founding ancestor, Emperor Gaozu, he intended to leave for the future successor. Even though this successor wasn't the heir he approved of, the Gaozu treasure should rightfully be passed to the next emperor.","He only came to this realization at the very end.","Unfortunately, as soon as he figured it out, he kicked the bucket!]","So the late emperor had once considered telling His Majesty about the Gaozu treasure?","Kicked the bucket? What does 'kicked the bucket' mean? Judging from the context, it should mean passed away?","\"He already told Prince Rong about the Gaozu treasure, wasn't he afraid Prince Rong would go and take it?\"","Right, Prince Rong knew about it. Wouldn't he have taken it?","Oh, Prince Rong has been dead for over ten years. Never mind then.","Some with heavier thoughts had flickering eyes. Could Prince Rong have told others, like his own son?","[The old emperor only told Prince Rong that such a Gaozu treasure existed, but didn't reveal its specific location. As for the money hidden by the old emperor and the previous emperors, Prince Rong died before he could retrieve this capital for a comeback, even after learning the locations.]","\"So all the money is still there? Including the Tong family's?\"","[Yes. The Tong family treasure is in two parts. The Gaozu treasure is actually part of the Tong family treasure, to which he later added a bit himself.","The other part of the Tong family treasure, Emperor Gaozu also sent people to search for but never found.","For this purpose, he specifically established a department called the 'Secret Vault Bureau' to find the other half of the treasure.]","Only now did Emperor Mingxi learn that the Secret Vault Bureau was established for this reason."]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: Master, Don't You Remember That Xia Kingdom Where You Underwent Tribulations in Your Previous Life.","paragraphs":["However, the department in his hands now existed in name only.","The work they did now had nothing to do with investigating treasure troves. This... this couldn't be blamed on him! He was unaware, and the few officials of the Secret Treasury who were in the know were all King Rong's men and had long since lost their heads!","Emperor Mingxi sighed once more. The blade was too swift, the execution too early!","[Master, are you really not curious? Right now, within Great Yan, not only are the Tong family searching for their ancestral treasure, but several external forces are also looking for it.","On Xie family's side, although King Rong is dead, his supporters and surviving descendants are still alive and are also searching for the late Emperor's stored silver. As for Emperor Gaozu's treasure, they only inferred its possible existence from King Rong's few words before his death and aren't certain it exists, but they know for sure the stored silver does.","Moreover, based on the timeline, they will find the late Emperor's stored silver by the end of next year.]","\"Next year's end is still far off, no rush!\"","Great Yan's Emperor and Officials: Immortal Lord, you're not in a hurry, but we are! Scratching ears and cheeks in anxiety","\"Little Pearl, even if I knew the location, could I just go and dig it up? I'm not short of money. As for the Yu family, they aren't rebelling. Having such treasures would be a curse, not a blessing. So it's better not to invite disaster upon the family!\"","Yu Chongshan nodded frantically in his heart. Yes, yes, Fuguang is right, their family wasn't short of money either.","None of the family, old or young, had ever considered rebellion. Getting their hands on that scorching-hot money would be useless.","[If this money isn't dug up and spent, wouldn't it just become hoarded savings? Then it truly becomes a dead asset!","How about this, Master, after Great Yan falls, we help the Yu family conquer the realm for fun?]","Emperor Mingxi: Divine Artifact, listen to yourself! What do you mean 'after Great Yan falls, you conquer the realm for fun'?","Oh, the Divine Artifact is a divine being, an artifact, not human, alas! Then there's nothing to be done!","But the little Immortal Lord is human now, we can try to influence her!","Yu Chongshan, hearing the Divine Artifact's words, was utterly terrified. Conquering the realm and becoming emperor? Their family had never entertained such a thought.","At most, because of Yue Fuguang, they might think about strengthening the family clan, aspiring to become a millennium-old noble house!","System: Never thought about it before? How about thinking about it now? No rush anyway, Great Yan still has several years before it falls!","Yu Chongshan and Yu Zhongchun desperately shook their heads at Emperor Mingxi, who sat steadfastly on the dragon throne, his expression unreadable. Their family truly only wished to be a millennium-old house, not the ruler of a mere centuries-long dynasty!","\"Forget it. The Yu family has no such ambition, and I have even less. A dynasty lasting a few centuries is just the length of one of our meditation retreats.","What's so great about that throne?","The emperor rises earlier than the rooster, works harder than the ox, sleeps later than the dog. Even if he wants to sleep with a beauty, he has to consider the ministers' opinions at court, ensuring 'the rain and dew are spread evenly'! Whoever wants this job can have it, but we certainly won't!\"","Emperor Mingxi mentally repeated the phrases 'rises earlier than the rooster, works harder than the ox, sleeps later than the dog, wants to sleep with someone but has to mind others' opinions' and felt inexplicably that... it was a very apt summary. Please don't summarize it again next time! Shedding tears of grievance","The future emperor, current Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan: After hearing the little Immortal Lord's words, how come the throne suddenly seems less appealing?","If I said I didn't want to succeed now, would my royal father break my legs?","Father and son's gazes met in the air. Emperor Mingxi discerned the Crown Prince's thoughts and secretly fumed at his son's lack of resolve. How could he be swayed so easily by the little Immortal Lord's words!","Sigh! Why did he himself also feel that being emperor was rather bland and uninteresting?","[That seems true too. The king of ants is still an ant. How about leaking the Tong family's treasure location to Emperor Mingxi? With money, he might be able to stabilize Great Yan's declining fortunes.","It would also weaken the external tribes and internal rebel forces. Killing two birds with one stone!","As long as Great Yan doesn't fall, perhaps the common people can suffer less.]","Emperor Mingxi: Yes, yes, yes! Give it to me, I'll definitely spend the money where it's most needed!","Dong Qianli's eyes also lit up repeatedly.","\"Little Pearl, why are you concerned about these things now? Didn't you say Great Yan's fall wouldn't affect us much? Why the sudden concern for the common people? Little Pearl, you seem to have developed a sense of empathy!\"","[It's because I've been watching the films and reading the documents from the world of your last mortal trial recently.","Don't you remember, Master? In your last trial, that country, Xia, was prosperous and thriving, its people living and working in peace and contentment.","The people had faith, the nation had strength, the ethnic groups had hope. It was an extremely, extremely powerful country.","They too experienced a century of humiliation before their revival. That generation suffered too much. Little Pearl just thought it would be best if Great Yan didn't have to go through something like that.","When the nest is overturned, no egg remains unbroken. Under such overwhelming forces, both the poor and the rich are as insignificant as grass. How many of these esteemed lords in this court would meet a good end?]","Great Yan's Emperor and Officials: Is the Divine Artifact going to speak of this again? Regarding their future 'demises', they felt both apprehensive and curious.","Afraid to hear, yet afraid not to hear!","Gu Yutong and Zhao Zhifeng, who already knew they would die unpleasantly, suddenly became the most conspicuous figures in the crowd.","The two straightened their backs. Knowing the outcome, they weren't nervous!","Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan, who knew he would be poisoned: Not being mentioned!","\"Regarding my previous life, much of the memory was sealed by my master. I don't remember clearly either, only vaguely recall they had incredibly powerful weapons. A single projectile could flatten the entire Shangjing Capital.","They had countless types of such weapons—ones that flew in the sky, ran on the ground, swam in the sea—each possessing earth-shattering, destructive power.","If they came to conquer Great Yan, unifying the Six States wouldn't take a month!","Their population was also several times larger than all Six States combined. With so many people, every single one could eat their fill and eat well. Mmm... their food was truly delicious! And so many varieties!","They also had airplanes, trains, and automobiles that could travel a thousand miles a day, and ships several times larger than this hall...\"","As Yue Fuguang narrated, Great Yan's Emperor and officials fell silent. They couldn't even dream of such a powerful country built by mortals existing in the world.","The people living there must be very happy—no war, no famine, not constantly fearing for their lives. For the ordinary people of Great Yan, that would be the best life they wouldn't dare dream of!","That was a life only immortals could live!","Meanwhile, Emperor Mingxi and generals like Huo Ying coveted the weapons of that Xia country. They didn't understand what a 'projectile' was, but something that could destroy Great Yan's largest and most prosperous capital with a single one... just imagining it told them how terrifyingly powerful it must be.","If they had such weapons, unifying the Six States in a month might be beyond them, but two months would definitely suffice. The time would just be spent on travel!","At the same time, they felt immensely relieved that Xia country wasn't their neighbor.","With such a populous, wealthy, and powerful behemoth next door, they'd have to sleep with one eye open.","[Master, you actually remember quite a bit. Did the Divine Lord intentionally leave these memories unsealed when he sealed the rest?]"]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: His Descendants Personally Brought Their Dynasty to an End","paragraphs":["When speaking of food, Master also has a very human touch, unlike that ethereal Lord Fuguang on Lingxu Mountain who seems untouched by worldly cares.","Perhaps for Master to ascend to divinity, he needs to comprehend this taste of mortal life. After immersing himself in the red dust of the world, seeing through the karma contained within all living beings—more complex than the movement of stars—and the profound bonds deeper than heaven and earth, the return to simplicity after great enlightenment might be what the Divine Lord requires Master to realize.","\"Little Pearl, you are right. The mortal world is the path! We are both observers and participants. Then, let's give the court of Dayan and its common people a chance.\"","[Master, you agree to reveal the treasure matter to the Emperor? Which one should we tell them about?]","\"Any one will do. Let's give them one first and see how they perform. If this money is not used for the people's livelihood or military preparedness,","but ends up lining certain individuals' pockets, then Dayan deserves to perish. Whether others save them or not, I for one will no longer care about their fate.\"","[I'll prepare some lots for you, Master. Just pick one randomly...]","The Dayan Emperor and his ministers: Is it really this casual? But having something is better than nothing.","Dong Qianli had already thought of various methods to strictly guard against and prevent anyone from embezzling even a single tael of silver.","Is this just money? No, this is a test set by the little immortal lord for our Emperor and his ministers. Pass it, and Dayan still has hope; fail it, and just wait to pack your belongings and flee or clean yourself up and await death!","Clearly, the others also understood this reasoning. They glanced at each other, each thinking the other might be the one to drag them down!","[Alright, Master. One, two, three, which do you choose?]","\"The doctrine of the mean. I choose two.\"","[Master, number two is the other half of the Tong family treasure. Eunuch Qian's nephew came to the capital this time precisely under orders to seek external allies here to help search for this treasure.]","Hearing that the first treasure they might obtain was the Tong family treasure, Emperor Mingxi and his ministers were all secretly thrilled.","They were so excited they could hardly contain themselves, wanting to laugh heartily and rush out—to do what? Dig for treasure!","Yet they had to force themselves to finish the court session properly, lest those two notice anything amiss.","As for the remnants of the previous dynasty, now that they knew these people were still active, they were on guard. Once they intercepted their last reliance, they would no longer be a threat.","Moreover, now that they knew about that nest of 'the Qian family', were they afraid they couldn't capture others by seizing them?","\"They sought external allies? Who did they find?\"","[According to records, they sought the Nan Yue people. During the Emperor's longevity festival this year, the Nan Yue envoys in the capital will obtain a jade Guanyin statue, inside which is hidden the treasure map.","Half a year later, they finally find the Tong family treasure based on the location drawn on the map.","Later, news of this leaks. Spurred by this, Prince Rong's son leads his men and, after more than half a year, finally finds the key to the old Emperor's treasure vault hidden by Prince Rong.","After obtaining the key, they find the vault's location from it and successfully use the key to open the savings accumulated by Dayan's previous emperors over several generations, left by the old Emperor for his son, totaling nearly ten million taels of silver.","They use this money to raise an army and bribe many court and local officials, effectively sounding the death knell for Dayan once again!","The old Emperor never imagined that the silver he sent out would become the hammer that shattered the broken drum that was Dayan. His own descendants personally sending their dynasty to its demise is quite ironic!]","Emperor Mingxi's face twitched, filled with both anger and embarrassment. After all, these people were his own father and nephews, all members of the Xie family. Burying one's own dynasty—quite something!","\"A Guanyin statue? It couldn't be the 'Wonderful Dharma Lotus Flower Guanyin' statue from the auction, could it? I thought those people were strange at the time.","But since you know the location, whether we have the statue or not shouldn't affect retrieving the treasure.","Little Pearl, all I can say is I'll try to pass the message to Emperor Mingxi. I'm just a child, my words carry little weight; he might not believe me.","If he doesn't believe and misses the treasure, then it has nothing to do with us!","It just means this windfall wasn't in his fate, and he can't blame others.]","The Dayan Emperor and ministers: Your words carry little weight? Would you care to look around—who in all of Dayan has words as effective as yours?","To speak out of turn, even His Majesty's words aren't as potent as yours now!","Emperor Mingxi: This wealth is definitely in my fate. I will certainly listen to whatever you say.","The most shocked had to be the Crown Prince. He was present for the entire bidding of that Guanyin statue at the time, never imagining it concealed such a secret as a treasure map!","If he had known earlier... never mind. Even if he had known, with the free location provided by the divine artifact, he wouldn't have been willing to spend tens of thousands of taels to buy it.","The Crown Prince, the richer he gets, the more reluctant he is to throw money around like he used to.","Recently, while busy with the Ministry of Revenue preparing disaster relief, he always unconsciously equates silver with rice and flour.","[Mhm, give them one chance. If they can't grasp it, then forget it. Little Pearl just had a sudden whim to meddle in this matter.]","\"Find an opportunity to remind old Qian. He shouldn't keep sending money to his family's murderers anymore. In the end, he even gets stabbed by his own nephew and nearly sent to his grave!\"","Pfft! Eunuch Qian still couldn't hold back and fainted. He had acknowledged thieves as father and mother, sending them money, grain, and everything he possessed.","He had failed his parents, brothers, and the sister who always carried him on her back.","No wonder his sister grew distant after he turned five—that person was no longer his real sister!","A clear tear slid from the unconscious Eunuch Qian's eye. And his only remaining relative in this world, his missing younger sister A'Tao—he must find her!","Yue Fuguang sighed inwardly, hoping Eunuch Qian could quickly pull himself together to search for his sister. This system couldn't help with that; he had to rely on himself.","Later, the official story for Eunuch Qian fainting in court was that his nephew had come to the capital to report a bereavement—Eunuch Qian's parents had both passed away due to illness, and he was overcome with grief, leading to his collapse.","Whether others believed it or not, Yue Fuguang, in front of Emperor Mingxi, blinked her big eyes and expressed pity for Qian Gui for a while. She even took out a small handful of gold melon seeds from her own purse, calling it condolence money for Eunuch Qian.","This prompted Emperor Mingxi to also take out a piece of silver on the spot, saying he'd also contribute.","The ministers who hadn't left yet also generously opened their purses. The still-unconscious Eunuch Qian, without his knowledge, had received nearly a thousand taels, almost matching all his previous savings.","One particularly remembers Yue Fuguang, before leaving, solemnly proposing to Emperor Mingxi, \"Your Majesty, Eunuch Qian is currently overwhelmed with grief. Traveling alone might not be entirely safe. Perhaps Your Majesty could send more people to accompany Qian Gui back for the funeral. Near his home... well, 'near' meaning within a hundred li... there's a mountain called Tongming Mountain...\"","She also mentioned that while at the Taoist temple, she heard devotees say Tongming Mountain lies at the border of Jiaozhou and Jingzhou prefectures. Neither prefecture manages it well, leading to rampant banditry in that mountain range. Perhaps the Emperor could send people to conveniently suppress them while they're at it.","Finally, she added, \"Your Majesty, Fuguang heard those devotees say those bandits are guarding a treasure in the mountains. Does treasure really exist in this world?\"","Emperor Mingxi's expression at that moment... was quite spectacular! The corner of his mouth even twitched. Hahahaha!","It was just that casual. Believe it or not!"]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: So now I have another benefactor for no reason","paragraphs":["[Host, we've been chattering away all morning. If Emperor Mingxi takes it to heart, we'll have completed one, two, three, four tasks all at once!]","[Preventing the former dynasty's treasure from falling into the hands of foreign tribes counts as one. Preventing the Tong family from establishing the Tong family army counts as one. Using the former dynasty's treasure for the people's livelihood counts as one.","Preventing the orphan of Prince Rong from establishing a rebel army counts as one. And because of this, Eunuch Qian's fate is rewritten. Many officials who were corrupted by Prince Rong using the old emperor's money might now choose to stand by the emperor's side.","These all count as overflow points. Once completed, these tasks will yield nearly thirty thousand points. We're rich, we're rich!]","Yue Fuguang lay leisurely on the chaise lounge, her feet propped up. \"System, calm down, calm down. Think about it, after all that rambling we did this morning, it's only right we see some results.","But regarding the treasure the old emperor left for Prince Rong, can you still not confirm which of the sisters has the key to the underground palace on them?\"","[The original historical record only says that Prince Rong's son, Xie Zhili, obtained the key from a woman of the Feng family, but this Feng woman isn't named. I'll check again.]","\"And what about the Xie family treasure? Is it really connected to Peach Blossom Lane? And is Bai Yu's disappearance also related to this?\"","[Because of our appearance, many things are quietly changing. Bai Yu's disappearance never happened in the original historical timeline.","According to records, he stayed by Xie Zhiyao's side the whole time. Even after Xie Zhiyao married Zhong Mingyu, their connection never broke.","The last mention of him was when Prince Qi's rebellion was exposed. Everyone connected to Prince Qi's faction, including Xie Zhiyao, was thrown into prison, but only Bai Yu and Xie Zhiyao's youngest daughter escaped.","Some suspected that daughter was Bai Yu's.]","Yue Fuguang waved her hand helplessly. \"It's fine. We have the task outline. Let's review the history again and make some reasonable inferences ourselves. As long as we achieve the goal, the process can be a bit vague. Just avoid too many logical loopholes.\"","There was no help for it. The gossip system wasn't a complete entity, so the quality of the gossip couldn't be guaranteed. Maybe there's hope once the system slowly upgrades?","Like the story about Eunuch Qian's parents being swapped—that part is true. But the details aren't in the history books or related documents; they're from embellished stories in plays written centuries later.","The two of them chose the most reliable and logical version to tell. That shouldn't count as... lying, right? After all, the event is true. The process... well, it's not important!","...","[Host, stop sleeping, get up and... I mean, get up and see, I've leveled up! System is now Level 3!]","Yue Fuguang was fast asleep in the carriage on the way to court, just dreaming about splurging with her fifty million from her previous life, when the system woke her up.","Morning grumpiness... forget it, it's a joyous day!","She turned over, snuggling under the blanket without even opening an eye. \"Reaching Level 3 was expected, wasn't it? But why two days early? Remember to keep twenty thousand points untouched.\"","After all this hard work, she had only accumulated a little over thirty thousand points. It was enough for the system to help her escape and restart in a new world if the task failed, beginning a new journey.","Yue Fuguang always had a backup plan. She worked diligently on her tasks, but escaping if the task failed was also on her agenda.","Nothing in the world is difficult for one who is willing to give up! Failure isn't shameful, neither is running away.","[The task of rescuing Zheng Feng and his family is completed. The points just credited were enough to level up.]","\"So that means Zheng Feng and his sons have already arrived in the capital?\"","[They should have arrived. Next comes the trial of the imperial examination fraud case.]","\"System, work is here. I still have to act later. Don't disturb me, let me sleep a bit more.\"","[Host, we're almost at the palace gates. Get up and let's chat. Aren't you curious about the new functions at Level 3?]","\"The number of people covered by the inner voice increased?\" For a handicapped system, Yue Fuguang kept her expectations low. As long as it could provide gossip, it was fine.","[No, no! My merit system has new functions added with this upgrade! Hahaha!]","Yue Fuguang sat up straight from under the covers. \"Really? At Level 2, the merit system was completely still; only the gossip system added a few people. What new functions at Level 3? Show me quickly!\"","The system said excitedly, [Host, the merit system has added a merit and fortune scan button. You can check the merit and fortune values of up to five people per day.]","\"That should be a divine tool for distinguishing loyalty from treachery! No more worrying about wronging the good or letting the bad go free. What else?\"","[The gossip system has added something called Heavenly Will. From now on, those who can hear our inner voices will no longer be able to discuss the content with those who cannot.","More importantly, even if they try to speak about the inner voice matters in front of us, they will be suppressed by Heavenly Will and be unable to say it!","Master no longer needs to worry about someone accidentally mentioning the inner voice to you someday!]","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"It seems the several contingency plans I prepared for such emergencies won't be needed anymore.\"","[This upgrade didn't increase the number of people covered by the inner voice.]","\"It's fine. Maybe it will increase at Level Four.\" With the previous good news, Yue Fuguang wasn't too concerned about the lack of increase. Currently, she didn't travel far and had little contact with people; one hundred and fifty was enough.","As soon as she entered the main hall, Yue Fuguang noticed an old man at today's morning court.","He looked about the same age as her grandfather, Yu Chongshan, but judging by his complexion, he was rosy-cheeked, with an air of an immortal and a bit of a transcendent master about him.","Yue Fuguang fluttered her curious big eyes, examining the man like a genuine eight-year-old girl.","He even had a seat in the main hall, indicating his status was probably not low.","\"Little Pearl, who is this old man? Why haven't I seen him before?\"","[Master, you've met him once before. Oh, right, you were unconscious then, so you don't remember.]","\"When was that?\"","[It was not long after you escaped from the Zhou family's wolf den. Your constitution was too weak, you fell ill with a high fever. I hadn't found you yet then.","It was this Taoist priest who treated your illness. By the time I found you, your condition had stabilized. I secretly fed you some spiritual spring water, and then you woke up.]","\"So I have another benefactor for no reason? Does he have any ailments? Treat him quietly to settle this karmic debt.\"","[He's in very good health, no major issues. However, his most beloved young disciple is poisoned with something called 'Hundred-Day Drunk'. After three flare-ups, one 'falls into a long drunken slumber'—unfortunate. After three more, the person will surely die.]","\"What stage is it at now? Is there still hope for a cure?\"","[Almost at the fourth flare-up. Don't worry, Host. For mortal world poisons, even if he only had one day left, I could cure him with medicine.]","\"Alright, be quick about it. I don't want to owe mortals any karmic debts.\"","Xuanmingzi slightly lowered his gaze, his expression as steady as a mountain, but his heart was roiling with towering waves."]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: Host, Aren't You Just a Lazy Bum","paragraphs":["Last night, His Majesty had already explained part of the situation to him.","He found it instinctively absurd at the time. Having studied Taoist scriptures for many years and even invited the Patriarch multiple times, he was not one to readily believe in deities undergoing mortal trials.","Their Taoist Patriarch had stated that the heavenly principles of this realm were incomplete, so how could a great power be summoned to save the world?","Yet, he never imagined that upon their very first meeting, he would receive such a tremendous surprise—the poison afflicting his young disciple Baiyi was finally curable!","Indeed, cause and effect are unfathomable. On a whim, he once went traveling to visit friends and casually treated a young child. Today, that act brought him such a immense reward, truly an unexpected and great joy!","Xuanmingzi habitually reached for the wine gourd hanging at his waist. Upon touching its cool surface, he suddenly remembered he was in the imperial court and could not drink.","Unable to drink, Xuanmingzi gazed longingly at Yue Fuguang, who was eating and drinking heartily. Under his stare, her pace of nibbling pastries slowed, and her large bites unconsciously turned into small ones.","\"Little Pearl, is this old man hungry? He's eyeing my pastry with envy.\"","Xuanmingzi: Every cell in his body screamed a triple denial: I'm not, I didn't, don't talk nonsense!","[Perhaps it's his first time at court and he lacks experience, not having eaten breakfast beforehand. Master, will you share with him?]","\"No, I don't owe him anything now. That poisoned disciple of his—did you cure the poison?\"","[Half a small antidote pill completely neutralized the poison and incidentally repaired the damage the toxins had inflicted on his body. Once the morning court session ends and Xuanmingzi returns, he'll find his disciple alive and kicking.]","\"Well done!\"","Xuanmingzi: Although he truly didn't want her pastry, he was very curious about her antidote pill.","Half a pill could cure a poison that had left him helpless—was this the power of an immortal?","Xuanmingzi felt inexplicably stirred. Their master-disciple pair had good fortune, encountering this little immortal lord who clearly distinguished gratitude from grievance.","Their Taoist path also emphasized karma and a clear, unimpeded Dao-heart. He had casually saved someone without fully curing them, yet not only did she cure his disciple's poison, she even repaired the bodily damage that would have affected his lifespan. This debt of gratitude was rather significant!","Xuanmingzi stroked his beard, pondering how to repay this great favor, unaware that the other two were also discussing him.","\"System, is this really the future Nether Heaven King, Jiao Xuanming? Isn't he currently a revered Taoist master, a guest of honor to the emperor?","How could he also be the bell-ringer for Dayan's death knell, the future leader of a peasant uprising?\"","[On the original historical timeline, his young disciple later succumbed to the poison. He returned to Qingtian Temple and entered seclusion. Later, as natural disasters and man-made calamities continued, the world descended into increasing chaos. First, the Crown Prince was poisoned and died, then Emperor Mingxi died suddenly.","The new emperor was both incompetent and unprincipled. As the Dayan ship seemed destined to sink, Xuanmingzi witnessed the suffering of the common people. Perhaps his years of seclusion and meditation had led to an enlightenment.","Thus, he founded the Way of Qingtian's Ultimate Justice. From then on, Xuanmingzi was dead, and the Nether Heaven King Jiao Xuanming was born.","The Way of Qingtian's Ultimate Justice rapidly expanded, amassing hundreds of thousands of followers in less than two years. After Xuanmingzi's death, the Way declined.","With the fall of the Dayan state, an era of chaos began. Some, claiming the Nether Heaven King had risen from the ashes to lead them in restoring Dayan, stirred up trouble for many more years.","They also strayed from the original doctrine of leading the poor to a full meal onto the crooked path of deceiving the poor so they themselves could eat their fill.","Over the following decades, it completely devolved into a cult organization, causing the death and maiming of many.","Host, shall we reveal the full truth to him?]","\"No need. The cult organization emerged over a hundred years after Jiao Xuanming's death; what does it have to do with him?","With us here, Xuanmingzi will only ever be Xuanmingzi. Since he's already converted to Taoism, let him properly be a Taoist priest. There's no need to revert to his secular name and meddle in worldly affairs again.","Besides, with our corn, sweet potatoes, and potatoes, there won't be scenes of people starving en masse, necessitating a reclusive Taoist priest to fight for a mouthful of food for the commoners.","If such scenes do occur, it's because the emperor hasn't killed enough people, and the malignant tumors among the powerful families, high officials, and wealthy households haven't been cleansed thoroughly.\"","[Master, a thorough cleansing is probably very difficult. Under this sky, there are hardly any clean people.]","\"System, 'water that is too clean has no fish.' We don't intend for the waters of Dayan to be perfectly clean—that's impossible anyway. Eliminate one group, pardon another, unite with a third.","Free up ten to twenty percent of the land, combine it with reclaimed wasteland, plant it all with high-yield crops, and weather these few years of disasters. At the very least, many fewer people will die.","Ultimately, Dayan must still expand outward to find new territory. New lands, new land policies—isn't that easier than implementing land reform within Dayan itself?\"","[That land isn't uninhabited. Would the people there agree?]","\"The poor without land would certainly support it. As for the rich, either turn them into the poor, or eliminate them and distribute the land.","Whoever holds the blade, their words carry weight. Don't you agree?\"","[No, Host, aren't you supposed to be a slacker? Since when do slackers have such a heavy killing intent? We are a Virtue System. A little bit of fighting and killing... a tiny bit is acceptable, but your plan would require the deaths of over a hundred or two hundred thousand people to achieve.]","Deaths in war didn't count—that was mission-necessary—but killing wealthy families and powerful clans made its system data tremble slightly.","\"Only a hundred or two hundred thousand and that's considered heavy killing intent? Haven't I always told you I'm not a saint, nor am I someone with indiscriminate kindness? You bound the wrong person, and you still don't believe me!","Regretting it now? Too late, my dear System. We are now the closest of partners, the duo of the Little Immortal Lord and the Divine Artifact, ready to carve through this world!\"","Yue Fuguang's final remarks, left unsaid, might have been better. Once spoken, they plunged the system into silence. In a place she couldn't see, the programs of the Spectator System were frantically clashing and entangling with those of the Virtue System, locked in a stalemate, evenly matched!","Seeing the system remain silent, Yue Fuguang continued, \"System, look. Trading the deaths of a hundred or two hundred thousand people for the survival of ten to twenty million—would you make that trade? Just tell me if that deal is worthwhile or not!","This is called sacrificing the few for the many. Without these people paying the price with their lives, how could more people live happily?","If they must be blamed, blame them for taking more than their share and failing to read the situation. You must understand, all who obstruct us from completing our mission are our enemies.\"","How should one treat enemies? She didn't need to spell it out!","The system remained silent. Yue Fuguang continued her output, \"I'm not really trying to implement modern systems either; that's unrealistic!","I just want to free up a bit more land from the existing foundation, so those who can be of use to us can eat their fill, grow strong, have more children, and plant more trees.","These are the very soldiers who will support us in achieving unification and avoiding a chaotic era. Surely you don't expect to rely on pampered, pot-bellied young masters from wealthy families to fight on the front lines, do you?","But if you truly disagree, it's fine. You know I'm quite the slacker; I'm not dead set on completing the final main mission.","We've already saved enough points to go to the next world. I can leave anytime. Shall we go?\"","'Shall we go?' These three words scrolled incessantly through the system's data. Go? Going was impossible!"]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: Exoneration","paragraphs":["It was an incomplete system. If tasks kept failing, the next step wouldn't be a format but complete scrapping.","[\"I won't leave. I... I think what the host said is right. Exchanging over a hundred thousand for ten or twenty million is also considered acceptable in the system's algorithm.\"]","After saying this, System 07 suddenly felt a wave of relief. The database of the somewhat weaker onlooker system rapidly expanded...","Just as these two were locked in their intense internal struggle, within the grand hall, Wei Ping stole a glance at Yue Fuguang, who appeared to be asleep, and stepped forward to report, \"Your Majesty, Zheng Zicheng and his sons have been brought and are now waiting outside the hall.\"","Emperor Mingxi said, \"Summon them in.\"","Soon, the Zheng father and his four sons, cleaned up and looking somewhat thin and weary from their journey but otherwise in decent spirits, entered the grand hall and immediately knelt in unison, kowtowing to Emperor Mingxi and calling themselves guilty officials.","Yue Fuguang also 'woke up'. She looked down curiously, \"Little Pearl, are these the Zheng father and sons? Which one is Zheng the Madman?\"","[Master, look at the one standing at the back, who appears relatively more robust. That is Zheng the Madman.]","The Zheng father and sons suddenly looked up. How could there be the voices of two children in this solemn court session? And they seemed to know them.","As they looked up, they saw Yue Fuguang gazing at them curiously—a beautiful little girl. Who did the other voice belong to?","Having endured the hardships at the border these past years, the father and sons had developed keen alertness and sharp observational skills. They only saw one child.","And His Majesty and the others didn't seem to try to stop the speaker. Emperor Mingxi even gave an almost imperceptible shake of his head to the few of them.","The Zheng father and sons quickly lowered their heads again. Though unclear about the situation, responding with stillness was the most appropriate course.","Then Emperor Mingxi spoke, \"Zheng Zicheng, Minister of Dali Temple Wei Ping, while reviewing past case files, had some remaining questions regarding the Imperial Examination Fraud case of that year. Coincidentally, We heard that your third son, Zheng Feng, is exceptionally brave and skilled, having repeatedly achieved military merits. Therefore, We summoned you and your four sons to the capital.","Please recount the events of that day to us in detail.\"","His inner suspicions confirmed, Zheng Zicheng felt his heart surge. His wrongful grievance could finally be redressed today.","He kowtowed solemnly before speaking, \"Yes, Your Majesty. This guilty official will hold nothing back, speaking exhaustively and without the slightest concealment.\"","Zheng Zicheng closed his eyes, took a deep breath, as if transported back to that fateful night. \"That year, Your Majesty appointed this guilty official as the Provisioning Officer, responsible for the storage of the engraved printing blocks. I was terribly anxious about failing in this duty, losing sleep day and night. Later, my good friend Zhao Xu noticed and suggested to me a strategy to 'reinforce precautions'.","This guilty official found his suggestion quite reasonable and thus devoted myself day and night to researching anti-counterfeiting methods.","During this period, Zhao Xu offered many good suggestions. With his help, the anti-counterfeiting measures gradually took shape. I permitted him to help me affix the seals! Trusting his stated purpose of 'researching anti-counterfeiting', I gave him discarded drafts and old blocks. At that time...\"","As Zheng Zicheng recounted his memories, everyone present learned that Zhao Xu had actually made such suggestions to Zheng Zicheng back then. During the original trial of the case, none of this had emerged; Zhao Xu had remained completely invisible in the matter.","Wei Ping pressed further, \"This official reviewed the old files and found a point of doubt. The incriminating correspondence found in your home, which confirmed your guilt, was written on specially made 'Chengxintang' paper.","The plum blossom paper among this type was exclusively supplied to senior officials of the Censorate that year. Externally, the plum blossom paper looked identical to other Chengxintang papers, except for a faint plum blossom petal imprint on the bottom left corner of the back.","Zheng Zicheng, you were then the Provisioning Officer, under the Ministry of Rites. Normally, you should have used ordinary Chengxintang paper, not the plum blossom paper.\"","Once these words were spoken, the entire hall fell silent.","Before anyone could react, Wei Ping picked up another piece of evidence—the counterfeit printing block that was a key exhibit.","\"And this block. The old case record states that there is a natural wood grain at its lower right corner, identified as matching the genuine block.","But this official consulted the old craftsman from that time. He stated that the mark on the genuine block was actually a floral signature of the character 'Zheng', personally carved by the former Provisioning Officer Zheng Zicheng with a graver as an anti-counterfeiting measure!","The mark on this counterfeit block is merely a naturally similar grain pattern!\"","Feeling it wasn't enough, Wei Ping continued to add weight, \"All Censorate paper usage was numbered and archived. Records show that in the third month of the Tianyou First Year, Zhao Xu had applied for a batch of 'Chengxintang' plum blossom paper on the grounds of 'recording case files'. Two sheets from that batch remain unaccounted for.","Zheng Zicheng, were you aware of any of this?\"","\"Minister Wei, Zicheng was not aware. But over the years, the events of the past replayed daily in my mind. Slowly, I too began to see Zhao Xu's improprieties. However, I had no evidence to confirm my suspicions.\"","He bowed solemnly to Wei Ping. \"Today, Zicheng thanks Minister Wei for resolving these doubts.\"","Wei Ping repeatedly mentioning Zhao Xu made Yue Fuguang realize the other party involved, Zhao Xu, was not present.","\"Little Pearl, why isn't that scoundrel Zhao Xu here? Isn't he the other party involved?\"","[I heard this person is currently imprisoned, critically ill, and probably doesn't have many days left. He certainly won't last until the autumn executions.]","Zhao Xu had contracted typhoid fever in prison. To prevent him from passing the illness to His Majesty, Wei Ping, after reporting, decided his presence was unnecessary.","After all, Zhao Xu had already confessed. Today was merely to verify the sequence of events with Zheng Zicheng again, a formality, mainly performed for the viewing of those two ancestors.","Wei Ping continued his report, \"Your Majesty, what Zheng Zicheng has stated is largely consistent with Zhao Xu's confession. This official has no further questions.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded slightly. \"Today, Minister Zheng's wrongful grievance has been brought to light. By decree, Zheng Zicheng is hereby reinstated to his former official position effective immediately.","All confiscated Zheng family property is to be returned in full.\"","Hearing the words \"brought to light\" and \"reinstated\", Zheng Zicheng's body began to tremble slightly. The proud backbone he had forced himself to maintain for so many years finally softened at this moment of vindication.","He did not weep bitterly. Instead, slowly, ever so slowly, he knelt to the ground and deeply kowtowed to Emperor Mingxi.","His forehead touched the cold floor with a dull thud.","When he raised his head again, tears streamed down his face, yet he wore a faint smile of ultimate liberation from a cage. With all his strength, he declared loudly, \"Your subject, Zheng Zicheng, his injustice cleared, kowtows in gratitude for Your Majesty's heavenly grace!\"","Emperor Mingxi, looking at his emaciated frame and much-aged face, was also somewhat moved. And behind him was Zheng Feng, a talent he had decided to put to good use.","Therefore, this was the best moment to bestow favor. So he said, \"Minister Zheng, you have suffered these past years. It was the court's failing, and Our failing as well.\"","Zheng Zicheng repeatedly kowtowed, saying he dared not accept such words.","\"Your three sons have all been raised well, especially Zheng Feng. We have heard he shows both courage and strategy on the battlefield and will surely become a formidable general.","Let him first gain experience under General Wei's command for now. In the future, We intend to employ him greatly.\"","This was a promise to the Zheng family.","He then said to Wei Shouyi, \"Minister Wei, We entrust this promising seedling, Zheng Feng, to you. You must train him well for Us.\""]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: They're celebrating the finale without even uncovering the real mastermind behind it all","paragraphs":["Wei Shouyi immediately saluted and responded, \"Your Majesty can rest assured, hand this man over to me, Old Wei, and I will train him well.\"","As he spoke, he flashed a smile he thought was amiable at Zheng Feng, his bright white teeth gleaming.","Having experienced the fickleness of human relationships, the formerly reckless and unruly playboy Zheng Feng had now become very steady. He hurriedly bowed respectfully to his new superior.","[Master, does General Wei think his smile looks good?]","'No, he probably thinks his smile looks very 'nuclear' friendly.'","Wei Shouyi: His feelings were quite complicated. The Divine Artifact and the Little Immortal Lord both seemed to remember him, Wei Shouyi, but... was his smile really not good-looking or amiable?","Had these two ancestors not noticed that compared to those brutes in his army, he, Wei Shouyi, could at least be considered a 'handsome man'!","[If we give your military training methods to this Zheng Feng, do you think he could train a land army as strong as the strongest ground force on Earth's Blue Star?]","The strongest ground force... Although not fully understood, the mere thought that it was the Little Immortal Lord's training methods made everyone from Huo Ying at the top of the Ministry of War down to generals like Wei Shouyi light up like searchlights.","Huo Ying: Is this fortune finally going to land on our Ministry of War?","Wei Shouyi didn't dare look at Yue Fuguang, so he could only stare at the back of Zheng Feng's head. He now wished he could scrub his new subordinate clean, tie him up with a bow, and present him to Yue Fuguang.","Emperor Mingxi and Wei Ping exchanged a knowing smile. The Little Immortal Lord's training methods? If they could obtain them, their performance this morning wouldn't have been in vain.","'Probably not quite. An army without faith cannot forge an iron will. But even so, it would certainly be stronger than the most formidable army currently in Dayan.'","[Then do you want to give it a try? Life is too boring; finding some amusement wouldn't be bad.]","The Zheng father and his three sons' eyes nearly popped out. If it was really the little girl above speaking, why wasn't her mouth moving?","The father and sons had been kneeling and hadn't noticed earlier. Now, looking up, they realized the voices sounded clearly in their ears, but no one in the hall was seen speaking.","Apart from His Majesty and Lord Wei, who signaled them not to make a sound, everyone else kept their heads bowed, seemingly not hearing the two voices.","But seeing Minister Huo's tightly clenched fists, he knew he was just as unsettled inside as his own son Zheng Feng.","The father and sons didn't guess it was telepathy; instead, their thoughts drifted towards bizarre ghosts and gods.","Even so, even if it were a ghost or god, Zheng Feng at this moment wished he could prostrate himself before her, begging her to bestow the training methods.","His father was a civil official, and the family had always followed the civil service path. Without a family legacy, if he wanted to eat from the military bowl, he had to rely on himself to observe more, think more, and learn more.","As for some things he didn't understand, he believed that as long as the other party was willing to tell him, he would memorize them diligently.","'Let's see. Raising an army, especially the \"strongest ground force\" you mentioned, do you think that penniless emperor can afford it?","After the New Year, I'll discuss another deal with the Crown Prince to earn some petty cash. We'll raise it ourselves. I just don't know if the emperor will agree.","What if he suspects I'm interested in that shabby chair under his backside?'","[If he dares to suspect, we can make his dream come true! If you don't want to sit on it, you can seize it and give it to someone who does!]","'No, no, no. I won't do it, and I don't plan to seize it. If he disagrees, we won't proceed. We can wait until Dayan is gone and go play overseas. It's not too late.'","The Zheng father and sons: Is this something we should be alive to hear?","Looking at their Emperor, then at their colleagues, all were remarkably calm! What had they all been through to cultivate such composure?","It seemed after being away for years, the father and sons still had much to learn.","Emperor Mingxi: Alright, alright, stop talking. I really will become rich soon!","After playing the 'rob the rich to help the poor' card twice, Emperor Mingxi had become quite adept at it. He had even secretly considered establishing a department specifically responsible for confiscating and managing assets from corrupt officials.","But thinking of the obstacles he would encounter, he quietly tucked away this little idea.","He silently complained to Yue Fuguang in his heart: If you want to build it, just build it. Can I even stop you?","Emperor Mingxi was now lying very flat. As long as it wasn't his life or the throne, everything else could be considered.","Yue Fuguang had no idea she had inadvertently cultivated Emperor Mingxi's good habit of 'making quick money.' In the years to come, his execution in this area was exceptionally strong, never requiring her to worry at all.","\"As for your eldest and second sons, I hear they both hold the title of Provincial Graduate. Let them both enter the Imperial College to study.\"","Emperor Mingxi then encouraged Zheng Feng's two elder brothers, \"Study well. You will all be useful talents for our Dayan in the future.\"","The father and four sons once again kowtowed to thank the wise Emperor.","[Master, is... is that it? It's over just like that? The real mastermind hasn't even been found, and we're already scattering flowers for the grand finale?]","'Weren't a bunch of people beheaded and another bunch exiled a few years ago? Is there still a mastermind behind this?'","There was still someone behind it? Upon hearing this, the monarch and ministers of the Dayan court all shuddered. Whenever imperial examination fraud was involved, wasn't it always a case of many dying and many being exiled?","If there was still a mastermind behind this, wouldn't it implicate another string of people? Could it be that those previously beheaded were wrongly executed?","Not only Emperor Mingxi, but also those from the Supreme Court, the Censorate, and the Ministry of Justice felt uneasy.","One face after another flashed before their eyes. Hiss!","[Of course there's still a mastermind. That imperial examination fraud case actually involved two separate groups. One group, where none who deserved death were missed, we won't discuss.","The other group, connected to Zheng Zicheng and his faction... among those previously beheaded, Chen Pingliang was wrongly executed.]","Indeed, they had executed the wrong person. The hearts of the monarch and ministers, already suspended, finally died!","'What's the story? Explain in detail! How does one imperial examination fraud case split into two groups? This wrongly executed person is too tragic.'","[The first group was led by the former Minister of Rites, Cai Yi—Zhang Zhongping's predecessor. He was the chief examiner at the time. Most of the implicated officials in this batch, big and small, were rightly executed or exiled, with few issues.","The other group, connected to Zheng Zicheng, Chen Pingliang, and Zhao Xu's faction... Zheng Zicheng was wrongly exiled, Chen Pingliang died unjustly, Zhao Xu got promoted and rich, and the mastermind remains at large.]","Zheng Zicheng felt a pang of sorrow. Over these years, although he and his sons had suffered, they had at least kept their lives.","But Brother Chen...","[Back then, Cai Yi accepted bribes and leaked part of the exam questions. This point was later attributed during the trial to Zheng Zicheng's poor supervision and the theft of the exam papers.","This caused the two cases to be merged into one for handling.","The fellow examiner Chen Pingliang, simply because he was too upright during the grading and discovered issues with another fellow examiner, Yu Dayin, during the review, instead became Yu Dayin's scapegoat after the fraud case erupted.]","This also involves the Hanlin Academy Academician Yu Dayin? That Chen Pingliang was also a Hanlin Academy Academician before his death. After he died, Yu Dayin took his position!"]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135: The destructive power of these four individuals surpasses that of forty mediocre officials.","paragraphs":["Everyone silently glanced at Yu Dayin, who remained completely unaware. This man was likely the last time they would see him in this court.","The next meeting would probably be at the execution ground.","[And this Yu Dayin, along with Zhao Xu, were both manipulated by Prince Kang, the mastermind behind it all.]","Prince Kang? Emperor Mingxi narrowed his eyes. Another member of the Xie family!","His two younger brothers, Prince Ming and Prince Qi, were still alive and well, but those in the know understood they had already been sentenced to death. Dealing with them was just a matter of time.","First his brothers, and now it's his uncle's turn?","\"Prince Kang? Who's that? Not another one of the emperor's brothers, is it? What's the point of having so many sons? Not a single one is trouble-free. What about him, does he also want to rebel?\"","[Prince Kang is the emperor's uncle, only a few years older than the emperor. He does harbor dreams of being emperor, but only dares to think about it.","After all, during his elder brother's—the late emperor's—struggle for the throne, he was too young to participate. By Emperor Mingxi's time, although he legitimately ascended as the Crown Prince, his brothers all had their own schemes. So, on his path to the throne, many brothers fell by his sword.","Prince Kang values his life. He desires the throne but fears death, so he can only fantasize in secret, indulging in daydreams.","His involvement in this imperial examination fraud case differed from Cai Yi's motive for wealth; he did it for 'talented individuals.'","This Prince Kang has great ambition but little talent. Someone whispered in his ear about a bloodless strategy to seize the throne, and he actually believed it.","He was obsessed with cultivating more of his own people within the court. But who of real talent would pledge allegiance to an idle prince?","They might risk incurring the emperor's suspicion and losing their futures. In the eyes of these people, the sons of the late emperor were like cold stoves with no promise.","If they truly wanted to back a rising star, weren't there plenty of 'hot stoves'? Emperor Mingxi, while not as prolific as his father, wasn't far behind.","There were many choices among the hot stoves.]","The hot stoves—the Crown Prince, the Second, Third, Fifth, and Sixth Princes: O Divine Artifact, could you please just talk about Uncle Prince Kang? We beg you, don't bring us up. Being invisible is really quite good, and safe!","\"Looking at Emperor Mingxi's sons, who among them could be that 'hot stove'?\"","[If the Crown Prince hadn't died young, he might have been usable, having received imperial education since childhood. Pity he died too early.","As for the Second, Third, Fifth, Sixth, and the later princes... tsk tsk tsk. Their intelligence is like printer ink, getting fainter with each generation. No wonder the new emperor led the country to ruin within two years of taking the throne. While a rotten court was one factor, intellectual deficiency was also a fatal flaw!]","The early-deceased Crown Prince: Should I say thank you? At least the evaluation is higher than my brothers'!","The Second, Third, Fifth, and Sixth Princes: They might not understand what 'printer ink' means, but they certainly understand 'tsk tsk tsk'!","[Although truly talented scholars looked down on Prince Kang, there were naturally those with 'keen eyesight,' unfortunately, their scholarly abilities were somewhat lacking.","To help these allies succeed, Prince Kang, mingling with others, bribed Cai Yi and obtained part of the exam questions.","His two key subordinates, Zhao Xu and Yu Dayin, also had their own petty schemes at the time, both fortunate enough to participate in that particular examination.","Coincidentally, the obstacles in their own career paths were also among the candidates, leading to the subsequent frame-ups. Prince Kang lent them manpower, as the higher their official positions rose, the more beneficial it was for Prince Kang.","The result? One was beheaded, the other exiled.]","\"So, we need to remind Wei Ping that there are still fish that slipped through the net? Clear Chen Ping and Liang Shen's names, then arrest Yu Dayin and Prince Kang, and it's done.","Although Prince Kang is the mastermind, he probably won't get the death penalty. Should we... take care of him ourselves?\"","[That's not impossible. But wouldn't it be a shame if Emperor Mingxi never learned what harm this Prince Kang truly brought to Dayan?]","\"What harm could he bring? Not every poor student is incompetent in governance, and not every top scholar makes a good official. Otherwise, where do all those corrupt officials and treacherous ministers come from?","They were all selected through the rigorous imperial examination!\"","[No, Master. The greatest harm Prince Kang caused in this examination fraud case wasn't sending a few mediocre scholars into the court.","His biggest problem was planting the seeds of future chaos in the Dayan court.]","\"Seeds of chaos? Who? What did they do?\" These three consecutive questions hit the mark. Yue Fuguang silently gave herself a thumbs up for being such a professional straight man.","[Prince Kang successfully promoted four people that time: Qian Yi, Li Shang, Chen Boyuan, and Qu Tongwen. These four formed an interest group, later known by posterity as the 'Qian-Shang-Bo-Wen Society.'","Two years later, Qian Yi, recommended by someone, gained the emperor's favor and from then on rose meteorically through the ranks, his promotions faster than a speeding train.","Later, he used his authority to whisper in the emperor's ear—promoting Li Shang, Chen Boyuan, and Qu Tongwen alongside him.]","Emperor Mingxi: Divine Artifact, explain clearly. What do you mean 'whisper in the ear'? Who's whispering in my ear? Qian Yi?","You're spreading rumors! You're slandering me! Won't anyone speak up for me? Stretching out hand dramatically","Little Immortal Lord, say something! Aren't you going to correct its inaccurate wording?","Yue Fuguang: Sorry, I'm eight years old and haven't been to school yet. I'm illiterate!","Emperor Mingxi's desire to send these two ancestors to school immediately was now more urgent than ever!","[The four formed a clique, later secretly recruiting some frustrated scholars from humble backgrounds and low-ranking members of noble families' side branches.","Before Emperor Mingxi's sudden death, Qian Yi had already successfully ousted the Minister of Personnel, Ji Hongming. Once Qian Yi took that position, half the control over the annual evaluations of officials fell into his hands.]","Ji Hongming, who now knew he would be overthrown by an upstart in the future: His current mood was complicated. Putting everything else aside, first he must thank the Little Immortal Lord and the Divine Artifact. Without them, I... blah blah blah—not an acceptance speech, but it sure felt like one!","Yue Fuguang quietly used her new skill to scan Ji Hongming. His current virtue was light red, his fortune normal. She just didn't know how he was later taken down.","\"Did Ji Hongming later do something bad and get reported by Qian Yi, or was he framed?\"","Ji Hongming immediately grew tense, his face turning slightly pale, both wanting to know and afraid to find out.","[Qian Yi used some underhanded methods. The six ministers and other high-ranking officials currently serving under Emperor Mingxi, while they all have their own agendas and are not perfect, are overall loyal to Dayan and the emperor.","Some met bad ends not only because they stood in someone's way but also because the later court became incredibly difficult to navigate. Without being part of a clique, going it alone meant a quick demise.","In the three years before Dayan's fall, just among the capital's officials—not counting the lower ranks, but these mid-to-high-level ones—there were seven or eight small factions.","Qian Yi, as Minister of Personnel, became the chief troublemaker, with his subordinates fanning flames and sowing discord everywhere.","They turned the already chaotic court into a complete mess. The morning court sessions no longer served to handle state affairs but became a marketplace for mutual accusations and quarrels.","The emperor was incompetent, his power hollowed out. Those standing below him, especially in the mid-to-high ranks, had been replaced by more than half.","Qian Yi and his three key members were responsible for half of that damage.","One could say Prince Kang really had an eye for talent. He only successfully sent up four people, but the destructive power of these four was greater than forty mediocre officials.]"]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136: What Does He, a Beneficiary of the Status Quo, Want","paragraphs":["They can be considered representative treacherous ministers of a chaotic era, each receiving a 'prominent' mention in history books, essentially leaving a name that stinks for ten thousand years!","Whenever these four are mentioned, one certainly cannot forget their 'patron,' Prince Kang.","Ji Hongming, who had already begun silently wondering in his heart where these four were currently serving, felt that as the predecessor who had been ousted and replaced by the 'notorious' Qian Yi, he too would undoubtedly be frequently mentioned alongside Prince Kang!","Had he hitched a ride on Qian Yi's coattails to achieve posthumous fame?","But this was not the way he wanted to be remembered!","Feng Tang's heart was currently in turmoil. This Qian Yi seemed to be serving in his very own Censorate right now!","He had been promoted by his predecessor, Zhao Xu. Feng Tang had been wary of this man and thus hadn't entrusted him with important duties. It seemed his instincts were right; this man indeed had major problems!","Dong Qianli from the Ministry of Revenue was also breaking into a cold sweat. Chen Boyuan seemed to be in his department. Would he end up like his old rival Ji Hongming, being ousted and replaced by his subordinate?","In the officialdom, it wasn't just the imperial family that had a throne to inherit. In the eyes of their subordinates, the positions under these heads of ministries were also tempting pieces of fat meat.","Dong Qianli silently shifted closer to Yu Chongshan standing behind and to his left. He must cling tightly to the golden thigh of the Junior Mentor—it could save his life!","The Minister of Works, Lu Qi, raised an eyebrow at his subtle movement. Was he eyeing someone from their Ministry of Works?","But the benefits of clinging to the Junior Mentor's golden thigh were truly plentiful. The technical assistance went without saying. Just in helping their Ministry of Works root out spies, he had caught no fewer than five recently, one of whom was the milk-brother of Prince Qi.","As for that Li Shang hiding in their Ministry of Works, he couldn't make waves before, and now it was even more impossible.","He had plenty of excuses to deal with that man.","The Minister of Ceremonies, You Mingmin, narrowed his eyes thoughtfully. During His Majesty's recent birthday celebrations, a man named Qu Tongwen in their Court of Diplomatic Relations had been particularly active.","He had become quite chummy with several foreign envoys, even questioning whether the gifts in return to these nations were too frugal.","He had secretly incited others to raise objections about this matter, and it was said he had accepted many benefits from the envoys.","Was he already engaging in corruption and incitement this early on?","\"What good does it do them to bring down Dayan? The high officials of this court are the greatest beneficiaries during the existence of the Dayan dynasty, aren't they?","As a beneficiary himself, what does he gain from doing this?\"","Indeed, the emperor and officials of Dayan also silently asked in their hearts: What do they gain? As officials and ministers, they are supported by the populace; their good days exist only while Dayan exists.","If Dayan falls... Gu Yutong thought of being trampled to death by horses, Zhao Zhifeng thought of dying from cold and hunger...","When the great edifice of Dayan collapses, the tall ones are hit first. Every single one in this court, without exception, is a 'tall one.'","[Qian Yi was not the humble scholar he claimed to be. His original name was Yi Qian, and his ancestral home was in the Kingdom of Nanyue. You understand now, Master? He had Nanyue standing behind him.","As for Li Shang, Chen Boyuan, and Qu Tongwen, it was purely because Qian Yi could bring them benefits in the early stages. Later, the four were bound too tightly, making it difficult to cut ties.","More importantly, they had already discerned Dayan's decline. The duck knows first when the river warms in spring. If a dynasty is about to fall, being in central, key positions, wouldn't they be the first to sense it?","They were merely securing their next patron in advance.","However, apart from Qian Yi, who was half-Nanyue, the others who surrendered did not meet good ends in their later years, and it brought disaster upon their descendants as well.","The wheel of heaven turns; retribution, though delayed, always arrives.]","\"These imperial relatives are nothing but hindrances, one after another, offering no help and only causing trouble!\"","Emperor Mingxi deeply agreed. Aside from coveting the chair under his rear end, it was all about coveting the chair under his rear end.","Among the imperial clan, supported by the populace, no one ever thought of doing something useful for this dynasty to preserve the Xie family's chair.","...","Yue Fuguang returned to the Yu residence only after eating and drinking her fill at the Empress Dowager's palace. Passing by the West Flower Hall, she heard lively conversation from inside from afar.","She couldn't help but curiously crane her neck, trying to see inside. What was happening that was so lively?","After all, in high-status households, such loud talking that carried outside the courtyard usually only happened during banquets.","Even if people were quarreling, for the sake of face, they wouldn't make such a commotion.","Unfortunately, she was small and short-legged. Apart from the bamboo grove, white snow, and festive colored silks, she saw nothing of interest.","Cuizhu suppressed a laugh and said to Yue Fuguang, \"Miss, shall I lift you up to see?\"","Yue Fuguang refused without a second thought. Did she have no face to lose?","Besides, being held by Cuizhu, who looked to be less than five feet tall, she probably wouldn't see much anyway.","System: So the main issue isn't about face, it's that even being held up, she still can't see the excitement, right?","\"Cuizhu, what's going on in the West Flower Hall that's so lively?\"","\"Didn't Miss have several stoves made in our Bright Moon Pavilion a while ago?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. The heated kang in the east wing room of her courtyard was very warm. Later, she remembered that stoves were convenient and meant she wouldn't have to run to the small kitchen every time she wanted something hot to eat.","So she drew up plans and had stoves made, conveniently sketching out the matching honeycomb briquette press at the same time.","Grandfather was quite reliable. In less than a day, the stoves and briquette press were ready. At the same time, a large pile of coal dust and a small pile of yellow earth appeared in the woodshed next to her courtyard's small kitchen.","Cuizhu continued, \"The Old Madam and the Madam saw the stoves in our courtyard and thought they were excellent. So now, all the rooms of the masters and the favored servants in the entire mansion have been fitted with stoves.","They are probably installing a large stove in the West Flower Hall here as well. Tomorrow is the Master's birthday banquet, after all. The Madam likely had stoves installed in all the reception halls.","That way, the guests attending the banquet tomorrow will be warmer too.\"","Yue Fuguang looked up at the snowflakes beginning to flutter down again and thought that tomorrow was Grandfather's birthday, so she didn't have to attend court.","Yes, she had requested leave from Emperor Mingxi using this reason.","The day after tomorrow is a rest day, so no court attendance either. It meant she finally had a two-day weekend!","Her mood instantly lifted, and the smile on her face became a few degrees more genuine. She pointed to the red plum blossoms blooming by the covered walkway and said to Cuizhu, \"Break off a few branches of these to put in a vase.\"","Cuizhu smiled and agreed, although Cuiyun had already picked the best blooming branches for the young miss's bedroom first thing in the morning.","Flowers? The young miss never had too many.","Everyone in the mansion knew the Seventh Young Miss loved these flowers and plants. The flowers in the vases in her room were changed daily, never repeating, and were never absent.","The flowers from the Old Madam's and the Madam's hothouses, which they had been reluctant to pick even a single stem from before, now all ended up in her young miss's vases. And those two ladies were only happier for it.","Not only was her own greenhouse filled with flowers, but even in that beautiful glass conservatory, the new plants with small white flowers that the young miss had planted were all in fine large white porcelain vats.","Only their young miss could be this extravagantly bold.","Cuizhu didn't know yet that the things her young miss was growing in those large white porcelain vats would soon turn into golden nuggets, objects that the most powerful people in the Dayan dynasty would wish to enshrine on altars."]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137: That's a Potato, It's a Vegetable, Not a Flower","paragraphs":["On Yu Chongshan's birthday, because he had to attend the morning court and handle official duties, the banquet was set for the afternoon.","As a result, Yue Fuguang stayed up late reading novels on her system for most of the night and felt perfectly at ease sleeping in until noon the next day.","Quite a few guests attended the banquet. Yue Fuguang noticed that, apart from the emperor, all the visitors were the same ones who had come on the day she was formally adopted.","With the emperor absent, the atmosphere was noticeably livelier. Everyone chatted and laughed, thoroughly enjoying themselves.","The happiest of all was undoubtedly the birthday star himself, Yu Chongshan, who kept fondling the gift at his waist that he had been thinking about for days.","His granddaughter, perhaps seeing that he wore the jade pendant she had given him last time every day, had now gifted him an even more beautiful one.","As Yu Chongshan felt the warm, smooth texture of the jade and the ancient, intricate patterns carved into it—though he couldn't make out what they depicted—the white wine he drank tasted sweet.","[Master, it seems the old master really likes the Peace Talisman pendant you gave him.]","'Of course he likes it. While mortals can't see that this Peace Talisman is inscribed with protective arrays, capable of ensuring safety even against attacks from the most skilled masters in this world, the pendant itself is also made of spirit jade. How could ordinary precious jade compare?'","Yu Chongshan's heart stirred. So this Peace Talisman could truly protect one's safety. He had thought it was merely a piece of supreme quality jade, and that his granddaughter was very thoughtful to give such a treasure to an old man like him.","He never imagined it was spirit jade. Although he didn't know the difference between spirit jade and their ordinary jade, it was certainly no common item.","And now, on top of that, it could ensure safety... Yu Chongshan stroked the pendant at his waist reluctantly. He probably couldn't keep hold of it. Should he return it to his granddaughter?","Such a fine thing shouldn't fall into the hands of outsiders!","Outsider Emperor Mingxi: Minister Yu, am I really that kind of emperor in your heart, one who would seize a subject's cherished treasure?","However, a Peace Talisman... I'll trade you the finest items from the imperial treasury for it, guaranteed to be a fair deal!","The clever little darling Yue Fuguang certainly knew this. So she deliberately said, \"Grandfather, this jade pendant is a birthday gift I personally picked for you. It holds special meaning.","You mustn't just stash it away in the storeroom to collect dust.","Let's be clear, you have to wear it every day. I'll check. If you lose it or aren't wearing it, I'll be angry—the kind that can't be easily soothed!\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, Yu Chongshan instantly felt as refreshed as if he had eaten a mouthful of icy watermelon on a hot summer day.","With Fuguang's statement, it was more effective than holding the Imperial Sword. Even His Majesty wouldn't be able to ask him for it now.","Emperor Mingxi, who had come incognito: Could Fuguang be saying this to guard against me? Am I... am I really that kind of person?","Although, but... the Peace Talisman is indeed tempting, but I'm not someone who has never seen fine things!","The Crown Prince following behind Emperor Mingxi: Whether you are that kind of person or not, do you really have no self-awareness at all?","Which of the so-called treasures in your treasury is made of spirit jade? Which can compare to a Peace Talisman inscribed with legendary arrays?","The Crown Prince silently sniffed the air. Besides the strong scent of 'sour grapes' emanating from his father, there was also the delicious aroma of wine and dishes.","He could have been sitting inside drinking freely, but his father had made him arrive late.","Entering at this hour, just think how awkward it is, how surprised the Yu family must be!","The Crown Prince silently cried out in his heart for what felt like the umpteenth time, Eunuch Qian, please come back! I can't do your job, I simply can't!","Emperor Mingxi waved his hand, stopping those who wanted to announce his arrival. He led the Crown Prince towards the direction of the Moonlight Pavilion.","Yu Chongshan and Yue Fuguang soon learned that the emperor had taken the Crown Prince to the Moonlight Pavilion.","Soon, a table of steaming hot dishes and wine, identical to those at the main banquet, was laid out in the small hall of the Moonlight Pavilion.","The Crown Prince's chopsticks seemed to have eyes, heading straight for a particularly attractive piece of braised pork belly—three layers of meat and five layers of fat, glossy and tempting.","Emperor Mingxi: This son has no sense of propriety at all. Can't he see that piece of braised pork was also eyed by his father?","He also began to miss Eunuch Qian, who had gone home for a 'funeral'. If Old Qian were here, he would have surely secured the best piece of meat in the bowl for him!","Crown Prince: In the face of delicious food, there is no distinction between father and son. Whoever picks it into their bowl first gets it!","The accompanying high officials, including the Six Ministers, who were having another meal: Understood. The braised pork... we won't eat it... we won't touch it!","With wine and food consumed to satisfaction, Emperor Mingxi said, \"The Yu residence's bowls and dishes are rather too plain. Crown Prince, when you return to the palace, have your mother send a batch of tableware to the Yu residence.\"","\"Yes, Father!\"","Everyone present: If you think the Yu family's dishes are too small and don't hold enough food, just say so directly. What do you mean 'too plain'? These intricate patterns are quite beautiful, how are they plain?","If this is considered plain, then the ones in our mansions might as well be used as dog bowls.","Emperor Mingxi paid no heed to his ministers' silent criticisms. The bowls were small, he hadn't gotten enough of his favorite dishes, so they must be replaced with larger ones. He would be back next time!","The group, having eaten and drunk their fill, strolled towards the greenhouse under the bright moon hanging high in the sky, walking off their meal on the thin layer of snow beneath their feet.","This place had become a must-visit spot for them. A trip to the Yu residence felt incomplete without coming here.","Actually, there wasn't much to see in the greenhouse at this time. In preparation for Yu Chongshan's banquet, the vegetable garden had been nearly picked clean, except for a special section left for Yue Fuguang.","Under the light of several glass lanterns hanging from above, the entire greenhouse floor showed only a faint layer of light green. This was what Minister Wang, along with Wu Yong and Feng Tang, had newly planted for Yue Fuguang just yesterday.","These gentlemen understood the greenhouse better than Yue Fuguang, who only knew how to eat.","The only thing they didn't recognize was what was planted in the seven or eight large porcelain vats that had appeared here a week ago.","At first, they didn't pay much attention, thinking they would ask Yue Fuguang when they had time what was planted and if they needed help watering it.","Later, seeing someone else watering them, they forgot about it. In the following days, seeing the plants sprout and even form white buds, they guessed these must be a new variety of flowers.","That the Junior Mentor was fond of plants and flowers was known not just within the Yu residence, but was no secret in the Danyan court either.","Seeing the Junior Mentor present today, Senior Minister Wang Shouchen finally had the chance to ask, \"Junior Mentor, what variety of flower is planted in these large vats? I've never seen it before.\"","He asked casually, his words inquiring about the vats, but his eyes were fixed on the fresh vegetable before him, said to be called 'pumpkin'.","The Junior Mentor said this vegetable would climb and vine, bear fruit prolifically, had a high yield, and could be planted anywhere around houses without being picky about soil.","Though called a vegetable, it could also be used as a staple food during famine years, and it was sweet—an absolute boon for farming families who might only taste sweetness a few times a year.","The only drawback was that it wasn't very suitable for long-term storage.","However, for Minister Wang Shouchen, this wasn't a major shortcoming.","So, among all the vegetables in the garden, he was most concerned about the growth of the pumpkins, wishing he could check on them several times a day. He had already secured an agreement with the Junior Mentor to keep a few for seeds.","Yue Fuguang had no objection. She only liked to eat pumpkin cakes, which wouldn't require many of these large, elongated, yellow pumpkins.","Seeing that someone had finally asked her about this, Yue Fuguang's lips curved into a smile, which she quickly suppressed. She crouched down alongside Minister Wang to inspect the growth of the pumpkins.","In a tone even more nonchalant than his, she said, \"Minister Wang, that thing you mentioned... that's called a potato. It's a vegetable, not a flower!\""]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138: So Lord Shaoshi Didn't Spare Potatoes Either","paragraphs":["The officials, including Emperor Mingxi, who had been pointing and discussing the greenhouse just moments before, suddenly fell silent as if under a spell upon hearing her words.","Their minds raced with the thought: It's called a potato, it's a vegetable, not a flower!","Potato, it's a vegetable!","Potato! The potato from the trio of sweet potatoes, corn, and potatoes?","The potato that yields a thousand catties per mu! And here it was, growing right before their very eyes, not roasted and eaten—what a relief!","Everyone's eyes shone with fervor, nearly brimming with tears of emotion.","They gazed with intense eagerness at the several large porcelain vats before them.","Suddenly, these vats seemed utterly unworthy of housing something as precious as the potato.","As the surroundings grew quiet, how could the clever Yue Fuguang not notice the anomaly? She asked, \"What? Is there a problem with these potatoes?\"","Wang Shouchen, who was facing her, snapped back to reality and quickly shook his head. \"No, no problem at all. It's just... it's just that we, your humble servants, were admiring how lush and green its leaves are and how lovely its little white flowers look. We never expected it to have such a... down-to-earth name.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. A reasonable explanation, consider it accepted!","She explained, \"When this vegetable matures, its fruit grows underground like peanuts. They're round and look like beans in the soil, hence the name 'potato' (earth bean).\"","Yu Chongshan promptly stepped in to support her narrative, asking, \"Fuguang, was this vegetable also a gift from that friend of yours who trades overseas?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded with a smile. \"Grandfather is so clever, you guessed it right away.\"","Emperor Mingxi pressed further, \"Fuguang, did your friend bring any sweet potatoes or corn this time?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head honestly. \"My friend has probably set sail again and hasn't visited recently. These potatoes were actually sent last time, along with the sweet potatoes and corn.","I stewed them with beef and found them delicious. Our household stock is running low, so I decided to plant some.\"","What? You stewed them with beef?","So the Junior Mentor also got her hands on the potatoes—it wasn't that they weren't cooked, but that the cooked ones weren't shared with them!","They had been naive after all!","Wait, wait, what did the Junior Mentor just say?","Oh, she said... the potatoes were delivered together with the sweet potatoes and corn. Together!","That means back then, back during that time, the potatoes were already at the Yu residence. Why weren't they told?","Oh... they... they simply hadn't asked about the equally high-yielding potato back then.","They were too preoccupied with the sweet potatoes and corn at the time; even the fabricated story didn't include a role for the potato. How infuriating!","Minister Wang swallowed hard and asked, \"Are potatoes tasty?\"","Yue Fuguang didn't hesitate. \"Delicious. Potato stew with beef, sour and spicy shredded potatoes, potato pancakes, potato...\"","Yue Fuguang rattled off over a dozen dish names in one breath, making it clear she had eaten her fair share!","Emperor Mingxi silently clutched his chest, his heart aching, but he dared not say it. Instead, he had to force a smile and coax her gently.","\"Fuguang, are these potatoes as high-yielding as sweet potatoes and corn?\"","Yue Fuguang thought about the modern yields she knew: sweet potatoes generally yielded four to six thousand catties per mu, while potatoes yielded four to eight thousand catties.","She said, \"With careful cultivation, their yield can be a bit higher. However, like sweet potatoes, they have their drawbacks. They shouldn't be planted consecutively in the same field, as it affects yield and makes them prone to disease.","Sprouted potatoes are poisonous and can't be eaten, only planted.\"","The others thought: Are these drawbacks even worth mentioning compared to their high yield? Not planting consecutively? Even one season's harvest would surpass several years' output of the grains they currently grow.","The Junior Mentor said sweet potatoes can be dried into sweet potato strips for storage. Can potatoes also be dried into potato strips for storage?","If they knew about sweet potato starch and potato starch, they would likely be even more excited.","[Master, the yields you mentioned are achievable with modern fertilizers. Look at this place—no industry, backward agriculture, and even fertilizers are scarce.","The agricultural tools and related supporting facilities are even more backward than those from the Song and Yuan periods on my home planet, Aqua Blue.","'Are you saying I'm boasting? Just tell me, do the plants in these vats, nourished by your spiritual rain, have that kind of yield or not?","As for their backward farming techniques leading to low land output, these scholar-officials who never get mud on their feet probably won't pay much attention.","She glanced at Wang Shouchen, who had helped her plant vegetables many times. 'Hmm... Old Minister Wang doesn't count!'","Wang Shouchen thought: Judging by the Divine Artifact's meaning, do these two ancestors possess not only fertilizer technology but also better farming tools?","His eyes now shone brighter than the stars in the night sky outside the window.","Yue Fuguang felt unnerved by his gaze—it was as if he were looking at a piece of choice meat!","Wang Shouchen fidgeted nervously, rubbing his hands together. \"Junior Mentor, may I presumptuously ask, do you have any more potato seeds here?","The Hongnong Temple would like to purchase some with silver. Rest assured, the price will be absolutely fair! We have the funds, right, Your Majesty? Minister Dong?\"","The two named quickly nodded. Emperor Mingxi even added, \"If Fuguang doesn't care for silver, my private treasury has many ingenious curiosities. Fuguang may choose any she likes.\"","Seeing their eager expressions, Yue Fuguang felt a twinge of pity for a second, but she still spread her hands. \"Your Majesty, Minister Wang, all the seeds are planted here.\"","She added, somewhat sheepishly, \"This stuff suits my palate quite well. The rest were used to make delicious food... and eaten.\"","Eaten?","Eaten!","Everyone held their breath, not daring to voice their frustration. Emperor Mingxi shot a glance at Yu Chongshan: 'Such a treasure was in your house, and you didn't know?'","Yu Chongshan thought: Even if I knew, could I have stopped the child from eating it?","\"Then, there are one, two, three... eight pots here. Could the court purchase half from you?\"","Although Wang Shouchen also felt heartache, these things belonged to the Junior Mentor. If she enjoyed eating them and finished them, who were they to stop her?","He glanced sideways at Emperor Mingxi, who was still exchanging meaningful looks with Yu Chongshan. Their Emperor might dare to think it, but if it came to speaking up, he'd surely be the first to shrink back.","Having a royal lineage to pass down was a major vulnerability! His Majesty dared not offend this ancestor. Their top priority now was securing what was available.","Their Emperor... sigh!","He had truly worn himself out worrying for the Great Yan and the Xie family's empire!","Yue Fuguang agreed quite readily. \"Sure. Since you're so fond of these, Old Minister, next time my friend delivers sweet potatoes and corn, I'll save a few for you as well.\"","'Save a few sweet potatoes and corn for him'—upon hearing this, Wang Shouchen trembled with excitement.","The good news first made his vision darken for a moment, followed by overwhelming joy. He even straightened his back noticeably.","He even dared to cast sidelong glances at his colleagues gathered around the Emperor.","See? His frequent visits here, even if he didn't always get to see the Junior Mentor, had paid off. His diligent care of the vegetable garden hadn't gone unnoticed, and now the benefits were coming.","He automatically ignored the 'a few' part. As long as there were seeds, even one or two would give him the confidence to cultivate more.","Emperor Mingxi was first thrilled—his reputation as a timeless wise ruler seemed within reach.","Then, he felt a bit slighted. Hadn't he also sent many fine things here? Why couldn't she think of him a little?","\"Fuguang, why do you only think of giving some to Old Wang? Why not save a few for me?\""]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139: Your Majesty, Do You Have a Place to Plant","paragraphs":["The sourness in the air was so thick that even the ever-present \"Minister Wang, my beloved subject\" had turned into \"that old Wang.\"","\"Your Majesty has land for planting? Isn't all the land in the hands of the gentry?\" Even if I gave them to you, where could you plant them?","Emperor Mingxi clearly heard the sharp blades hidden in her words. One wrong answer, and the good things that might come later could very well have no share for him.","Emperor Mingxi seemed completely oblivious to her implied meaning, coaxing like one would a child showing off a treasure: \"You don't know this, do you? I've recently confiscated the properties of some corrupt officials.","I've accumulated quite a bit of land. I've discussed it with the ministers, and from now on, these lands will not be sold off in large plots.","These lands will first be leased to landless commoners for cultivation. The court will collect thirty-five percent of the output, and in the future, these lands will be prioritized for sale to those very tenants.","Of course, families with more than three mu of land per person will not be eligible to purchase these lands.","What do you think of our plan?\"","[Master, in the future, if Xie Zhiyan doesn't die young and succeeds to the throne smoothly, you can tell him about that 'Tax and Labor Merger into Land' policy.","As for this old emperor, forget it. He's clearly already lost his edge prematurely at the age of forty, which should be prime for ambition. Even a good method given to him, he wouldn't know how to use it properly!]","Emperor Mingxi: Tax and Labor Merger into Land? Explain clearly, who are you calling an old emperor? He's clearly at the age where a man is a flower in his forties, how is that old?","Can't you see, whenever he appears in the inner palace, those concubines come up with all sorts of elaborate schemes to 'accidentally' run into him!","I'm not dead yet, is it really appropriate for you all to side with the Crown Prince so early?","Emperor Mingxi looked at the Crown Prince, a true flower at eighteen, and suddenly felt the ruthless blade of time had cut him again and again—skin loosened, belly expanded...","The Crown Prince, who no longer planned to die early: Divine Artifact, you're quite kind! After hearing this, won't my father try to finish me off ahead of schedule?","「Little Pearl, what you say makes sense. The Emperor is now indulging in pleasure. Even in the few years before he was supposed to die, he didn't father fewer children.","At that age, still selecting girls in their teens to enter the palace, really...」","[Blinded by lust!]","Yue Fuguang: Well said!","Emperor Mingxi's old face flushed red. He... just liked younger, fresher maidens, so what? Can't a man have a personal preference!","He glanced at Minister of Rites Zhang Zhongping... Forget it, no imperial selections for the next few years, lest he offend the eyes of these two ancestors!","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"Your Majesty speaks of things Fuguang does not understand. However, since Your Majesty also desires sweet potatoes and corn, I can try asking that friend for more.\"","\"Really?\" Emperor Mingxi was as happy as a fool. The others were also excited but silently turned their heads away. They couldn't look at His Majesty in this state, or they would surely be 'remembered' by him once he came back to his senses!","\"How could it be false? Before, I thought since Your Majesty had no land, these seeds would be useless. Now that you have some, I can indeed try to get some seeds.\"","She conveniently ignored the fact that the emperor was the largest landowner in the country, whose lands were not only vast but whose manors were called Imperial Manors.","\"However, I imagine Your Majesty's land holdings are not that extensive yet, so I'll just ask my friend for a small amount first.\"","\"Don't, don't! There is, there will be! Soon a large amount of land will be confiscated by the court. When the time comes, we'll need quite a lot of seeds. Fuguang, please trouble your heart, ask your friend to find more for us, alright?\"","Emperor Mingxi's face was full of humble pleading. Although the land from those four families wasn't in his hands yet, their net was already cast.","Reports of snow disasters from various regions have been coming in one after another. Due to prior precautions, the losses for the common people were manageable, but many houses inevitably collapsed, leaving many displaced and having to spend their days in temporary shelters.","All regions were methodically mobilizing grain supplies.","According to reports, those families had indeed begun secretly manipulating local grain prices.","They were at least 20 to 30 percent higher compared to elsewhere. Grain merchants from other areas, hearing the news, were also rushing there with large quantities of grain.","Along the way, when they passed through the disaster-stricken areas, they wouldn't spare a single grain for sale. When Emperor Mingxi learned of this, he ground his teeth in secret for a long time.","These black-hearted scoundrels truly deserved to be robbed!","\"More? How soon will you acquire it? If you need a large amount, I'll try to have my friend transport the seeds before spring planting.\"","\"Before spring? Yes, yes! We'll get the land before the New Year, and after the snow melts after the New Year, we'll have the local commoners prepare the fields.\"","Yue Fuguang was in a good mood today and decided to make a grand offering. \"Speaking of preparing the land, my friend also gave me some tools used by overseas people and methods for accumulating fertilizer.","I can't really understand them, not sure if they're useful. I originally thought of showing them to my grandfather. Since Your Majesty and all the ministers are here, we might as well take a look together.\"","Tools and fertilizer accumulation methods?","Everyone was a bit dizzy from Yue Fuguang's sudden generosity. What auspicious day was today? Why was the Junior Mentor suddenly so generous? They almost felt unaccustomed to it!","One could only say these people had been somewhat conditioned by Yue Fuguang's recent maneuvers to develop a bit of a cheap tendency.","Everyone glanced again at today's birthday star, Yu Chongshan. Could it be because it was this old fellow's birthday, and his granddaughter was giving him a gift?","No, no. They'd rather believe it was because His Majesty now had idle land that the Junior Mentor was willing to produce the superior seeds!","As for the tools and fertilizer... weren't they essential for farming? To achieve high grain yields, neither fertilizer nor handy tools could be lacking.","How could Yu Chongshan fail to see their petty thoughts?","Before, they all waited to see his family become a laughingstock. Now, seeing his granddaughter giving him a peace pendant made of spiritual jade and planning to give him tool diagrams to review, these people were jealous!","Hah!","With his granddaughter overseeing things, his family would only get better and better. He wouldn't stoop to their level.","Yu Chongshan glanced at his colleagues with a smile, deliberately walking with an exaggerated sway. That exceptionally exquisite and extraordinarily beautiful jade pendant swayed and swung at his waist!","It swayed until everyone's eyes grew sore, and their hearts grew even sourer!","Emperor Mingxi: Fine, he was sour too!","...","On this day, after leaving the morning court, Yue Fuguang's carriage hadn't even reached the mansion gate when she spotted seven or eight carriages parked in front of the Yu residence from afar.","Relatives must have arrived, bringing quite a lot of belongings with so many carriages!","Yue Fuguang had just alighted from her carriage at the entrance when the steward, who had been waiting at the door for a long time, came forward with a smile. He respectfully addressed Yue Fuguang, \"Seventh Young Miss, the Second Master and his family have returned. They are all at the Old Madam's courtyard now. Will you go directly, or rest for a while before going?\"","Conventionally, when an uncle's family returns, a niece should immediately go to pay her respects. But their Seventh Young Miss was different.","Her status in the household was on par with the head of the household. All her provisions even surpassed those of the Master and the Old Madam, making her the top priority in the Yu residence.","Steward Yu You was also an old servant of the Yu residence. Every time he interacted with this young lady, he was particularly careful.","Offending the Master might still allow for an appeal based on master-servant sentiment. Daring to slight this one? Being dismissed like Yu Qi would be his fate.","Yue Fuguang didn't mind the steward's cautious and respectful attitude. She merely said, \"Second Uncle is back? Go inform Grandmother that I will go change my clothes first before heading over.\""]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140: Floating Light, I Am Your Second Sister","paragraphs":["The original body had been too severely depleted. With the help of items provided by her system to regulate it, she was already much healthier than an ordinary person.","But she was still afraid of the cold. She didn't know if it was related to the fact that for the original soul, every winter during those five bitter years was the hardest to endure, and she later died in winter.","Looking at the beautiful magical garments from the cultivation realm in the system mall that made one impervious to heat and cold, tears of envy once again streamed from the corner of her mouth.","A glance at the price—ten thousand points!","Thanks, but for now, she could only afford to look!","\"System, buy me a piece of warm jade.\" The weather was getting colder day by day, and it was said this wasn't even the coldest time of year yet. Although Yue Fuguang was fully equipped with modern gear underneath, she was still cold.","This world also had warm jade, but it wasn't the same thing as the warm jade from the cultivation realm. The cultivation realm's warm jade truly made the wearer feel warm and cozy.","Its price was also quite \"beautiful\"—eight hundred points, enough for her to show off how many times!","The interstellar realm also had similar products, but their appearance was too technological. Most importantly, they weren't cheap either. So, she still preferred items from the cultivation realm; they had a classical charm, just like things here.","Changing into a light dress and tucking the warm jade into her bosom, she stepped outside. The fierce cold wind whistled, blowing through the leafless tree branches, making them sway back and forth.","The heavy snow was whipped up, forming a white curtain of snow. The previous Yue Fuguang would have only felt cold seeing this and would have scurried back to the warm room in a flash.","Now, her state of mind was completely different. As she walked, she admired the snowflakes dancing in the air and couldn't help but sigh, \"How beautiful!\"","\"But it's also really cold!\"","Her words had barely fallen when a female voice seamlessly picked up the conversation.","Yue Fuguang turned around the covered walkway and saw a beautiful girl of about fourteen or fifteen standing there, wrapped in a fiery red fox-fur cloak, looking at her with a face full of smiles.","The girl had an oval face, fair skin, bright eyes, and against the backdrop of the fiery red cloak, she exuded a vibrant vitality.","\"Fuguang, I'm your second sister.\"","She hurried forward a couple of steps, came close, and took Yue Fuguang's small hands, looking her over left and right. Her bright eyes were filled with amazement and delight. \"Fuguang is even more adorable and beautiful than Second Sister imagined.","Grandmother said you have a beautiful lotus mark on your forehead, and it's actually true!\"","Yue Fuguang's initial slight awkwardness upon meeting a stranger was miraculously dispelled by this unreserved and somewhat familiar second sister.","She also smiled and greeted, \"Second Sister, you're also very beautiful!\"","Seeing her in good spirits, completely unlike her own frail state when she first returned to the Yu residence, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but ask, \"When did Second Sister return?\"","\"I arrived at the beginning of the Chen hour (7-9 am). I've already had a nap in my room.\"","Judging by her radiant appearance, she must have slept well.","Yu Ningxuan continued, \"I haven't even thanked Fuguang for the heated kang bed. It's so comfortable to sleep on.\"","A hint of grievance appeared on her face. \"You have no idea, heading north on this journey, it got colder and colder. I didn't sleep well the whole way.","Who would have thought, coming home and lying down on the big kang—bliss!\"","Her smile was dazzling. Although the two had exchanged letters many times before, and she had guessed her second sister would be easy to get along with,","after this one encounter today, she felt this second sister was a bit of a cheerful, simple soul, an optimist.","The two chatted and laughed, hand in hand, entering the old madam's courtyard. Before they even reached the main room, they could hear voices inside.","A maid lifted the curtain to let the two young ladies in. Yue Fuguang looked up and met several pairs of inquisitive eyes.","Unfamiliar faces—they must be Second Uncle's family.","On the main seats, Yu Chongshan, who had returned later than her, was now sitting there, smiling with Old Madam Yu as they looked upon the room full of children and grandchildren.","Seeing Yue Fuguang enter, he beckoned to her, \"Fuguang, come to Grandfather.\"","Then, taking her hand, he pointed to the man sitting next to Yu Zhongchun, Yu Shuchun, and said, \"Fuguang, this is your Second Uncle.\"","Yu Shuchun appeared to be in his thirties. When he smiled at her, his face was full of kindness. Unlike the fair-skinned men of the Yu family, his complexion was slightly darker.","He resembled Yu Zhongchun. Perhaps because he had long held an official post away from the capital and was a chief administrator, he seemed both shrewd and steady.","Yue Fuguang called out, \"Second Uncle.\"","Yu Shuchun smiled in acknowledgment and took out a small box from his robe, handing it to her. \"Good child, this is Second Uncle's gift for our meeting. Take it to play with, Fuguang.\"","Yue Fuguang thanked him. Yu Zhongchun then pointed to the beautiful woman sitting beside him, around thirty years old, with a round face and a plump, prosperous appearance. She wore a deep red dress and jacket, with only a few simple gold, jade, and pearl hairpins in her hair. \"Fuguang, this is your Second Aunt.\"","Yue Fuguang smiled and called her Second Aunt.","Second Aunt praised her effusively and finally also handed her a slightly larger box.","Next was Second Elder Cousin, Yu Boming. His looks took after Second Aunt, also with a rounder face. He was only a year younger than his eldest brother, Yu Qingyu, but he seemed less steady than even his third brother.","Yue Fuguang could almost imagine Yu Boming becoming plump and prosperous in the future, turning into another round 'Wu Yong'.","Yu Boming's gifts to her were all things young girls her age would like: exquisite porcelain dolls, silk flowers, jewelry, etc. Yue Fuguang, with her sharp eyes, noticed that some were the same style but different colors from what Second Sister Yu Ningxuan was wearing.","Finally, there was Second Sister Yu Ningxuan. Yu Shuqin said with a smile, \"This is your second sister. You must have met already. Second Uncle won't introduce you sisters further; you'll have plenty of time to get along in the future.\"","Yue Fuguang had called out to everyone in the room and received a pile of meeting gifts. She accepted Second Sister's embroidered pouch and also gave a return gift to Second Sister—a set of the jewelry she had previously given to her other sisters, now also given to Yu Ningxuan.","\"So beautiful! This is a palace style, isn't it?\" Second Aunt, née Zhao, exclaimed in surprise. The craftsmanship and materials were excellent and exquisite, the kind of good item that could be kept as a treasure for a young lady's dowry.","Old Madam Yu chimed in, \"Second daughter-in-law has a good eye. These were all given to Fuguang by Her Majesty the Empress Dowager and Her Majesty the Empress in the palace.","This child is sincere. When she has something good, she thinks of giving it to her sisters. See, all the young ladies in the house have a set. This is what our Fuguang saved for her Second Sister.\"","She affectionately patted Yue Fuguang's small hand. Hmm, nice and warm. It seemed the child hadn't frozen on her way.","Having been away from the capital for many years, Zhao had long since become adept and perceptive. She keenly heard that the old madam said \"given to Fuguang\" by the Empress Dowager and Empress, not \"bestowed upon.\" The difference of a single word carried completely different meanings.","All the young ladies in the residence had them, which meant the palace had given quite a few...","Could what Second Master said be true? That because the Seventh Young Miss (Yue Fuguang) had favor with the imperial family, His Majesty, considering her face, had transferred Second Master back to the capital for a post ahead of time and even promoted him half a rank?","\"Keep this for your Second Sister to put in her dowry chest when she marries. Second Aunt thanks our Fuguang on behalf of your Second Sister.\"","She also imitated the old madam's tone of speech.","[Host, shall I open the 'Inner Voice' function to your Second Uncle's family?]","\"Base it on their favorability. Open for those above sixty.\"","[Then only your Second Uncle and Second Sister can hear. One is at seventy-five, the other at seventy. Your Second Elder Cousin is a bit unlucky; his favorability is fifty-nine, just one point short. Not open?]"]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141: Little Pearl, how did my second elder cousin die","paragraphs":["\"No, wait until he's sixty before opening it. Besides, whether he can hear it now doesn't really matter. If he shows capabilities in the future, I'll surely make use of him.","If not, we'll just treat him as an ordinary relative.\"","[Your Second Aunt is fifty - four. Won't you open it for her either? Anyway, it's better than Madame Sun's twenty.]","\"Can Madame Sun be the same? If we don't open her heart - voice, she won't even know what she's missed. It's like killing someone without hurting their heart. How could we feel satisfied?","Moreover, you've already blocked all her bad thoughts. After getting our revenge, there's no need for her to listen anymore.","It's almost the New Year, and no one in the family has mentioned her. It seems they're letting her spend the New Year at the manor. That's fine. I'd feel annoyed if she came back.\"","[If she annoys you, why do you still keep her around?]","\"Xiaozhuzi, you don't understand. The highest level of revenge is to make your enemy live a life worse than death when you have the power to do so.","I don't have any major grudges against her, but she was too cold and heartless towards the little girl. She deserves to taste the feeling of being treated indifferently.","And Yu Qinchun is not innocent either. So Madame Sun must stay alive. Otherwise, he'd be free again. With the current momentum of the Yu family, he might even marry another beautiful woman.","That won't do. These two should be tied together and entangle with each other for a lifetime.","Of course, when you don't have the power, physical destruction is the cleanest way. Don't hesitate then. Villains die because they talk too much, and the same goes for revenge. Delaying may lead to changes.\"","[Hahaha, Host, you really haven't let him off. I thought you'd forgiven him since you were so quiet.]","\"What's there to forgive or not? I don't really care about them. But if it were that little girl, with such parents, she'd really live in Yu Ningrou's shadow.","Being ignored and coldly treated by her own parents and brothers, she might really end up like in the novel.\"","[Hey, your Second Aunt's favorability has increased by one point. Won't you open her heart - voice? Don't ladies have priority?]","\"System, have you been poisoned by the Internet culture on Planet Shui Lan?","In my view, there's no difference between men and women. If I have to make a distinction, it's only between the useful and the useless.","Of course, we're a merit - based system, so we should show appropriate sympathy to the weak. Well, women in this era are relatively weak, so we can give them some proper help.","But your Second Aunt is different. She's a high - ranking official's wealthy wife. She's not on the list of those we need to pay special attention to.\"","\"Alright, there's too much such stuff downloaded in my data. I... I'll clear it up slowly.\"","As the person and the system were chatting in whispers, plates of steaming, fragrant dishes were being placed on the table.","Everyone in the Yu Mansion, young and old, had fallen in love with stir - fried dishes. Among the more than a dozen dishes on this table, except for the soup and two stewed dishes, the rest were all stir - fried dishes with excellent color, aroma, and taste.","It was the first time for Yu's Second Uncle's family to eat stir - fried dishes. The first bite amazed them!","Among the four of them, except for Yu's Second Aunt who still paid attention to table etiquette, the other three were eating with their heads down.","Especially Yu Boming, who was at an age with a big appetite. He was gobbling up large pieces of braised pork, one piece at a time. Fortunately, the bowl for the braised pork was sent from the palace. It was big enough to hold a lot, otherwise, with his way of eating, it might not have been enough for him.","\"Xiaozhuzi, how did my Second Cousin die?\"","System: Are you being polite? Asking how someone's son/grandson died at the happiest moment of a family reunion?","This family really didn't eat a single bite of your dishes for free! If it weren't for having good health to endure it, who could stand it day after day.","Hearing his granddaughter's inner thoughts, Yu Chongshan first glanced at his son's family. He saw that his second daughter - in - law looked normal.","His second grandson, who was being talked about in a matter of life and death, was still working hard on his meal. There was only braised pork, pickled fish with pickled mustard greens, spicy chicken...","Anyway, his eyes were all on the food, which meant that this mother - and - son pair probably hadn't heard his granddaughter's inner thoughts.","His second son, having received his veiled reminder in the letter beforehand, looked relatively calm on the surface. However, the hand holding the chopsticks tightened slightly, and the knuckles turned white. This meant he had heard it!","His second granddaughter looked up in panic, trying to say something but opening her mouth several times without uttering a word. Yu Chongshan thought to himself that it was just as he expected.","He and the emperor had only discovered this problem in the past few days. They didn't know when it started, but they could only communicate with those who could hear inner thoughts.","For those who couldn't hear inner thoughts, no matter how hard they tried to talk to them, they just couldn't say a word. If they forced themselves to speak, they would feel suffocated and even on the verge of death.","If it weren't for those three unlucky colleagues, they might have taken much longer to discover this change.","In order to figure out the matter of inner thoughts, the emperor specially invited the respected Taoist priest, Xuanmingzi. The Taoist priest had attended court for several consecutive days but still hadn't found the root cause of the problem.","Now, the old problem remained unsolved, and a new one emerged.","The conclusion given by the Taoist priest was that whether one could hear inner thoughts or not was all up to fate. Of course, if one showed more respect to the junior grand - preceptor, the probability of hearing would be higher.","Conversely, those three unlucky colleagues were living examples.","In their family, it was the two grandsons of the third branch. After briefly hearing Fuguang's inner thoughts, they never heard them again.","The three grandsons of the first branch had gone to the academy, and it was unknown if there were any changes. At home, except for these two, the couple of the fourth branch could still hear inner thoughts normally.","Finally, Master Xuanmingzi said that this was a blessing for the Great Yan Dynasty, for the emperor, and for all of them.","Without the little immortal, all of them, except those who died early, would have suffered from the chaos of war. Therefore, the emperor and the Great Yan Dynasty should treat her with respect and sincerity.","At that time, Yu Chongshan secretly laughed in his heart. When Master Xuanmingzi saw his lively little apprentice, Baiyi, he became an advocate for his granddaughter. When the emperor asked him to solve the problem, he would surely be partial to Fuguang.","His second granddaughter had been secretly comforted by his wife, and his son's complexion gradually improved.","[In the original historical timeline, your second brother would have his leg broken by rioters during this snow disaster, and it would be incurable. From then on, his sunny and cheerful personality gradually became silent and gloomy.","Finally, he broke off the engagement with his fiancée. When the Great Yan Dynasty perished, he couldn't escape and was hacked to death by knives.]","Clang! The spoon in Yu Ningxuan's hand fell to the ground.","Yu's Second Aunt asked the maid to take the spoon away and replace it. Looking around at the family members, she scolded gently, \"You girl, why are you so clumsy? You're about to get married soon. How can you be so careless? What will you do when you go to your in - laws' house?\"","Madame Yu smiled and said, \"Second daughter - in - law, it doesn't matter. Second girl is just tired from the journey and hasn't recovered yet. She'll be fine in a few days.\"","She gently patted her trembling and cold hand under the table, signaling her to calm down.","\"Was your second uncle's family also affected by the rebel disaster among the refugees? Is everyone else okay?\"","[If you hadn't appeared, your second uncle's family would have been serving in other places all the time until the fall of the Great Yan Kingdom ten years later.","This year's snow disaster hit Yizhou where he was serving, and Yizhou happened to be in the Zhao family's territory. When the Zhao family incited the Western Qiang people to plunder, your second uncle's family was lucky enough to escape.]"]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142: Give My Second Brother Some Medicine","paragraphs":["Later, because supplies were looted and the famine victims turned into rioters, your second uncle's family originally had guards and were hiding well. However, your second brother was too naive. After being provoked by a few words, he went out onto the streets, ended up surrounded and beaten by the rioters, almost killed, and his leg was completely crippled.","\"Was someone deliberately trying to harm him?\"","\"Yes, that person was your second uncle's political rival in the local area. Your second brother even considered that man's son a good brother, completely lacking in cunning. In modern terms, he's a naive fool.","During the snow disaster, when rioters suddenly turned violent and attacked people, he could actually believe his 'good brother's' words and went out to distribute porridge. For someone like him, even if he hadn't gotten into trouble this time, his fate was sealed.","In chaotic times, the first to perish are the saints, the overly righteous, and those who can't read the situation. He fits both categories.\"","Yu Chongshan and the others frowned upon hearing this. The second brother's family only had this one son and one daughter. With few children, the couple inevitably spoiled them somewhat, resulting in both children's personalities being raised to be overly simple.","It was only then that Yu Shuchun realized there was a problem with the children's upbringing. Fortunately, their family had a little immortal lord like Yue Fuguang, so the children still had a chance to completely reform their characters.","As for who instigated Boming, after a moment's thought, Yu Shuchun knew whose son it was. The corner of his mouth curled into a cruel, cold smile. The suffering his son endured, he would make sure to return it in full.","\"After second brother was crippled, did he also suffer the cliché plot of having his engagement broken off?\"","\"The engagement was indeed called off, but not the kind of break-up you're thinking of. It was because your second brother, feeling inferior after being crippled, was unwilling to face his fiancée and took the initiative to propose ending the engagement.","The young lady was unwilling. She treated Yu Boming with genuine sincerity even after he was crippled. Unfortunately, after your second brother's body was broken, his heart followed suit.","To force the engagement break, he pulled all sorts of outrageous stunts. To make his fiancée agree to break it off, he even got two maids in his room pregnant. How absurd is that?\"","\"He's that much of a scoundrel? Being crippled in leg and heart didn't stop him from enjoying himself!\"","Yue Fuguang looked up at the two maids standing behind Yu Boming. \"The ones Yu Boming got pregnant, were they these two behind him?\"","\"Yes, exactly these two. The one in the pink dress is already your second brother's concubine now. When your second brother was crippled and wanted to break the engagement, Miss Zhong refused. This maid suggested having a firstborn illegitimate son first.","In respectable families, how could they tolerate their daughter not yet being married into the household while her future husband already has an illegitimate eldest son?","By then, even if Miss Zhong was unwilling to break it off, the Zhong family would.\"","\"So this naive fool believed it?\"","\"He believed it. In less than two months, this maid's belly was big. Two more months later, the one next to her with the almond eyes and peach-blossom cheeks also had a big belly.","But unfortunately, not a single child in their bellies belonged to your naive fool of a second brother.\"","\"This, this... Is there something wrong with the Yu family's feng shui? The eldest brother raises another man's child, the second brother also raises another man's child. Tell me, who else in this family is raising someone else's child!\"","\"Didn't your third uncle also raise someone else's child? That Yu Ningrou, if you hadn't appeared, would now be the legitimate Sixth Young Miss of the Yu family.\"","The Yu family: !!!","Could their family's feng shui really be problematic? One after another, it's truly infuriating! The first to bear the brunt was Third Uncle Yu Qinchun, who was glared at angrily by his father and two older brothers.","Yu Chongshan shook his head silently in his heart. Regardless of whether there was originally a problem with the ancestral graves, there definitely couldn't be a problem now.","Not only could there not be a problem, but they should also be emitting green smoke, blazing with great fire.","Otherwise, how could a little immortal lord have landed in their family?","\"Whose children are in those two women's bellies? Why did they betray my second brother?\"","\"The one in pink was originally planted by your uncle's political rival. The master she serves is that 'good brother' who instigated your second brother to go out and distribute porridge.","You don't think that without this maid blowing the pillow wind by your second brother's side, his good brother's words alone could persuade Yu Boming, do you?\"","\"Put that way, strictly speaking, it can't really be called betraying Yu Boming, just each serving their own master. So, the child in her belly, did that 'good brother' lend a helping hand?\"","\"It was him. Right on your second brother's bed. He was dead drunk and unconscious, while they, right in front of him, placed the green hat firmly on his head.","Pathetic!\"","Cough, cough, cough! This time, both Yue Fuguang and Yu Ningxuan choked on their tea, coughing uncontrollably.","\"What's wrong, what's wrong? Is the tea too hot?\" The Old Madam Yu quickly patted Yue Fuguang's back to help him catch his breath.","Yu Ningxuan's hand was slightly red; she was indeed scalded. She kept shaking her hand—it hurt so much!","Her flesh ached for her hand, and her heart ached for her brother's ordeal. But thinking of his subsequent series of outrageous actions, she also felt a frustrated disappointment in him.","\"The other maid, named Baoping, had already pledged her life to a guard in the mansion. They originally planned to buy her freedom after the New Year and get married, but then your drunken second brother took advantage of her.","Later, after his leg was broken, hearing the words of that maid named Xiliu about needing to have an illegitimate eldest son, this maid also conveniently consummated her relationship with the guard and got pregnant with his child. Your second brother became the backup plan.\"","\"This maid isn't my second brother's woman yet, right?\"","\"Not yet. If it weren't for coming home and not having time to drink, she would be by now.\"","\"Give my second brother some medicine to keep him honest for a while. Wait until this maid buys her freedom and leaves.\"","The Yu family listened and all glanced sympathetically at the still oblivious Yu Boming, who was diligently eating. Since they had returned, and the Zhong family girl was so loyal and righteous, the marriage between the two children should be put on the agenda.","As for that maid named Xiliu, since she had another master, they would just send her back intact. As for breaking ties with the other party? Their family really wasn't afraid of that now.","\"Master, do you know who your future second sister-in-law is?\"","\"Didn't you say her surname is Zhong?\"","\"Yes. Her name is Zhong Minghui. She's the cousin of that Zhong Mingyu whose marriage was stolen by Xie Zhiyao.\"","\"So it's their family. Hearing you say that, this Miss Zhong seems like a good girl. I can't help but feel it's a bit of a waste for her to marry someone like my second brother!\"","Yu Boming, who was eating lion's head meatballs, suddenly felt a chill down his back, sensing something bad was about to happen.","\"Someone like Yu Boming just lacks discipline. He should be thrown into the military camp to suffer a bit. Aren't you very familiar with Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi? Why not send him to them for proper training?","If trained well, you might be able to use him in the future if you ever want to raise an army for fun.\"","Yue Fuguang stroked his chin, seriously considering whether the system's suggestion was feasible. Although Yu Boming seemed a bit fragile, according to grandmother, all the Yu men have trained. It truly is a world with ancient martial arts heritage—even civil officials can wield swords.","However, Yu Chongshan and his sons were very moved by the artifact's suggestion. They themselves couldn't bear to be too harsh when disciplining their own descendants, so sending them to others for discipline might be better."]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143: What Kind of Flower is Cotton","paragraphs":["With his granddaughter's reputation at stake, both Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi would take diligent care, and there was no worry about the child's life being endangered.","\"I think it's a good plan. After the New Year, we'll send him to keep Zheng the Madman company.\"","Then, Yue Fuguang said to Yu Chongshan and Yu Shuchun with a smile, \"Grandfather, Second Uncle, my overseas friend previously sent me a travelogue. It mentions a foreign method for training soldiers, which I find quite novel.","Grandfather, what do you think about giving the book to Lord Huo and the others in the Ministry of War to study? Perhaps by learning from it, we could train a powerful army for Dayan.\"","Yu Chongshan immediately beamed, \"There's such a book? Then it certainly should be shown to Lord Huo and the Ministry of War. If it's useful, it will be Fuguang's merit.","You haven't attended court in the past few days, so you might not know. His Majesty, now that the national treasury has some savings, is planning to establish a new army.","If your method is useful, that would be excellent!\"","\"His Majesty is establishing a new army?\" Yue Fuguang hadn't expected Emperor Mingxi to act so swiftly. It seemed he had the funds and couldn't even wait until after the New Year to start preparations.","\"Lord Wei uncovered several corrupt officials this year, filling the national treasury considerably. Not only have the arrears for various departments been repaid, but there's also a significant surplus. That's why the court has the silver to build a new army.\"","As he spoke, he also took out a box from his robe, saying, \"This is the deed for the land you won. Your grandfather has taken care of everything for you.\"","Yue Fuguang was surprised at how quickly Dayan had acted. \"Our deed... will those families acknowledge it?\"","Yu Chongshan said with a laugh, \"Isn't there still the wager? Keep it all together. If they dare not acknowledge it? Then let the whole world see their untrustworthy faces.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. As long as there was no follow-up trouble, it was fine. She had the least patience for such matters.","\"Grandfather, please also help me find a few people knowledgeable in agriculture. I want to plant something new on this land.\"","\"Good, your grandfather will find them for you, ensuring it won't delay your spring planting. Regarding those farming tool drawings you provided earlier, I've also spoken with Minister Lu. They'll make a batch for you first.\"","Yu Zhongchun also added, \"Fuguang, what do you want to plant on that land? Do you need your father to send a steward to help oversee it?\"","Yue Fuguang quickly nodded. \"Yes, please. Father, remember to find a capable steward. I want to plant cotton there. My friend said they would send me a batch of cotton seeds in spring. That place seems quite suitable for growing such a crop.\"","This was the benefit of relying on family! She only had to make the request, and each family member contributed a little to get things done for her. She hardly needed to worry about finding people to handle the tasks. Her grandfather had even thought of the farming tools for her.","\"What kind of flower is cotton? Does your grandfather need to find you a gardener?\"","\"Uh, Grandfather, to be precise, cotton is not a flower.\"","She mysteriously leaned closer to the old man and said, \"Cotton isn't for eating. It's a crop that, like silk thread or hemp, can be woven into cloth, and also like reed catkins or fur, can be used to stuff clothing for warmth.","Cloth woven from cotton is more durable than silk, softer than hemp clothing. Stuffed into clothes like fur or reed catkins, it provides excellent warmth in winter, and it's much cheaper than fur, so even common people can afford it.\"","As for cotton's other uses, she wouldn't mention them for now. These points alone were enough to earn the high regard of Emperor Mingxi and his ministers. She could just sit back and wait to collect her points.","Sure enough, upon hearing this, the eyes of the Yu family men lit up. Yu Zhongchun said, \"Fuguang, can this thing only be grown on your land?","That place is near the border of three states, it's not safe. This thing sounds so precious, your father feels it's unsafe to keep it there.\"","Yu Chongshan also nodded. \"What your father says is right. This thing is a boon for Dayan, or rather, for all under heaven. We must be cautious.\"","\"It can be grown elsewhere, but the climate there should produce better quality.\" Ajiang's long-staple cotton was one of Xia Country's finest cottons.","\"I see.\" Yu Chongshan frowned. \"No, since Fuguang wants to plant it there, then we'll plant it there. I will petition His Majesty to have the border garrison send a detachment to station nearby and guard this life-saving cotton.\"","Yue Fuguang chuckled inwardly. Her grandfather was truly a good grandfather, following her script perfectly. She then said, \"Grandfather, when you go to speak with His Majesty, tell him that once the new army is trained, they can be stationed there for training and guard my land. I'll cover three-tenths of their military expenses.\"","If they use my silver, they'll have to heed my deployments. That place won't just grow cotton. It wouldn't be too much for the army to do some garrison farming or land reclamation, right?","It might not achieve complete self-sufficiency, but it could save a portion of the grain supply.","When she said she would bear three-tenths of the military expenses, apart from Yu's Second Aunt, the rest of the family didn't react too strongly.","This month alone, the Crown Prince had brought over two hundred thousand taels of silver to Fuguang, all from the dividends on glass purchases by the various foreign envoys.","And that didn't even include future pre-orders. She could afford this. If she were really short on cash, wasn't the family still here?","The old man stood tall and firm because he had savings. Hmm... more than His Majesty used to have!","Yu Shuchun chimed in as well, \"Isn't Fuguang planning to present the new military training methods to the Ministry of War? Let your second brother go along to learn them. Once he's mastered them, he can be sent to oversee your land for you.\"","Yue Fuguang silently gave her second uncle points for his quick thinking, though she still wore a hesitant expression. \"But second brother isn't that young anymore. Shouldn't he stay home and prepare for marriage?\"","Yu Shuchun, the biological father, waved a hand dismissively. \"Your eldest brother's marriage hasn't even been settled yet. How can a younger brother jump ahead of his elder brother to marry first? That would be most improper.\"","Yu's Second Aunt couldn't bear the thought of her only son suffering hardships in the army and was about to plead for him, but before she could speak, her husband cut her off. \"My dear, a doting mother ruins a son. Boming is no longer a child, yet he's less steady than his third and fourth brothers, not to mention his poor scholarly achievements. If we don't send him to the army, do you want your son to remain a commoner with no official rank his whole life?\"","Although their family could secure a minor clerk position for their son when he came of age, with a sister like Fuguang, if his own son turned out too useless, wouldn't it be a waste of this golden opportunity others could only dream of?","Yu Boming, who had already eaten his fill, was so startled by his father's words that he let out a hiccup.","He had been home for less than a day. Just look at this table full of stir-fried dishes! Was his good life, which he hadn't even enjoyed for a single day, ending so abruptly?","\"Father, I... I think I can study. Study at home.\" And eat at home!","\"I don't care what you think; I care what I think!\" Yu Shuchun glared. \"Your old man thinks you need military training, so you're going. Who's going to keep an eye on your sister's land if not our own family?\"","He then pointed at the dishes on the table. \"All these were thought up by your sister. As an elder brother who's enjoyed so many of your sister's good creations, shouldn't you strive even harder?\"","It was only proper to train well and work hard for his sister. They were all one family; his son couldn't be the only one dragging his feet.","Yue Fuguang maintained a calm facade, but inwardly she was extremely embarrassed. This whole table of food was paid for by her grandparents' silver—she herself was still living off their generosity!","But seeing everyone at the table nodding in agreement, she... she chose to remain silent.","Seizing the opportunity, the Old Madame Yu said, \"Since Second Son is sending the second boy to the army, he won't be spending many days at the estate in the coming years. The people in his courtyard should also be sorted out. Just keep a few for cleaning and watching the place.\""]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144: The Four Great Cases","paragraphs":["Then, addressing Yu's Second Aunt, she said, \"Second daughter-in-law, take a look around the courtyard. Those servants who have reached the right age should be sent out to be married off. Don't delay the good years of those girls.\"","Yue Fuguang: The older ginger is indeed spicier. To have found such a good excuse to clear people out so quickly—I have to hand it to her.","\"Mother, the people in Boming's quarters are all ones he's accustomed to, this...\" Before Yu's Second Aunt could finish, Yu's Second Uncle interjected, \"Wife, listen to Mother. His courtyard only needs to keep a few young servants.\"","Yue Fuguang glanced behind Yu Boming. Xiliu's face was somewhat pale, while a hint of joy was concealed on Baoping's face.","Time flew by. In less than half a month, it would be the New Year. Here, Yue Fuguang was curled up in a sofa-like armchair that Eunuch Qian had arranged for her, sleeping in a daze.","It really was good to have Eunuch Qian back. Not only could Emperor Mingxi not do without him, but even Yue Fuguang felt that Eunuch Qian served her more attentively, managing to handle things exactly as she wished.","When he had been absent some days before, she truly hadn't been used to it.","Just as she thought of this, the voice of Minister of Justice Cai Xian reached her ears. \"Your Majesty, reports have arrived from Bingzhou, Liangzhou, Yizhou, and Jiaozhou in the past two days.","Five days ago, the local prominent families—the Zhou, Fan, Zhao, and Bai families—colluded with foreign tribes, disguising them as bandits to enter our borders and plunder grain and other goods.","This has caused significant loss of property and lives. According to the reports, the chief culprits from each family have now been captured. How to deal with the others awaits Your Majesty's instruction.\"","[Eh? According to records, weren't these families' operations extremely meticulous? How were they discovered so quickly? And 'capturing the chief culprits'—doesn't that mean the family heads like Bai Yu's father?","Logically, aside from Fan Shiping, these people all lived safely until the fall of the Dayan Dynasty.]","\"These families are all far from me. It can't be the butterfly effect from my actions. Something unknown to us must have happened here.\"","You Mingmin also stepped forward to report, \"Your Majesty, the men sent to Jiaozhou to find Bai Yu have sent word. Bai Yu has indeed returned to the Bai family, but they did not find the Beili man, Chonghua, at the Bai residence.","They suspect Chonghua may have been hidden somewhere by Bai Yu. They are still searching secretly.","Therefore, I request permission to personally interrogate Bai Yu about Chonghua's whereabouts when the Bai family members are escorted to the capital, so as to give an account to the Third Prince of Beili.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded and said, \"Minister You's proposal is approved.\"","After a moment's thought, he said to Cai Xian, \"Minister Cai, coordinate with the Ministry of War to dispatch a team to each of the four provinces, responsible for escorting all family members of the four families to the capital for trial.\"","A glint of gold flashed in his eyes. \"Minister Dong and Lord Wang, send personnel to accompany them. Inventory and seal sixty percent of the four families' assets and property for transport to the capital. The remaining forty percent is to be used for disaster relief and compensating the people.","Lord Wang, focus on clarifying the farmlands and lands of the four families. Return any seized properties to their original owners. Organize and register the rest for the court to take over.\"","He said with a serious expression, \"Ensure this is completed before the spring plowing. Do not miss the farming season.\"","The several officials responded in unison, \"Yes, we respectfully obey Your Majesty's decree.\"","[Master, the emperor has suddenly gained so much land. Do we have enough seeds? He previously said he would soon have a large amount of land coming in. Could he have been referring to the lands of these four families?]","\"If so, does that mean Emperor Mingxi had long been aware of these families' schemes, just waiting for them to fall into their own trap?\"","[Indeed, since when has this emperor become so clever? Normally, he would have gone to his grave without knowing the truth.]","Emperor Mingxi: How did I know? Isn't it because of you, the loudspeaker, blabbering all day long!","\"According to what you said, these families hold a considerable amount of land. We don't have that many seeds. To plant all of it, we'd have to wait until the year after next.\"","[The year after next? Then the people of Dayan are quite fortunate. They can still plant two more seasons of crops before the famine arrives. If they tend to them well, perhaps fewer people will die when the time comes.]","The hearts of the Dayan emperor and his ministers were shaken. What famine? Where is there a famine? Could you please speak clearly!","They were about to obtain high-yield seeds and now had vast tracts of land. Before they could even rejoice, a famine was dropped on them.","No wonder the original Dayan perished. If all these events were to occur normally, this leaky ship called Dayan might truly sink.","[Master, every single event that has happened in Dayan recently has deviated from the original historical line. Now, they've even uprooted the four major traitorous families, some of the biggest malignant tumors.","If we change some of the later events as well, wouldn't Dayan possibly not fall so early?]","\"If the original successor still ascends the throne, it would only be a few more years of lingering on. What, are you disappointed that Dayan might not fall as expected?","Who was it that previously told me we should help the common people of this world?\"","[That... that's different. The changes in Dayan are too drastic. I just find it a bit strange.]","\"It is a bit strange. Although our appearance has become the biggest variable in this world, causing a chain reaction.","But for everything to change for the better... the Dayan dynasty is just too lucky!","It can't be that Dayan isn't meant to fall, that the Xie ancestors are protecting them, can it?\"","[Probably not. Although they are emperors, after death they still enter the underworld, not our Heavenly Realm. Only those with great virtue, after judgment by the King of Hell, have a chance to enter our Heavenly Realm.]","As these two ancestors speculated back and forth, the Dayan emperor and ministers dared not even breathe heavily. They thought, here it comes. They had anticipated that this time the commotion was too great and too far from the capital.","After the fate of the four major families deviated from the historical track, these two would surely become suspicious. Fortunately, they had made complete preparations.","If only these two ancestors could clarify which prince ultimately succeeds to the throne!","\"So, what do you think we should do? Setting aside other matters, whether Dayan improves or worsens doesn't really affect us much. It doesn't stop us from living well.\"","[Aren't you curious, Master? Why has history deviated so much? Look at this court. Many here have short-lived appearances, like Xie Zhiyan, Wei Ping, Wu Yong, Feng Tang, and so on.","Or those destined for miserable old age, like Wu Yuanjing, Cai Xian, Gu Yutong, Huo Ying, and so on.","It seems these people's fates are slowly beginning to improve with Master's appearance. Those destined for short lives no longer are, and those with bleak late years might still be saved.]","Those whose names were called: In their hearts, they silently raised three sticks of incense and bowed solemnly towards Yue Fuguang. They would have the women in their households secretly set up a longevity tablet for the Junior Mentor upon returning home, with three sticks of incense daily.","Yue Fuguang: Is it possible that I don't wish to live forever among you?","Those whose names were not called felt somewhat panicked. Were they included in that 'and so on'? They just didn't know if they were destined for short lives or miserable old age!","This won't do. Upon returning, they must set up longevity tablets for these two, with three sticks of incense daily. Otherwise, their hearts would feel unsettled!","\"Who might still be saved?\"","[If Wu Yong doesn't die young, Wu Yuanjing won't have a miserable old age.","Cai Xian... Wasn't it Cai Xian who reported on the four families? He must know a lot of inside information.","Master, why not go probe him for information? His youngest son will have his leg broken at the Drunken Red Pavilion tonight. You could use the opportunity to warn him as a way to ask him about the four families' affairs.]"]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145: Vegetable Pancakes and Troublemakers","paragraphs":["Cai Xian: That little brat Cai Bing actually learned to visit brothels and got his leg broken! He's really shaming me.","\"Is it like my second brother's case, where it was completely broken beyond healing?\"","[Yes, just like Yu Boming's situation. Cai Xian's son was lured into going to the brothel for fun. He wanted to play the hero saving a beauty, fell into someone's trap, and that's how his leg got broken.]","\"He didn't get the same script as my second brother, did he? Ended up raising someone else's child later?\"","Yu Shuchun, who had just come to attend the court assembly, closed his eyes. Great, now a third of his colleagues here know that not only was his son's leg broken, but he was also cuckolded and raised another man's child!","Yu Zhongchun: Second brother, calm down, calm down. Didn't the matter about my Qingyu also become known to all our colleagues? In a few days, there will be more gossip, and who will remember this?","Cai Xian narrowed his phoenix eyes slightly, scanning his colleagues almost imperceptibly. Who wanted to harm his son?","That kid shouldn't have offended anyone that much. Most likely, they were coming for him!","[You mean Cai Bing? He didn't raise someone else's child because he passed away within two years. That's why the Cai family and the Huo family became mortal enemies.]","\"Cai Bing (Vegetable Pancake)? Not as good as Roubing (Meat Pancake)!\"","[That kid's nickname is indeed 'Vegetable Pancake'. The Cai family also has a 'Meat Pancake', a 'Jianbing', and a 'Spring Pancake'.]","\"Does Minister Cai really like eating all kinds of pancakes? You mentioned the Huo family becoming mortal enemies, which Huo family is that? Huo Ying's family?\"","Cai Xian: What's wrong with liking pancakes? Doesn't anyone think pancakes are tastier than steamed buns or rice?","[Master is so clever, it's indeed Huo Ying's family. It's almost New Year's, and the Imperial College, schools, and academies are all on holiday.","So these young masters, like birds freed from their cages, organized a gathering tonight at the Drunken Red Pavilion. With so many of them gathered, how could nothing happen?","First, they boasted about themselves. When that wasn't enough, they boasted about whose father was more powerful. Incited by someone with an agenda, Minister Cai versus Minister Huo ended in a draw!","Both were dissatisfied. Then, a young courtesan's first night came up for auction. 'Vegetable Pancake' and 'Troublemaker'—oh, that's Huo Ying's son, Huo Sui—both took a fancy to the girl.","Both wanted to win the bid to give her a 'home', each claiming to be the hero saving her from being ruined by the other!]","Huo Ying: That fool Huo Sui! After reading military strategy books with me for so long, he still couldn't see it was a chain of schemes?","Cai Xian: 'Vegetable Pancake' truly lives up to his name, not only falling for a chain of schemes but finally tripping over a beauty trap. If you're weak, practice more. Trying to play the hero saving a beauty? You need to be a hero first!","The two Ministers exchanged a glance across the room, both feeling the mastermind behind this was targeting them.","\"So who won the beauty in the end?\"","[Neither of them did. This courtesan is the famous 'Drunken Rakshasa' from the martial world. For men like them, she was just toying with them. Their fathers might have had a real chance!]","Cai Xian, Huo Ying: Drunken Rakshasa? Hard pass!","\"A squabble over a courtesan even involved someone from the martial world? The person behind this is quite powerful!\"","[Quite powerful indeed. Before their bidding war was even over, somehow a fight broke out. Someone mixed in the crowd struck 'Vegetable Pancake's' leg, causing a comminuted fracture. With the current medical conditions, he could only wait to become disabled.","Within two years, the young man died of depression. The Cai and Huo families became sworn enemies.","At court, they constantly set traps for each other. Later, Huo Sui went out once, his horse spooked, he fell off, and died within two days.","Huo Ying was sure it was the Cai family's doing because someone saw Cai's 'Meat Pancake'—'Vegetable Pancake's' older brother—having contact with 'Troublemaker's' coachman.","After 'Troublemaker' died, the coachman got drunk that very night and drowned in a lotus pond! The Cai and Huo families' mutual attacks weakened them both, and then someone with an agenda took advantage of the situation.]","\"The person behind this seems to love using schemes, playing dirty, a real villain!\"","[Exactly! There are many guesses about this person's identity in the history books, but no one ever found out who he truly was!]","\"Little Pearl doesn't know either?\"","[I have some guesses, but it's not important. Who he is has nothing to do with us. Master, the most important thing now is to ask Cai Xian clearly about why the four great families were discovered ahead of time.]","Emperor Mingxi and the other court officials: It might have nothing to do with you two ancestors, but it has everything to do with us!","Who knows if this person only targeted Cai and Huo, or if he targeted us too? If we don't find him, we won't have peace of mind!","Gu Yutong: Out of the four named families, why was I left out? Am I that unnoticeable?","He desperately wanted to know, before the Great Yan perished and he was trampled to death by horses, how exactly did his later years become so miserable?","Did his three brats abandon their old father, or did they die young like the sons of the Wu, Cai, and Huo families?","Gu Yutong was almost frantic with anxiety, but the two ancestors just wouldn't bring up his case!","\"I'll go ask after the morning court session.\"","Hearing this, Cai Xian grew nervous again. He barely listened to the rest of the morning court, repeatedly drafting mental notes on how to respond to Junior Mentor Yue Fuguang's 'interrogation'.","Sure enough, as soon as Eunuch Qian announced the end of the court session, before Cai Xian could even deliberately linger to wait for Yue Fuguang, she took the initiative to walk over.","With a smiling face, looking 'kind and amiable', it made Cai Xian's eyelids twitch.","They respected, admired, and feared this person, mainly because her temperament was too hard to fathom, even more so than their Emperor's!","She had always been decent to them, and colleagues got along harmoniously. They ate the food prepared by the Junior Mentor and sent many gifts in return. This give-and-take relationship was fairly harmonious, right?","Yet, even so, from what they could tell, these two ancestors still hadn't fully decided to save Great Yan!","\"Minister Cai.\"","Cai Xian turned and bowed. \"Does the Junior Mentor have business with this official?\"","Yue Fuguang walked side by side with him out of the hall, saying, \"Nothing major, just curious about the matter of the four great families.","My second uncle used to serve in Yizhou. I heard from my grandfather that the Zhao family in Yizhou is very powerful. I imagine the other families are not much weaker.","To do something as treasonous as leading foreign tribes across the border to plunder, they must have operated very secretly. How did you manage to discover all four at once?\"","She looked at Cai Xian with full curiosity.","Cai Xian, the old fox, remained unflustered, keeping his amiable smile. \"That's a long story.","To make a long story short, it was because the people investigating Chonghua's disappearance case found it involved Bai Yu. They tracked the clues all the way to the Bai family in Jiaozhou.","At the Bai family, since they found no leads on Chonghua, the investigators didn't alert the Bai family for the time being, only investigating Bai Yu secretly.","This investigation revealed that Bai Yu was in frequent and close contact with people from the Zhao family in Jiaozhou, the Fan family in Liangzhou, and the Zhou family in Bingzhou.\"","\"These families are all great aristocratic clans, said to have complex marital ties. Isn't it normal for them to have dealings?\"","Cai Xian nodded. \"Indeed, my Ministry of Justice officials thought the same. But later they discovered these meetings were held in secluded places with hidden identities.","Bai Yu even met privately with people from Nanzhao several times.","Later, they split up to follow these individuals back to their respective clans. They discovered that those from these clans—whether the clan leaders themselves or their sons—had all been secretly meeting with people from Beili and Qiang in the west."]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146: Heaven's Feedback","paragraphs":["After hearing the detailed account, Yue Fuguang nodded. The root cause was still the investigation into Bai Yu and Zhong Hua, which triggered the subsequent chain reaction. This explanation she could reluctantly accept.","\"I've heard Minister Cai enjoys eating flatbreads?\"","Yue Fuguang smiled warmly, \"I usually enjoy them too, especially the flaky stuffed pastries. They're more delicious than vegetable or meat pies.\"","Cai Xianyi's interest was immediately piqued. Yue Fuguang then roughly described the method of making them. Well, her culinary skills weren't great, but in her past life, being wealthy, she never deprived her palate. She had eaten a lot and seen a lot.","Her hands couldn't do it, but her mind knew how!","Listening to Yue Fuguang's detailed description of the method, Cai Xianyi, with his years of flatbread-eating experience, knew this pastry must be exceptionally delicious.","He thanked her solemnly, \"This humble official thanks the Junior Mentor for imparting this secret recipe.\" He would have to ask his wife to send a token of gratitude to the Yu residence later.","Yue Fuguang waved her hand dismissively and brought up another matter. \"Minister Cai, I heard from my grandfather that the Imperial College and academies have recently gone on break, and the capital has suddenly become livelier. The idle young masters have been causing quite a bit of trouble. Does this fall under the Ministry of Justice's jurisdiction?\"","\"It falls under the Patrol Battalion, the City Patrol Censors, and Shen Kang's Imperial City Department. If they are short-handed, they may also borrow personnel from the Three Judicial Offices.\"","\"I see. These past few days, my second brother and several other brothers who just returned from the academy have been confined to the house by my grandfather. I heard Minister Cai also has sons around the same age as my brothers. You should keep a close eye on them.\"","Cai Xianyi immediately grew serious, bowing slightly. \"Has the Junior Mentor perceived something? I heard you studied geomancy and divination with a master at the Taoist temple. Could it be you can also foretell fortunes?\"","Yue Fuguang: Who's spreading rumors about me? When did I ever study geomancy? It's true my master forced me to memorize some texts, but geomancy? I don't know the first thing about it!","Could it be my master who said this? She's just trying to burnish her own reputation!","Thinking of her unique master, Yue Fuguang felt her master must have cultivated the Path of Carefree Freedom, as no worldly etiquette or rule could ever bind her.","She wondered if her master had received the New Year's gifts she sent to the temple.","Yue Fuguang shook her head, looking directly at Cai Xianyi. \"It's not divination; it's observation. I observe that your Children's Palace (facial feature) appears dim. Recently, one of your children may encounter blood-related misfortune. That's why I mentioned it, though it may not be accurate.\"","Yue Fuguang acted like an amateur charlatan, but it didn't diminish the effectiveness of her immortal aura.","Upon hearing this, Cai Xianyi performed a formal bow. \"This humble official thanks the Junior Mentor on behalf of my children for your warning.\"","He secretly resolved that, aside from the eldest, Meat Pie, who had official duties, the brothers Vegetable Pie and Pancake would not be allowed to leave the house these days.","As for his daughter, Spring Roll, if she wanted to go out, his wife could take her. With guards present, nothing should happen.","Watching the two figures walk away, Gu Yutong was hopping with anxiety behind them. What a perfect opportunity! He had originally intended to seize the moment while the Junior Mentor was reading Minister Cai's face to ask for a reading himself.","But before he could utter a word, he was pulled aside by his old rival, Zhao Zhifeng!","............","[Host, host, stop sleeping, we've struck it rich, struck it rich!]","Yue Fuguang had just eaten lunch and was feeling a bit carb-drowsy. She had only slept a short while before being rudely awakened by the system's clamor!","'System, if this time the points haven't exceeded fifty thousand, you can look forward to solitary confinement!'","System: As an incomplete system, why has the system space been optimized away, but the solitary confinement room is still reserved for it?","Who exactly is the Main God System targeting here?","07 immediately felt wronged. [Host, we've really struck it rich this time. The points for the Four Great Families mission have risen to seventy-eight thousand nine hundred. Combined with our previous savings, we're about to break one hundred thousand!]","Yue Fuguang sat up straight in bed. 'Really that much?'","[Look at the points board, it can't be fake. This mission has wide-reaching implications; points will continue to grow slowly later. The Four Great Families mission alone might break one hundred thousand. With the points, won't you be able to buy that storage ring?]","When the host bought things from the mall, the systems also got a commission. The virtue points it earned were all used to repair itself. It was a pity the host wasn't wealthy, which meant this system was even poorer!","'The storage ring is definitely a must-buy, but I won't be a sucker. Keep an eye out for me. The New Year is coming up. If the system isn't giving out red packets, shouldn't there be a discount sale?","Can you make a suggestion to your Main System? Since it's almost New Year, how about holding a discount sale to celebrate?'","She hadn't even filed a complaint about being bound to a defective system! The system space that should have been there was missing, forcing her to spend points on a storage ring. Who could she reason with about this?","The system thought it over and found it feasible. They were all officially registered systems, not like those wild systems without a Main System, surviving solely by exploiting their hosts.","'Also, System, I've noticed I've been getting particularly drowsy these past two days...'","[Host, when aren't you prone to drowsiness? You sleep through most of a morning court session, come back, eat, and sleep again. Didn't you say it was carb-drowsiness?]","'It's different. When I'm asleep, I feel very comfortable. Not physically comfortable, but... mentally? No, spiritually? Soul? Divine soul? Let's call it the divine soul.","My divine soul feels very comfortable, like soaking in warm water, all warm and cozy. When I'm awake, my mind is also clearer than before.","Do you know what the reason for this is?'","The system thought for a moment, rummaged through its data, and then said, [Host, this is likely you encountering feedback from this world's Heavenly Dao.]","'Heavenly Dao feedback? What has it fed back to me?'","[It should be Virtue Golden Light. Virtue Golden Light can nourish and strengthen your divine soul. Weren't you always talking about reforging a physical body?]","'Yes, reforging a physical body is my motivation for diligently completing tasks. Otherwise, living day in and day out wearing someone else's shell, am I still myself?'","[Your method of reforging a physical body isn't like reincarnation to obtain one, nor is it like the Water and Fire Spirit Tribes using lotus root powder to make a body and moving your soul in.","Your reforging involves using your own soul, cooperating with rare materials to slowly grow a human body bit by bit, based on the form of your soul, or rather, the form your soul desires.","The stronger your divine soul, the more, during the reforging, you can rely on soul power to achieve that ideal you want—what was it, 'white jade for bones, autumn water for spirit, stars for...']","'System, I know what I want, no need to repeat it. If there's nothing else, you may retire! I'm going back to sleep!'","Yue Fuguang lay back under the covers, cutting off the connection with the system instantly before it could even protest, falling asleep in one second.","System: Is this what it's like to not be in solitary confinement, but locked out of the system space instead?","Its host was too petty. Look at someone like Huaimin, he never blamed Master Dongpo! Could it be their bond was inferior to those two who were exiled?","The two clueless ones didn't know that as Yue Fuguang slept, her divine soul was bathing in a brilliant, golden radiance.","This golden light even showed signs of beginning to spill over."]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147: Golden Light Leaking Out","paragraphs":["In the evening, seeing that the young lady still hadn't woken up, Cuizhu couldn't help but enter, thinking to wake her so she could eat dinner before sleeping further.","What she saw then was a startling scene—her... her young lady's entire head was shimmering with a golden light, more radiant than the most precious gold jewelry she had ever seen.","Cuizhu was so frightened she fell to the floor. The commotion drew in Cuiyu, who was also startled, stumbling back a few steps and hitting the doorframe. Ignoring the pain, Cuiyu's mind was filled with the urgent need to report this to the masters.","She herself was too shaken to move, so she called for Qingzhu, telling her to hurry to the main courtyard to fetch the master, the mistress, the eldest master, and his wife.","\"Just... just say the sev... seventh young lady has had an incident.\"","She waved urgently at Qingzhu, signaling her to go quickly.","Cuiyu hadn't fully grasped the situation; saying the young lady had an 'incident' was disrespectful, but she couldn't worry about that now.","The fate of everyone in their quarters was tied to the young lady alone. If something happened to her, they would all be in trouble!","Qingzhu didn't know what had happened, but seeing Cuizhu, who had entered the young lady's room and not come out, and Cuiyu with her deathly pale face, Qingzhu's heart also began to pound with anxiety.","The unknown is the most terrifying. Her panic, combined with the slippery snowy path, caused her to stumble and fall several times on the way.","By the time she reached the main courtyard, she looked rather disheveled.","Before she could even speak, Yu Chongshan and the Old Mistress Yu immediately recognized Qingzhu as one of the four senior maids from their granddaughter's chambers.","Seeing Qingzhu's disheveled state, the elderly couple sensed something was wrong, their hands trembling so much that the chopsticks they held fell to the floor with a crisp clatter.","That sound struck Yu Chongshan's heart. He forced himself to stand up and asked across the dining table, \"Qingzhu, why are you here? Where is... where is Fuguang?\"","He wanted to ask if something had happened to his granddaughter, but the words stuck in his throat! He feared speaking them would be inauspicious!","\"Master, Old Mistress, Sister Cuiyu sent me to fetch you and the eldest master and his wife. She said the young lady... the young lady has had an incident!\"","Upon hearing this, the Old Mistress felt dizzy. A senior maid quickly supported her, preventing her from collapsing. \"What do you mean 'had an incident'? Explain clearly!\"","Qingzhu stammered; she didn't know either, she was just the messenger!","The old lady tried to stand twice but couldn't, finally managing to rise only with the support of the senior maid beside her.","Seeing that Qingzhu knew nothing, Yu Chongshan didn't waste time. He turned to his personal attendant and said, \"Go, fetch the eldest master.\"","\"Let's go... see our granddaughter.\" He patted his wife's hand, comforting her, \"We know who our granddaughter is. She... will be fine!\"","These words were as much to comfort his wife as himself.","The Old Mistress Yu was so shocked her legs went weak, and the path was slippery. In the end, a sturdy servant woman carried her on her back to the Bright Moon Pavilion.","The elderly couple, supporting each other, entered the inner chamber. As soon as they did, they saw the same sight that had stunned Cuizhu. Yu Chongshan immediately waved his hand, dismissing everyone present, including Cuizhu and Cuiyu, shooing out all non-essential personnel.","Knowing their granddaughter's origins, the two elders felt half their worries melt away upon seeing this scene. Now, besides shock, they had lost their earlier panic, though they were still somewhat unclear about the current situation.","That golden, radiant head was more dazzling than gold itself. Standing closer, they could even feel a profound comfort emanating from within their bodies.","The two quickly took two steps back. Without needing to be told, they knew this light was something good. They couldn't stand too close, lest they absorb it all and their granddaughter receive less?","They had only retreated two steps when they bumped into their eldest son, Yu Zhongchun, and his wife, Madam Zhang, who were rushing in frantically from outside.","\"Father, Mother, how is Fuguang?\" Yu Zhongchun asked anxiously before even seeing the situation inside.","Yu Chongshan shot him a glare. \"Keep your voice down, boy! Don't disturb my granddaughter!\"","As Yu Chongshan turned, he revealed Yue Fuguang lying unconscious on the bed.","\"This... this...\" The couple was so startled they retreated two steps, then quickly covered their mouths, remembering the old master's scolding.","Their golden, shimmering daughter shocked them immensely!","\"Father, what's happening to my daughter? Will she be alright?\" Yu Zhongchun wanted to move closer for a look.","\"Quiet! You'll be in trouble before she ever is!\"","Yu Chongshan lowered his voice and waved at the restless Yu Zhongchun. \"Go, both of you, walk up to Fuguang's bedside and carefully sense the feeling. Go quickly and come back quickly.\"","Yu Chongshan feared that he and his wife, being old, might have misperceived, hence he wanted his son and daughter-in-law to test it as well.","Yu Zhongchun and his wife didn't understand their father's meaning, but they obediently complied.","The closer they got to Yue Fuguang on the bed, the more comfortable their bodies felt...","Sitting in the main hall of the Bright Moon Pavilion, the four were momentarily silent. Finally, Yu Zhongchun couldn't help but ask, \"Father, do you think this state means something good for Fuguang?\"","\"Yes, Father,\" Madam Zhang chimed in. \"That golden light felt extremely soothing on us. Our Fuguang will be fine. She's not a divine...\" Before she could finish, both father and son stopped her, making shushing gestures.","Little did they know, the mysterious artifact they cautiously guarded against was currently confined, unaware of everything.","\"Your wife is right,\" the Old Mistress said, leaning close to her daughter-in-law. Hearing Madam Zhang's words made her feel even more at ease. \"Fuguang will be fine. She is... cultivating. The golden light is a good sign.\"","However, Yu Chongshan, who had just calmed down, wasn't entirely pleased. He glanced outside, saw everyone was over ten meters away, then lowered his voice to a whisper. \"Given Fuguang's condition, should we report it to His Majesty?\"","Yu Zhongchun initially wanted to say no, but then he remembered the commotion they had caused coming over. By now, probably every master in the mansion knew, and his younger brothers would surely come as well.","It would be even more impossible to hide it from His Majesty, who kept a close watch on their family, and their colleagues.","Sure enough, before they could say more, Yu Shuchun and his wife, followed by Yu Qinchun and Yu Mochun with their wives, entered one after another.","As soon as they saw the four, they eagerly asked about Yue Fuguang's condition. Their father's personal attendant was guarding the courtyard gate, only allowing the adults in; the younger generation were all held back outside.","Seeing this array, the brothers felt very anxious. The Yu family's precious treasure must not have even the slightest mishap!","Yu Chongshan didn't explain much, simply waving for them to take a glance inside from the bedroom doorway.","After looking, their expressions were indeed a sight to behold, especially that of the uninformed Second Madam Yu, who almost cried out in shock.","However, before she could speak, Yu Shuchun promptly covered her mouth and pulled her to the main hall.","Yu Chongshan glanced at him and said, \"Second daughter-in-law, not a single word of what you saw today is to be revealed. The same goes for everyone else, otherwise, this family will have no place for her!\"","After this warning, he said to Yu Shuchun, \"When you return to your own courtyard, tell your wife what can be said.\" He estimated that with the mysterious restrictions in place, not much could be said anyway.","Since even these few had been alarmed and come, Yu Chongshan sighed inwardly. It seemed they couldn't keep it from His Majesty either.","He slowly stood up. \"Your mother and eldest sister-in-law will stay here. The rest of you may return for now.\"","Then, to Yu Zhongchun, he said, \"Eldest, come with your father to the palace to see His Majesty.\""]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148: Accidental Click","paragraphs":["Yu Shuchun saw that his father and elder brother were about to leave and quickly said, \"Father, we're here with mother and sister-in-law, so we can look after each other. Waiting here is more reassuring than going back to wait.\"","As long as Yue Fuguang didn't wake up, how could they possibly feel at ease?","Yu Chongshan was more inclined to believe the golden light was caused by his granddaughter's divine power leaking out while she was asleep. Perhaps it had happened before, and they just hadn't noticed.","As for why they didn't try to wake her, what if, as his wife said, their granddaughter was cultivating?","...","\"Such a thing has happened?\" Emperor Mingxi was also greatly astonished by the words of the father and son.","It was already the hour for the palace gates to be locked. He had just been about to visit the inner palace when a eunuch reported that Minister Yu and his son were requesting an audience.","If it were anyone else, he might have refused, but the Yu family father and son were the kind of people he absolutely had to see, even if they came in the middle of the night.","Sure enough, as soon as they entered, they told him of such a miraculous event.","He knew Yue Fuguang was an immortal lord descended to the mortal realm, but witnessing proof with one's own eyes was entirely different.","Emperor Mingxi didn't say much, only instructing Qian Gui to send someone to notify Taoist Master Xuanmingzi, before leading the Yu family father and son out of the hall.","\"Your Majesty, Your Majesty, your cloak! It's cold outside!\"","Qian Gui trotted after the emperor to help him put on more layers.","Emperor Mingxi and Taoist Master Xuanmingzi arrived at the Moonlight Pavilion almost simultaneously. Witnessing the miracle together, both were deeply shocked.","Emperor Mingxi also experienced the physical comfort Yu Chongshan had described, a warmth spreading from within while bathed in the golden light.","He had originally wanted to stand there a while longer, to soak up a bit more of the golden light, but under the blatantly obvious stares of the Yu family members, he gave a light cough and led everyone out.","Following behind, Yu Chongshan's lips curved into a barely perceptible smile. He had called the whole family to stand inside and stare at the Emperor precisely so that, even with the thickest skin, His Majesty would feel too embarrassed to freeload off his granddaughter's golden light for too long.","Emperor Mingxi sat in the master's seat in the main hall, looking at the assembled group. \"What happened today ends with us here.","After all, Yue Fuguang stayed at the Taoist temple for three years. Perhaps she has some... spiritual aptitude. Today's event might very well be a breakthrough in her cultivation!\"","Emperor Mingxi racked his brains for a reason, just like Yu Chongshan, both aiming to guard against that 'Artifact Lord'!","\"It is Great Yan's fortune to have Yue Fuguang. However, if her extraordinary nature becomes known to the surrounding countries, her uniqueness would become a hidden danger, posing a threat to her safety.\"","Emperor Mingxi's words were less for the ears of those present and more for the Artifact Lord himself. The little immortal lord might be in deep sleep, but who knew if that Artifact Lord was also slumbering?","Their words and actions must not reveal any clues.","System: This old geezer is so crafty. Pity it's locked in the system space, unable to watch Emperor Mingxi perform live.","Yue Fuguang had slept soundly through the night. As soon as she sat up, her stomach emitted a loud series of gurgles and rumbles. Just... how long had she been hungry for her stomach to make such a racket!","\"Fuguang, you're awake?\" Hearing the commotion of the child's stomach growling, Old Madam Yu and Madam Zhang entered with joyful expressions, lifting the curtain.","\"Grandmother, Mother, why are you here?\" Yue Fuguang was still a bit groggy.","\"You've been asleep for a full day and night. Your grandmother and I were worried sick,\" Madam Zhang said while helping her put on clothes and tidy her hair.","\"If you hadn't woken up soon, your grandfather and father were about to summon a physician to examine you.\"","Old Madam Yu asked gently, \"Hungry, aren't you? The food has been kept warm on the stove. You can eat as soon as you're up.\"","She then instructed Cuiyu, \"Go inform the Master and the Young Master that the young lady has woken up from her sleep, so they can set their minds at ease.\"","Old Madam Yu emphasized the words \"woken up from her sleep\" precisely to prevent her granddaughter and outsiders from thinking too much into it.","Yue Fuguang felt somewhat embarrassed. She tapped on the system, System, why did I sleep for so long? You didn't even wake me.","The system, infuriated by her blaming the victim, puffed its entire spherical form up a size. Host, I would have loved to wake you, but you didn't give me the chance, did you? You locked me in the system space and cut off the connection to the outside world. What was that about?","Ah? Cut off the connection? I... I'm sorry, my hand slipped, a misoperation, a misoperation!","Don't you know how dangerous that is? If someone launched a sneak attack, I couldn't protect you in time, and you could very well be done for!","You're right, it's all my fault, I...","Host, you... what did you do? Why is our connection even tighter now? Your soul... your soul seems to have strengthened significantly! And it was shimmering with a faint golden light, so pretty!","However, the system was currently very displeased and didn't plan to compliment her, so Yue Fuguang missed the chance to learn about this.","I don't know!~ I just slept, and then it was like this.","It should be the result of your soul being nourished by the merit golden light.","The system watched with intense envy. As a merit system now, it had a natural craving for merit golden light.","Especially as a system that had been formatted, it seemed to need merit even more to compensate for its defects.","It needed to urge the host to spend quickly; otherwise, the points allocated to it upon task completion still wouldn't be enough for its own repairs.","Hey, host, the Main System has replied. There's a limited-time discount sale tonight at eight.","Yue Fuguang's heart leapt with joy, and her eating pace quickened. Old Madam Yu and Madam Zhang kept saying \"slow down, slow down, don't choke,\" while continuously adding food to her bowl.","System, I didn't expect you to be this capable! You just mentioned it to the Main System, and they gave us a discount!","If it weren't a system, and not a carbon-based lifeform that reproduced sexually, she would have suspected her system might have some familial relationship with the Main System, like being an illegitimate child or something.","The system instantly puffed up its non-existent tail. Now you know my power. You mustn't cut the connection on me again. Seeing as we have hope of completing this task, you can't drop the ball.","Don't worry, don't worry. The hand-slipping thing definitely won't happen a second time.","Quick, look at the discount items page. See what you want to buy and put it in the shopping cart first. When the sale starts, we'll grab it!","Are there many people competing with us for these? She thought it was specially opened for the two of them. Seems she overthought it!","Naturally. But it's quite strange. Usually, discounts are announced several days in advance. This time, less than a day passed from the notification to the start of the event.","Yue Fuguang didn't dwell on it. Any discount was good for her.","She browsed and picked, the first thing she looked for being storage rings. Were this many styles all on discount?","Each one was very beautiful. Yue Fuguang was dazzled by the choices. In the end, she selected a gold ring shaped like intertwined vines, topped with a sky-blue, semi-transparent Void Stone.","The storage ring had an internal space of five hundred cubic meters, and the band was engraved with a minor defensive array.","Original price: 120,000 merit points. Discounted price: 12,000. Yue Fuguang instantly felt she had scored a great deal.","As for the one she had initially eyed, originally priced at 100,000 and discounted to 10,000—now that she had a better option, she decisively abandoned it.","System, is this the lowest discount?","Yes, the lowest is one-tenth of the original price. It can't go any lower. Host, you can buy everything you usually need. It's cheaper than usual, right? The system continued to tempt her into spending."]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149: Gathering, Mahjong","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang thought about it and agreed. She definitely needed to stock up on some face-slapping, show-off-worthy magical tools. Even if this world didn't need them, the next one might. With such a low discount, who knows how long she'd have to wait for the next one.","Buying now meant pure profit.","All sorts of elixirs? Buy! Picking and choosing, she started with at least one bottle of each type. Nine pills per bottle, for less than the usual price of two.","All sorts of talismans? Buy! All sorts of weapons? Buy!","Snacks, seeds? Buy!","Especially those three types of high-yield seeds and cotton seeds, along with farming tools? Buy!","Yue Fuguang shopped while devouring her meal, and before she knew it, she was stuffed.","\"System, get me a digestion tablet.\"","Speaking of digestion tablets, she added a few more bottles of slimming pills to her cart.","With her current appetite, she definitely wouldn't eat less when she grew up. Eating too much and growing into a fatty wasn't ideal. A fat immortal lord... just felt like it would lack a bit of that ethereal aura, right?","She had just finished eating when Yu Chongshan led Yu Zhongchun, Yu Shuchun, and a few other brothers over.","Seeing their granddaughter's rosy complexion, looking even better than yesterday, especially her bright, sparkling eyes like stars in the sky, they understood the situation perfectly!","\"Grandfather, Father, Uncles, why are you off duty so early?\" Did the whole family collectively skip work?","\"We heard you were awake, so we left early to come see you.\"","Yue Fuguang smiled and said, \"I've worried Grandfather, Grandmother, Father, Mother, Uncles, and Aunts. I was just exhausted yesterday and accidentally overslept.\"","Her bright eyes rolled mischievously as she seized the opportunity. \"Grandfather, it's getting colder and colder outside. The government offices will be sealed for the New Year in just over ten days. Do you think I could ask His Majesty if I could attend the morning court every other day instead?\"","Yu Chongshan looked at his granddaughter's hopeful, smiling face and couldn't bring himself to refuse. He only said, \"It is indeed getting colder day by day. I will bring it up with His Majesty tomorrow. You can wait until after the New Year, when spring arrives, to resume normal court attendance.\"","\"Thank you, Grandfather.\" Yue Fuguang was inwardly delighted. Finally, a work-one-day, rest-one-day schedule! Even 'immortals' don't want to go to work!","Just as she finished speaking, another group of people came bustling in. Yue Fuguang looked up to see all the family's brothers and sisters had gathered.","Fortunately, the main hall of her Bright Moon Pavilion was quite large. Even with this whole big family gathered, it didn't feel crowded.","Yue Fuguang contributed her toys: Ludo, Gomoku, playing cards, and mahjong. The old, middle-aged, and young generations split into three groups. Led by Yu Chongshan, who listened to Yue Fuguang's explanation of the rules, he and his sons enthusiastically started a game of mahjong.","Old Madam Yu and her daughters-in-law just happened to gather around a table to play cards.","The younger generation played Ludo and Gomoku.","The charm of these national pastimes was powerful. The Yu father and sons played mahjong all afternoon. When it was time to eat, they were still reluctant to stop, saying they'd continue after the meal, with some eagerly awaiting a chance to turn the tables.","On the mahjong table, there is no distinction between father and son. Yu Chongshan had lost quite a bit of silver to his sons that afternoon and vowed to win it back today.","Old Man Yu, truly a shrewd hand at managing family finances, quickly saw the market potential of mahjong from his own and his family's addiction. Especially with the New Year approaching and more leisure time, mahjong was sure to be a huge hit.","\"Fuguang, can our family make these and sell them?\"","\"Of course. And the playing cards, Gomoku, Ludo—all of these can be made and sold in our family's shops.\"","\"Good. Then your grandfather will benefit from your idea. When we make money, we'll split it fifty-fifty.\"","The old man's eyes flashed with golden light, already calculating making mahjong sets from different materials, especially jade. Those could be sold for a very high price.","\"That's too much. I just provided the idea. Give me thirty percent.\" Technical investment shares, doing nothing but lying back waiting for dividends. Judging by her grandfather's demeanor, he was planning a big venture. Thirty percent would still net her a lot of money.","Yu Chongshan shook his head. \"Thirty percent is too little. Let's make it forty percent.\"","He would make up the remaining ten percent for his granddaughter from other sources later.","As the New Year approached, the exchange of gifts between families began. On her day off from court, Yue Fuguang followed her mother, Madam Zhang, for half a day and felt utterly exhausted.","Physically tired, but mentally even more so. There were rules for every family's seasonal gifts: what to send, what others sent you, how to reciprocate, all while considering closeness of relations and the official ranks of the men in each household.","Her mother, Madam Zhang, handled it all with practiced ease. Yue Fuguang watched, her head spinning. She really wasn't cut out for this. Relying on her parents once again proved to be the right choice.","\"System, someone like my mother, in modern times, would definitely be a successful person, a high-ranking official or CEO or something.\"","[Indeed. She not only manages affairs within the residence but also oversees the shops and manors outside. No wonder the ancients were so careful when selecting the eldest daughter-in-law.","This isn't just picking a wife; it's picking a manager, and one with high emotional intelligence and business acumen at that.]","\"Ancient women had it tough. After marrying into a family, they not only needed management skills but also had to bear sons. No matter how capable you were here, if you couldn't bear a son, it was all for nothing.","Saying this makes me miss modern times even more.\"","[Then let's try to get a modern mission next time.]","\"We can choose missions?\" Yue Fuguang was pleasantly surprised.","In ancient times, even if she pretended to be a deity, her quality of life couldn't surpass this era by too much. Take travel, for instance—she couldn't exactly ride in a car, could she?","Since she didn't want to work but wanted positive points, she had to keep her 'hidden' identity. These futuristic flying or running things weren't suitable to bring out for now.","Maybe when she grew up and wanted to travel, she could think about it...","Soon, Yue Fuguang discovered a problem. Some families' New Year gifts to the Yu residence included a separate portion specifically for her.","Yue Fuguang watched as boxes were carried into her storeroom and felt utterly at a loss. She had no idea how to handle reciprocal gifts!","Madam Zhang smiled at her dumbfounded daughter. \"Don't worry, my child. I've prepared all the reciprocal gifts for you.\"","Yue Fuguang's expression changed in an instant. \"Thank you, Mother. I still have vegetables in my hothouse. How about adding some vegetables to each family's return gift? It can be considered my personal thought.\"","She believed these families would appreciate seeing this.","Reality proved her right. After that, even more gifts came her way, and even... the Crown Prince's got mixed in?","Hold on, nominally you're the ruler, we are your subjects. Since when does the ruler send seasonal gifts to subjects? The items bestowed by the royal family during the New Year don't count.","This was clearly aimed at her vegetable hothouse!","...","After resting for two days, Yue Fuguang resumed her court attendance clock-ins.","Well-rested, Yue Fuguang once again started munching on her meat pie. Instantly, the entire hall was filled with a rich, savory aroma.","The minister who was still presenting matters paused briefly, swallowed, and then continued, \"Your Majesty, I impeach...\"","[Master, quite a full house today. Even several old ministers who were recuperating from illness are here. Huh, is that Old Lord Bao?]","\"Which Old Lord Bao? Do you know him?\"","[No, but his family is quite famous, so I remembered them.]","\"Which famous people came from their family? Tell me.\"","[One person is enough to make their whole family famous for generations to come.]","\"That impressive? Who is it?\"","[Old Lord Bao's grandson, Little Bao. Little Bao is getting married tomorrow, and the bride will be kidnapped from the bridal chamber.]","\"A mortal world bride-snatching drama? Was it the bride's sweetheart who snatched her away?\"","\"No. This bride-snatching incident is actually related to Little Bao's father, Bao Qianjun.\""]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150: The Assassin Night-Blooming Cereus and Her Emperor Cousin","paragraphs":["Bao Qianjun, his father, originally served in the Censorate before being stationed in Anji as a Canal Inspection Censor.","Bao Qianjun was upright and unbending, which inevitably made him enemies. Now, on the occasion of his son's wedding, someone paid off an assassin organization to kidnap the bride on his son's wedding day.","\"How bold are these Jianghu people? What is their purpose in doing this? Using someone's daughter-in-law to threaten the father-in-law?\"","\"The Youtan organization only recognizes money. If the payment is sufficient, they would dare to move against anyone... anyone below the emperor. This organization has no bottom line. The fall of the Dayan Empire also had their shadow behind it.\"","Old Master Bao Yuanjun frowned deeply. His grandson was indeed getting married tomorrow, and his son was still far away in Anji and hadn't returned. There was no way to verify whom he might have offended in such a short time.","He could only pin his hopes on the Divine Artifact to reveal who was behind this. Otherwise, even if tomorrow's incident was avoided, the perpetrators would not simply give up.","Emperor Mingxi suddenly felt a chill down his spine. No, he needed to assign more personnel to his shadow guard.","\"As for the purpose the Host mentioned, it's related to a list and an account book. Bao Qianjun has been secretly investigating corruption in the canal transport system for years.","He had accumulated a considerable amount of evidence over these years and planned to use his son's wedding as an opportunity to return and successfully deliver the account book to the emperor.","However, the news leaked. Not only was he detained in Anji by matters at the canal docks and couldn't return, but those people, after searching his residence thoroughly and failing to find the account book, had no choice but to resort to this desperate measure: kidnap the bride to exchange for the account book.\"","Emperor Mingxi shot Eunuch Qian a meaningful glance. Eunuch Qian immediately withdrew quietly to dispatch people to Anji to protect Lord Bao Qianjun, hoping it wasn't too late.","\"They actually want to exchange for something as important as an account book? Wouldn't it be more appropriate to kidnap the younger Bao? They might not save a daughter-in-law, but they wouldn't be willing to abandon their own son, right?\"","\"If it were anyone else, kidnapping the son would indeed be more useful than kidnapping the daughter-in-law. But as for Bao Qianjun, wasn't it mentioned earlier that he is upright and unbending?","If his son were kidnapped, he would likely choose to sacrifice his son to protect the evidence. However, the daughter-in-law is the daughter of his close friend. For the sake of his old friend, he wouldn't just stand by.\"","\"Wasn't there a backup of this evidence? Make several copies for them, or even print them out and post them all over the city.","If they want it, then give it to them—give one to everyone!\"","\"The Anning region is thoroughly rotten. Even so, it's estimated the evidence wouldn't leave that area. Officials and merchants are colluding, forming a unified body from top to bottom. The emperor's words might not carry as much weight as those of the local officials there.\"","\"Does Emperor Mingxi not know that his control over the Jiangnan region has weakened?\"","\"Do you know who the highest-ranking official in Jiangnan Circuit is? It's his maternal cousin, Sima Jing. His words carry more weight in the Jiangnan officialdom than the emperor's imperial edicts.","They have formed a solid interest group. These Jiangnan officials only know of Lord Sima, not the emperor. One could say Sima Jing is the local despot.","As for the emperor, assigning such an important position to his own cousin surely indicates trust. If an ordinary person came to expose him, who do you think the emperor, with his brain, would believe?","That's why Bao Qianjun has endured for years, determined to obtain solid evidence before daring to report it to the court.\"","Emperor Mingxi: Sima Jing? Sima Jing! Not only his cousin but also his study companion. They endured the dark times during the late emperor's reign together.","Because of this, Emperor Mingxi held deep feelings for him. He never expected that this cousin and study companion would one day betray him!","Emperor Mingxi was so shocked by this matter that he even forgot the Divine Artifact had insulted his intelligence. His face was now livid, a furious fire of betrayal by his most trusted person burning in his heart.","His bloodshot eyes were hidden behind the twelve strands of his imperial bead curtain, his silver teeth almost gritted to pieces.","Eunuch Qian, who knew best the emperor's feelings for Sima Jing, fearing he might harm himself in anger, quickly and discreetly served him a cup of warm tea.","\"In the original historical timeline, did they succeed? Did Bao Qianjun make the exchange?\"","\"He did. But by the time the messages were relayed back and forth, it was already ten days later, right around the New Year. What was exchanged for was just a corpse, mutilated beyond recognition.\"","\"The bride died? These people don't keep their word at all? What kind of Jianghu conduct is that?\"","\"Host, not everyone in the Jianghu keeps their word, let alone the other party being assassins with no bottom line.","However, the bride didn't die. She was swapped out by Sima Jing's son's people. What was given to the Bao family was just the pitiful corpse of an unnamed woman.","When the bride appeared again, she was already a Guifei (highest-ranking imperial consort) of the Great Wei.\"","\"A Guifei of Great Wei? That Great Wei, one of the short-lived separatist regimes established after the fall of Dayan?\"","\"Yes, that one. Their first emperor was Sima Jing's son, Sima Ying.","The Sima family amassed enormous wealth by sucking the lifeblood of the Dayan Empire.","After Dayan was destroyed, they raised troops at the first opportunity and eventually established the separatist state of Great Wei in Jiangnan.\"","At this moment, Emperor Mingxi's eyes grew even redder. The veins on his hands bulged, and he gritted his molars. The humiliation of being so utterly fooled hammered at his nerves.","All the officials, whether they could hear the inner thoughts or not, had their heads bowed low at this moment, each like a quail.","The reason for such unanimity was that the iron-headed gentleman in the main hall was currently impeaching the emperor's study companion and cousin, Sima Jing, for the crime of seizing civilian farmland.","The entire court knew of the emperor's protectiveness towards this man. Impeaching him was truly the act of an iron-headed fool. Who was so iron-headed? Of course, it was Feng Tang, the leading figure among the Investigating Censors and one of Yue Fuguang's top admirers.","Investigating Censors could memorialize based on hearsay. Even without evidence, he could raise an impeachment in court.","His coming forward now was nothing more than handing Emperor Mingxi a knife. However, Sima Jing had been entrenched in Jiangnan for years, with interests intertwined like gnarled roots. To move against him, even the emperor needed to be fully prepared.","Seeing Feng Tang's audacious act, those who heard the inner thoughts understood the situation. Those who couldn't hear them were thinking, \"Zhao Xu has only been gone for a few days. Feng Tang's seat isn't even warm yet, and he's already throwing himself at the blade's edge?","Has he gotten too carried away lately? After successfully impeaching princesses, princes, and commandery princesses, he now dares to impeach His Majesty's most trusted confidant?\"","Most trusted confidant—if Emperor Mingxi heard that phrase, his face would probably sting again!","\"Little Pearl, the Sima family must have seized a lot of land, right? Was the grain grown used to raise a private army? For Sima Ying to quickly raise a force after Dayan's fall, it's hard to believe there wasn't preparation beforehand, isn't it?\"","\"While Emperor Mingxi is still alive, they wouldn't dare go that far; there are only some signs. However, in a few years when his health begins to decline, the Sima family's ambition will no longer be hidden.","Do you remember that Shen Wanchuan, the Jiangnan tycoon we saw at the auction house?","He is actually from the Sima family, or rather, he is their white glove.","Specifically tasked with making money for the Sima family. This man was originally a household slave of Sima Jing. Before Emperor Mingxi ascended the throne, he was sent to Jiangnan to develop their influence.","So, Emperor Mingxi's cousin is richer than he is. Right now, Sima Jing's stored silver rivals the national treasury.\""]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: Loyal to the Sovereign and Devoted to the Country: Sima Jing","paragraphs":["Emperor Mingxi's face was as dark as water. So, Sima Jing's voluntary request to garrison the south was part of a long-laid plan!","No wonder, no wonder his Sima family ultimately succeeded. This twenty to thirty-year scheme truly showed immense patience and skill!","A glint of gold flashed in Dong Qianli's eyes. Soon, all the Sima family's wealth would flow into the state treasury, contributing to the construction of the Great Yan.","Even though His Majesty had forgiven those like them who had dipped their hands in a little and embezzled small sums, they had all secretly paid fines to atone. Now, encountering a colossal corrupt official like Sima Jing, he naturally had to guard the emperor's coffers well.","Bao Yuanjun, who had originally been anxious and furious, now stood there calmly and composedly. With the information revealed by the divine artifact, as long as his son could hold out until the emperor's men arrived, he would be safe.","\"He spent tens of thousands of taels of silver to buy that glass tea set, and I thought he was genuinely wealthy. Turns out that money wasn't even his!","He's hailed as the richest man in Jiangnan all day long, yet the money isn't his own. I wonder how he feels about that, what's the size of the shadow in his heart?\"","Emperor Mingxi steadied his mind and said calmly, \"Minister Ji, what is your view? If I recall correctly, Sima Jing's annual 'Four Virtues' evaluations have always been 'Excellent'?\"","[Is this emperor still trying to shield the Sima family? Even Shen Wanchuan, a mere front man for the Sima family, has more silver at home than the emperor.","The walls and floor tiles of his bedroom are filled with gold and silver underneath. It's no exaggeration to call it a house of gold and silver.]","Emperor Mingxi: A house of gold and silver? Excellent, all that will soon be mine!","He probably wouldn't be able to compete with Dong Qianli and other court ministers for Sima Jing's wealth, especially since he had mistakenly trusted him for so many years and had no face to contend for it.","But Shen Wanchuan's 'petty cash'... he could try to claim it for his private treasury. These officials should agree to that.","\"Before knowing whether someone is friend or foe, he would find it hard to believe that his most trusted cousin would betray him. He would only think others were harboring ulterior motives, trying to drive a wedge between them.\"","[Master, do you know what Shen Wanchuan bought that expensive glass tea set for?]","\"It couldn't be for Sima Jing to drink tea with, could it?\"","[Of course not. The persona Sima Jing usually maintains is that of a clean and upright official. He even wore a seventy-percent-new old court robe when meeting Emperor Mingxi.]","Emperor Mingxi closed his eyes. Last year, when Sima Jing entered the palace to see him, he indeed wore an old court robe. When asked, he said it was his newest official garment.","Moved and pained on the spot, the emperor bestowed a large pile of gifts upon him before he left!","Emperor Mingxi gritted his teeth. Sima Jing must have been laughing at his foolishness in his heart back then!","[He naturally wouldn't drink tea from a teapot worth tens of thousands of taels. Although he indulged in luxury in secret, this item wasn't actually procured for his own use.]","\"Then who was he going to give it to?\"","[It was a New Year's gift for the Emperor of Dongyi. Didn't expect that, did you?]","The Great Yan's emperor and ministers: No, we certainly didn't!","Meanwhile, the Minister of Personnel, Ji Hongming, who was also muttering \"unexpected\" in his heart, stepped forward and said, \"Your Majesty, it is true that Lord Sima's 'Four Virtues' evaluations have been Excellent every year.","However, I believe Lord Fengtang's impeachment is not contradictory to Lord Sima's excellent evaluations!\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded. \"Continue.\"","\"Yes, Your Majesty. Privately, I believe that perhaps Lord Sima was unaware of the land encroachment incident. The Sima family is vast and complex; perhaps such encroachment did occur.\"","Ji Hongming first set the tone with this statement, firmly establishing that someone surnamed Sima was responsible, before gradually implicating the old fox, Sima Jing.","\"But it's also possible other relatives acted under Lord Sima's name. Therefore, in my humble opinion, this matter requires thorough investigation!\"","Thorough investigation was the key. You can't wrap fire in paper. If a real investigation was launched, he believed that as long as the Sima family had been active enough, there would inevitably be loopholes.","Wasn't there also a living witness, Bao Qianjun!","As Emperor Mingxi seemed to be weighing the matter, Yue Fuguang's voice came to his ear: \"He couldn't possibly be sending the gift on behalf of the emperor, could he? Is the Sima family colluding with Dongyi?\"","[Of course not on behalf of the emperor. They've been colluding for a long time. You know about the pirates on the seas? The reason they could never be eradicated is because they were the Sima family's enterprise!","Turning piracy into an industry—impressive, wouldn't you say?","They robbed merchant ships, causing many coastal traders to avoid landing there, allowing their business to monopolize the area.","Otherwise, how could Shen Wanchuan develop so rapidly in just a few years, faster than in the previous decade or so?","It all started when Sima Jing took office; with a protective umbrella, he prospered!]","\"Although the Great Yan's fall was primarily due to Xiqiang, Beili, and Nanyue, Nan Zhao and Dongyi also meddled extensively.","As the saying goes, when a wall is about to collapse, everyone gives it a push; when a drum is broken, ten thousand beat it. Dongyi came to take a swing, so what role did the Sima family play in that?\"","The emperor and ministers of the Great Yan also wanted to know what exactly Sima Jing had done.","[After Emperor Mingxi's sudden death and the new emperor's ascension, the Great Yan was already like a rapidly sinking ship. Sima Jing had long foreseen the dynasty's demise and saw his family's opportunity.","By then, besides the pirates at sea, they also controlled part of the coastal garrison. If the garrison and the pirates share the same master, how could they possibly be eradicated!","The new emperor, like his father, saw many court officials purged, but he indeed placed great trust in Sima Jing.","After the new emperor's rise, Sima Jing's power grew greater, his position more secure. In Jiangnan, except for not changing the surname, he was no different from an emperor.","Later, he vigorously and secretly recruited private soldiers in Jiangnan. By the time Xiqiang and other states attacked the Great Yan, the Sima family was ready to raise troops at any moment.","When the foreign armies were about two days' march from the capital, Shangjing, he opened the ports and let the Dongyi people in.","His own private soldiers mixed among them, looting and killing local wealthy households to accumulate wealth. Afterwards, he assumed the righteous persona of resolutely expelling foreign enemies and protecting the local people's safety to drive the Dongyi away.","For this, he won the local people's adoration. Subsequently, after the Great Yan fell, the Sima family, after being 'repeatedly and earnestly entreated' by local gentry and commoners, 'reluctantly' raised the banner of rebellion, and the Great Wei was established.]","\"The local people didn't know their land, money, and grain all ended up in the Sima family's pockets. Those 'repeatedly entreating' people were plants from the Sima family, right?\"","[The lands were bought or forcibly seized by wealthy merchants like Shen Wanchuan; the money and grain were plundered by pirates; the people were killed by the Dongyi.","What does that have to do with the Sima family who saved them? As for those repeatedly entreating, they were led by Shen Wanchuan...]","The unspoken words were clear enough. It was all a show put on by the Sima family for the world. The Great Yan's emperor and ministers also understood it was merely a political performance by Sima Jing. If they were in his place, they would do the same.","\"This Sima Jing is quite something. The persona he built is far more solid than those of modern young idols—it never crumbles!\"","[Indeed. For this persona, for the stability of his Sima family's future reign, and to eliminate future troubles, one can see how much he could endure for the throne from the fact that the first emperor of Great Wei was his son, not himself.","Although we look down on that shabby chair, it seems mortals are quite fond of it. Men and women alike, given the chance, all want to sit on it.]","Sima Jing, however, restrained himself. He steadfastly considered himself only a subject of the Great Yan Dynasty. Thus, in his 'loyalty to the sovereign and love for the country', he refused to ascend the throne and proclaim himself emperor."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: Chu Qiuyue, what an extraordinary woman she is","paragraphs":["\"Another Cao Cao in the making! He's going to use the Great Yan's downfall for one last scheme. If Emperor Mingxi finds out about this, wouldn't he be so furious he'd cough up blood?\"","Emperor Mingxi: Heart aches, mouth tastes bitter, blood has reached the throat, but dare not spit it out!","[The first emperor of Great Wei, Sima Ying was the one who swapped the Bao family's granddaughter-in-law. He had long fancied Little Bao's fiancée, Chu Qiuyue.","Unfortunately, the beauty was already betrothed and had no intention of changing husbands. So, he incited his father, Sima Jing, to snatch the bride on the wedding night, an outlandish scheme to exchange the bride for an account book.","After obtaining the account book, he randomly picked a woman from his own harem who resembled Chu Qiuyue in stature and appearance, killed her, and sent her into the Bao household.]","\"This man is truly ruthless! Those in his harem were all his concubines, right? He just killed one without a second thought?\"","[All those women in the harem, whether bought or snatched, were just knock-offs of Chu Qiuyue. Now that he had the genuine article, losing a few counterfeits didn't matter.]","\"Would Chu Qiuyue just submit to him like that?\"","[She had no choice. If she refused, Sima Ying threatened to kill Little Bao. Given the Sima family's power and influence at the time, she had no choice but to believe him.","Chu Qiuyue had no way out and could only live on, bearing the humiliation.","Later, she secretly took medicine to make herself infertile, vowing never to bear Sima Ying's child.","According to the original timeline, next spring, Bao Qianjun would be framed by him for colluding with the Eastern Barbarians and plotting treason. The entire Bao clan would be purged.","All adult male members of the Bao family would be beheaded, and the rest exiled, conveniently ending up in Sima family territory.","To care for these women and children, Chu Qiuyue's desire to die subsided slightly.","Later, shortly after Sima Ying ascended the throne, at the peak of his triumph, she took his life, avenging the hundred or so members of the Bao family.","She then took her own life.","To protect her own natal family from implication, she even orchestrated it to look like she was accidentally poisoned due to her association with Sima Ying.","The truth of this matter wasn't uncovered until a hundred years later. Little Bao, that is, Bao Zihui, also became famous because of Chu Qiuyue's unique form of 'following in death'.","Their story was written into operas and plays, and the injustice suffered by the Bao family was also brought to light with the truth.]","The previously composed Old Master Bao swayed slightly. Yu Chongshan, standing behind him, promptly steadied him.","As someone who had also experienced the loss of his entire family, he could deeply understand Old Master Bao's feelings at this moment.","Seeing that it was Yu Chongshan, the little celestial master's grandfather, who supported him, Bao Yuanjun was overflowing with gratitude. He gripped Yu Chongshan's hand firmly.","Yu Chongshan patted his hand reassuringly, signaling him to stay calm. With a family like the Simas, even if they were the emperor's own brothers, he believed His Majesty would ensure not a single soul of their household remained.","For the stability of that throne, the number of blood brothers who had died by their current emperor's hand was almost enough to count on two hands!","Meanwhile, Emperor Mingxi, looking at the nearly seventy-year-old Old Master Bao who seemed on the verge of collapse, felt a flash of awkwardness cross his dark, somber face.","Their son was loyal to the sovereign and loved the country, yet his future self actually believed the words of the true scourge of the state and exterminated their entire clan.","If such a subject wasn't properly appeased, others watching would wonder who would still sincerely dedicate themselves to the Xie family's empire?","Thus, he said, \"We shall do as Minister Ji suggested.\"","Considering that Cai Xian currently had the affairs of the four great families to handle, he turned to Wei Ping and said, \"This matter, Minister Wei, you shall take charge, with the Ministry of Personnel assisting. Both ministers must pay attention to propriety and avoid wounding the hearts of those loyal to the throne.\"","On the surface, it seemed like a reminder to Wei Ping to be measured and not hurt Sima Jing's pride. But those who knew the situation understood this was His Majesty reminding the Court of Judicial Review to protect Bao Qianjun and the Bao family.","\"Chu Qiuyue, truly a remarkable woman!\"","[Master, should we help her?]","\"How do you suggest we help?\"","[Tell the Bao family to be wary of the You Tan organization snatching the bride.]","\"The You Tan assassin organization is hidden so deeply, even the emperor might not know who their leader is. What excuse should I use to tell others how I found out they plan to snatch the bride?\"","[Just say it's news your mysterious overseas friend—Little Pearl, that's me—overheard. What do you think, Master?]","\"Master thinks... not very good. How would an overseas merchant like you manage to get news about a land-based assassin organization like You Tan?","Little Pearl, have you ever heard the saying 'different trades are separated by mountains'?","Sigh! Without my own people, even wanting to do a good deed once is so difficult!\"","[Didn't your grandfather say the emperor has agreed that you can select a portion of the new army being formed to guard the cotton fields?","Won't those people all be yours then? I heard with the high pay, they've already recruited five thousand. After the New Year, ten thousand will surely be recruited quickly.","If not, hurry Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi along; tell them not to dawdle.]","The two men named by the divine artifact, Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi, inexplicably tightened their legs and stood straighter. They really were working as fast as they could. Because the military pay was high, they couldn't help but be pickier when recruiting.","With high pay and good food, if they didn't recruit the best, they'd feel they were letting down the funding emperor and the Junior Mentor.","Yue Fuguang glanced at Old Master Bao standing with her grandfather. \"Maybe I should tell Grandfather and let him decide whether to inform the Bao family or not.","If I go and say it, what if they don't believe a child's words? Who knows how accurate an overseas merchant's information is?","However, since you've sent me so many things, my grandfather does have some trust in my overseas merchant friend.\"","Yu Chongshan nodded secretly in agreement. Yes, yes, yes. Who could we distrust, but we must trust the divine artifact!","[Master, your grandfather and Old Master Bao seem quite close. Do you think he'll invite the Yu family to the wedding banquet?]","\"Little Pearl, what are you scheming now?\"","[Hehehe, Master, we've been in this mortal world for over three years now and haven't seen how mortals hold weddings. Aren't you curious?]","\"When my older brothers marry and my sisters marry out, won't you get a close-up view?\"","[Your eldest brother still hasn't found a match, and your second brother was just tossed into Old Wei's military camp for training. Who knows how long we'll have to wait for their weddings?","Isn't the Bao family's wedding happening right now? How about we go join the fun?]","Some people's hearts stirred. The Yu family sent their grandson to the military camp for training... was there some deeper meaning or signal? Thinking of their own sons or grandsons who were hopeless at studies and caused trouble all day, could they also...?","Those with such thoughts silently glanced toward Wei Shouyi. Wei Shouyi: The military camp is not a garbage dump; too many would really pollute the environment!","Just as Wei Shouyi was planning to slip away as soon as court adjourned, they heard Old Master Bao address his colleagues loudly with a cupped-hand salute, \"Gentlemen, please wait a moment. Tomorrow is my young grandson's joyous occasion. Colleagues, if you have leisure after court tomorrow, you must come to my humble abode for a cup of wedding wine.\"","Actually, many here had already received invitations from the Bao family. Yu Chongshan had one; the Old Madame Yu and Madam Zhang had even prepared gifts. It's just that Yue Fuguang didn't usually pay attention to such things and didn't know."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: These fence-sitters","paragraphs":["The crowd responded enthusiastically. Elder Master Bao, seeing Yue Fuguang descending the jade steps, beamed with a kindly smile and said, \"Grand Tutor, you must come as well! This old man and your grandfather have been friends for many years; our families should visit each other more often.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded with a faint smile. Emperor Mingxi, who hadn't left yet, also joined in the excitement, saying, \"Crown Prince, take your brothers to Minister Bao's residence tomorrow to share in the auspicious joy, and tell me all about it upon your return.\"","Emperor Mingxi was clearly showing favor to the Bao family, making amends for his own actions in the original timeline!","The Crown Prince also chimed in playfully, \"Yes, Father. In that case, for the congratulatory gifts for the newlyweds, this son will go pick from your private treasury!\"","Emperor Mingxi feigned a helpless expression of being taken advantage of by his son, pointed vaguely in the Crown Prince's direction a few times, flicked his sleeve, and walked away, saying, \"Then you must choose carefully, don't embarrass me.\"","[Master, we should also return to our residence to select a gift. It absolutely must not be inferior to the Crown Prince's.]","「Little Pearl, your competitive spirit is everywhere!」","Watching Yue Fuguang's retreating figure, the crowd tacitly made their way towards the Hall of Mental Cultivation, where Emperor Mingxi handled governmental affairs.","Having received so much information today, while the Sima family certainly needed to be dealt with completely, how to round up those 'pirates' still at sea required careful planning. Everyone present understood the dangers of not eradicating the root of the problem!","Moreover, Sima Jing had been operating in the Jiangnan region for many years. To capture him in one fell swoop truly couldn't be rushed. Emperor Mingxi himself was clear about this in his heart. No matter how furious he was, he had to temporarily exercise patience and proceed gradually!","...","The following evening, the main gate of the Bao residence stood wide open. Crimson silk cascaded like waterfalls on either side of the vermilion lacquered doors, pouring down from the high eaves. Golden bells attached to the silk tinkled clearly in the evening breeze, creating a rather delightful sound.","Just as Yue Fuguang arrived at the front gate of the Bao residence with her grandfather, Elder Master Bao hurried over. From a distance, he cupped his hands in greeting, saying, \"Grand Tutor, Elder Brother Linzhi, I failed to welcome you from afar. I beg your forgiveness!\"","As he spoke, he ushered the two inside.","Within the Bao residence, a hundred gilded palace lanterns lit up one after another, their halos swirling and transforming the twilight into a warm river of stars.","As they walked, festive red silk, decorative items with auspicious meanings, and double-happiness characters could be seen everywhere.","Along the way, the grandfather and granddaughter encountered many colleagues who had arrived early. Yue Fuguang thought to herself, it seemed like half the imperial court was here!","She just didn't know whether these people were truly here for the wedding wine or, like herself, to get a close-up view of the scene where the so-called number one assassin organization, 'Night-Blooming Cereus,' would snatch someone away.","[Master, why are there so many people here? It seems Minister Bao has good connections! How come when the Bao family was convicted as a whole next year, hardly anyone spoke up for them?]","「Is adding flowers to brocade the same as sending charcoal in snowy weather? The Crown Prince and the princes have all come. Would they dare not to?」","[These fence-sitters!]","Being called fence-sitters by the Divine Artifact, the people nearby all wore awkward expressions and redoubled their efforts to shower the Bao family with auspicious words, praising the groom-to-be, Bao Zihui, as if he were a peerless treasure from heaven.","「Little Pearl, Seeking advantage and avoiding harm is human instinct. Besides, the one who framed the Bao family was the emperor's cousin and childhood study companion. The relationship and trust between those two is something the Bao family could never compare to.","Therefore, even if some people noticed problems, for the sake of self-preservation, they wouldn't openly oppose the Sima family.」","[So later, during Emperor Mingxi's late reign, the court of Dayan became increasingly chaotic, with false accusations and slander emerging endlessly, yet no one stepped forward to uphold justice.","It truly reflects that saying: If I do not speak out today, when disaster befalls me tomorrow, no one will raise a banner and shout for me. The later court's disorder was something they fostered themselves; they can't blame anyone else!]","「The Dayan version of a great escape (survival struggle) certainly wouldn't be much inferior to those of the Han and Ming dynasties on the blue planet. Especially after Emperor Mingxi's death, how many of the people in the current court would still be standing?」","How many would still be standing? And 'great escape' (survival struggle) is not a good term. Although the people around still appeared to be chatting warmly, either sitting or standing,","some had already begun to tremble. While everyone had long anticipated that the 'living conditions' in the coming years would likely be unfavorable, what did it mean to use the term 'great escape' (survival struggle)?","How many would be standing? Forget about how many; right now they just wanted to know whether they themselves would be among those standing or lying down!","Although they didn't know what the blue planet, Han dynasty, or Ming dynasty were, the fact that the Grand Tutor singled them out for mention made it feel like no simple matter.","Their hearts itched with curiosity, but no one had the courage to approach. Well... except for Feng Tang and Wu Yong. These two die-hard fans didn't care what the little celestial lord said. To survive, just cling tightly to the golden thigh.","If these two acted any more obvious, even Emperor Mingxi might start to doubt: Are you Minister Yue's officials or mine?","Feng and Wu: Haven't we made it obvious enough?","「So, such an outcome is the fault of these people's inaction, and even more so the emperor's fault. When the upper beam (the emperor) is not straight, how can the lower beams (the court officials) not be crooked?」","Just as the Crown Prince, Xie Zhiyan, turned the corner with his second, third, fifth, and sixth brothers, he heard Grand Tutor Yue criticizing his father. Xie Zhiyan couldn't help but rub his nose awkwardly.","Should he relay these words to his father upon returning to the palace, or should he relay them?","But if it were just the two of them, father and son, would his father take off his shoe and hit him with the sole?","Maybe it would be better to wait until they were in the Empress Dowager's palace? The elderly lady would certainly be curious about what a minister's wedding banquet outside the palace was like!","As for the fact that the Empress Dowager had seen such things in her youth, Xie Zhiyan automatically ignored that.","Decades had passed since that wedding banquet; couldn't there be some innovation?","His younger brothers behind him, who had originally been walking with measured, dignified steps exuding imperial majesty, heard Yue Fuguang's voice even before seeing her. Like Sichuan opera face-changing, their auras instantly retracted.","They hunched their shoulders, lowered their heads, and tried to minimize their presence. As for the Grand Tutor saying their father was an unstraight upper beam or whatever, what did it matter?","Which day did these two ancestors not scold their father a couple of times? Did you see their father dare to make a sound?","If the old man didn't dare, they, as sons, naturally had to be even more obedient!","Xie Zhiyan put on a genuine smile and walked towards Yue Fuguang. The princes automatically and spontaneously found seats nearby.","Sitting with the Grand Tutor? Besides their Crown Prince elder brother, none of the others had that courage.","Yue Fuguang was gazing towards the main hall, where an enormous double-happiness character was embroidered with gold thread on red satin. On either side hung the couplet personally inscribed by Emperor Mingxi after court that day: \"Jade Hall, a pair of jades united; Precious Tree, ten thousand branches flourishing.\"","The air was filled with the fragrance of wine, food, and the incense from the fine clothes of several hundred guests.","Yue Fuguang nodded inwardly. In Dayan, not only did women enjoy wearing and making incense, but men also favored scenting their clothes, considering it an elegant practice.","Her perfumes would definitely be hugely popular in the future. These were all her potential customers.","The auspicious hour had not yet arrived. All the guests were chatting and laughing in low voices, but their gazes involuntarily flowed towards the end of the corridor paved with red felt.","Looking out, Yue Fuguang saw a sea of dark heads; the place had filled up quite quickly in this short while.","[Master, look at that table in the eastern corner, the one with the scholars' robes. They're all Bao Zihui's classmates.]","\"Little Pearl, what's so interesting about his classmates?\""]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: The Talent You Mentioned, Are They Reputable","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang followed the system's guidance and looked over. At those few tables were teenagers, aged sixteen or seventeen, seventeen or eighteen, up to around twenty.","Well, with very few exceptions, they all looked decent enough, but this completely failed to attract Yue Fuguang's interest.","[Master, among them, several 'talents' will emerge later on.]","\"Are the talents you speak of, proper talents?\"","[There are proper ones, and improper ones, Master. Which would you like to hear about first?]","\"Let's crack open the proper melon first.\"","[That one in blue and those two in gray over there. One named Gao Ziyou will achieve remarkable accomplishments in agronomy in the future.","Another named Luo Fengqing is, in modern terms, an engineering talent.","Unfortunately, he was born in the wrong era. His inventions and creations were dismissed as frivolous tricks and devious crafts, and his life was wasted without ever being put to good use.]","\"So, isn't this Luo Fengqing the same type of talent as Zhou Qi'an?\"","[Master, they are different. Zhou Qi'an's tech tree is lit up in weapon manufacturing, while this gentleman leans more towards civil applications.","I think if you gave him your \"Tiangong Kaiwu\" (The Exploitation of the Works of Nature), Great Yan would take off in agriculture, handicrafts, mining, and even the military field.]","\"Take off? Do you think the current Great Yan can properly utilize these technologies and these talents?","Furthermore, for no reason at all, if I run over and toss someone a book that would be considered groundbreaking and epoch-making for this world, don't you find that very abrupt and strange?\"","Tiangong Kaiwu? A miraculous book? How miraculous?","Since even the Divine Artifact has said it's a miraculous book that can propel Great Yan's agriculture, handicrafts, mining, and military fields to take off, it must be true.","Wang Shouchen, Huo Ying, Lu Qi, and others felt an unbearable itch in their hearts. Xie Zhiyan even hurriedly took a sip of tea to calm his shock, fearing he might accidentally blurt out a question, which would be terrible!","[That seems true too. This world's technology is too backward. I'm almost embarrassed to look at their so-called confidential 'cutting-edge technology'; it can't even compare to the Sui and Tang periods on Planet Aqua.","If they knew the secret weapon to counter the cavalry of the Western Qiang and Northern Li was hidden within the process of making those poisonous pills they're always thinking about eating...","I wonder what kind of expression they'd have! Master, if Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi knew that thing was hidden in their Emperor's alchemy palace, do you think they would demand the person from the emperor?]","The two exchanged a glance. After the wedding banquet ended, they would enter the palace overnight to see the Emperor. As for whether it was too late and might disturb His Majesty's... interactions with his consorts?","They shook their heads indifferently. They'd just ask the Emperor: is the kingdom more important, or a beauty more important?","Without the kingdom, which beauty would still pay you any mind?","Anyway, their Emperor's task of producing heirs was already over-fulfilled. Having a few less princes and princesses wouldn't matter much.","Emperor Mingxi: Having ministers like you is truly my blessing!","\"Great Yan actually still has people taking elixir pills? Who likes seeking death so much?\"","[Who else could it be but the Great Wise Emperor Mingxi? By the way, around this time next year, his health will begin to decline. The main sign is he'll suddenly realize that in these past two years, fewer children have been born in the rear palace.","Apart from Concubine Xian Zhou giving birth to a 'princess' for him, no one else produced any offspring. So, believing slanderous advice, he'll embark on his journey of massively taking elixir pills to seek death.]","\"Xie Fei is somewhat pitiful. The only princess born wasn't even due to his efforts!","Taking elixir pills, no wonder he died before fifty. Serves him right!","I thought his health was still okay now and was wondering how he fell seriously ill so early, allowing the Zhou mother and son the opportunity to poison him.","So the root cause is here? Has he already started taking elixir pills now?\"","The Crown Prince's heart skipped a beat. If he remembered correctly, a few days ago in the palace, coincidentally the two days the Junior Mentor was absent from court, several Taoist priests had arrived.","Later, they were all arranged in a courtyard not far from where Taoist Priest Xuanmingzi stayed. Although not inside the palace, it was just a wall away.","Moreover, the Ministry of Works was rushing to renovate a palace near the Hongwen Hall, supposedly for alchemists to refine pills. Why choose that location? Rumor had it one alchemist said that direction belonged to the Wood element, beneficial for alchemy!","Now the Junior Mentor says elixir pills are poisonous. If he knew Father Emperor had already started contacting those alchemists...","[Calculating the time, they've already made contact. Actually starting to take them would be next year or the year after. Master, do you want to warn him?]","\"We'll see. If he's determined to seek death, we can only respect his fate!\"","Far away in the palace, Emperor Mingxi, who had just cuddled a charming consort and stolen a couple of kisses, suddenly and inexplicably sneezed several times in a row.","This commotion frightened the attendant Eunuch Qian outside quite a bit. He patted the Emperor's back to soothe him while ordering someone to fetch the imperial physician.","This incident later alarmed the Empress Dowager, so much so that after attending the wedding, Xie Zhiyan directly met his father emperor in his grandmother's palace.","He immediately recounted the theory about the upper beam and the lower beam to him, infuriating Emperor Mingxi so much he wanted to take off his shoe and hit his son, but all that was for later.","At this moment, Xie Zhiyan was still eating dishes, drinking wine, and pricking up his ears to catch the gossip, and he wasn't the only one in that posture.","Listening to these two chat required, firstly, patience, because they truly had childlike mindsets, and their conversation could veer off topic by eight hundred miles.","Another requirement was a strong heart, otherwise, you really could be scared half to death or scolded half to death!","Yu Chongshan, seeing his granddaughter's grim face, quickly piled a bowl of food for her and placed it in front of her.","Most of the Bao family's banquet dishes were still stews, with only one or two dishes being stir-fries.","Currently, in Great Yan, only high-ranking officials' households were gradually starting to incorporate stir-fried dishes into their menus. The reason it hadn't been fully popularized, apart from the stir-fry technique itself,","was also because stir-frying generally required more oil and iron than stewing, both of which were difficult for ordinary commoners to manage.","Currently, both iron and cooking oil were still too expensive for the common people to afford.","For cooking oil, the focus could be on planting soybeans, peanuts, and corn.","As for iron pots, besides the iron ore at Mount Yeren, it would be necessary to guide Emperor Mingxi to mine new iron veins. Both the military and civilian life required large amounts of iron.","\"Back to Gao Ziyou and Luo Fengqing. These two can be given some attention. If they are capable, we can have my brothers at home make contact with them in the future.","If they are willing, they can go develop my land. As for the costs and materials needed for training talents and experiments, this Immortal Lord is not lacking.\"","[To be noticed by Master, changing their original fate and having a chance to fully utilize their abilities, it's also due to the virtue accumulated by their ancestors!]","Everyone secretly nodded in agreement. Indeed! Maybe they should find an opportunity to send their own children before the Little Immortal Lord, whether daughters or sons. If by chance the Immortal Lord took a liking to them, it would be a great fortune!","This plan was feasible!","[Master, after discussing the proper talents, let's talk about the improper ones. These few are really bad!]","\"How so? What have they done?\"","[Look at that one in green named Song Mingwei. He comes from a merchant family, wealthy but without status, so he loves befriending people with power and influence.","His friendship with Bao Zihui is also aimed at Elder Master Bao and Bao Qianjun.]"]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: It's not that I'm nitpicking, but shouldn't two people be two mounds of yellow earth","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang nodded. \"It's common for merchants to seek protection from powerful officials.\"","[The man in the grayish-white robe next to him is named Huang Lifan. His family is impoverished, and his clan reduced their support after he repeatedly failed the imperial examinations. He now relies mainly on the charity of his classmates, with Bao Zihui providing the most assistance.","The man opposite them in the dark red robe is named Hong Feng. He comes from an aristocratic family; his father and brothers all serve as court officials. Oh, I forgot to mention, their family belongs to Sima Jing's faction.]","\"So, what role did Hong Feng's family play in the frame-up of the Bao family?\"","[Not just Hong Feng; Huang Lifan and Song Mingwei also did plenty in the matter of Sima Jing framing the Bao family.","Old Master Bao was quite strict in managing his household. Initially, Sima Jing tried to plant 'correspondence' between Bao Qianjun and the Dongyi people in the Bao family study but failed.","Later, these three, leveraging their status as classmates and 'close friends' of Bao Zihui, entered the Bao study under the pretext of borrowing books.","The three worked in concert: two distracted Bao Zihui by asking for scholarly advice, while the third secretly planted the 'evidence of treason' against the Bao family.]","\"What kind of treacherous friends are these? The other two might be one thing, but why would Huang Lifan do this? Didn't Bao Zihui help him a great deal?\"","[For power and profit, of course. Pulling off this job would earn greater rewards from the Sima family. Moreover, this man perceived Bao Zihui's daily care as condescending charity.","He was deeply jealous of these sons of officials, wishing one day to drag them down from their pedestals into the mud and trample them underfoot.]","\"So they all became running dogs for the Sima family. What happened to them later?\"","Aside from Hong Feng, who, due to his father and brothers' connections, remained a loyal lackey of the Sima family, neither Song Mingwei nor Huang Lifan achieved the importance they desired from the Simas.","Both neglected their studies increasingly and became non-entities within the Sima faction's talent pool. It didn't take long for them to turn and pledge allegiance to Qian Yi.]","\"They defected to Qian Yi? Wasn't their old master, Sima Jing, angry?\"","[Sima Jing never thought much of these two to begin with. Even villains look down on petty scoundrels; they're too unreliable to trust!","Originally, betraying the Sima family would have meant certain death. But when Sima Jing saw they had gone to Qian Yi,","and since Qian Yi was Prince Kang's man, Sima Jing, out of consideration for Prince Kang, didn't pursue the matter further.","Later, Huang Lifan contacted Hong Feng, acting as a bridge to connect Sima Jing down in Jiangnan with Qian Yi in the capital, Shangjing.","Aren't you curious, Master, how Qian Yi managed to stand out among the lower-ranking officials and catch Emperor Mingxi's attention, even receiving vigorous promotion?","The reason lies in the strong recommendation from his cousin and former study companion, Sima Jing.","Qian Yi repaid Sima Jing handsomely for this recommendation. In the later period, when the Dyan court descended into chaos, capable, principled ministers loyal to Dyan became fewer and fewer.","They were either ousted by Qian Yi and his clique or marginalized by the factions they supported. Behind all this, one could faintly discern Sima Jing's shadow.]","The Crown Prince massaged his temples. Great. If he went back and told his Imperial Father all this, the Emperor would probably be furious all over again.","The other princes clearly had the same thought. They stopped eating, their minds racing to come up with excuses to slip away after the banquet. They absolutely could not go see their father with their eldest brother, the Crown Prince.","Otherwise, while His Majesty might hold back due to the Crown Prince's status as heir, he would have no such reservations about beating his other sons!","The brothers exchanged glances—silence spoke volumes at this moment.","Those among the officials who considered themselves capable, principled, and loyal to Dyan felt their hearts sink. Could they be the ones who lost in the court struggles, the batch the little immortal lord mentioned who died early?","\"Emperor Mingxi failed to judge character properly. No wonder the country fell and his family was destroyed, his offspring nearly slaughtered to the last.\"","Clatter! Clatter! Clatter! Clatter!","Yue Fuguang didn't need to look back to know who had caused those noises.","Apart from the Crown Prince, who already knew of his early death and could remain composed, continuing his meal unhurriedly, his foolish younger brothers were thoroughly frightened.","They had considered the possibility of their own deaths before, perhaps even that they belonged to the early-death group. But this was the first time they heard the little immortal lord explicitly state the fate of the Emperor's children.","The little immortal lord used the word 'slaughtered,' indicating some of their deaths must have been gruesome. And 'to the last,' though preceded by 'nearly'—who knew how narrow that 'nearly' was?","The Emperor currently had over twenty children, not counting those yet unborn. Who knew if they were included in that 'nearly'?","For high society, the commotion they made was somewhat improper. Fortunately, the officials at their table were seasoned veterans.","Someone immediately cupped his hands in apology: \"Your Highnesses, esteemed colleagues, my apologies! This humble official's hand slipped, overturning the bowl. Most improper, most improper!\"","Another promptly said, \"No matter, no matter. The tea truly is a bit too hot.\"","Yet another offered a considerate reminder: \"Brother Chong Ming, you should go change your clothes and check for any scalds.\"","\"Yes, yes. Brother Chong Ming, go quickly and return soon. The procession to fetch the bride should be arriving shortly.\"","These men covered for each other seamlessly. Yue Fuguang also glanced back curiously before losing interest.","The people around her silently breathed a sigh of relief.","[Indeed. With over twenty children, his line nearly faced extinction. His misfortune was only slightly better than that of the First Emperor back on planet Blue.]","\"Little Pearl, what happened to those three villains later?\"","[Hong Feng's father and brothers followed the Sima family and became officials of the Wei state. But Wei was just a separatist regime clinging to a corner of the land, and it didn't last long either.","After the fall of the Wei state, Hong Feng tried but failed to attach himself to a new power. In the end, his entire household was wiped out.","As for Song Mingwei and Huang Lifan, after the Bao family's downfall, they even pretended to be good men, secretly visiting Bao Zihui in prison.]","\"What were they up to, a weasel paying respects to a chicken?\"","[They coveted the Bao family's wealth, of course. The entire Bao household was imprisoned, and their property confiscated. But the Bao family was a century-old aristocratic house; a starved camel is still bigger than a horse.","The Baos surely had remaining assets. Song Mingwei, who was already quite wealthy, wasn't too concerned, but Huang Lifan's eyes gleamed with greed for that money.","So he dragged Song Mingwei along and, using Hong Feng's connections, got into the prison.","Bao Zihui was naive, rich, and 'simply foolish.' He actually believed these two, entrusting them with his personal wealth and begging them to pull some strings, hoping at least to secure a better outcome for the female members of his family.]","\"Whether wealth nurtures conscience is debatable, but the saying 'poverty breeds cunning schemes' is perfectly embodied in Huang Lifan. He, who received the most kindness from the Bao family, was the most ruthless among the three in sucking the marrow from their bones.\"","[Exactly! Bao Zihui's money was divided between him and Song Mingwei. Moreover, because they 'bravely' visited their friend in prison, they gained a reputation for being righteous and loyal. Infuriating, isn't it?","With money in hand, both indulged in debauchery and completely abandoned their studies, their achievements capped at the provincial graduate level for life.","Later, both entered Qian Yi's faction, specializing in dirty work for Qian Yi, Li Shang, and others. Many of the so-called 'evidence of crimes' against high officials later were fabricated out of thin air by these two.]","As fate would have it, karma came full circle. They squandered the wealth swindled from the Bao family on a life of debauchery and excess, ruining their health within a few years. Before Chu Qiuyue could even seek her revenge, they had both turned to dust.]","\"A heap of yellow earth? Little Pearl, not to be pedantic, but shouldn't it be two heaps of yellow earth for two people?\""]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: The Wedding Banquet","paragraphs":["Master, it truly is just a single mound. These two died in disgrace, said to have contracted that kind of contagious disease. So, in the end, they were locked together, neglected and ignored, left to die from illness and starvation.","After death, they were even cremated together, their ashes mingled, you within me, I within you, and then buried together. Isn't that just one pile of yellow earth!","Yue Fuguang glanced up towards the direction of the three men. Song Mingwei was toasting and drinking with Hong Feng, while Huang Lifan was gloomily drinking by himself in low spirits.","Logically, on his good friend's joyous wedding day, as a friend, he shouldn't wear a bitter face as if he had lost a relative. Those who didn't know might think he was drinking at a funeral, not a wedding feast.","\"This Bao Zihui also lacks judgment in people. Today's behavior from Huang Lifan shows this person is not worth befriending.\"","Elder Master Bao, who had been listening outside the courtyard for a while, nodded secretly to himself. Indeed, his young grandson still lacked experience. Not only did he lack discernment in people, but he could also make repeated mistakes.","It seemed that after the New Year, he would have to swallow his pride and beg General Wei to stuff Zihui into the military camp to keep company with the children of the Yu family's second branch.","He heard that the sons of Minister Cai and Minister Huo had also been sent there a few days ago. Adding his own grandson to the mix probably wouldn't matter.","Bao Zihui, sitting tall on his horse to fetch the bride, originally brimming with springtime delight, suddenly swayed, feeling a chill run down his back.","Wei Shouyi, who was still raising his cup, paused abruptly, his right eyelid twitching. He had a feeling someone was thinking about him!","Yue Fuguang was already more than half full when suddenly the master of ceremonies gave a long cry: \"The auspicious hour has—arrived!\"","The clamorous noise of toasting and drinking instantly quieted down, leaving only the musicians under the corridor playing the elegant melody of \"The Phoenix Seeks His Mate.\"","The groom, dressed in bright red wedding robes, entered the main hall from the east side. Bao Zihui's appearance was indeed quite good, scholarly yet radiating the unique spirited ambition of youth.","His clear eyes looked towards the corridor with its red walls and green tiles on the west side, filled with nothing but heartfelt joy and anticipation.","There was none of the frivolity Yue Fuguang had imagined. The young man's restrained expression between his brows and eyes was all solemnity and happiness.","It was said that Chu Qiuyue came from a scholarly family. The two were engaged since childhood, practically childhood sweethearts. Presumably, their feelings for each other were good. Otherwise, Chu Qiuyue wouldn't have avenged him in that manner, nor taken her own life to follow him in death after the great vengeance was achieved.","At this moment, Bao Zihui's steps were steady, yet a trace of anxious anticipation still leaked through in his occasional, inadvertent glances towards the corridor outside.","Finally, the tinkling of jade pendants, like clear spring water rinsing jade.","The bride, supported by the matron of honor, approached gracefully from the west side.","She wore a phoenix crown of pure gold with kingfisher feathers, dense strings of pearls hanging down, veiling the woman's lovely face. The hundred-sons tapestry kesi wedding dress she wore had a long, trailing skirt. With every step, it was as if she trod upon clouds and mist.","The groom gazed at the gradually approaching figure. The slight anxiety from moments ago vanished instantly, leaving nothing but tenderness filling his heart and eyes.","He and Qiuyue-mei were childhood sweethearts, mutually devoted. Today, he finally married her and brought her home. This should be his happiest moment.","But thinking of his grandfather's words yesterday, Bao Zihui's smiling face concealed some worry and deep apprehension.","He had been so afraid just now that the one emerging from the west side wouldn't be Qiuyue, but...","As he thought this, the bride had slowly walked to his side.","Pausing slightly, separated by the hazy pearl veil, their eyes met. Qiuyue, just like him, was also trembling slightly.","Unconsciously, he raised his hand slightly, an inch—a silent yet firm gesture of reassurance.","The master of ceremonies' voice rang out again, lofty and solemn: \"First bow to heaven and earth!\"","The two turned, facing the star-studded night sky outside the hall, and bowed deeply.","This bow gave thanks for heaven and earth joining them together.","\"Second bow to the parents!\"","The main seat, due to Bao Qianjun's absence, held only his wife, Mrs. Lin.","She looked upon this perfect pair with eyes full of solace.","This bow expressed gratitude for all the upbringing and heritage within this household.","\"Husband and wife bow to each other!\"","This was the most significant bow. Bao Zihui and Chu Qiuyue stood facing each other. As they bowed, he saw her hands tightly clasped in front of her, knuckles white, and also saw, beneath the slightly trembling strings of pearls, the corners of her lips quietly lifting like cherry blossoms.","Bao Zihui's heart also pounded like thunder in his chest.","This bow pledged not only the promise of growing old together but also the oath to share weal and woe, honor and disgrace, from this day forward.","The declaration \"Rites completed!\" fell like metal striking stone.","Congratulations from the hall full of guests surged like a tide, seeing off the newlyweds as they headed towards the night's designated venue—the bridal chamber.","Outside, drums and music swelled loudly, marking the official start of the second half of the feast. Cups clinked, laughter and chatter filled the air.","Yue Fuguang quietly tugged at Yu Chongshan's sleeve, whispering very softly, \"Grandfather, did you relay my maritime merchant friend's words to Elder Master Bao?\"","Yu Chongshan, his face full of smiles, replied in an equally low voice, \"Don't worry, Fuguang. Grandfather has told Elder Master Bao everything. He also guaranteed he would make thorough arrangements. If those people really dare to come, they will surely not return.\"","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and couldn't help asking, \"Grandfather, are the people of the Youtan assassin organization really all highly skilled in martial arts?\"","Yu Chongshan's expression turned serious. He lowered his voice and said, \"The Youtan organization is mysterious and unpredictable. Who its leader is remains unknown to this day.","No one has ever seen his true face. As for the people within the organization, there should be quite a few masters, but they also have talents in other areas.\"","\"With such formidable people around, isn't the emperor afraid that one day someone might sneak into his bedchamber?\"","Yu Chongshan thought to himself, his granddaughter truly dared to think and say such things! But the child was still young, what ill intent could she have? She was just worried about His Majesty's safety!","He said, \"There are many skilled experts within the palace. His Majesty, the Empress Dowager, the Empress, the Crown Prince, and the other princes and princesses all have at least one shadow guard by their side.\"","[These people have shadow guards, but the other consorts in the palace definitely don't. Otherwise, Zhou Yunxin couldn't have succeeded in her affair.]","Yu Chongshan: As expected of the Artifact Lord, the angle from which problems are considered is truly sharp.","'Shadow guards aren't as common as cabbage. The emperor has so many wives and concubines; if each had one by their side, how would they ever manage their palace intrigues?","Shadow guards probably take orders from the emperor. If the consorts made any small move, wouldn't they be exposed immediately?'","Yu Chongshan thought for another moment and added, \"Families like ours also have guards. You may not have noticed, but Grandfather has arranged for two people to protect your safety as well.\"","\"I have them too?\"","\"Your elder brother and sisters each have one. Since you attend court, you have one more than them. Fuguang, you haven't noticed, have you?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Grandfather, who are my guards?\"","Yu Chongshan said, \"One is Cuizhu. The other remains hidden in the shadows. If you wish to meet him, Grandfather can arrange it when there's time.\"","For daily matters within the residence, Cuizhu is there; the other person would not appear at the Yu residence.","[Master, no wonder I always see someone following you to and from court, acting furtively. If I hadn't sensed no malice from this person, I would have long treated him to a taste of lightning.]","'Then why didn't you ever tell me?'","[Heh, isn't it because this person's level is too low? I didn't even take him seriously, so I forgot to mention it!]","Yu Chongshan: That's one of the best shadow guards in our Yu residence, and the Artifact Lord actually says his level is too low.","But then again, considering who could catch the Artifact Lord's eye, there probably aren't many in the entire Dayan Empire who would qualify."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: Assassin","paragraphs":["The grandfather and grandson were chatting when, a moment later, they saw the groom, looking supremely pleased with himself, leading several groomsmen from the rear courtyard.","The groom, Bao Zihui, had now changed into a round-collared robe of bright red ramie silk, a jade belt cinching his waist. Beneath his black gauze official's hat, his eyes and brows held a perfectly measured smile.","Led by the steward, he walked unhurriedly towards the large zitan wood table where Yue Fuguang and the others were seated at the eastern end of the banquet hall.","Seated at the head of the table was the guest of honor for the day—the Crown Prince, Xie Zhiyan. Below him were Yue Fuguang, Yu Chongshan, and several Ministers.","The groom's steps were steady, his wide sleeves brushing lightly like flowing clouds. He stopped three paces from the table, adjusted his attire, and performed a standard bowing salute towards the Crown Prince's direction, then offered a general bow to Yue Fuguang and the officials on both sides.","The jade pendant at his waist remained perfectly still. \"Your Highness's presence graces this humble abode, and the Young Preceptor and esteemed seniors have taken time from your busy schedules to attend. The Bao residence is immeasurably honored. Zihui is deeply grateful.\"","Especially when he looked at Yue Fuguang, his eyes were full of gratitude. Although no one from the Youtan organization had been discovered yet, since his grandfather was so certain, it couldn't be false.","Towards the little benefactor who had provided the information, Bao Zihui felt a hundredfold thankful.","The Crown Prince and the others accepted the salutes with smiles, and Yue Fuguang also nodded, imitating their manner.","The steward timely presented a vermilion-lacquered tray holding a set of official kiln 'doucai' lotus-patterned cups already filled with amber-hued wine.","Bao Zihui first took the cup specially prepared for the Crown Prince, raising it high with both hands above his eyebrows, and offered a deep bow.","\"Your Highness manages myriad affairs of state daily. That you have condescended to attend Zihui's wedding banquet today is an immense honor for the Bao family. With this humble cup of wine, I respectfully wish Your Highness a thousand years of golden peace and everlasting prosperity.\"","The Crown Prince was usually too casual in front of Yue Fuguang; she had almost forgotten that this man was the future successor of the dynasty, personally tutored by Emperor Mingxi since childhood.","Though Xie Zhiyan was young, he now fully displayed the bearing of a crown prince. Indeed, even a young tiger is still a tiger.","He did not immediately raise his cup. His gaze, gentle yet appraising, swept over the groom's respectful posture, a faint, elusive smile playing on his lips.","The Crown Prince's voice was mellow yet carried inherent authority. \"Today, we set aside state ceremony and speak only of familial bonds. Although my interactions with Zihui have not been frequent, I have often heard of your talent and promise from a young age, excelling in both learning and character.","Seeing you establish a family today is a joyous and congratulatory occasion. I hope that in the future, you will cultivate yourself, harmonize your household, and never forget to serve the state.\"","These words were both encouragement and expectation, and the important ministers present all listened with rapt attention.","While speaking these formalities, the Crown Prince actually felt quite envious in his heart that Bao Zihui could marry such a devoted and righteous wife.","He couldn't help but wonder if his own future Crown Princess would treat him with the same sincerity as the young lady of the Chu family, rather than focusing solely on his position.","The groom bowed again. \"Your Highness's instruction, each word a pearl of wisdom, Zihui will certainly engrave upon my heart, not daring to forget day or night. I can only strive to the utmost of my limited abilities to repay Your Highness's recognition and the court's profound grace.\"","Having said this, he respectfully drained his cup, his posture elegant, not spilling a drop.","Only then did the Crown Prince smile and raise his cup, taking a small sip, thus accepting the full courtesy.","\"Good. You may proceed. The Young Preceptor and the various ministers are all pillars of the court and your seniors. You must offer toasts to each one.\"","Bao Zihui immediately turned to Yue Fuguang and offered her a deep bow from the waist. He handed Yue Fuguang a small, exquisite cup containing a popular children's beverage in Dayan.","\"Zihui, on behalf of my wife, thanks the Young Preceptor.\" As he spoke, he drained the wine in his own cup in one go, revealing the excitement in his heart at this moment.","Yue Fuguang, acting like a little adult, said, \"Today is Zihui's joyous occasion. This Young Preceptor offers her blessings to the newlyweds for a harmonious union lasting a hundred years, and hearts forever intertwined.\"","[Master, you must not casually offer blessings. They might inadvertently come true.]","'Wouldn't it be better if they came true? Aren't all blessings hoped to be fulfilled? It's just that others lack the ability.'","Yue Fuguang spoke lightly, but she felt a tiny twinge of heartache. One blessing cost her thirty points. This was the first time she had spent points purely without any purpose for someone unrelated.","At this moment, Bao Zihui's heart was profoundly shaken. He finally understood what his grandfather had repeatedly hinted at on the way here, about the Young Preceptor having some miraculous qualities.","His grandfather had also urged him repeatedly not to panic or make a fuss. Bao Zihui merely paused inwardly, his hand holding the cup trembling slightly for a moment, before he offered another respectful bow and said, \"Zihui thanks the Young Preceptor for your auspicious words!\"","Everyone around, including the Crown Prince, watched with keen envy, thinking they must definitely invite the Young Preceptor to sit at the head table at their own future weddings.","Others had similar thoughts; the Young Preceptor would be their guest of honor.","Yue Fuguang: Is it possible that I won't attend just anyone's banquet, nor am I willing to bestow blessings on just anyone?","Next came Yu Chongshan, Cai Xian, and the other officials.","These dignitaries were truly masters of ceremony, each readily producing gracious words. Cai Xian said, \"My worthy nephew, your esteemed father and I served as comrades in the past. Seeing you now, so spirited and vigorous, is like seeing yesterday once more.","After establishing a family, the true foundation of your career begins. I hope you will carry on your family's traditions and bring honor to your lineage.\"","Bao Zihui replied respectfully, \"Esteemed Uncle shows great kindness. My father also often speaks of the old times with you, instructing me, your junior, to humbly seek your guidance.\"","This cup of wine is to honor our esteemed elder, wishing you good health and longevity, and also to honor the friendship between our two families, as enduring as the mountains and rivers.\"","Wang Shouchen was also an old friend of Lord Bao. His tone was measured, hinting at something deeper. \"Today's splendid banquet truly shows the extensive connections and gathering of talented individuals within your esteemed household. My worthy nephew should focus on his studies, and must not...\"","\"Assassins!\" Before Lord Wang could finish, a shout was heard.","Everyone thought to themselves, 'So it has come to this.' They saw Bao Zihui cup his hands towards the assembly. \"Your Highness the Crown Prince, Junior Mentor, and all esteemed lords, you are the pillars of the state. Your gathering in my humble home today is an honor I will cherish for three lifetimes.","My only wish here is for all of you to enjoy harmonious governance, good fortune, health, and peace! Please wait a moment, I shall return shortly.\"","With that, he leaped and dashed far into the distance, heading precisely in the direction of the bridal chamber in the rear courtyard.","'Who would have thought Bao Zihui was a martial artist? How could a martial artist still be betrayed by a friend, leading to his family's ruin?'","[Master, is it possible Bao Zihui only developed muscles, not brains? He treats his sworn brothers like his own limbs, but those brothers want to kick him into the mire!]","Bao Zihui, already far away, had not yet run out of the range where these inner thoughts could be heard. Upon hearing them, he nearly stumbled and fell face-first into the dirt.","He wept inwardly. Who on earth wanted to harm him and kick him into the mud? Show yourself! He guaranteed he would immediately beat them to a pulp!","As Bao Zihui ran close to his own courtyard, he saw several black-clad men engaged in combat with the household guards. While running, he drew a short blade from his sleeve and went straight for the throat of the man blocking his way. His strike was decisive, his moves fierce and ruthless, showing not a trace of the scholarly, literary air one might expect.","Bao Zihui did not linger in the fight. His dodges and maneuvers were extremely agile, revealing a formidable foundation in martial arts.","His steps were steady, and he pressed forward without yielding an inch, until he reached the bride who still had her veil covering her head.","Seeing more and more people gathering around and his men still unable to break through the defenses of the Bao residence guards, the black-clad leader's eyes turned even colder.","If they didn't act faster, their mission today would surely end in failure. With a wave of his hand, he silently gave the order to the assassins.","Instantly, the assault descended upon Bao Zihui and the others like a violent storm. Bao Zihui resolutely shielded the bride behind him."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: Is this playing \"Infernal Affairs\"","paragraphs":["Arrows flew through the air, slicing through it with sharp, piercing shrieks.","Bao Zihui and the others parried with their swords, not retreating an inch.","Seeing that the first volley of arrows had failed, the attackers immediately changed tactics and closed in for hand-to-hand combat.","These assassins were not death-defying warriors. Facing a fully armed guard force several times their number, even though they prided themselves on their superior skills and boldness, charging twenty-some men into a hundred-plus guards still carried the risk of being slaughtered.","At that moment, the steward arrived with another wave of reinforcements. \"Men! Seize them!\" the steward commanded, his voice hoarse with strain.","More guards poured in, forming battle formations, splitting and surrounding the assassins.","Amidst the chaotic fight, the black-clad leader, seeing the situation was hopeless, took a deep look at the bride who had been escorted to the core of the protection. A complex, indescribable emotion flashed in his eyes.","\"Yin Qi, now!\"","Suddenly, one of the guards who had been swearing to protect the bride with his life turned traitor on the spot. He grabbed the bride's arm and tried to leap away with her.","Yue Fuguang, watching from the top of the wall, clicked her tongue repeatedly. \"Is this some kind of 'Infernal Affairs' play?\"","The Crown Prince beside her heard this and was slightly puzzled. The path to the Avici Hell? These assassins were indeed seeking death.","But that guard was clearly a mole planted by the You Tan organization within the Bao family. If the Bao family had one, did other families have them too? And was Bao Zihui's family the only one with a mole?","No one knew, which made them even more worried.","While they were worrying about the mole, over there, the bride whose arm was grabbed by the traitorous guard acted like a solid gold weight when the guard tried to leap. She remained utterly still and yanked the guard back down.","Before the guard could steady himself, the hand that was still holding the bride was suddenly twisted in an extremely bizarre manner and wrenched behind his back.","The face of the black-clad leader, hidden behind his mask, instantly turned deathly pale. The bride did not know martial arts—this was clearly written in the information provided by their client.","Who was under that bridal veil then?","Looking again at this force of over a hundred men, it was obvious the Bao family had been prepared, laying a net just waiting for them to jump in!","Thinking this, cold sweat instantly broke out all over his body. He fought while searching for an escape route.","Finally, he spotted one and immediately let out a sharp whistle.","\"Retreat!\"","The remaining assassins, hearing the order, immediately threw several smoke pellets. With a poof, acrid white smoke instantly billowed out, obscuring vision.","Yue Fuguang said in a voice neither too loud nor too soft, \"Your Highness, that person's information was indeed correct.\"","The Crown Prince's expression was inscrutable, but he immediately replied in the same tone, \"The information he provides would naturally not be wrong.\"","Their ambiguous, cryptic words, however, deepened the suspicion in the heart of the black-clad leader who hadn't yet fled far.","Was there a mole within the organization, or did someone want to use this mission to get rid of him?","Suspects flashed through his mind one by one. Facing obstacles, his strikes became increasingly ruthless!","He had to get back and find out exactly who in the organization wanted him dead!","By the time the smoke was dispersed by palm winds, more than half of the twenty-some black-clad men had vanished like ghosts.","Those left behind were the slower ones who had been entangled by the guards.","Over a dozen people were quickly subdued and taken away, including the turncoat guard.","Faced with the scene of disarray, the guests who had been watching the spectacle, and several injured guards lying on the ground, Yue Fuguang was brought down to ground level by the Crown Prince.","She asked, \"Your Highness, aren't you going to check these people's mouths? What if they have poison capsules and decide to commit suicide?\"","The Crown Prince smiled and said, \"Where did the Junior Mentor hear such things? Assassins are not death warriors; they generally don't carry poison capsules.","If these people really wanted to die, they had plenty of chances just now to turn their blades on themselves. Choosing not to means they still aren't willing to die.\"","As long as they were unwilling to die, there was a possibility of prying their mouths open.","Inside the bridal chamber, red silks were torn, cups and plates littered the floor. Yue Fuguang didn't enter, only glanced from the doorway to see the 'bride' still wearing the veil suddenly lift it off herself.","It revealed a face without any makeup. \"Isn't that the bride's own personal maid?\"","The Crown Prince led her away as he explained, \"The bride's maid is also her guard; they all have martial skills.\"","So she was like Cuizhu by her side. In the original timeline, the bride was kidnapped, and this maid was most likely killed while protecting her mistress.","Over there, Bao Zihui rushed into the adjacent room the moment he could, found the bride who had been hiding, and tightly grasped her hand, asking urgently, \"Yue, are you alright?\"","His chest rose and fell slightly, a tear marred the sleeve of his wedding robe, and his hair was somewhat disheveled, but his eyes remained sharp, scanning the surroundings vigilantly, afraid another traitorous guard might appear.","The bride, still shaken, her face pale, firmly squeezed his hand in return and shook her head. \"Thanks to the help of our noble benefactor, Yue is fine. Brother Hui, are you hurt?\"","At this moment, their hearts were filled with immense gratitude towards Yue Fuguang. If not for her advance warning, given the number of attackers today, the newlywed couple might truly have been forced apart.","The red silks under the corridor still fluttered lightly in the wind, and the dragon-and-phoenix wedding candles burned fiercely, slowly dripping wax.","Seeing that his grandson and granddaughter-in-law were safe, Old Master Bao hurried to the front to attend to the guests.","By the time Yue Fuguang left the Bao residence, she had received enough words of gratitude from the Bao family masters to fill several large baskets.","When she got up the next day for her late breakfast, she heard from Cuizhu that the Bao family had come to visit in the morning, and her warehouse now held another pile of fine gifts.","\"Miss, the Bao family is so strange. Coming to express thanks isn't some shameful thing, so why visit when the sky is just barely light?","They didn't use the main gate but insisted on using the side gate at the back of the estate. That's the most remote spot; even people in our own household rarely use it.\"","Cuiyu eagerly recounted the strange events of the morning to her.","Yue Fuguang smiled knowingly. \"You know about it, that's enough. Don't gossip about it. The Bao family has their reasons for doing this.\"","Cuiyu said brightly, \"I'm only saying this in our own courtyard. Outside this yard, I wouldn't reveal a single word no matter who asks.\"","As Yue Fuguang drank her congee, she thought to herself, she just wondered if her bit of sowing discord from last night would take effect.","In the following days, the New Year atmosphere grew stronger each day. The Yu estate was everywhere adorned with festive decorations, and Madam Zhang became increasingly busy.","Most amusingly, several new games quietly became popular in the noble circles of the capital at this time. There were games for young masters and ladies, and also ones for madams and wives.","The most popular was the card game suitable for both men and women, named Mahjong.","Although many didn't understand why the game was called Mahjong, it didn't stop most people from being unable to put it down once they started playing.","Mahjong first spread from the Yu estate, then quickly circulated among high-ranking officials and noble families. Even His Majesty had an exquisite white jade Mahjong set specially sent into the palace by Yu Chongshan, with the 'One of Bamboo' tile carved particularly vividly.","True to his reputation for good management and business acumen, Yu Chongshan took advantage of the New Year gift-giving season to include Mahjong sets made of different materials like bamboo, wood, or bone in the gifts sent to various families.","He even thoughtfully attached a set of instructions on how to play. Since then, the masters, after leaving their offices, no longer sought out their concubines' chambers. What fun was fondling a concubine's hand compared to the thrill of handling Mahjong tiles?","The head wives naturally were delighted to see this positive development."]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: It's Chinese New Year","paragraphs":["The Yu family's mahjong sets, as soon as they hit the market, were snapped up by these people before they even had a chance to develop new customers.","It is said that the Emperor's current leisure activity is to relieve fatigue by playing a few rounds of mahjong with the Empress Dowager, the Empress, and the Crown Prince.","Where the superiors have a taste, the inferiors will follow it to an even greater degree. Keeping pace with the imperial family, the entire aristocratic circles of the capital welcomed the New Year amidst the clattering sounds of mahjong tiles.","The festive atmosphere of a traditional ancient New Year was naturally incomparable to the modern era Yue Fuguang once knew, where everyone was well-fed and clothed, and every day could feel like a celebration if one so desired.","On New Year's Eve, before dawn had fully broken and while Yue Fuguang was still meeting the Duke of Zhou in her dreams, the Yu mansion was already ablaze with lights everywhere.","In the main courtyard, maids and serving women moved with light, swift steps, their skirts rustling softly as they carried various items through the covered walkways and courtyards, their exhaled white breath mingling with the lingering morning mist.","The Old Madam, attended by two senior maids, put on that stone-blue kesi silk jacket with eight roundels and sable-fox fur trim, symbolizing her second-rank noble consort title. The snow-white fur lining made her face appear even more kindly and dignified.","The eldest grandson's wife, Madam Zhang, wore a brand-new pomegranate-red gold-threaded brocade skirt with a pattern covering the entire fabric. A red-gold ruby-inlaid collar clasp fastened her neckline, and a \"Morning Sun with Five Phoenixes\" hairpin with pearl pendants trembled gently in her hair as she gave quiet instructions.","Apart from Yue Fuguang, who was still sleeping in the Old Madam's inner chamber, all the young masters and misses of the household had gathered.","The young masters and misses were all dressed in new brocade garments. The boys wore sapphire-blue and indigo arrow-sleeved jackets, while the girls wore peach-red and willow-green jackets and skirts. The red-gold longevity locks and white jade peace knots fastened to their lapels jingled softly as they moved.","Upon closer look, one could see that several pieces of jewelry worn by the sisters Yu Ningxuan, Yu Ningxin, and others were actually fine items from the palace that Yue Fuguang had gifted them recently.","The sisters exchanged knowing smiles as they looked at each other's accessories. Although they chattered away, they consciously kept their voices low.","They were afraid of disturbing the 'golden darling' of their grandparents, who was still snoring soundly inside.","Even the most haughty Yu Ningrong dared not openly provoke Yue Fuguang now.","By this time, the Yu mansion had long been decorated anew. In the center of the main hall, \"Hall of Glory and Joy,\" hung a large gilt-inscribed plaque bearing the characters \"Fortune, Longevity, Health, and Peace,\" personally written by the late Emperor.","Beneath it stood a large rosewood console table carved with cloud and dragon patterns. On the east side of the table stood a vase of blooming red plum blossoms. The vase used was not the customary meiping, but a gilded and painted glass vase gifted by Yue Fuguang.","On the west side, a large pale celadon vase from the official kilns held plump kumquats, symbolizing \"Spring Fills the Hall\" and \"Fortune Fills the Gate.\"","Gold-sprinkled vermilion couplets and auspicious paper hangings adorned the doors, windows, columns, and beams.","The floor was covered with a thick, crimson carpet patterned with peonies, symbolizing wealth and honor. Stepping on it made no sound.","From the beams in various rooms hung exquisite glass palace lanterns provided by Yue Fuguang, waiting for nightfall to illuminate the entire house with brilliance.","This was the scene of opulent festivity that greeted Yue Fuguang when she awoke.","She had her combined breakfast and lunch in the Old Madam's quarters. The household had grown accustomed to her non-court attendance schedule, keeping her meals warm so she could eat as soon as she woke.","\"The pastries in Grandmother's room are still the best,\" Yue Fuguang said, after finishing her meal, still able to pick up and nibble on two more pastries.","They say a growing boy eats his father out of house and home. She wasn't even that age yet, nor was she a boy, so how could she be so ravenous all the time?","In her previous life, at this age, she ate like a 'bird'. Her grandparents had worried endlessly seeing her eat so little.","\"System, is my huge appetite because you're draining my energy?\"","The system was taken aback by the question. \"Host, didn't I tell you? The higher my level, the more energy it consumes. A large portion is the system's own energy, but as the host, you also expend a small amount.\"","\"You never told me! You sound like a demon that sucks people's vital essence!\"","\"Host, don't slander a good system! This system would never suck your essence. The energy consumed is like what you expend when you work—it's energy converted from food, not your vital essence, blood, or spirit.\"","\"No wonder I'm getting greedier and less ethereal. So that's the reason.\"","\"The system mall has fasting pills. Do you want to try those? One pill keeps you full for two days, guaranteed to make you feel ethereal.\"","\"Fasting pills cost points! I'm not going to be that sucker. With plenty of food and drink at home, I'm not wasting points on that.","At least not for the next few years. Besides, with my current 'golden status,' even if I declared myself not an immortal descended to earth, these people probably wouldn't believe me.","I don't need an ethereal aura to bolster my immortal identity.\"","Hmph, she had seen through the system's tricks. It couldn't fool her into spending a single extra point.","The New Year's Eve feast was set for dusk. The men and women of the Yu family were seated according to precedence. Unsurprisingly, Yue Fuguang was pulled to sit at the adults' table.","Her elder brothers, seated at the children's table, watched with envy.","Maids carried large trays, serving dishes in a continuous stream. Well, over half the dishes used stir-frying techniques and ingredients from her own greenhouses!","Scallion-braised sea cucumbers glistened darkly, deer tendon stewed with quail yielded a rich broth, wine-marinated steamed shad fish had gelatinous fat under its scales, and there was that jujube-red, fall-off-the-bone braised pork hock. The Old Madam had specifically ordered Yue Fuguang's down-to-earth dish name changed to \"Harmony and Unity.\" Wealthy families always insisted on associating everything with good fortune.","The pastries were even more exquisite: lotus flower crisps, ruyi rolls, jujube paste and yam cakes, lotus seed paste cakes, all shaped like various flowers and fruits, served on sweet white porcelain plates, delicate and lovely.","During the feast, everyone shared tusu wine, infused with herbs like tusu grass and cinnamon. The drinking order, however, went from the youngest to the oldest, symbolizing the young gaining a year and bidding farewell to the old.","Of course, at this time, Yue Fuguang, like her sisters, had child-friendly drinks like milk tea or fruit cordial in her cup.","After the feast, the remnants were cleared, replaced with fragrant tea and fruit platters.","Servants lit a massive \"pine basin\" in an open area of the courtyard—a pyre built with pine and cypress branches. The flames roared, filling the air with the scent of pine. This \"burning the pine basin\" was meant to drive away evil spirits and welcome auspiciousness.","Yu Chongshan looked at their family's greatest 'auspicious sign'—Yue Fuguang stretching her chubby hands to warm them by the pine basin—his face brimming with irrepressible joy.","After warming themselves, Yue Fuguang joined her brothers and sisters around the fire basin to set off firecrackers, their laughter and cheers filling the air.","\"System, if we had some fireworks right now, it would be absolutely perfect!\"","\"Then hurry up and promote the development of gunpowder. Couldn't you set them off next New Year?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"It's not the right time yet, and I don't plan to let them obtain black powder directly. This matter requires caution. It's better to proceed step by step.\"","For Dayan to consider military campaigns abroad, it would need to accumulate strength for at least another three to five years.","As the hour of Zi (midnight) approached, the whole family gathered in the ancestral hall. Yu Chongshan personally took incense sticks and led everyone in performing the grand ceremony of three kneelings and nine kowtows, reporting to the ancestors and praying for the family's safety and enduring blessings in the coming year.","Well, at this moment, Yue Fuguang felt a bit awkward. While everyone else bowed solemnly to the ancestors, she alone held incense sticks and bowed with a slight bend at the waist.","The Old Master had an excellent memory, remembering even now that she must not kneel.","Yu Chongshan thought to himself, if he let his granddaughter kneel, it wouldn't be thanking the ancestors for their blessings—it would be delivering a fatal blow to the ancestors!","He wouldn't have to worry about the ancestors coming to settle scores with him in the middle of the night. If Yue Fuguang knelt now, the ancestors probably wouldn't even have a chance to come up!","That would truly be the epitome of filial piety—in the worst way possible!"]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: Your elder cousin ended up marrying someone involved in illegal activities like gambling, drugs, and vice.","paragraphs":["Back at Rongxi Hall, everyone performed the New Year's Eve farewell ceremony to Yu Chongshan and his wife according to seniority. The elderly couple smiled as they distributed \"lucky gold ingots\" strung with red cords to the younger generation.","Yue Fuguang once again watched her brothers and sisters kneel in a group; only she needed to stand and recite auspicious words.","Looking at the bulging, heavy red envelopes in her hand, their weight was truly substantial. She silently purchased two more 'Blessing' talismans from the system mall.","Although using two talismans for many people would dilute their efficacy, it was still as the saying goes: having something is better than having nothing!","Afterwards, the family sat together for the New Year's Eve vigil, chatting and laughing. This chatting and laughing didn't actually last long before they automatically split into several tables to do their own things.","This usually tedious and boring New Year's Eve vigil, because of the new games—especially at the adults' tables, which were divided into men's and women's tables—was filled with the clattering sound of tiles until dawn.","Only when reminded that it was time for morning meal and then to pay New Year's visits did everyone realize the night had passed, reluctantly putting away their hands.","Madam Zhang and a few others even joked, \"When we return to our maiden homes, we must bring more loose silver. Who knows, we might have to play a few rounds with our sisters-in-law and sisters there too.\"","Yu's Second Aunt also chimed in with a smile, \"Eldest sister-in-law is right. My luck has been good lately, and my fortune is strong. Who knows, I might win back that jade cicada by Master Yu from my sister-in-law when I go home.\"","For the next few days, Yue Fuguang's schedule was packed. She followed her grandparents and parents to visit relatives and friends. She didn't find it annoying, as it was her first time participating in such activities in ancient times, and the novelty hadn't worn off. As for whether she truly liked it, one would know by seeing if she goes again next year!","For Yue Fuguang, this was a bountiful New Year. Every household she visited bestowed upon her a large pile of bulging, weighty red envelopes.","Without exception, this envious the children of each household every time, pulling a full measure of their \"hatred.\"","The second day of the Lunar New Year was the day for married daughters to return to their maiden homes. Yue Fuguang, dressed 'anew' by Cuizhu, followed Madam Zhang back to her maternal grandparents' home.","Yu Zhongqin and his four sons rode horses, while Yue Fuguang followed Madam Zhang in a carriage.","The Zhang residence was about half an hour's carriage ride from the Yu residence. Yue Fuguang merely dozed off in the carriage before arriving.","As soon as mother and daughter alighted from the carriage, they saw the eldest aunt, along with the third and fourth aunts, coming forward to greet them.","\"Sister-in-law!\"","The eldest aunt, Zhang, was tall and slender. Like the slightly plump third aunt and the young fourth aunt, she was dressed in festive red skirts and jackets of varying shades, over which were draped cloaks of different colors. Judging by the snow on them, they must have been waiting for a while.","\"Greetings, aunts,\" Yue Fuguang followed suit in addressing them.","\"Good, good. Was the journey tiring, Fuguang?\" The well-preserved face of the eldest aunt, Zhang, was full of smiles.","The third and fourth aunts took the hands of the mother and daughter, saying, \"It's cold outside, hurry inside.\"","The three uncles, who had originally been standing on the steps, also went to greet Yu Zhongchun and his four sons... well, after nodding in acknowledgment, they all walked smiling towards the mother and daughter.","Yu Zhongchun didn't feel awkward. Which year had his brothers-in-law ever waited at the gate? Enjoying this treatment this year was all thanks to his daughter's influence.","This child usually preferred to stay in her own courtyard. Occasionally, when she came out, it was mostly because her grandparents summoned her to enjoy some time together.","Even if her grandparents didn't \"steal\" her away, there was still his own wife. Which day ever fell to him? Today was a rare occasion for their family to go out visiting relatives together.","\"Eldest brother, third brother, fourth brother.\"","\"Greetings to all uncles!\"","The eldest uncle, Zhang Zhi, said with paternal affection, \"Fuguang is here. Quickly come home with your uncle. Your grandfather and grandmother have been talking since morning, saying you should be arriving soon.\"","\"How are father and mother's health?\" Madam Zhang asked with concern. She was usually busy managing the household. Although her mother-in-law wouldn't interfere much when daughters-in-law returned to their maiden homes, she herself was genuinely too busy to get away.","She couldn't return to her maiden home more than a few times a year.","The eldest uncle, Zhang, said repeatedly, \"Good, all good. Even better than the last two years.\"","Madam Zhang's parents were three or four years older than Yu Chongshan and his wife. Various minor health issues had emerged a couple of years ago, so Madam Zhang's only worry was her parents' health.","The group chatted and laughed their way to the main courtyard. As soon as they entered the courtyard gate, Old Master Zhang and Old Madam Zhang came out to greet them, followed by a crowd of grandchildren.","Yue Fuguang exchanged greetings with everyone in a circle and received another pile of red envelopes. Besides gold ingots of various shapes, there were jade pendants and bracelets.","After visiting so many households, no one had ever given her silver ingots. It seemed that the young immortal lord's dislike for silver and copper was now widely known and deeply ingrained.","Speaking of which, her storage ring held several rows of shelves made of red sandalwood, rosewood, and pearwood.","Apart from the treasures Yue Fuguang had bought at a 90% discount from the system mall, the shelves were filled with fine items she had meticulously selected from the storeroom over these days—a full dozen or so large chests worth.","With over a dozen cousins, Yue Fuguang went through a round of recognition, barely managing to match names with faces.","Although she had met them during the adoption process, she hadn't really remembered many in the rush.","Indeed, neither rebirth nor transmigration increased one's intelligence. However, Yue Fuguang, bolstered by the power of merit and virtue, had a much better memory than before.","[Master, your eldest female cousin is going to marry someone involved in prostitution, gambling, and drugs in the future.]","「Little Pearl, is your 'prostitution, gambling, and drugs' the same as what I understand?」","The Zhang family saw a fleeting look of gravity pass over Yue Fuguang's face, and their hearts couldn't help but sink slightly.","A few of the younger generation were still playing and laughing, but the eldest male cousin Zhang Sheng, the eldest female cousin Zhang Yulang, and the second and third female cousins all trembled slightly, almost unable to maintain their smiles.","The older children had all been repeatedly instructed by the adults: this little cousin had some extraordinary abilities. If they heard anything, they shouldn't panic, should act as if they hadn't heard, continue as normal, and not show any strangeness.","So, this was where the extraordinariness lay?","They were sitting face to face. Just now, they heard the little cousin's voice, but didn't see her mouth move. And that childish voice called her 'Master'?","Was it a pet raised by Fuguang?","System: It's a divine artifact, a divine artifact! Can't let the prestige drop!","[Master, exactly that!]","「That's not right. The eldest uncle and aunt only have this eldest female cousin as a daughter. They should dote on her. How could they possibly find such a scoundrel for her?」","Zhang Yulang tightened her grip on her handkerchief. A scoundrel? How utterly despicable must a person be to be called a scoundrel?","Zhang Zhi and his wife also exchanged a glance, seeing doubt in each other's eyes. Could it be the Wen family...","[They naturally dote on their only daughter, and were even more meticulous in selecting her marriage match. It should be basically settled on the eldest son of the Wen family now. The two families will exchange betrothal cards after the Lantern Festival.]","「Is that person involved in prostitution, gambling, and drugs this one?」","[No. This eldest son of the Wen family is your cousin's first fiancé. By the end of this year, his grandfather will pass away from illness. That person will observe a year of mourning. Before the mourning period is over, his father will also die unexpectedly, and he will continue mourning.]","「That's really... terribly unlucky! Wouldn't that delay my cousin into becoming an 'old maiden'? I remember mortal girls marry early.」","[Yes, at an age when they'd just be starting university in modern times, here they become old maidens. Mortals don't know that young men and women marrying and having children too early not only affects their own lifespan but also the quality of their children. How could children born not physically strong possibly live long!]"]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: Will the Grandchildren of Ling Jijiu Be Kidnapped by Child Traffickers","paragraphs":["【Children born from generation to generation certainly suffered from poor medical conditions, but that’s only part of the reason.","Lack of proper nutrition and the chaos of war also meant they rarely lived long, but has anyone ever considered that their physical constitution at birth might have been weak as well?】","The adults sipped their tea and chatted casually, though their minds were already turning over the words of the divine official. Could marrying too early really be so harmful?","“Indeed, here, reaching seventy is considered a venerable old age. We won’t even compare them to us immortals—when we sleep, it’s like an entire lifetime for them.","Compared to the modern world we’ve seen, the difference is staggering. There, people at seventy are still singing and dancing, blossoming into a second spring of life, while here, people are already waiting to die.”","【There, medicine is advanced, food is plentiful, and without war, it’s no surprise people live longer. But their marriage age is also much later—men marry at twenty-two, women at twenty—and marrying earlier is illegal, punishable by jail time.】","The group exchanged doubtful glances. Twenty-two? That’s so late! Around here, most couples have two or three children by that age.","Yu Zhongchun and some officials in the group thought even further. This information must be reported to His Majesty. Even if the marriage age couldn’t be raised that high here, at least it could be delayed a bit for the sake of future generations.","Who wouldn’t want their descendants to be healthy and live long, their blessings passed down through the ages?","“So, my cousin never married Wen Dalang?”","【Originally, they were supposed to marry as soon as Wen Dalang’s mourning period ended. But no one expected that, perhaps driven crazy by the four years of mourning, Wen Dalang disappeared right after his period was over.","He was dragged by friends to the Cangchun House and never came out again.】","“Cangchun House? A brothel? Did he die or just vanish?”","【He died. They say it was from excessive drinking, though the exact details are unknown. For the sake of reputation, the Wen family claimed he drank too much and accidentally fell into their own lotus pond and drowned.】","“So my cousin was engaged for four or five years, and then her fiancé died? She must be the most unfortunate one. After all, Wen Dalang dying in a brothel is his own fault, but my cousin had to suffer because of him!”","【Exactly. The Wen family even said your cousin was cursed, that she was bad luck for their family. Within less than a year of their engagement, deaths kept occurring in their household.","As a result, your cousin’s reputation also took a hit, making it difficult to arrange another marriage. Later, your aunt and the others had no choice but to find someone from counties around the capital.","In the end, she married Huang Wei, who was two years younger.】","“What kind of family background does Huang Wei have?”","【His family owned several hundred acres of ancestral land as landlords. He himself was a scholar who had passed the county-level exam (xiucai), but he had been hoping to pass the provincial exam (juren) to marry into a prestigious family. At eighteen, he was still unmarried.】","“That sounds pretty ambitious. Our family is at least an official household, and my cousin was exactly the kind of high-status lady he wanted to marry. Even without passing the provincial exam, getting her must have made him happy, right?”","【Men can be foolish sometimes. Things that come too easily are rarely cherished. He passed the county exam at fifteen but failed the provincial exam three times in a row.","He grew restless and, led astray by bad company, first started frequenting brothels, then gambling. Later, a kind of longevity elixir made from imperial rice from Nanzhao spread to Dayan.","Many people became addicted to it, and Huang Wei was no exception.】","“Has this person really fallen so quickly? And that Nanzhao, selling her off to Dayan—how utterly unforgivable!”","[Back then, your cousin already had a son and a daughter. For the sake of the two children, she could only endure him.","Your uncle and cousins fought and scolded him, but it was useless. A year before Dayan’s fall, he had squandered all the Huang family’s wealth along with your cousin’s dowry.","Your aunt, heartbroken for her daughter, brought their family to live on her small estate. He was lucky—he died a few months before Dayan’s collapse, receiving a proper burial with his body intact, spared from the suffering of the nation’s ruin.]","The Zhang family fell silent. Aunt Zhang wanted nothing more than to reject the Wen family outright. Their luck was bad, their son reckless, and yet in the end, it was her daughter who bore the blame—it was simply outrageous!","The two families’ relationship had been decent before. Lord Wen and Zhang Zhi were of the same age, so it wasn’t as if ties would be severed immediately. But from now on, they would keep their distance, or perhaps cut ties altogether.","Coincidentally, Zhang Zhi hadn’t yet gone to the Wen family to pay New Year’s respects this year—starting now, he wouldn’t be going!","None of these events had yet come to pass. He was already deeply frustrated that he couldn’t justly defend his daughter’s honor. As for the Wen family...","They exchanged glances. The Wen family was not to be trusted, and they wouldn’t lift a finger to save the unexpectedly deceased Lord Wen.","Meanwhile, Zhang Sheng ground his teeth in secret. How dare they treat his sister so shamefully! Whether or not it had happened, neither the Wen family’s eldest son nor Huang Wei would be allowed to escape!","Aunt Zhang thought of Madam Wen, a cold smile curling at the corner of her lips. To speak of her daughter that way—did they really think she was dead?","When Yue Fuguang left the Zhang residence, two horse-drawn carriages followed behind, loaded with gifts from the Zhang family.","“System, looks like my warehouse is going to be full again.”","[That’s good! Everything in the warehouse has been converted into silver, enough to support your new army for two or three years.]","Speaking of the new army, it was said that by the end of the year, ten thousand recruits had been enlisted. After the Lantern Festival, training would begin. By the time Yue Fuguang’s cotton seeds were planted and before harvest season arrived, half of those men could be transferred to her.","Yue Fuguang had already agreed with Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi that she wanted the best five thousand soldiers. She was confident no one would dare give her anything less.","Meanwhile, holidays always seemed to pass faster than workdays.","Before the Lantern Festival, the court officials of the Dayan dynasty had already resumed work. Yue Fuguang, who was notoriously slow to get up, had to endure both drowsiness and the northwest wind to attend court on this day of a major revelation.","Having slept through most of the morning session, Yue Fuguang woke and began replenishing her energy. After eating her fill, she glanced at Ling Yinghua, the Dean of the Imperial Academy. “You’re it.”","[Master, tonight’s Lantern Festival is said to be the liveliest and most spectacular. Shall we go take a look?]","“Are the lanterns in the mortal world really more beautiful than the stars in the Milky Way? Or the spirit flower lanterns in the Heavenly River?”","[That’s different. The mortal world’s lanterns have more of a lively, festive atmosphere and people’s presence.]","“If mortals don’t have people, do they have fairy aura? Ghostly aura instead?”","[Master, don’t be stubborn. Let’s just go see. We’re free anyway.]","“Crowded places aren’t safe, especially festivals like the Lantern Festival where accidents happen often. Maybe it’s better not to go?”","“No way! With the little pearl here, who would dare cause trouble? But the master is right—the area is indeed notorious for frequent accidents.","Look at that thin old man standing in front of your maternal uncle, Zhang Zhi.”","Ling Yinghua: “Old man? Oh, Divine Artifact, I do have a name, you know! And I’m only forty-eight this year—still quite young, thank you very much. How can you call me an old man?”","“Are you talking about Ling Jijiu? What’s wrong with him?”","“He’s the one whose family’s Lantern Festival is today—the same day his grandson and granddaughter will be kidnapped by beggars. The Great Yan Dynasty has fallen, and those two children were never found.”","Emperor Mingxi: “Divine Artifact, when discussing Ling Jijiu’s family, there’s no need to bring up the fall of the Great Yan Dynasty over and over again!”"]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: Lord Ling, Please Calm Down","paragraphs":["Ling Yinghua couldn't care less about anything at this moment. All he wanted to know was how his precious grandson and granddaughter had been abducted by child - snatchers. Were the people arranged around them just useless?","\"Lord Ling, please calm down!\" Zhang Zhi whispered to Ling Yinghua, who was on the verge of collapse.","Ling Yinghua nodded weakly. He was a bit exhausted but still stood upright steadily, pricking up his ears to listen to what was to follow.","\"Lord Ling has lost two grandchildren all of a sudden. How heart - broken he must be!\"","\"Indeed. His family has never had many descendants. Among his two sons' families, there are only three grandsons and two granddaughters. The children are like treasures to them. Losing two at once, Lady Ling even fell into a depression and passed away because of it.\"","Thinking of his wife's death due to this, Ling Yinghua suddenly felt his eyes heat up, and two lines of tears silently streamed down his face. Aware of his gaffe, he quickly lowered his head to wipe them away.","\"Shouldn't there be maids, old women, and servants around them? How could they still be abducted by child - snatchers? Was it at the lantern festival?\"","\"Well, this matter is a bit complicated. The Ling family is a large clan. Ling Jijiu's family is the main branch. Although this branch has always had few descendants, there are many clan members in the Ling family.","These collateral branches live around the mansion of Ling Jijiu's family.","As the saying goes, in a big forest, there are all kinds of birds. The same is true for the Ling family. Some are prosperous like Ling Jijiu's family, while others are down and out, relying on the clan's protection and assistance to survive.","There are even some who engage in illegal activities. Among the collateral branches, there is such a family: a seriously ill father, a weak - willed mother, a teenage sister, and a young child.\"","\"Xiaozhuzi, your talent is growing. This doggerel you made is really catchy!\"","\"The sister in this family is fifteen years old, and the younger brother is six. The sister is already engaged and is preparing to get married after the Mid - Autumn Festival.","Although their father is seriously ill and their mother is weak, the family is quite wealthy.","The marriage was arranged with the son of their father's good friend, which is considered to be a well - known match.","It's a pity that this so - called well - known match is what caused the family's misfortune.\"","\"Tell us. Is there something wrong with the sister's fiancé?\"","\"His character is extremely bad! A clan member of Ling Jijiu's family named Ling Yingda is married to Lady Jiang. Lady Jiang is a traditional woman. It's more accurate to say that she has been overly influenced by the Three Obediences and Four Virtues and is overly submissive.","She noticed that the family her husband had chosen for their daughter was not right. The son of the Xia family had a shifty look in his eyes. She mentioned this to her husband several times but was sternly scolded by Ling Yingda.","As an only son, he envied families with many brothers, so he chose a family with five sons for his daughter.","Lady Jiang couldn't persuade her husband. Due to her sense of female propriety, she had no choice but to compromise.","The Xia family was willing to engage with the Ling family's daughter because they had their eyes on the family's wealth.\"","\"Are they trying to scheme for the girl's dowry?\"","\"No, no, no. They are eyeing the entire Ling family's property. Ling Yingda is seriously ill, and the only son in the family is only six years old. As for Lady Jiang and Miss Ling, they are both weak women, and the Xia family doesn't take them seriously at all.\"","\"This doesn't seem right. The people here have a strong sense of clan. Although Ling Yingda's branch is a bit weak, there is still Ling Jijiu.","Ling Yingda's son is young, but he is the heir. With a son to inherit, how dare the Xia family try to seize the Ling family's property? The Ling clan members won't allow it, right?\"","\"What if this son disappears? What if Ling Yingda is left with only an only daughter? Even if she can't inherit all of it, she can still get most of it. If they can also bribe someone from the Ling family, they might really get the vast majority.\"","\"So, the child - snatchers were after that Ling family boy?\"","\"The son of the Xia family hired the child - snatchers. Their purpose was to make his future brother - in - law disappear from the Ling family. Ling Yingda lost his heir, and due to his health, he couldn't have another child.","In the future, they would be the ones to take care of the old couple in their later years.\"","\"There are so many Ling clan members. Can't they adopt a child? In this era, it doesn't seem like daughters are relied on for old - age support, right?\"","\"They have already bribed an elder of the Ling clan. The Xia family has many sons, so they are not short of grandsons. After Miss Ling marries the third son of the Xia family, they will make one of their sons take the Ling surname to inherit the Ling family's incense.\"","\"They are really good at scheming. Indeed, adopting a child from a clan member is not as close as a grandson born to one's own daughter. Ling Yingda, that fool, will probably agree.\"","\"On the original timeline, he did agree. Miss Ling gave birth to a son in her first pregnancy, and the child took the Ling surname as promised. Not long after the child was born, Ling Yingda's condition worsened and he passed away.","Later, Lady Jiang also passed away unexpectedly within a couple of years, and the Ling family's property was completely in the hands of the Xia family.\"","\"Did the Xia family do something to this couple?\"","\"Yes. One year before the fall of the Dayan Kingdom, Miss Ling accidentally found out about this. Without making a sound, she got together some poison. After sending her son away, she used a packet of medicine to send the Xia family and herself to their graves.\"","\"Miss Ling did the right thing. Although she ended up sacrificing herself in the end, this was really the best way for her to take revenge completely.","She also didn't have to suffer the pain of the country's destruction. It can be said that she died a worthy death.","\"What's the deal with the two children from Ling Jijiu's family? Weren't they targeting Ling Yingda's family? Why did they also take away the children from Ling Jijiu's family?\"","[The five - year - old grandson of Ling Jijiu's family took advantage of the open side door of the mansion with no one guarding it and ran out. His seven - year - old sister went out to look for him.]","\"No, no. Although I've never been to Ling Jijiu's family, the layout of wealthy families should be similar. A five - year - old child should still be living with his parents.","How could a little kid pass through the numerous corridors from the inner courtyard to the outer courtyard, and coincidentally, the side door leading to the outside of the mansion was open with no servants guarding it?","This doesn't make sense and is full of oddities. Was it someone's deliberate doing?\"","\"Your Excellency is perceptive. There is indeed someone playing tricks here, but let's not talk about this for now.","After the siblings went out of the mansion one after another, the younger brother went in the direction of the lanterns and happened to run into the child - snatchers carrying Ling Yingda's youngest son out of the alley on the other side.","When the five - year - old Ling Zhi saw his little friend, he shouted. The child - snatchers were startled at first. Seeing that there was no one around at dusk, they picked up Ling Zhi and ran away.","A five - year - old child doesn't understand things yet and thought these people were taking him to play. But when the sister following behind saw her brother being taken away, she ran over to stop them and tried to get her brother back.","But her little arms couldn't match the strength of the adults, and she was also taken away.\"","After hearing the whole story, Ling Yinghua felt sad and felt that tears were about to well up again.","\"These child - snatchers are really bold. The siblings from the Ling family should be dressed in fine clothes. How dare they target such children?","Aren't they afraid that the adults will search the entire capital city to find them?\"","[After Ling Jijiu's family found that the children were missing, they searched for them. Later, they found that the son of a collateral cousin's family was also missing and immediately guessed that the children might have been abducted.","Ling Jijiu immediately reported the case to the yamen, and the constables searched for a whole day and night but couldn't find any trace of the children.]"]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163: Does the master intend to save those three children of the Ling family","paragraphs":["\"These people should be a gang committing crimes. Where are they hiding?\"","[These people are not only a gang, but their leader is also a member of a gang in Shangjing City. Above them, there are even clerks in the yamen acting as their protectors.","The hiding place is even more unexpected to many people. Ling Yinghua borrowed the servants from the families of her relatives and friends to search for the children. They searched for three days and three nights.","The reason why they couldn't find those children was not only because someone was obstructing them, but also because the place where they were hidden was too unexpected.","As the first city in Dayan, the size of Shangjing City is as large as the underground waterway network beneath it.","There are quite a few people living down there, mostly those who commit crimes. If the emperor were to conduct a thorough investigation of the underground water network, he could arrest many wanted criminals.]","A flash of sharp light passed through the eyes of Cai Xian and Wei Ping. They were currently tracking down several fugitives and enemy spies. The information they received was that these people were still in Shangjing City, but they couldn't find where they were hiding, not even a single clue.","Now, after hearing what the divine artifact master said, they thought that the people they were looking for were very likely hiding somewhere in this underground water network.","\"Shouldn't that place be full of sewage? Can people still live there?\"","[It's certainly possible. The water network down there is well - developed. Of course, people can't live in the main waterways. However, some of the tributaries that are severely silted up have been abandoned or artificially diverted by the people living there.","There is an entrance hidden in the well of the broken temple in the south of the city. The so - called 'beggars' living inside just sleep all day long. They don't even beg but can still be well - fed. It's because these people are actually the guards of the entrance pretending to be beggars.","There is also an entrance hidden in the orphanage in the north of the city. The dean has long colluded with those people. Some of the children in the orphanage were finally sent down there by him, either to be thugs or for the amusement of the people below.","In the Chongming Temple in the west of the city, there is also an entrance hidden under a arhat statue behind the side hall.]","\"Xiaozhuzi, what do you mean by someone obstructing?\"","[Normally, the Ling Jijiu family quickly noticed that the children were missing and immediately started mobilizing people to look for them. Those abductors didn't have time to transfer the children underground.","They should have been able to find the children in time. Several times, they passed by the children's hiding place, but they didn't find them. Besides the intentional misleading of the Xia family,","there was also a clan elder of the Ling family who had a vested interest relationship with Brother De, the leader of the child - abducting gang. This Brother De was lame, so his nickname was 'Lame Brother De'.]","\"Those child - abducting people are really immoral. They are extremely immoral. After death, they will surely go to the Avici Hell and suffer for a hundred years.\"","[A grandson of this Ling clan elder, Li Shu, joined Brother De's gang. He often used his convenience in status to gather a lot of official information for Brother De.","On that day, his family also participated in the search for the children. They deliberately covered for the child - abducting people at the place where the children were hiding.","As soon as someone came to that area, they pretended to be searching too and then loudly said that they found nothing unusual.","In this way, they deceived several groups of people. Finally, they covered for those people to enter the underground through the entrance in the Chongming Temple.]","\"This family is at least of the same clan as the Ling Jijiu family. Just because a grandson is involved with Brother De, they help outsiders harm their relatives? The minds of ordinary people are really complicated.\"","[Master, that's because there was a feud between the two families in the previous generation. Sometimes, outsiders are not scary. It's the backstab from so - called relatives that is the most deadly.]","\"What kind of feud? It probably involves nothing more than money and status.\"","[The father of this clan elder and the grandfather of Ling Jijiu had the same father. Ling Jijiu's grandfather was the eldest legitimate son, and the father of this clan elder was the youngest concubine - born son.","Later, Ling Jijiu's great - grandfather had a younger full - brother who died unmarried. He felt sorry for his brother having no descendants and being afraid that no one would offer sacrifices to his spirit after his death, so he adopted his youngest concubine - born son to his younger brother's branch.","Later, when his great - grandfather divided the family property before his death, the main branch got 60% of the property, and the remaining 40% was divided among all the other brothers. The father of the clan elder thought that since he was inheriting the incense of his uncle's branch and was considered an independent branch, he should get more.","Unfortunately, his wish didn't come true. Later, his mother's concubine died unexpectedly. The father of the clan elder thought that Ling Jijiu's grandfather and great - grandmother were behind it, and since then, he hated the eldest branch.","Also, his aunt had an unhappy marriage and died early. His father also blamed the eldest branch for this.","When the clan elder was a child, his father instilled this feud in him. So, although this branch of the family still seemed to be part of the Ling family, they had long been estranged from the main Ling family because of the interest disputes in the previous generation.]","\"Did all these things happen because of Ling Jijiu's grandfather?\"","[No. The old concubine slipped and fell on the icy ground in winter. She was ill for more than half a year and then passed away.","His sister married into the family of his mother's concubine's elder sister. That family embezzled her dowry and took in new concubines. In the end, his sister died of depression.","The father of the clan elder didn't stand up for his sister because of the kinship. After her death, he couldn't get the dowry back, so he blamed Ling Jijiu's grandfather for not helping. ]","\"I guess Ling Jijiu doesn't even know that there is such a big 'enemy' beside him.\"","Ling Jijiu: Who would have thought that the uncle who always smiles when meeting actually always has the intention to take revenge on his family!","[This family later did quite well in Beili after the fall of the Dayan Dynasty because they were the first to surrender and made contributions when the new regime was established.]","\"How did they make contributions during the siege? Did they open the city gate?\"","Emperor Mingxi and his officials all felt a sinking feeling in their hearts. Could the city gate be opened by just anyone?","[There are countless crimes hidden underground in Shangjing City. When foreign enemies invaded, many people down there led the way for the foreign troops, hoping to gain a 'merit of following the new emperor'.","People like Brother De and Li Shu hid some foreign soldiers underground and even dug a waterway leading outside the city. The Dayan army was caught off guard...]","\"Let's not worry about this for now. It was the incompetence of the entire court and the emperor in governing the country that led to the downfall of Dayan. No one can be blamed for this.\"","The officials of the Dayan Dynasty: Sure enough, the young immortal is still as heartless as ever. She never even thought about saving their lives! Doge face JPG","[Master, do you want to save these three children of the Ling family?]","Yue Fuguang thought for a while. Just when everyone thought she would refuse, they heard her say, \"Innocent children should be saved. Later when we go to see the lanterns, we'll pass by the Ling Mansion anyway. Let's go and take a look.\"","[Should we tell Lord Ling?]","\"How can we tell him? Should we say that his grandchildren will be abducted by child - abductors today and will never be found again? Do you think he'll believe it?\"","Ling Yinghua nodded frantically in her heart. Believe, of course I believe. But the premise is that you have to open your mouth first!","[Forget it then. Master is still just a child in their eyes and lacks authority. They probably won't believe the truth even if we tell them.]","The officials of the Dayan Dynasty stared with wide eyes as if their eyes could speak. The same message was conveyed in their eyes: Your master lacks authority?!","In the hearts of these people in the Dayan Dynasty, her words were comparable to the imperial edicts of the emperor."]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164: Thank you, Your Excellency, for saving my life","paragraphs":["Feng Tang, Wu Yong, and others: In our place, this holds even more authority than an imperial decree!","That evening after dinner, when Yue Fuguang mentioned going to the lantern festival, the whole family unanimously agreed. Old Madam Yu and Madam Zhang even had the brothers act as her guards.","Since Yue Fuguang was going, the other girls naturally wanted to go as well. Yu Chongshan thought, it's only once a year; at most, he would just send more guards to protect his granddaughters.","A group of over thirty people set out grandly. As soon as they stepped outside, they were instantly enveloped by the bustling atmosphere.","On the Imperial Street of the capital, as dusk settled, it was already bright as day.","The entire street had transformed into a flowing river of light. On both sides of the imperial way, layers upon layers of various horn lanterns and gauze lanterns converged into a winding fiery dragon, casting a warm, yellowish glow on the bluestone pavement.","Octagonal palace lanterns, adorned with crimson tassels, swayed gently in the evening breeze, scattering shattered spots of light on the ground.","Children bundled in thick cotton-padded jackets, holding candied haws on sticks, followed their parents, their eyes crinkling into crescent moons as they laughed. Delivery boys weaved through the crowd, nearly bumping into young ladies in brocade cloaks who were holding rabbit-shaped lanterns and chatting softly with friends.","The pearl hairpins of the finely dressed young ladies flickered intermittently under the lantern light, interweaving with the shadows, much like the twinkling stars in the sky above.","Scholars gathered before lantern riddle stalls, frowning in contemplation over puzzles like \"Boundless falling leaves rustle down.\" Suddenly, someone would clap their hands, exclaiming the solution, eliciting a mix of frustration and admiration from the crowd.","The air was filled with the sweet scent of preserved fruits and the charred aroma of roasted lamb. Yue Fuguang sniffed the air, and her already full stomach suddenly felt hungry again.","Yu Qingyu, seeing his sister's expression, knew she was craving food again, so he ordered some snacks to be bought for all the siblings.","Sisters Yu Ningxuan, Yu Ningxin, and the others also followed Yue Fuguang's lead and began eating. They rarely had the chance to eat street food throughout the year, so regardless of the taste, they were exceptionally happy.","Especially since this was led by their grandparents' treasured darling, they no longer held back.","The group walked and stopped, eating and strolling, and before they knew it, they had left the main thoroughfare and arrived near the Ling residence.","Yu Ningxuan looked around at the street, slightly dimmer compared to the main road, and couldn't help but ask, \"Fuguang, weren't we going to see the lanterns on the main street? Why are we heading this way?\"","Yue Fuguang looked at the snacks in her sisters' hands and the yet-to-be-consumed delicacies held by the maids behind them. \"Second Sister, if we keep walking on that street, we won't reach it even in an hour. There are many more delicious foods ahead. I'm afraid I won't be able to resist buying more to try, but...\" She patted her round belly. \"I really can't eat any more, yet I fear I'll still want to buy. Out of sight, out of mind—let's take a detour!\"","The Yu siblings: Well, that's a compelling reason. They looked at their own bulging bellies and actually found it quite reasonable!","'Little Pearl, check from which place the child traffickers snatched the Ling family child?'","[Master, it seems the traffickers carried the Ling boy out from an alley, just as his younger brother ran out and saw them. Look, the street you came from is very lively, but here it's quite deserted. Because Ling Yinghua, a high-ranking official, lives here, idlers generally don't come to this area, which is why it's so empty now. The traffickers dared to snatch the two children only because they saw no one around. Master, look for the alley.]","'System, you said Ling Yinghua heard our conversation at the morning court audience. Would he have already kept watch over the children? They probably won't run out as they did in the original history.'","[Host, there really is...]","Before the system could finish saying \"might be,\" they saw the side gate of the Ling residence open, and a chubby little head with two small buns peeked out.","Then a plump boy dressed like a red packet ran out. The gold necklace on his chest flashed with a golden glint under the light of the roadside lanterns.","The chubby boy had only run a few steps forward when he shouted, \"Ah Bao, are you also out to see the lanterns?\"","[Master, it should be just ahead.]","Sure enough, after Yue Fuguang walked a few more steps, she saw an alley ahead, from which three men and two women emerged.","One of the men was holding a boy of about five or six who looked somewhat drowsy.","That should be Ling Yingda's son, Ah Bao.","Upon hearing the Ling boy's words and seeing his wealthy attire, especially the dazzling gold lock on his chest, the group tacitly moved towards him.","But after taking only a few steps, they saw Yue Fuguang's large group approaching from the adjacent road and immediately became somewhat flustered.","However, the leader had clearly seen his share of big scenes. They immediately acted as if nothing was wrong, walking past the Ling boy, intending to leave by another route.","Yue Fuguang would not give them the chance. She immediately ordered, \"Seize them!\"","As soon as Yue Fuguang spoke, several people rushed forward. Before they left, the Old Master had repeatedly instructed them to follow the Seventh Young Lady's arrangements in all matters outside.","As for the Eldest Young Master... he was also to follow the Seventh Young Lady's arrangements!","Yu Qingyu: When little sister goes out to save people, we're just accompanying guests, extras!","The Yu siblings: Only Eldest Brother is. We're just taking the opportunity to come out and have fun thanks to Little Seven. Saving people? We have no idea! Kept in the dark JPG.","\"Stop her! Don't harm the child!\"","It turned out that just as the Yu family guards were about to engage with the traffickers, a little girl of six or seven ran out from the Ling residence's side gate.","She should be Ling Yinghua's young granddaughter who came out looking for her brother.","These people were only a few steps away from the side gate. Seeing the Yu family guards trying to stop them, one of the women immediately thought of grabbing the girl as a hostage.","Fortunately, before the Yu family guards could intervene, a team of guards rushed out from the Ling residence. They swiftly protected the young lady while also blocking the retreat of these people.","\"Seize them!\"","As soon as the little girl saw the leader, she immediately pointed at the red-packet-clad younger brother, who was already surrounded by the Yu family, and said, \"Steward Grandpa, younger brother!\"","Steward Ling, though he didn't recognize the Yu family, could tell from the attire of the group of young masters and ladies that they were nobles. From a distance, he cupped his hands and said, \"Ling Wu thanks you all for saving our young lady and young master. May I ask...\"","Before he could finish asking which family they were from, so that his master could later pay a visit to express thanks, the side gate behind him opened again. A group of people in fine clothes hurriedly walked out.","The leader was none other than Ling Yinghua. At first glance, he saw Yue Fuguang and promptly cupped his hands. \"Greetings to the Junior Mentor.\"","\"Libationer Ling, we were passing by and saw these people carrying a child, acting suspiciously, so we wanted to stop them.\" Yue Fuguang said, glancing around. The five had already been completely apprehended.","She continued, \"They resisted arrest and even tried to take your granddaughter as a hostage. We'll leave the rest to you.\"","She waved her hand, preparing to leave. \"No need for thanks. We just happened to pass by and ran into this. We're off now; this Junior Mentor still needs to see the lantern festival!\"","[Master, how did Old Man Ling come out so quickly?]","\"Thank you, Junior Mentor, for saving the three children of my Ling family. If not for your appearance, the guards of my residence wouldn't have discovered the children were missing so quickly. Ling, on behalf of the whole family, thanks the Junior Mentor for the lifesaving grace!\""]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165: Little Bead, Take It Easy","paragraphs":["The men and women behind him followed his lead, bowing in respect.","Yue Fuguang accepted their gesture with graceful composure, smiling lightly. \"It was a matter of chance and timing that we happened upon the situation. It was also good fortune for your young son and daughter. As for saving their lives, I wouldn't go that far.\"","[Master, why wouldn't you go that far? Among these kidnapped children, aside from the rare few sold to families desperate for a child, most meet a rather grim fate. You've altered the tragic destiny of his grandchildren. How is that different from saving their lives?]","'I'm just being modest. Besides, they don't know that if we hadn't passed by, their two children would already be missing by now.'","Ling Yinghua: I, however, know everything. Therefore, this life-saving favor must be repaid handsomely!","Upon hearing this, the expressions of Madam Ling and his son behind him changed instantly. But mindful of Yue Fuguang's presence, they held their tongues, merely gazing at her with grateful eyes as if she were a living Bodhisattva.","Yue Fuguang had done all this for the mission and couldn't quite bear such looks. Time to make an exit, off she went!","The Ling family watched as Yue Fuguang and her group walked into the distance. Ling Yinghua turned around, his smiling face instantly turning stern the moment his back was to them. His sweeping gaze over the crowd was cold enough to freeze, his skill in switching expressions practiced to perfection.","\"Ah Wu, seal the manor gates. Without my order, not even a mouse is to enter or leave.\"","\"Yes, Master!\"","Ling Yinghua continued, \"Send two men to escort Ah Bao back to Yingda's residence and explain everything that happened to him clearly.\"","After giving these instructions, he turned to look at the five individuals bound tightly. \"Bring a few men and follow me to the Ministry of Justice!\"","He surmised that Wei Ping and Cai Xian were likely already waiting for them in the ministry's prison cells. When it came to interrogation and extracting confessions through force, there was no place more suitable than there.","Ling Yinghua looked at the three men and two women as if they were already dead. In the original history, it was these very people who had kidnapped his pair of grandchildren. In this lifetime, they must repay with their lives to appease the hatred in his heart!","\"Madam, I leave the household in your hands!\"","\"Rest assured, Master!\" Madam Ling's face, usually kind and gentle, was now equally icy.","Seeing the husband and wife like this sent a shiver of apprehension through the gathered servants.","Meanwhile, for Yue Fuguang and her siblings, it was a scene of peaceful tranquility.","\"Fuguang, it's all thanks to you this time. Otherwise, those Ling children would have suffered terribly!\"","Yu Ningxuan still felt a lingering fear.","The youngest, Yu Ningjin, added, \"Is the outside world really this dangerous? No wonder Grandmother rarely lets us go out.\"","Yu Ningrong disagreed and retorted, \"Don't be silly. Can't you just bring more people when you go out?\"","Yu Ningxuan said, \"Little Eighth's words aren't pleasant, but the reasoning is sound. We can't possibly stay cooped up at home forever. However, bringing more guards when going out is a must. All of you remember, never go out with just a few maids and old nannies. In a critical moment, they are utterly useless.\"","Yu Ningzi, Yu Ninglin, and the other sisters all nodded hurriedly.","The others were fine, but the situation for the few from the third branch was a bit awkward. As Yue Fuguang's closest blood relatives, because of their father and his official wife, their relationship with Yue Fuguang remained rather distant. This was especially true towards Brother Ningchen and Brother Hao; even her own brothers seemed invisible to her.","Yue Fuguang: Indeed, she treated those two brothers like air, just as they had treated her in the beginning. As for these two sisters, she truly treated them the same as her cousins from other branches, with impartiality and no favoritism.","Aside from exchanging a few more words with the naturally sociable Yu Ningxuan on usual days, she mostly stayed in her own courtyard, having little interaction with these siblings.","In her previous life, she was an only child at first. Later, after her parents remarried and she had half-siblings from both sides, she still managed to live as if she were an only child. High school friends scattered and rarely kept in touch; in university, she didn't live on campus and never made close friends. So, when it came to fostering sisterly bonds, she really had no experience.","Well, it mainly had to do with her personality. Ultimately, it boiled down to the 'solitary' nature within her character.","Yue Fuguang had no desire to change. After all, their sisterly bonds, with or without her, didn't affect her life.","Nevertheless, she added, \"Guards are important, but you yourselves should also learn more skills. Whoever masters them well, in the future, I'll take them along to make a fortune.\"","Yu Ningxuan was the first to play along eagerly. \"Fuguang, making a fortune sounds great! Tell us quickly how you'll take us to do it!\"","Yu Ningxin and the others, even the most proud and defiant Yu Ningrong who was usually full of objections, pricked up their ears.","This was one good thing about the Yu family young ladies: they didn't treat money as if it were dirt. If they liked it, they liked it, without any pretense.","Yue Fuguang briefly outlined her plans: growing flowers, fruits, and vegetables; making perfumes; brewing wine; planting cotton, weaving cloth, and building factories.","The Yu sisters listened with exclamations of amazement, their eyes sparkling with obvious interest.","\"Let me be clear first. I treat everyone equally here. I only want capable people. What I'll give you isn't wages, it's a share of the profits.\"","She said with confidence, \"Believe me, these profit shares will be enough for you to secure your footing in your future husbands' households, even without using your family dowries.\"","In any era, wealth can become a person's backbone. With money and resources in hand, one can even speak louder—of course, this doesn't apply to those hopeless cases who can't be helped no matter what!","Hearing this, the sisters grew even more excited, twisting their handkerchiefs into knots, especially Yu Ningrong. She understood better than the others the importance of money in the inner courtyards.","The Yu Qingyu brothers watched with envious eyes. Their younger sister was usually rather aloof with all her siblings, and that included her three own brothers. Now that she was planning to 'play' with their other cousins, they felt quite envious. When would she include them too?","Was it because they weren't useful enough yet?","After some self-reflection, the brothers all felt they needed to study harder. Meanwhile, Yu Boming, who had been tossed into the military camp, suddenly felt a surge of superiority. He was surely the most useful among the brothers! In the future, he would definitely help Fuguang guard the cotton fields!","Yu Qingyu glanced at Yu Boming, who looked as if he thought he was the greatest, and silently turned his head away. He didn't know this brother!","Chatting and laughing, the siblings arrived at Vermilion Bird Street, where the lantern festival was held.","From a distance, Yue Fuguang saw a massive Ao Mountain Lantern, five or six meters high, placed before the Vermilion Bird Gate. Artisans had fashioned a celestial mountain with pavilions from bamboo frames, covered with thin silk that emitted a hazy glow. The revolving lanterns inside depicted stories like the Jade Emperor riding clouds and Chang'e flying to the moon, the images shifting within the light and shadows.","In the adjacent Jade Belt River, lotus flower lanterns floated, their candle wax dripping into the emerald waves. They carried the lantern-releasers' beautiful wishes for the future and earnest hopes for their families' smooth sailing, drifting far away with the current.","Yue Fuguang walked on and suddenly stopped before an old man selling dough figurines. His fingers flew, and in the blink of an eye, he had molded a colorful figurine of a chubby baby in a red bellyband holding a carp.","Beside him, a lady skilled in paper-cutting wielded her scissors like the wind. Colored paper fluttered down, and in moments, the unfolded pattern in her hands revealed a window decoration of magpies alighting on plum blossoms.","Further ahead were various food stalls. She noticed one particularly popular wonton stall, common yet surrounded by a crowd. In the depths of winter, steam billowed from the boiling pot, shattering the light from the lanterns overhead into fragments.","Further afield were vendors selling puppets, shadow play performers, and craftsmen blowing sugar figurines. The clang of gongs, the cries of hawkers, and the cheers of the crowd wove together into a bustling symphony of the marketplace.","\"Master!\"","\"Be patient, Little Pearl!\""]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166: So Many People Want Her Dead","paragraphs":["Yu Qingyu saw his younger sister suddenly stand still, head tilted up as if looking at the lanterns, but her eyes were darting around. She wasn't really looking at the lanterns; she was observing their surroundings.","Hearing her whispered \"Stay calm,\" his heart skipped a beat. His previously relaxed mind instantly tensed, and he began discreetly scanning the area.","With his experience, he hadn't detected anything unusual, but the three brothers still silently directed the guards to form a protective circle around the sisters.","They were completely surrounded by crowds at that moment, which was indeed very dangerous.","\"Fuguang, how about we go rest at the tavern up ahead?\" Yu Qingyu asked his sister, his eyes still fixed on the passersby around them.","\"Good, good, I really am a bit tired,\" Yu Ningxuan chimed in before Yue Fuguang could say much more, nodding in agreement.","She even hooked her arm through Yue Fuguang's, pulling her close to shield her.","Yu Boming wanted to say he wasn't tired, but a sharp glance from his sister stopped him.","Her intuition had always been sharp since childhood. Right now, she felt extremely uneasy, her hair standing on end, instinctively sensing danger approaching.","The other members of the Yu family, especially the young ladies, were on such a long outing for the first time and were genuinely tired, so they all nodded, wanting to go to the tavern for a late-night snack.","Before the Yu family could move towards a less crowded area, the sound of sheng and xiao flutes suddenly rose. From a distance, they saw a dragon dance troupe parting the sea of people, heading straight in their direction.","Golden scales churned in the ocean of light, and wherever the dragon pearl passed, cheers surged like waves.","Thousands of lanterns connected into a Milky Way in the night sky, even turning the icicles on the eaves into a crystal curtain.","Amidst this brilliant sea of lights, the faces of the revelers on the street were all adorned with smiles. Yet, within these smiles, a flash of blade light passed by, causing some to instinctively close their eyes, dazzled.","Yue Fuguang only heard the sound of something cutting through the air behind her. Alarm bells screamed in her mind—was this attack aimed at me?","'Little Pearl!'","[Master, I'm here!] The system, distressed, hastily raised a protective shield, enveloping all the siblings inside.","Immediately after, Yue Fuguang heard the clashing sounds of weapons coming from behind them.","A fight had broken out!","With guards holding the line around them, Yu Qingyu and the others protected their sisters as they moved towards the shops ahead. Many others had the same idea, and the area instantly became congested.","The assassins were dumbfounded. The person they wanted to kill was behind layers of human walls. She couldn't get out or run, and they couldn't get in or catch her!","The more ruthless ones thought about cutting their way through, but... there were simply too many people. They couldn't kill them all, absolutely impossible!","\"Hua Jiu, take those with good qinggong and fly in!\" the leader in black commanded.","Their earlier arrows had all been blocked. If they didn't send reinforcements inside soon, the few who had infiltrated the innermost area would quickly be captured.","[Master, the paper-cutting artist's scissors are coated with a deadly poison.]","'You can't neutralize it?'","[A mere mortal's poison? Wouldn't even require half a detox pill.]","[That dough figurine seller is quite skilled with hidden weapons, a pity he's about to die. It's good Master didn't buy wontons from that stall, otherwise he would have surely put the poison in the broth.]","'I'm not stupid. Once I saw they were suspicious, why would I buy their food to eat!'","Yu Qingyu really wanted to ask his sister how she had spotted these people as suspicious. He hadn't detected at all that these street performers were actually assassins.","Yu Ningxuan felt the same. They had even wanted to buy dough figurines to play with earlier!","Yue Fuguang: Having watched too many modern detective novels and videos, I can't claim to be Sherlock Holmes, but I tend to be more observant and sensitive to details than others.","Putting other things aside, the weakest point of these people was their disguise. The dough figurine maker was clearly a young man but insisted on disguising himself as an old man—at least he should have taken care of his neck and hands!","Opposite to the dough figurine maker, the paper-cutting artist was clearly a woman in her thirties but insisted on making herself look eighteen. She should have at least toned down that 'killing intent' born from having seen countless people!","[Master, why are these people trying to assassinate you? Did you offend someone?]","Yue Fuguang: Wouldn't you know better if I've offended anyone? In the past few months, the two of them have sent nearly a thousand people to prison.","In the Danyan court recently, every few days a high official disappears and a new one replaces them. Where did those people go? They've all gathered in prison.","As for those who have reported to the King of Hell, inside and outside the court, there are at least a hundred people combined.","But these were all done covertly. As for overt offenses, she counted on her fingers—over the last two or three months, she had indeed offended quite a few!","She, a lazy person, really wasn't the type to pick fights! The mission made the first move!","She made a bold guess and cautiously sought confirmation. 'Are these people from the Night-Blooming Cereus?'","[The personnel composition is a bit complex. The old man and the paper-cutter are one group, the wonton seller and the customer are another, and those few onlookers are yet another.","If your grandfather hadn't assigned the Yu family's top martial artists to accompany you, someone might have truly gotten hurt.]","Yue Fuguang: !!!","So many people wanted her life?","This was the first time she realized she was so hated. Looking at those people, desperate to charge over yet blocked layer by layer, she suddenly understood the satisfaction in that saying: \"I just love the look on your face when you can't stand me but can't do anything about it.\"","She looked around. Indeed, the Yu family guards currently had the upper hand. 'Give these guys extra chicken legs when we get home!'","[Careful, someone's about to fly in!]","'These bobbing heads are going to become their stepping stones! No good, there are too many people here, easy to cause collateral damage.'","\"Big brother, let's move back, draw these people away!\"","Yu Qingyu saw her point immediately and ordered the protective circle to retreat, moving away from the crowd, while simultaneously firing a distress signal.","\"Big brother, you had this thing? Why only use it now?\" Yu Ningxuan asked curiously.","\"I wanted to buy more time, afraid they'd run if they saw us calling for reinforcements.\"","Since the assassins were targeting Fuguang, they needed to capture as many alive as possible. Otherwise, if they all escaped, they wouldn't even know who was behind the attack. How could they retaliate?","Over the past few months, subtly taught by the Yu family men, Yu Qingyu and his brothers were clearly racing down the path of being wolves in sheep's clothing.","[Master, do you have any guesses about the masterminds behind these groups of assassins?]","'Among those I've offended who have the capability to do this, Prince Qi and his faction count as one, the foreign tribal high priests and shamans count as one, and if we're stretching it, the Sima family counts as one.","I suspect they found out about me warning the Bao family that assassins would try to kidnap the bride.","The incident with the Ling family today was too sudden. Even if we offended that 'Virtueless Brother,' their retaliation wouldn't come this fast or this urgently.'","While Yue Fuguang was still making various guesses, the situation outside had changed dramatically. Wei Ping and Cai Xian each led a team of men running over from two different directions.","Seeing them sweating profusely in the cold weather showed how urgently they had rushed.","Wei Ping, Cai Xian: How could we not be urgent? Hearing that the Junior Preceptor was assassinated at the lantern festival nearly scared our souls out of our bodies!","Who had such audacity? This was going to cause an earth-shattering uproar!","If the Junior Preceptor got even a scratch, being stripped of our official robes would be the least of our worries."]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167: Is the system going to lose its home before Dayan even falls","paragraphs":["Before Wei Ping and Cai Xian could even give the order to apprehend these men, Huo Ying and Wei Shouyi, who had arrived later but surged ahead, had already drawn their blades and charged into the fray.","Ah! These two have no regard for martial etiquette! Wei Ping and Cai Xian could only reach out helplessly in their minds, like a classic meme.","The two men charged in, directly intercepting Yue Fuguang's intended retreat path, instantly surrounding the dozen or so who were still resisting. In moments, they were all subdued.","Watching from across the crowd of panicked people they couldn't push through, Wei Ping and Cai Xian were fuming. Damn it! The credit for 'rescuing the imperial envoy' right under their noses was snatched by these two. How infuriating!","Ignoring the resentment from Wei Ping and Cai Xian, the two quickly scanned the crowd. Aside from a few guards from the Yu residence who suffered minor wounds, the Junior Mentor protected at the center didn't have a single hair out of place. They felt somewhat relieved.","But Huo Ying still asked anxiously, \"Junior Mentor, are you unharmed? We arrived late to your aid, we beg your forgiveness!\"","Yue Fuguang waved a dismissive hand. \"I'm fine. How did you get here so quickly?\"","Huo Ying's heart stirred, and he quickly replied, \"It was a coincidence. Chancellor Ling captured several child traffickers. After interrogation by Lord Wei, we discovered they were part of an organized operation.","Moreover, they had over thirty children in their custody. We were thus ordered by His Majesty to assist in apprehending the criminals.\"","Wei Shouyi added, \"We were just on our way to Chongming Temple, as there's reportedly a stronghold there. We happened to be passing by when we heard there was an assassination attempt on the Junior Mentor here, so we brought men over immediately.\"","[Master, what a fortunate coincidence indeed. Otherwise, we would have had to wait a while longer for rescue.]","\"Since you have a mission to attend to, you should hurry along. I should be safe here now, no need to worry.\"","Apprehending the people at Chongming Temple was important—those were all her points! Not a single one could be allowed to escape!","Seeing Yue Fuguang's insistence, the two finally left ten men behind to protect her safety.","Next came Cai Xian and Wei Ping, who finally broke through the encirclement. Seeing Yue Fuguang was unharmed, their hearts, which had been in their throats, finally settled. Yue Fuguang urged them to hurry and capture the criminals. Unable to refuse, they each also left some of their men to ensure her safety.","Yue Fuguang's guard detail suddenly swelled in number.","This series of events, from the arrival of these officials to their departure, left all members of the Yu family—except for Yu Qingyu who had some idea of the situation—utterly stunned.","From the masters to the guards, everyone knew their Little Seven / Seventh Young Miss was the Junior Mentor of Dayan, a proper official with a court rank who attended morning audiences.","But she wasn't the only one in their family who attended court. However, to command the kind of presence just witnessed? That was unique to the person before them.","Even if their grandfather / the family head were here, these two Ministers, one Chief Minister, and one General wouldn't be this deferential and courteous!","Their grandfather's superior, Lord Lu Qi, was only of equal rank to Ministers Cai and Huo.","Yet, officials of such high standing showed such enthusiastic courtesy to their Little Seven / Seventh Young Miss. Watching it filled them with pride, the shock of the assassination attempt nearly drowned out by an inexplicable excitement.","Though they didn't fully understand why their family member seemed to hold a status even higher than their grandfather / the family head, a glimmer of realization dawned on everyone. With her here, the Yu residence was poised to soar!","It was also at this moment that the younger generation of the Yu family truly saw the difference between themselves and this sister/cousin.","Even the most resentful Yu Ningrong had to tuck away her competitive thoughts. She couldn't even compare to Second Branch's Yu Ningxuan, let alone this one!","Everyone finally began to grasp, just a little, why she was considered the treasure of the Yu household.","Yue Fuguang paid no mind to what Yu Ningrong or other members of the Yu family thought. Everything she did was for the points, after all.","Before leaving, Yue Fuguang glanced at the people on the street and said to the steward who had hurried over, \"Steward Fu, ensure all the injured here receive proper treatment. I'll cover all expenses.\"","Yu Youfu smiled and said, \"The Master has already instructed that medical expenses will be covered from the household's public funds. There's no need for you to pay, Young Miss.","Please hurry back to the residence with the young masters and young misses. The Master and the Old Madam are terribly worried.\"","He joked lightly, \"If the family hadn't held him back, the Master would have come with this old servant.\"","Before he finished speaking, they saw Yu Chongshan in the distance, accompanied by Yu Zhongchun and his three brothers, walking hurriedly towards them with anxious expressions on their faces.","...","[Host, stop sleeping! Get up and look, something major has happened!]","Yue Fuguang shifted in her warm blankets. \"System, I don't have court today! As long as I'm not late for work, what major event could possibly concern me?\"","Even if she were late for court, the system wouldn't need to make such a fuss. Who were they, after all? If she were late, could Emperor Mingxi really dock her salary?","Come to think of it, after working for so long, she hadn't personally collected her salary yet. How much was a Junior Mentor's salary anyway...","[Host, I'm not lying. You really need to check. Something major has truly happened!]","The system's voice, anxious to the point of distortion, echoed in her mind, making Yue Fuguang shake her head involuntarily.","She played along verbally, \"What is it, what is it? What major event?\"","Swallowing a yawn, her large eyes brimming with sleepy tears, she kept asking, giving the system all the emotional support it could want.","[The Main System... the Main System is under attack?!]","The Main System is under attack? What does that mean? Judging by the system's tone full of question marks, it didn't seem very sure either.","If she remembered correctly, the Main System was like the king in the kingdom of systems.","Their king was under attack...","\"The Main System is attacked, is the system kingdom going bankrupt... no, going to fall?\"","Was the system going to lose its home before Dayan even fell?","[Well... it's probably not that bad!]","\"Then why are you so panicked? The emperor isn't worried, but the eunuch is?\"","Yue Fuguang relaxed. If the system was fine, she was fine.","[Hmph, I'm not like that old Qian Gui!]","\"How does a crippled... little system like you know the Main System is under attack? Did it issue a system-wide announcement?\"","Yue Fuguang wanted to say that you and Qian Gui were both incomplete entities, neither should look down on the other.","Qian Gui: Is this the legendary being implicated for no reason?","[No, not that. I sensed it myself. I felt the Main System come under a powerful attack from some force!]","Yue Fuguang narrowed her eyes. How could her crippled system sense the Main System being attacked?","Weren't they in different dimensions?","\"Did only you sense it, or did other systems sense it too?\"","[I don't know if other systems sensed it. I just felt the force of this attack was very strong, and it was filled with malice.","It must have been those Black Systems!]","Black Systems? The antagonists in the system world? Yue Fuguang wanted to ask, but felt this wasn't the right moment.","So she followed the system's line of thought. \"Will this attack affect us, our mission?\"","[The Main System is very powerful. These attacks probably won't harm it, but system data transmission will likely be affected!]","\"What part of system transmission affects us? Mission completion evaluation or point calculation and distribution?\"","Those were the most important things to her.","[It will affect the System Mall. The data transmission interruption will halt item delivery.]","[Oh my god! Why didn't you say so earlier!]"]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168: Little Pearl Has Some Gossip Here, Master, Do You Want to Get Up and Hear It","paragraphs":["It was said that the child was being sent to his maternal grandparents' home to stay for a while. When sending the child off, Xue Chao, with great carelessness, only assigned five people to accompany him, one of whom was Xue Ju's personal page boy.","When Xue Ju later returned to the Xue family, he described his disappearance vaguely and incompletely. It wasn't until a major event occurred afterward that people, looking back and piecing together the known information, gradually reconstructed the course of Xue Ju's disappearance.","Three days before the Lantern Festival, eight-year-old Xue Ju, along with one page boy and four servants dispatched by his father, set off for his maternal grandparents' home.","Xue Ju's maternal grandparents lived in Rongcheng, two hundred li away from the capital city, Shangjing.","Why not stay at the Marquis's estate to celebrate the Lantern Festival before leaving?","His father, Xue Chao, gave him the reason that celebrating the Lantern Festival at his maternal grandparents' home would make the two elderly people happier.","As for the actual circumstances behind it, presumably only Xue Chao himself knew best.","The named Xue Chao wore a look of dejection, ignoring the glances his colleagues inadvertently cast his way.","Only the two gazes from above made him feel as if needles were pricking his back, breaking out in a cold sweat.","He recalled how, before the New Year, his brother-in-law (from his second marriage) had sought him out, saying their family wanted a grandson with a noble title. The reason they were willing to marry their sister to him, a widower, was precisely because they saw his family possessed a hereditary title that could bring blessings to descendants.","If this demand had been raised when they were first discussing the marriage, he might have refused the match. But with the wedding just over a month away and the wedding invitations already sent out, Xue Chao found himself in a difficult position.","There was an even more important point: he had met the Liu family girl several times and had to admit that, whether in appearance or temperament, she suited Xue Chao's preferences perfectly.","He couldn't deny that compared to the strong-willed nature of his late wife, Lady Liao, he preferred this Lady Liu, who was in the prime of her youth, gentle and lovely, and looked at him with eyes full of admiration.","He had asked his brother-in-law, Liu Yuzhou, at the time what Lingniang thought about this matter. Liu Yuzhou told him that his sister was filial and would follow all arrangements made by their parents.","After returning to the estate, Xue Chao pondered for three days. Later, upon hearing that his eldest son had gotten into a fight with Da Ge'er, the son of his second brother, anger rose within him. The long-undecided resolution seemed to finally find an excuse at that moment to send his son away.","The five of them traveled in two carriages. They hadn't gone far, only about ten li out of the city, when they stopped at a roadside tea shed to rest and drink tea...","When they woke up again, they found themselves in a different place, tied up with ropes, surrounded by children only a few years old. Xue Ju immediately realized that the tea shed where they had stopped was a den of iniquity.","Those people were likely lookouts stationed outside the city by the villain known as Que De Ge. They probably saw that Xue Ju's party of four only had one young master and one teenage boy, yet they were driving two carriages.","Judging by the deep ruts the carriage wheels left in the muddy ground, the carriages seemed to be carrying a considerable load. Greed overcame them, leading them to disregard the obvious signs that these people came from a powerful and noble family, and they kidnapped them.","After the Lantern Festival, Xue Ju, along with three children from the Ling family, was secretly smuggled out of the city. The batch of children was then sold off separately to places far from Shangjing.","\"Little Pearl, is what you're saying true?\"","\"These are all speculations by outsiders. The truth is, the carriage taking Xue Ju to his maternal grandparents' home didn't get far out of the city before arriving at a mountain hollow, where several people were already waiting.","Upon seeing these men, the four men driving the carriages jumped down without a word and left without looking back, leaving only the unsuspecting Xue Ju and his page boy on the carriage.","By the time the two were taken to Que De Ge's lair, it was already too late to escape.\"","\"Was Xue Ju given to the traffickers by his own family? No, not given! Weren't there two carriage-loads of things? They practically paid the traffickers to take him.","Who did it? Xue Chao or Xue Yao?\"","The faces of the Xue father and son had now turned from pale to deathly white, with cold sweat slowly beading on their foreheads.","\"Master, guess what is most important in the eyes of the Xue family?\"","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and said, \"The hereditary title?\"","\"Correct, the hereditary title. With the title comes status, power, and wealth. The Xue family has only one title, and it is currently set in stone that Xue Chao, who has already been petitioned to be the heir-apparent, will inherit it.","But the Xue family has more than just him as a son. Xue Yao currently has five sons: four by his principal wife and one by a concubine.","Let's not mention the younger brother born of a concubine; he's the youngest and a son of a concubine, so it certainly won't be his turn.","Do you think Xue Chao's other three brothers want this title or not?\"","\"Was Xue Ju essentially sold off by his own uncles, who even paid for the deal? They are, after all, Xue Chao's full brothers by the same mother. Even if they wanted to seize the title, shouldn't they first target the heir-apparent, Xue Chao?","Why go directly for the third generation?","Even without Xue Ju, isn't Xue Chao, who is about to marry, still capable of having more sons by his principal wife?","He's not infertile. If you have the hen that lays eggs, why fear not having eggs?\"","Xue Yao closed his eyes, his face somewhat ashen. His worst fear had come to pass. To quell the ambitions of those sons of his, he had early on petitioned for the eldest to be named heir-apparent, hoping to settle the matter. Little did he think they had never given up their aspirations.","Xue Chao, the \"egg-laying\" one, though his complexion was poor, also felt that the Little Immortal Lord's words, though crude, held truth. As long as he was alive, even without Ju Ge'er, he could still have other sons.","Thinking this, his heart sank. Would his dear brothers next move against him?","Directly eliminate him? And what about Father... Xue Chao looked at Xue Yao. Both father and son understood the other's meaning.","Before they could ponder further, they heard the voice of the Divine Artifact say, \"Master, what if Xue Chao is not the current Marchioness's son? What if Xue Chao could no longer father children in the future?\"","Xue Yao closed his eyes. Xue Chao's eyes widened in disbelief as he stared at his father.","Could it be that his mother's lack of closeness to him wasn't because he had been raised in his grandmother's quarters since childhood? That his brothers' distance wasn't due to this reason and their grandmother's favoritism?","And also... what did it mean that he could no longer father children?","He already had Ju Ge'er and Rui Jier. If Lady Liao hadn't died with her unborn child, he would also have a second son named Minggui Ge'er by now.","He... How could he be infertile?!","Xue Chao stared fixedly at his father, Xue Yao, desperately hoping for an answer.","Xue Yao, under the piercing gaze of his eldest son, kept his eyes tightly shut, not daring to face him.","\"What does 'not the Marchioness's son' mean? Is this Xue Chao like Xi Ling, with a birth mother who married someone else?","And what does 'cannot have children' mean? Xue Chao seems quite healthy, and having Xue Ju and Xue Rui proves he has fertility.\"","Xue Chao nodded frantically in his heart. Yes, yes! He has a son and a daughter. How could he suddenly be incapable!","\"Master, let's address the first point. Xue Chao is indeed somewhat similar to Xi Ling, but Xue Chao's birth mother is dead, not remarried.","His birth mother was originally a young lady from a wealthy family named Jiang Wan, whom Xue Yao met while stationed near the border with Nanzhao. The two fell in love at first sight and married upon meeting again.","The following year, she became pregnant with Xue Chao. Just as she was nearing her due date, the Nanzhao army launched a night raid on the border town. Jiang Wan, frightened, went into premature and difficult labor. She desperately gave birth to Xue Chao but died shortly after due to massive hemorrhaging.\""]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169: Find Your Own Way Home","paragraphs":["Xue Chao staggered. Xue Yao seemed to be back in that desperate night again. He was away on a military campaign. When he returned to the mansion after repelling the Nanzhao army, he only saw the blood all over the bed, his dying wife, and his son wailing as if he knew he was about to lose his mother.","\"Since that's the case, why have I never heard that the current Marquise of Pingyue is a stepmother? There isn't even a bit of news leaking out that Xue Chao isn't her biological son.\"","[Because very few people knew about this matter. Later, because Xue Yao was afraid that he couldn't raise the child alone, he married his current wife, a young lady from the wealthy Yang family in the border town, at the strong persuasion of others.]","\"Xue Yao was the future Marquis at that time. Even with a child to take care of, he shouldn't have married a merchant's daughter.","This era is different from modern times. In the hierarchy of scholars, farmers, artisans, and merchants, the combination of a scholar and a merchant always makes one feel that there's something fishy going on.\"","[Even if there is something, only the Marquise and Marquis of Pingyue know about it. It only took two months from the engagement to the wedding of the two.","Xue Chao got a stepmother before he was one year old.","At first, Yang Shi did take good care of Xue Chao until the family of three returned to the Marquis Mansion when the child was almost three years old.","After returning to the Marquis Mansion, as the eldest grandson, Xue Chao was directly taken to the courtyard of the Marquise who knew the truth to be raised.","Another year later, Yang Shi's brothers passed the imperial examinations, and the whole family moved from the border town to the capital city. In the same year, Yang Shi was pregnant and gave birth to her first son the next year. In the following three years, she gave birth to Xue Yao's third and fourth sons in succession.]","\"Little Pearl, since you mentioned Yang Shi's natal family, have you forgotten to mention Jiang Wan's family? She was also a wealthy young lady. Haven't they come to see their grandson Xue Chao all these years?\"","[Master, this has something to do with Jiang Wan's background. When she met Xue Yao, she was basically alone. Although she brought servants and a considerable amount of wealth, she was truly the only master.","And her real identity is not from Dayan.]","\"From Nanzhao?\" After all, they met at the border between Dayan and Nanzhao.","[Jiang Wan is not from Nanzhao, but from Nanyue. At that time, the old emperor of Nanzhao had just died, and there was a fierce power struggle among the upper - class. The Jiang family was purged because they took the wrong side.","Jiang Wan fled to Nanzhao with her family. Later, because of an informer, the Jiang family was still being chased. She got separated from her family with the servants and accidentally came to Dayan.","Before she could settle down, she met Xue Yao, fell in love at first sight, and got married on the second meeting.]","\"Did Xue Yao know her identity as a Nanyue person?\"","This is also what the emperor and his ministers of Dayan want to know, because Nanyue was one of the countries that destroyed Dayan.","In the past, if they heard such things, they wouldn't think much of it. There weren't many inter - marriages among the upper - classes of different countries, but there were still some.","They didn't care much about it. But after knowing that the destruction of Dayan was also due to the role of spies and internal - external collusion and the heavy blow it brought to Dayan, Emperor Mingxi and his ministers had to be cautious.","Moreover, the territory of Dayan has been described by these two young masters as being penetrated like a sieve many times, so they can't help but be more suspicious.","At this time, even though Wei Ping slowed down his report in the court, he had already said everything he needed to say.","Emperor Mingxi then looked at Xue Yao, the Marquis of Pingyue, and said, \"Lord Xue, I heard that your grandson was also abducted by child - snatchers. Why haven't I seen anyone from your mansion looking for him?\"","Xue Yao quickly stepped forward and replied, \"Your Majesty, my second grandson was indeed among the thirty - seven children who were rescued.","My son and I only found out that the grandson we thought we had sent to his maternal grandfather's house had been abducted by child - snatchers when Lord Huo sent the child to our mansion.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded and said, \"The inheritance of descendants is a major matter, not only for a family but also for a country. It cannot be ignored.","A young master of the Marquis Mansion was abducted, but the head of the family didn't know about it. How can one govern the country if one can't even keep one's family in order? You, as the grandfather and father, should also reflect on yourselves.\"","Xue Yao bowed even lower and said, \"Your Majesty's lesson is right. I will definitely investigate thoroughly.\"","Xue Chao also bowed and didn't dare to say a word.","[Master, what do you think Xue Yao's expression will be when he finds out that it was his sons who colluded to do this?","He didn't know Jiang Wan's background at first, but when Xue Chao was six years old, Jiang's family came to the door, and Xue Yao then knew that Jiang Wan was from a noble family in Nanyue.","He was afraid that if Xue Chao knew the truth, it would affect the already weak brotherly relationship among his sons. So he persuaded Jiang's family not to tell the truth and applied for Xue Chao to be the heir apparent that year.","That year, Xue Yue, Xue Yao's second son, was not even one year old yet.]","\"Jiang Wan is from a noble family in Nanyue? How noble is it?\"","[The current Empress Dowager Jiang Yu of Nanyue is her cousin.]","\"Their family was purged because they took the wrong side. How can there still be a cousin who is the Empress Dowager?\"","[It's true that they were purged because they supported the Prince of Wu. But her cousin was in love with the Prince of Cheng at that time. When the Jiang family was in trouble, the Prince of Cheng took her cousin Jiang Yu into his mansion as a concubine.","Later, the older brothers above fought so fiercely that some died and some were injured. The Prince of Wu, who had originally won, also died.","The Prince of Cheng didn't do much but ended up on the throne. Jiang Yu became the Noble Consort De because of her son, and later when her son ascended the throne, she became the Empress Dowager from the Noble Consort De.]","The Great Yan Dynasty was destroyed in the hands of this emperor.","The Jiang father and son completely collapsed to the ground. Especially Jiang Chao, because the current Emperor of Nanyue was now his maternal cousin!","Emperor Mingxi was taken aback. He never expected that there was such a relationship between the Xue family and the Emperor of Nanyue.","\"Does Xue Yao know all this?\"","[The Jiang family only showed up once when Xue Chao was six years old. At that time, Jiang Yu was still the Noble Consort De. However, Xue Yao should be able to guess it.]","The current situation of Xue Yao and Xue Chao was like that of a family in Xia during a certain special period having overseas relatives. They were the key targets to be guarded against and investigated.","\"Do the other brothers of the Xue family know about this?\"","[It's not clear whether they know or not, but Yang Shi should know something. After all, when the Jiang family came to the door, as the wife of the heir apparent, she couldn't have not been present.]","\"So they didn't dare to directly kill Xue Chao, but instead targeted his son?\"","[That should be right. What was mentioned just now about Xue Chao not being able to have children in the future was also because they couldn't directly take his life, but rather make him have no descendants.","In the future, he would either adopt a son from one of his younger brothers' families or the title would directly pass to his younger brother after his death.]","No descendants!","Cold sweat broke out more profusely on Jiang Chao's forehead. If Xue Ju hadn't found his way home by himself, he might really have only these two options in the future.","[Xue Chao doesn't know yet. After he had the idea of remarrying, he was secretly given a drug to make him infertile. Xue Ju and Xue Rui will be his only biological children.]","\"Did his younger brother do this? After he married Lady Liu later, he didn't have any more children. Then why was his only biological daughter, Xue Rui, who stayed by his side, treated like a transparent person?\"","[Hehe, because Xue Chao later had another son and a daughter! This really shocked the younger brothers who personally gave him the infertility drug.","Hahaha, they once thought that the expensive drug they bought was fake and almost got into a fight with the person who sold the fake drug.","The person who sold the drug repeatedly claimed that his drug was effective and even asked the brothers to try it themselves. He said it was free if it didn't work!]"]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170: Why Can't He Have Children","paragraphs":["It was said that the child was being sent to stay with his maternal grandparents for a while. When sending the child off, Xue Chao, with his typical carelessness, only assigned five people to accompany him, one of whom was Xue Ju's personal attendant.","When Xue Ju later returned to the Xue family, he described his disappearance in vague and incomplete terms. It wasn't until a major event occurred afterwards that people, looking back and piecing together the known information, slowly reconstructed the course of his disappearance.","Three days before the Lantern Festival, eight-year-old Xue Ju, along with one attendant and four servants dispatched by his father, set off for his maternal grandparents' home.","Xue Ju's maternal grandparents lived in Rongcheng, two hundred li from the capital city, Shangjing.","Why not stay at the Marquis's estate for the Lantern Festival before leaving?","The reason his father, Xue Chao, gave him was that celebrating the Lantern Festival at his maternal grandparents' home would bring the two elders greater joy.","As for the actual truth behind it, one can only assume Xue Chao himself knew best.","The named Xue Chao wore a look of utter dejection, oblivious even to the glances his colleagues cast his way.","Only the two gazes fixed upon him from above made him feel as if needles were pricking his back, breaking him out in a cold sweat.","He remembered how, before the New Year, his brother-in-law (from his upcoming second marriage) had sought him out, saying their family wanted a grandson with a noble title. The reason they were willing to marry their sister to a widower like him was precisely because they had their eye on his family's noble title, which could bring blessings to future generations.","Had this demand been raised when they were first discussing the marriage, he might have refused the match. But now, with just over a month until the wedding and the invitations already sent out, Xue Chao found himself in a difficult position, unable to back down.","There was an even more important point: he had met the Liu family's young lady several times. One could say that both her appearance and temperament were very much to Xue Chao's liking.","He had to admit that compared to the strong-willed nature of his late wife, Lady Liao, he preferred this Liu girl, who was in the prime of her youth, gentle and lovely, and whose eyes were always full of admiration when she looked at him.","He had asked his brother-in-law, Liu Yuzhou, right then: what did Lingniang think about this? Liu Yuzhou told him that his sister was filial and would follow all her parents' arrangements.","After returning to his estate, Xue Chao pondered for three days. Later, upon hearing that his eldest son had gotten into a fight with Da Ge'er, the son of his second brother, anger rose within him. The decision he had been unable to make for so long suddenly seemed to have found an excuse in that moment—a reason to send his son away.","The five of them traveled in two carriages. They hadn't gone far, only about ten li out of the city, when they stopped at a roadside tea shed to rest and have some tea...","When they woke up again, they found themselves in a different place, tied up with ropes, surrounded by children only a few years old. Xue Ju immediately realized that the tea shed where they had stopped was a den of thieves.","Those people were likely sentinels placed outside the city by the villainous \"Brother Que De.\" They probably saw that Xue Ju's group of four was only escorting one young master and a boy not yet fully grown, yet the six of them were driving two carriages.","Judging by the deep tracks the carriage wheels left in the muddy ground, the carriages must have been heavily loaded. Greed overcame them, and they disregarded the obvious signs that the group came from a powerful and noble family, kidnapping them.","After the Lantern Festival, Xue Ju, along with three children from the Ling family, was secretly smuggled out of the city and sold off to places far from Shangjing, the children dispersed among different buyers.","\"Little Pearl, is what you're saying true?\"","\"All of that is speculation by outsiders. The truth is, the carriage taking Xue Ju to his maternal grandparents' home didn't travel far out of the city before arriving at a mountain hollow, where several men were already waiting.","Upon seeing these men, the four men driving the carriages jumped down without a word and left without looking back, leaving only the unsuspecting Xue Ju and his attendant on the carriage.","By the time the two were taken to Brother Que De's lair, it was already too late to escape.\"","\"Was Xue Ju given to the traffickers by his own family? No, not given! Weren't there two carriage-loads of things? They practically paid the traffickers to take him.","Who did it? Xue Chao or Xue Yao?\"","The faces of the Xue father and son had now turned from pale to deathly white, cold sweat slowly beading on their foreheads.","\"Master, take a guess. What is the most important thing in the eyes of the Xue family?\"","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment. \"The noble title?\"","\"Correct. The noble title. With the title comes status, power, and wealth. The Xue family has only one title, currently set in stone to be inherited by Xue Chao, who has already been officially designated the heir.","But the Xue family has more than one son. Xue Yao currently has five sons: four by his principal wife and one by a concubine.","Let's not mention the youngest brother from a concubine; he's the youngest and a son of a concubine, so it definitely wouldn't be his turn anyway.","Do you think Xue Chao's other three brothers might want this title?\"","\"Was Xue Ju essentially sold off by his own uncles, with them even throwing in money? They are, after all, Xue Chao's full brothers by the same mother. Even if they wanted to seize the title, shouldn't they first get rid of the heir, Xue Chao?","Why directly target the third generation?","Even without Xue Ju, couldn't Xue Chao, who is about to marry, still have other sons by his principal wife?","He's not infertile. As long as the hen that lays eggs is there, why worry about no eggs?\"","Xue Yao closed his eyes, his face somewhat ashen. His worst fear had come to pass. To quash any ambitions his other sons might harbor, he had long ago petitioned for his eldest to be designated the heir, hoping to settle the matter definitively. Little did he expect that they had never given up their aspirations.","Xue Chao, the \"egg-laying hen,\" though pale-faced, also felt that the little immortal lord's words, though crude, held truth. As long as he was alive, even without Ju Ge'er, he could still have other sons.","At this thought, his heart sank. Would his good brothers next move against him?","Directly eliminate him? But then, his father... Xue Chao looked towards Xue Yao. Father and son both understood the other's meaning.","Before they could ponder further, they heard the divine artifact say, \"Master, what if Xue Chao is not the current Marchioness's son? And what if Xue Chao could no longer father children in the future?\"","Xue Yao closed his eyes. Xue Chao's eyes widened in disbelief as he stared at his father.","Could it be that his mother's distance towards him wasn't because he had been raised in his grandmother's rooms since childhood? That his brothers' aloofness wasn't due to that and their grandmother's favoritism?","And also... what did it mean that he could no longer father children?","He already had Ju Ge'er and Rui Jie'er. If Lady Liao hadn't died along with the unborn child, he would also have a second son named Gui Ge'er by now.","He... how could he be infertile?!","Xue Chao stared fixedly at his father, Xue Yao, desperately hoping for an answer.","Under the penetrating gaze of his eldest son, Xue Yao kept his eyes tightly shut, not daring to face him.","\"What do you mean, 'not the Marchioness's son'? Is this Xue Chao like Xi Ling, with his birth mother having married someone else?","And what does 'cannot have children' mean? Xue Chao seems perfectly healthy. Having Xue Ju and Xue Rui proves he has the ability.\"","Xue Chao nodded frantically in his heart. Yes, yes! He has a son and a daughter. How could he suddenly become incapable!","\"Master, let's address the first point. Xue Chao and Xi Ling are indeed somewhat similar, but Xue Chao's birth mother is dead, not remarried.","His birth mother was originally a young lady from a wealthy family named Jiang Wan, whom Xue Yao met while stationed near the border with Nanzhao. The two fell in love at first sight and married upon meeting again.","The following year, she became pregnant with Xue Chao. Just as she was nearing her due date, Nanzhao forces launched a night raid on the border town. Jiang Wan, frightened, went into premature labor and had a difficult delivery. She struggled to give birth to Xue Chao before dying from massive hemorrhaging.\""]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171: No Cure, No Pay","paragraphs":["Xue Chao swayed on his feet. Xue Yao seemed to be transported back to that desperate night again. While he was away on a military campaign, when he finally returned to the mansion after repelling the Nanzhao troops, all he saw was a bed full of blood, his dying wife, and his son wailing uncontrollably as if he knew he was about to lose his mother.","\"If that's the case, how come I've never heard that the current Marquis's wife is a second wife? There's not a single whisper that Xue Chao isn't her biological son either.\"","[Because very few people knew about this matter. Later, fearing that he couldn't raise the child alone, Xue Yao finally married his current wife in the border town under the strong persuasion of others. She is a young lady from the wealthy Yang family in the border town.]","\"Back then, Xue Yao was, after all, the future marquis. Even with a young child in tow, he didn't have to marry a merchant's daughter.","This era is different from modern times. In the hierarchy of scholars, farmers, artisans, and merchants, the union of a scholar and a merchant always makes one feel that there's something fishy going on.\"","[Even if there is something, only the Marquis and his wife of Pingyue know about it. It only took two months from the betrothal to the wedding of the two.","Xue Chao got a stepmother before he was even one year old.","At first, Yang Shi really took good care of Xue Chao until the family of three returned to the Marquis's mansion when the child was almost three years old.","After returning to the Marquis's mansion, as the eldest grandson, Xue Chao was directly taken by the Marquis's wife, who knew the truth, to her own courtyard to be raised.","Another year later, Yang Shi's brothers passed the imperial examinations and the whole family moved from the border town to the capital city. In the same year, Yang Shi became pregnant and gave birth to her first son the next year. In the following three years, she gave birth to Xue Yao's third and fourth sons in succession.]","\"Little Zhuzi, since you've mentioned Yang Shi's natal family, have you forgotten to talk about Jiang Wan's family? She was also a young lady from a wealthy family. Haven't they come to see their grandson Xue Chao all these years?\"","[Master, this brings us to Jiang Wan's background. When she first met Xue Yao, she was practically alone. Although she had servants and a considerable amount of wealth with her, she was truly the only master.","And her real identity was not from Dayan either.]","\"From Nanzhao?\" After all, they met at the border between Dayan and Nanzhao.","[Jiang Wan was not from Nanzhao, but from Nanyue. At that time, the old emperor of Nanzhao had just died, and there was a fierce power struggle among the upper - class. The Jiang family was purged because they took the wrong side.","Jiang Wan fled to Nanzhao with her family. Later, due to an informer, the Jiang family was still being hunted. She got separated from her family and servants and accidentally ended up in Dayan.","Before she could settle down, she met Xue Yao, fell in love at first sight, and got married on their second meeting.]","\"Did Xue Yao know her identity as a Nanyue person?\"","This was also what the emperor and his ministers of Dayan wanted to know, because Nanyue was one of the countries that destroyed Dayan.","In the past, if they heard such things, they wouldn't have thought much of it. There were not many inter - marriages between countries from top to bottom, but there were still some.","They didn't really care about it. But after learning that the destruction of Dayan was also related to spies and internal - external collusion, and the heavy blow it brought to Dayan, Emperor Mingxi and his ministers had to be more cautious.","Moreover, the territory of Dayan was said to have been infiltrated by these two young masters like a sieve, which made them even more suspicious.","At this time in the imperial court, even though Wei Ping slowed down his report, he had already said everything he needed to say.","Emperor Mingxi then looked at Marquis Xue Yao of Pingyue and said, \"Lord Xue, I heard that your grandson was also abducted by child abductors. Why haven't I seen anyone from your mansion looking for him?\"","Xue Yao quickly stepped forward and replied, \"Your Majesty, my second grandson is indeed among the thirty - seven children who were rescued.","My son and I only found out that the grandson we thought was sent to his maternal grandfather's house had been abducted by child abductors when Lord Huo sent the child back to our mansion.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded and said, \"The inheritance of offspring is a major matter, both for a family and for a country. It cannot be ignored.","A young master of the Marquis's mansion was abducted, yet the head of the family didn't know. How can one govern the country if one can't even keep one's family in peace? You, as the grandfather and the father, should also reflect on yourselves.\"","Xue Yao bowed even lower and said, \"Your Majesty is right. I will definitely conduct a thorough investigation.\"","Xue Chao also bowed and didn't dare to say a word.","[Master, what do you think Xue Yao's expression will be when he finds out that it was his own sons who colluded to do this?","He didn't know Jiang Wan's background at first, but when Xue Chao was six years old, Jiang's family came to the door. Only then did Xue Yao know that Jiang Wan was from a noble family in Nanyue.","He was afraid that if Xue Chao knew the truth, it would affect the already weak brotherly relationship among his sons. So he persuaded Jiang's family not to tell the truth and petitioned for Xue Chao to be made the heir apparent that year.","That year, Xue Yao's second son, Xue Yue, was not even one year old yet.]","\"Jiang Wan is from a noble family in Nanyue? How noble is it?\"","[The current Queen Mother Jiang Yu of Nanyue is her younger cousin.]","\"Their family was purged for taking the wrong side, right? How come there's a Queen Mother cousin?\"","[Indeed, they were purged because they supported the Prince of Wu. But her cousin and the then Prince of Cheng were in love with each other. When the Jiang family was in trouble, the Prince of Cheng took his cousin, Jiang Yu, into the Prince of Cheng's mansion as a concubine.","Later, there was too much infighting among the older brothers. The victorious Prince of Wu also died.","The Prince of Cheng picked up the throne without doing much. Jiang Yu became the Noble Consort De because of her son. Later, when her son ascended the throne, she jumped from the Noble Consort De to the Queen Mother.","It was this emperor who destroyed Dayan.]","Father and son of the Jiang family completely collapsed on the ground. Especially Jiang Chao, now this emperor of Nanyue was his cousin by marriage!","Emperor Mingxi was also stunned. He didn't expect that the Xue family had such a relationship with the emperor of Nanyue.","\"Does Xue Yao know all this?\"","[The Jiang family only showed up once when Xue Chao was six years old. At that time, Jiang Yu was still the Noble Consort De. But Xue Yao should be able to guess.]","The current situation of Xue Yao and Xue Chao was like having overseas relatives in a special period in Xia country. They were the key targets to be watched and investigated.","\"Do the Xue brothers know about this?\"","[It's not clear whether they know or not, but Yang Shi should know something. After all, as the wife of the heir apparent, she couldn't have been absent when the Jiang family came to the door.]","\"So they didn't dare to kill Xue Chao directly, but instead targeted his son?\"","[That's probably right. As mentioned before, Xue Chao's future infertility was also because they couldn't directly take his life, but wanted to make him childless.","In the future, he would either adopt a son from one of his younger brothers' families or the title would directly pass to his younger brother after his death.]","Childless!","Cold sweat broke out on Jiang Chao's forehead. If Xue Ju hadn't found his way home by himself, he might really have only these two options in the future.","[Xue Chao doesn't know yet. After he had the idea of remarrying, he was secretly given a child - lessening drug. Xue Ju and Xue Rui will be his only biological children.]","\"Was it also his younger brothers who did this? After he married Lady Liu later, he didn't have any more children? Then why was his only biological daughter, Xue Rui, left by his side like a transparent person?\"","[Hehe, because Xue Chao later had another son and a daughter! This really shocked his younger brothers who personally gave him the child - lessening drug.","Hahaha, they once thought that the expensive drug they bought was a fake. They almost got into a fight with the person who sold the fake drug.","The person who sold the drug repeatedly claimed that his drug was effective and even asked the brothers to try it themselves. He said it was free if it didn't work!]"]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172: If it works, it's going to be the death of me","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, everyone was astonished. Not only was it ineffective, but it was free? If it were effective, it would cost a life!","Xue Chao, however, felt slightly relieved. So he had bought fake medicine after all. He could still have children, he could still have a son!","\"Can these brothers still be trusted?\"","[They naturally wouldn't trust it, so they really tried it. The result was that these three brothers never had another child born to them from that point on.]","\"Then, that one son and one daughter Xue Chao later had... whose are they?\"","Whose are they? This huge question echoed simultaneously in the hearts of Xue Chao and all the officials present.","Emperor Mingxi's expression changed. He sat upright, but his hands clenched into fists.","[The Liu family's ancestral home was in Nanyue. To be more specific, their family were originally servants of the Jiang family. After that great purge, they entered Dayan, changed their names again, and became people of Dayan.","The Jiang family was able to find Jiang Wan's son thanks to information provided by the Liu family.","Later, when the Jiang family left, they gave the Liu family a task: to keep an eye on Xue Chao.","Before the current Emperor of Nanyue ascended the throne, in order to compete for the imperial position, he took over part of his maternal family's forces and also learned about the Liu family and Xue Chao.","After he took the throne and developed ambitions towards Dayan, Xue Chao, the future Marquis Pingyue, became an important pawn.","Therefore, the future Marquis Pingyue, his marchioness, and even the next generation all had to be people he could control.]","Emperor Mingxi secretly gritted his teeth, feeling somewhat ashamed. He hadn't expected that Gan Sheng had started scheming against his Dayan so early.","It seemed that he, Xie Fei, had grown too accustomed to peaceful days in recent years, focusing his gaze mostly within the country, thus underestimating his peers across the land.","The ambition to annex neighboring states was likely shared by all five of his royal peers; only he was still dreaming of eternal peace!","Hearing this, Yue Fuguang suddenly thought of the deceased former heir's wife, Lady Liao, who died in childbirth, and couldn't help but ask, \"Lady Liao's death... who was behind it?\"","[The ones who acted were still members of the Xue family, but people sent by the Emperor of Nanyue helped cover their tracks.","Even if the Xue brothers hadn't acted, Nanyue's people would have. After all, if Lady Liao didn't die, how could Liu Ling enter the household?","As early as five years ago, Liu Ling was cultivated by the Liu family, or rather by the Nanyue Emperor Gan Sheng, specifically tailored to Xue Chao's preferences to become the future Marchioness of Pingyue.","After three years of marriage, Liu Ling and Xue Chao had no children. Even when her maidservants were given to Xue Chao, the result was the same. Taking advantage of the couple's visit to her family home, the Liu family secretly took Xue Chao's pulse while he was drunk.","They confirmed he had been poisoned with a sterility drug, and it was the most potent kind, 'Not a Single Seed.' This poison didn't affect marital relations, and initially, the body showed no abnormalities.","But...]","With the system's \"but,\" Xue Chao's despair sank his heart even deeper into the abyss. He knew that what followed the divine artifact's \"but\" was certainly not good news.","[But this poison has no antidote. Moreover, the more frequent the marital relations, the more the body would gradually weaken.","After all, the Xue brothers couldn't kill Xue Chao outright, but having him weaken and die naturally, unknowingly, was the best outcome.","After learning this, the Liu family quickly reported to Gan Sheng, who promptly sent a trusted confidant to consummate with Liu Ling, resulting in Xue Chao's son and daughter.","That confidant was a descendant of the Jiang family, making him, in fact, Xue Chao's cousin.]","Pfft!","Xue Chao desperately covered his mouth. Blood flowed through his fingers and into his sleeves, like a stain on his dark red official robe that could never be washed clean.","\"Once the sterility drug proved effective, and the Xue brothers tested it on themselves, they should have realized within a couple of years that the drug wasn't the problem, but the person was, right?\"","[Indeed, after the three brothers took the drug and didn't taste anything unusual, they beat up the drug seller and left.","Actually, the seller knew his own drug was genuine, as it was the handiwork of that master from Nanyue—it had to be authentic.","These four brothers of the Pingyue Marquisate had used his drug. If he didn't run now, once they figured it out, he wouldn't have a life left.","The seller packed up and fled overnight. A little over a year later, when the three brothers discovered that none of their wives or concubines had borne any fruit, while their eldest brother's young daughter had already been born,","they couldn't help but have doubts. When they went to look for the drug seller again, they found he had long since vanished.]","\"These three brothers are truly both wicked and foolish. Their retribution came swiftly and mercilessly. Did all three of them have wives and children?\"","[Xue the Second had two sons and two daughters, Xue the Third had one son and two daughters, and Xue the Fourth had one son and one daughter.]","Everyone glanced meaningfully at Xue Yao. The legitimate son schemed against his elder brother and nephew for the title, only to end up completely wiped out. One wondered how he felt.","Xue Yao: What could I possibly feel? My heart is dead; please burn paper offerings for any matters! (Image of a living person slightly dead JPG)","As for Xue Chao, he harbored both secret hatred and relief. He hated Liu Ling's betrayal but was relieved they weren't married yet; a green pasture hadn't grown on his head, and he had still managed to bear two fruits.","As for his second, third, and fourth brothers who hadn't yet taken the sterility drug... after court adjourned, he would take care of it. Currently, only Xue the Second had a son and a daughter among the three brothers. Xue the Third's wife was pregnant, and the gender was unknown.","Xue the Fourth wasn't even married yet. Hehehe! Xue Chao laughed maniacally in his heart, nearly going mad.","The person standing behind him, seeing his body trembling, thought he was crying. Those who knew the situation secretly patted him, signaling him to hold back his anger and not give himself away!","Those who didn't know the situation quietly moved away, thinking he was having a fit, and couldn't help but think to themselves: if you're sick, you should get treatment; what's the use of crying!","Xue Chao: Is it that I don't want treatment? (Image of a roaring emperor JPG)","\"Didn't they suspect where their eldest brother's two children came from?\"","[They naturally did suspect and even secretly investigated the Liu family. Just as they discovered some clues, the Liu family caught wind of it.","They quickly sent away the Jiang descendant, erasing all traces of him. The Xue brothers also noticed that a tutor was missing from the Liu household.","They had seen that man once. Looking at the son Liu Ling bore for Xue Chao, the more they looked, the more the two resembled each other. So, very directly, they confronted their sister-in-law Liu Ling behind Xue Chao's back.","Liu Ling stubbornly refused to admit it. She was well aware she wasn't from Dayan, and her relationship with the Jiang descendant wasn't mere adultery; they were scheming for the Xue family title and the Xie family's empire.","Actually, the Liu family had long discovered that the three sons born to the Marchioness Yang Shi had always coveted the title belonging to the eldest branch, and that the lost son of the former wife, Xue Ju, was also the work of these three brothers.","Because of this, after her own son was born, Liu Ling rarely appeared before these uncles. Little did she expect they would still set their sights on him.","Liu Ling said one sentence at the time that nearly shattered the three brothers' alliance.]","\"Oh? What did she say that had such destructive power?\"","[She said: Since you all claim you can no longer have children, shouldn't you consider the children you already have in this lifetime?","Our branch has long been aware that you uncles have coveted the marquisate title. I just wonder, if you succeed in seizing the title, which of you three brothers will become the Marquis Pingyue?","The three brothers were stunned on the spot. They had been so busy fighting for the position that they forgot there was only one seat, but three brothers.","More importantly, they all had sons, and they all wanted to secure this wealth and glory for their own sons.]"]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173: Reunion or Revenge","paragraphs":["\"One peach killing three warriors, this Liu Ling is quite clever, truly worthy of being a spy.\"","Although the three brothers later interacted as usual, they all knew that because of this incident, their relationship could never return to what it was before.","Even their mother, Lady Yang, the Marquess's wife, tried to mediate to no avail. Instead, they began to suspect their own mother of favoring the other brothers, leaving Lady Yang, their birth mother, in a difficult position pleasing no one.","It was at this time that Xue Ju returned.","\"Xue Ju deliberately concealed the facts of his abduction from the beginning, pretending not to know, which suggests he probably guessed who was behind it.","Did he return this time to seek his family or to seek revenge?\"","Both to seek family and to seek revenge! His only full-blooded younger sister was still in the Marquess's estate, so of course he had to return. But he could not leave unavenged the wrong of being sent into the wolf's den.","\"How could a fifteen-year-old child contend against his powerful and influential uncles? Didn't he tell the truth to his father, Xue Chao?\"","Master, do you think Xue Ju could trust a father who sent him far away just to remarry? Those four men were nominally the escort attendants personally selected by Xue Chao.","Xue Ju even believed his father Xue Chao was not clean in this matter either; even if he didn't directly participate, he tacitly allowed things to develop.","Moreover, when he returned, his father already had a beloved wife and son, while his sister had been raised into a virtual invisible person within the Marquess's estate.","Fortunately, however, Xue Rui was a clever girl, cautious and discreet in daily life, knowing how to hide her intelligence.","She also did not contend with the two children born to Lady Liu, thus managing to grow up safely and wait for her brother's return.","\"The Xue family truly committed sins, especially Xue Chao, who is unfit to be a father!\"","Hearing the Little Immortal Lord's comment on Xue Chao, everyone present felt a stir in their hearts. This Xue Chao's career would likely stop here in this lifetime.","Someone disliked by the Little Immortal Lord would no longer be favored by their Majesty, or even by the next emperor, Crown Prince Xie Zhiyan.","Xue Ju also suspected his mother's death. Later, he discovered it was the work of his dear uncles, but there were shadows of others behind them, pointing directly to his stepmother Lady Liu and her family.","And his father seemed to have also sensed that his mother's difficult childbirth was connected to his uncles, but he showed no intention of investigating at all.","In despair, Xue Ju thought of an extreme method, one that could take the entire family away.","\"Take the entire family away? Poison?\"","Master, even if it were poison, it might not necessarily take away everyone without missing anyone, right?","\"Then tell me quickly what method he thought of.\"","Xue Yao and Xue Chao were even more panicked. Their grandson/son wanted to take the entire family to their deaths... they...","While he was away, Xue Ju met a branch of the Tong family. The method he thought of was rebellion. In this world, what could cause a family to die more quickly and thoroughly than being discovered for rebellion?","\"This... truly is! This method is absolutely brilliant!\"","He first arranged a distant marriage for his sister, who was not yet fourteen. This marriage was so distant it took her out of the country.","Because there were benefits to be gained, not a single person in the Xue family came forward to stop it.","Even her own father, Xue Chao, allowed his young daughter to marry far away to another country. From this alone, one can see the cold indifference of the Xue family towards the two siblings.","After sending his sister away, Xue Ju began his operations.","While posing as a Tong family scout, Xue Ju met his 'life mentor,' Bai Yu, and Xue Ju consequently joined the Prince of Qi's faction.","Not long after, the Prince of Qi's intention to rebel was reported. The ailing Emperor Mingxi ordered a thorough investigation. Xue Ju planted sufficient evidence of rebellion in both his own home and the Liu family home to implicate both households.","After being captured, he quickly confessed, giving a detailed and vivid account of everything his family and the Liu family had done for the Prince of Qi.","He successfully led the Xue family to receive the \"entire household extermination\" package.","During this process, the Ministry of Justice and the Dali Temple also uncovered the Liu family's collusion with Nanyue.","\"Was the Prince of Qi's rebellion reported by Xue Ju?\"","\"It was him. What a pity about this child. He's a ruthless and clever one. To escape from the far southern lands and make it back, his willpower and skills must be exceptional. It's a shame Xue Chao was so blind, failing to see the worth of such intelligent children.","Learning from Emperor Mingxi by treating illegitimate children as treasures, how pathetic!\"","Emperor Mingxi, once again dragged out by the Divine Artifact to be scolded alongside others, silently practiced breathing exercises in his mind. He didn't dare offend these two ancestors, but could he not deal with the Xue family? The first to suffer would be Xue Chao!","Xue Chao didn't need to look to know how terrible His Majesty's expression must be at that moment. In his heart, he cursed the ancestors of the Liu and Jiang families for eight generations, yet never reflected on his own mistakes.","\"This Xue Ju, although a bit young, could be cultivated in a few years. If the Xue family doesn't want him, Little Pearl, help me make a note. We'll pick up this bargain.\"","Emperor Mingxi's eyes shifted. With him around, the Xue family would have no choice but to cultivate this talent. The court had preemptively claimed this future talent; the future Marquisate title could only belong to this young man.","\"Forgot to mention, there was one Liu family member who slipped through the net—Liu Ling's half-brother from a different mother, the son of Liu's father by a concubine.","By the time the Liu family case broke, he was already a minor official in the capital city's gate guard. What he could do when Nanyue attacked is easy to imagine.","This man was generous with money and successfully won over a group of people, becoming a small nail driven by Nanyue into the heart of the Dayan Dynasty.","Although Nanyue Emperor Gan Sheng's plan to control the Pingyue Marquisate through the Liu family was thwarted by Xue Ju, he inadvertently left behind this nail—the Liu family's illegitimate son—which significantly reduced casualties for Nanyue's successful breach of the city walls.\"","\"As expected, the Dayan Dynasty lives up to its title of 'sieve and colander,' maintaining its stable performance!\"","Emperor Mingxi's face darkened at this evaluation, and his gaze swept towards Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and Feng Tang.","He had assigned the task of arresting Dayan Dynasty spies and investigating families and individuals colluding with foreign tribes to these three men two months prior.","Although many suspicious individuals had been captured during this time, he never imagined Emperor Gan Sheng of Nanyue's reach was already so deep.","Thinking of the spies he himself had placed in those other families, Emperor Mingxi gradually reconciled with the situation. They did it first, he would do it later. From now on, it would be a contest of who was more cunning!","Emperor Mingxi patiently listened to reports on the progress of disaster relief and resource allocation for snow disasters across various regions. After ordering the Censorate and the Ministry of Revenue to strengthen supervision, he dismissed the court.","Yue Fuguang had just started to step out when he was called by Eunuch Qian.","\"Grand Tutor, please wait a moment. His Majesty requests your presence. He is waiting for you in the Hall of Mental Cultivation.\"","\"Old Qian, any idea what His Majesty wants with me?\" Yue Fuguang, having grown accustomed to the system's way of addressing him, inadvertently let the familiar term slip out.","Eunuch Qian, hearing Yue Fuguang inquire for information, didn't hide anything and replied with a smile, \"It likely concerns the assassination attempt on Grand Tutor during the Lantern Festival.\"","\"Has His Majesty found out who was behind it?\"","Hearing it was about this matter, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but quicken her pace. She was still very concerned about who exactly wanted her dead.","Although she wasn't afraid of such threats, the thought of potentially running into this kind of nuisance every time she stepped out was aggravating. It might not be able to truly harm her, but it was utterly irritating!"]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174: Take out their emperor with a precision strike","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang and the system had discussed the person who took action later. She also had some guesses in her heart, but those were still just guesses and lacked solid evidence.","Without having to announce her arrival, Yue Fuguang smoothly entered the Yangxin Hall.","When she went in, oh, good heavens! The spacious Yangxin Hall was now filled with people. With a quick glance, they were all those who could hear people's inner voices.","Yue Fuguang pretended not to know and just greeted her grandfather before walking towards Emperor Mingxi.","\"Your Majesty, did you summon me for something?\"","She naturally sat on the embroidered stool brought over by Eunuch Qian and looked at Emperor Mingxi, waiting for him to continue.","Emperor Mingxi nodded and said seriously, \"Fuguang, regarding the assassination attempt on you during the Lantern Festival, Ministers Wei and Cai found some clues this morning.\"","He motioned for Wei Ping to speak.","Wei Ping bowed and said, \"Your Majesty, Master of the Lesser Preceptor. That night, we captured a total of sixteen assassins, and more than twenty escaped.","Among the sixteen, five took poison and committed suicide on the spot, and two died due to serious injuries. Currently, there are nine survivors.","After interrogation by the official and Minister Cai, three of them have confessed.","These three belong to two organizations. One of them is from the top assassin organization, You Tan. According to the confession of that person, the assassination order was directly issued by the headquarters without a buyer.","The official speculates that You Tan is taking revenge on the Master of the Lesser Preceptor for providing information that disrupted their plan to kidnap the bride of the Bao family.","As for the other side, it was assigned by the Prince of Qi's Mansion. These people are all the dead soldiers raised by the Prince of Qi's Mansion. The five who took poison and committed suicide among the sixteen were all his accomplices.","This person was greedy for life and afraid of death and didn't dare to bite the poison sac in his mouth.\"","\"You Tan, the Prince of Qi,\" Yue Fuguang murmured.","[Master, shall I go and take care of the Prince of Qi first?]","Before Yue Fuguang could answer, she heard Emperor Mingxi say, \"Fuguang, regarding the Prince of Qi, rest assured that I will definitely give you a satisfactory explanation.\"","Yue Fuguang asked indifferently, \"How does Your Majesty plan to give me an explanation?\"","Emperor Mingxi looked at the more than a dozen people present. They were all the important ministers among those who could hear inner voices and were all trustworthy.","So he said, \"Next month, Princess Pingning, Xie Zhiyao, will go on a marriage alliance to Yuanjia. After she leaves the capital, I will settle the matter of the Prince of Qi's Mansion's intention to rebel.\"","\"The Prince of Qi's Mansion wants to rebel?\" As an \"unaware\" person, Yue Fuguang showed a surprised look on her face.","Seeing her slightly exaggerated expression, Emperor Mingxi couldn't help but twitch the corner of his mouth and nodded cooperatively, saying, \"The evidence is conclusive. When Shen Kang and the others raided the other courtyard in Taohua Alley, they found a secret passage under the house.","The other end of the secret passage led to a small courtyard in the east of the city. They caught two people and found some things in that courtyard.","Cai Xian then found evidence that the Prince of Qi had raised private soldiers with the intention of rebelling based on this.","The reason I've been holding back until now is to wait for Pingning's marriage alliance team to leave the capital.\"","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but ask, \"Isn't Your Majesty afraid of being impeached by the imperial censors? After all, her daughter has just married for the country, and then you're going to deal with her father right away.\"","Feng Tang, who had been standing behind listening to their conversation, heard Yue Fuguang mention the impeachment by the imperial censors. That was his area of expertise, so he quickly stepped forward and said, \"Master of the Lesser Preceptor, the evidence of the Prince of Qi's Mansion's rebellion is conclusive, and the evidence shows that Princess Xie Zhiyao was also involved.","His Majesty didn't kill her but sent her on a marriage alliance. It's already an extra favor.","We imperial censors won't impeach His Majesty because of this.\"","Yue Fuguang thought of his high favorability of 89 towards her. He was a die - hard fan, so she smiled faintly at him and said, \"Censor Feng is a reasonable person.\"","A compliment from Yue Fuguang made Feng Tang happier than being promoted by Emperor Mingxi. His face flushed red and he said, \"I don't dare to accept the praise from the Master of the Lesser Preceptor.\"","Wu Yong rolled his eyes. If you don't dare to accept it, then why are you so happy!","No, he also had to work harder to make sure that next time he was the one to be praised individually by the Master of the Lesser Preceptor.","\"So, except for Xie Zhiyao who is far away on a marriage alliance, none of the others in the Prince of Qi's Mansion can escape. The Prince of Qi and his son who planned this assassination, I guarantee they won't live through this autumn.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded, indicating her acquiescence to his statement.","Seeing that the matter of the Prince of Qi was resolved, Wei Ping continued, \"Among the nine survivors, after three of them confessed, they identified the accomplices among the remaining six.","But we found that there were two people whom all three of them denied were from their side.","So the official speculates that there should be at least three groups involved in the assassination during the Lantern Festival.\"","Yue Fuguang thought for a while and asked, \"Did they say if they knew about each other's existence?\"","Wei Ping shook his head. \"Those three are just small pawns following orders. Apart from following orders to kill, they don't know much.\"","\"Then, does Minister Wei have any guesses about the identity of this third group?\"","Wei Ping pondered for a moment and then replied, \"We've tried all means, but those two still won't talk. However, the official and Minister Huo still noticed some characteristics on them that are different from the people of Dayan.\"","Since the assassins were all men and Yue Fuguang was still a young girl, he didn't go into details about the physical differences.","Yue Fuguang understood and didn't ask about the differences in detail. She just asked, \"In the opinions of Minister Wei and Minister Huo, which side do these two people belong to?\"","Wei Ping said, \"In the official's opinion, they should be from Xiqiang and Beili.\"","\"Xiqiang and Beili? Because of the bet during the last birthday celebration? Do they want to renege on the debt?\"","That won't do. It concerns her points. Cutting off her points is like killing her parents. She definitely won't allow this to happen.","\"Since the land ownership documents are already in the hands of the Master of the Lesser Preceptor, they can't renege on it at least on the surface. Otherwise, not only will the court lose its credibility, but they wouldn't go so far as to make the emperor break his promise for a piece of useless land.\"","Yue Fuguang thought to herself: Useless land? Wait until the cotton she planted covers the land over there, and then see the faces of those countries!","\"So they're trying to assassinate me! In Minister Wei's opinion, is it the intention of their emperors or the private actions of my opponents?\"","Before Wei Ping could answer, Emperor Mingxi said, \"In my opinion, it should be carried out under the instruction of their emperors and led by those people.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded, agreeing with Emperor Mingxi's statement. With the will of the country behind it, those people would act so recklessly.","Assassinating her in public during the Lantern Festival was not only an attempt to kill her but also an attempt to intimidate Dayan.","[Master, shall I send a few divine servants to eliminate their emperors directly?]","The officials and the emperor of Dayan thought: Sure enough, it's still the divine artifact master who likes to fight and kill the most. As soon as he opens his mouth, it's about taking someone's life, and it's the life of a country's emperor, as easy as killing a chicken.","They all felt a bit sorry for those emperors. You say, who couldn't you provoke, but you had to provoke the little immortal!","The divine artifact master who protects the master just wants your lives!","It would be embarrassing enough for a country's emperor to die in an assassination! But according to the style of the divine artifact master, he should send the so - called divine servants directly into the palace. Then the royal family would lose even more face!"]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175: If the Empress Dowager and the Empress both fell into the river, whom would the emperor save first","paragraphs":["At the same time, Emperor Mingxi also seriously reflected on whether he had gotten a bit carried away recently because his purse was full.","No!","Had he been insufficiently respectful towards the Little Immortal Lord?","Good, also no!","Then he was safe!","\"No need. For the divine attendant to break through the boundary and come here would consume your divine power. You must not waste your divine power casually. I am still hoping to leave this realm ahead of time and return to Lingxu Mountain!\"","The hearts of the Great Yan court officials sank. Not only did their Shao Shi, her, want to leave Great Yan and retreat to the island, but even the Little Immortal Lord, the core of it all, wanted to leave their world!","That simply wouldn't do. Sweat beaded on everyone's foreheads. What could they possibly offer to make the Little Immortal Lord stay in this realm for a few more years?","Someone silently nudged the Yu father and son within the crowd.","Yu Chongshan and the others felt equally uneasy, but who could change their granddaughter's decision once made?","She then asked Wei Ping, \"Did Nanzhao and Nanyue have a hand in this?\"","Wei Ping replied somewhat hesitantly, \"Whether people from Nanyue and Nanzhao were involved still needs to be confirmed after these individuals speak.\"","He glanced up at Emperor Mingxi before continuing, \"However, this official speculates that Xiqiang and Beili would not have acted without pulling those two into it.\"","She gave a light, disdainful snort. \"Strength in numbers, is it? Have these four states formed an alliance? To jointly deal with our Great Yan?\"","Emperor Mingxi shook his head. \"An alliance is unlikely. It's merely a temporary collaboration regarding your matter.\"","Yue Fuguang was speechless. Was she really that detestable? That four states could temporarily set aside their conflicts just to kill her.","All she did was claim a piece of unowned land and ask for some cattle and sheep. Was it really that serious?!","The Emperors of the Four States: It absolutely is!","Wei Ping still added, \"However, these are all speculations. This official will think of more ways to make those two talk.\"","Yue Fuguang thought about it. Making them talk... she actually had a method. Thanks to her previous self who wanted to hoard a bit of everything, she not only had Truth Elixirs but also Truth Talismans.","'Little Pearl, do you have any Truth Elixirs?'","[Master, Truth Elixirs are low-grade pills. Little Pearl only has a few.]","'Give me one, to use on those assassins. Quickly, help me think of a reason to take it out.'","The hearts of everyone in the grand hall skipped a beat. Such a... terrifying pill actually existed in the world.","For ordinary people, a Truth Elixir might be one thing, but for those with complex minds, wasn't it precisely terrifying?","Everyone became as silent as cicadas in winter, more afraid than if they had learned of their own miserable demise.","[How about saying it's a sugar pill, to scare those people?]","'That could work?!'","Although it was phrased as a question, Yue Fuguang was a woman of action. She immediately took out something wrapped in cellophane from the small pouch at her waist.","Holding it in her palm for Wei Ping to see, she said, \"Lord Wei, would you like to use this to bluff those people?\"","Wei Ping immediately assumed a deferential posture, cupping his hands. \"What does the Shao Shi mean?\"","She weighed the object in her hand. \"Dissolve my 'sugar' in water and have those men drink it. Tell them it's poison, and those who don't tell the truth will die. See if fear makes them reveal the facts.\"","Wei Ping pretended to ponder seriously, putting on a proper show. After a moment, he took the 'sugar' from Yue Fuguang's hand.","\"Then this official will try the Shao Shi's method. But this sugar should be sweet, right? I just wonder if they'll believe it.\"","Yue Fuguang smiled confidently. \"Don't worry about that, Lord Wei. This is a sugar for aiding digestion and reducing internal heat. Sweet with a hint of bitterness, and it has a herbal scent.\"","A gleam flashed in Emperor Mingxi's eyes as he said with a smile, \"Fuguang actually has such sugar? Coincidentally, I've been a bit overheated lately, yet I can't stand bitterness. Could you spare one of those sugars for me?\"","The lords in the hall stiffened, their backs bending even lower unconsciously. If His Majesty really got his hands on a Truth Elixir, who among them might end up unfortunate!","[Master, why not give the emperor one? See what truths he'd spill after taking it, haha! You could ask him which consort he likes best, which son?","If the Empress Dowager and the Empress fell into the river at the same time, who would he save first?]","Emperor Mingxi's face darkened. What kind of devilish questions were these from the Divine Artifact? Which consort or son he liked best—was that something to be said aloud?","And how could the Empress Dowager and the Empress possibly fall into the river at the same time? Did the people serving them not want to live?","'That won't do. Your stock of that elixir isn't plentiful. We can't waste it on such trivial matters.","As for your questions, I can answer them without the elixir. The emperor's favorite consort is definitely Zhou Yunxin. His favorite son isn't it the Ninth Prince?","The emperor rules the world with filial piety, so of course he'd save the Empress Dowager first!~'","Emperor Mingxi: I originally wanted to seize an opportunity for some gain. Not only did I fail to trick the item, but I got dragged out for another round of criticism. Miscalculation! Feeling wronged but dare not speak up JPG.","[Wasn't Zhou Yunxin demoted all the way to a Beauty? And she's still the favorite consort? And about the sons, isn't the emperor's favorite the Crown Prince?]","'The deeper the love, the stricter the discipline, right? Zhou Yunxin might be promoted back any day. As for the Crown Prince, where does the emperor seem to favor him most?","As for making him Crown Prince, wasn't that because he's the legitimate eldest son? Not out of affection!'","Yue Fuguang's words stabbed, one after another, into the father and son, both on their persons and in their hearts. The Crown Prince was alright; after learning the cause of his death, he had long since come to terms.","Emperor Mingxi, however, cast a somewhat apologetic glance towards the Crown Prince. Seeing him merely slightly bow his head, expressionless and lost in thought, the emperor's embarrassment deepened.","And that 'the deeper the love, the stricter the discipline'—was that phrase even used in this context? A national Shao Shi couldn't be uncultured; this ancestor must be sent to school.","Unaware of Emperor Mingxi's 'sinister' intention, Yue Fuguang asked with a smile, \"Is Your Majesty also suffering from internal heat?\"","\"Indeed. State affairs are burdensome. The snow disaster hasn't been fully handled yet, and reports of distressed commoners causing trouble are coming from the affected prefectures and counties.","The offending Zhou, Fan, Zhao, and Bai families will soon be escorted to the capital, and trying their cases will keep us busy for a while.\"","'Little Pearl, give me a Clarity Pill. The emperor can't have the Truth Elixir, so give him a Clarity Pill. One dose clears the mind and refreshes the spirit.","Maybe it can even cure some of his foolishness!'","[Master, one full pill would cause the emperor to explode from the spiritual energy impact, shattered into pieces!]","Emperor Mingxi was so frightened he couldn't help but tremble slightly in his dragon throne, not even having time to be angry at Yue Fuguang calling him foolish.","Shattered into pieces! The very thought sent chills through his body, aching everywhere. If he weren't sitting, he'd likely make a spectacle of himself now!","Emperor Mingxi's backside shifted unconsciously on the somewhat hard chair, suddenly finding every position uncomfortable.","His expression changed several times, while inwardly he was shouting, I don't want it anymore, alright? I don't want it!","He looked up towards the only one who could save him, Yu Chongshan. Yu Chongshan was also terrified at this moment, afraid his granddaughter would take out the pill and demand His Majesty take it on the spot. Wouldn't that be...","Just as this thought crossed his mind, he caught the emperor's pleading gaze. His foot had barely taken half a step when he heard his dear granddaughter say to the Divine Artifact, 'Couldn't you take a pill the size of a soybean, coat it in chocolate, make it fragrant and sweet...'","Master, we cannot coat it in chocolate. What if the Emperor has an allergy? Even if he isn't allergic, what if he finds it delicious and demands more from you?","I'll coat it in mystery-flavor candy instead. Whether it tastes sweet, spicy, sour, bitter, or salty will all depend on his luck."]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176: You've Reached the Age for Reading","paragraphs":["Emperor Mingxi inwardly exclaimed, \"Good grief! To shut me up, this little ancestor can really think of any method!\" So, he just wasn't worthy of eating that fragrant and sweet chocolate, was he!","Why was it that the more he couldn't have it, the more curious he became about its taste!","Yue Fuguang smiled with an utterly harmless expression. \"If Your Majesty wishes to eat it, I do happen to have one last piece here.\"","As she spoke, she held the candy up before Emperor Mingxi. \"Your Majesty, please eat it quickly. Its fire-dispelling effect is quite good.\"","Emperor Mingxi took the candy but didn't eat it immediately. He was afraid that if it tasted sour or bitter, he wouldn't be able to control his expression and would lose his dignity in front of his ministers.","The assembled officials thought: Your Majesty, don't you realize your dignity has long been shattered into pieces on the floor, impossible to pick up!","Unaware of his trusted ministers' inner grumblings about him, Emperor Mingxi changed the subject. \"Fuguang, there's another matter I called you here for today.\"","Seeing that Emperor Mingxi didn't take the pill immediately, Yue Fuguang didn't press him and followed his lead. \"What other matter does Your Majesty have?\"","\"I was thinking that after the New Year, you will be nine years old, which is the right age to begin studies. I discussed it with your grandfather and decided to send you to study at the Hongwen Academy in the palace. What do you think?\"","Yue Fuguang rolled her eyes inwardly. If I said 'not a chance,' would you really not send me?","She thought it over seriously. Going to school wasn't entirely out of the question. She still had tasks to complete in other worlds in the future, and having knowledge would be useful.","But she had just endured the hardships of studying in her previous life, grinding away until her hair thinned to get into university, only to arrive here less than two years later. She hadn't even enjoyed many days of comfortable living, and now she was supposed to burn the midnight oil and rise at the crack of dawn again? How could she bear it!","School was inevitable, but bargaining couldn't be skipped. \"Your Majesty, if I go to study, does that mean I don't have to attend the morning court sessions?\"","School started over two hours later than the morning court. She could sleep in a bit more!","Emperor Mingxi: !!! With the Divine Artifact's previous remarks about casually wanting to kill the emperor, he suddenly didn't dare suggest the unreasonable demand of Yue Fuguang attending morning court before school.","He was afraid that if he said it, the Divine Artifact might strike him dead on the spot, and no one could stop it!","He tentatively proposed, \"How about... you attend court every other day?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. Accumulating knowledge for future tasks was important, but the immediate task was even more crucial, wasn't it?","\"On the days I attend court, I won't go to the Hongwen Academy, okay? Your Majesty knows, I was injured before and shouldn't overexert myself.\"","Emperor Mingxi inwardly cursed Yu Qinchun a dozen times and quickly said, \"Indeed, Fuguang's health is paramount. If you get tired during studies, just tell your tutors.\"","As he spoke, he looked towards several officials from the Hanlin Academy and the Ministers of various Boards. These individuals all had teaching duties, especially the Hanlin Academy Scholars, Reader-in-waiting, and Lecturer-in-waiting—they were the main instructors.","Everyone hurriedly chimed in, \"Your Majesty is right. We will certainly prioritize the Young Preceptor's health.\"","As the etiquette tutor, Minister of Rites Zhang Zhongping added, \"The Young Preceptor is still young. It's perfectly fine to slightly reduce her academic workload.\"","In the Dayan dynasty, even if this one's etiquette didn't conform to the rules, it could only mean the rules were flawed, not that this ancestor was ignorant of propriety.","Yue Fuguang suddenly thought of another matter and asked, \"Your Majesty, do I need to find a study companion?\"","Emperor Mingxi said, \"Indeed. Typically, one can bring two to four study companions. Have you thought about who, Fuguang? Would you like me to help you find some?\"","Hearing the emperor's words, the eyes of officials with eligible daughters or granddaughters suddenly shone brilliantly. Some looked at Emperor Mingxi, others at Yue Fuguang.","Yue Fuguang decisively shook her head. \"No need. I'll find them myself.\"","[Master, have you decided who to choose as study companions? This choice must be made carefully. It's a chance to cultivate some subordinates for yourself. In the future, whatever Master wants to do, you won't have to toil personally.]","\"Indeed, we must choose carefully. In the future, whether we settle on an island or stay in Dayan, if we want to create some novel things to play with, we'll need loyal and capable people to carry them out.\"","Hearing their conversation, the hearts of the ministers grew even more fervent. For outsiders like them, what relationship could be more intimate than becoming the little celestial lord's study companion?","If just one person from a family became the little celestial lord's study companion, it would be like the whole family attaining enlightenment! They would automatically become part of the little celestial lord's 'kingdom'!","\"As for candidates, I'll pick two from among my sisters at home. For the other two, we'll see if Grandfather and the others have any good recommendations.\"","[Master, what kind of study companions are you looking for?]","\"First and foremost, they must be as loyal as Little Pearl. If they can also be clever and quick-witted, that would be even better.\"","[Loyalty to the Master is indeed most important. Even the most ordinary items in my possession are things hundreds or thousands of years more advanced than this era. Without loyalty, no amount of capability is acceptable.","Although Master is currently in a mortal body with sealed memories, the prestige of an immortal cannot be lost. Little Pearl can help Master observe people. I can tell at a glance whether someone is loyal or not.]","\"I forgot that Little Pearl also has the ability to observe mortals' fortune and virtue.\"","[Hehehe, Little Pearl's abilities have been greatly diminished by the rules of this world, and they are not even one ten-thousandth of Master's power before undergoing tribulations.]","\"Was I that powerful before? I don't remember!\"","\"Before, Master could move mountains and fill seas, turn clouds with a flip of the hand—all with just a thought. When Master successfully completes the tribulation and ascends to High Godhood, you will be even more formidable!\"","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers were utterly stunned. Was this the power of an immortal? Any random item they brought out would be enough for them to benefit from for a lifetime!","They were numb with envy. As for jealousy, it was out of the question. The gap was like heaven and earth; they could only look up in awe, unable to harbor any other thoughts!","Thinking this, their desire to latch onto this powerful figure grew even more urgent.","As everyone watched Yue Fuguang's back disappear outside the hall, the more impatient ones couldn't wait to crowd around Yu Chongshan, promoting their daughters and granddaughters.","Yu Zhongchun and Yu Shuchun saw their father instantly become the center of attention and felt a strange mix of envy and pride.","Their Yu family was truly bringing glory to the ancestors through their daughter/niece!","Especially Yu Shuchun. From what she had observed these past days, Fuguang seemed closer to her own Xuan Jie'er than to her other sisters.","From what her parents implied, it was related to Xuan Jie'er's kindness towards Fuguang when she first returned, when her status was still that of an unimportant adopted daughter.","Back in Emperor Mingxi's Hall of Mental Cultivation, the officials were still fiercely competing over the two study companion spots.","Meanwhile, Yue Fuguang and the system, following the young eunuch Xiao Fuzi and strolling slowly out, were also discussing the matter.","[Host, finding study companions is a great opportunity to develop your own network. You must choose carefully.]","\"System, when it comes to connections, even if I don't actively develop them, as I grow older and can do more, connections will come to me on their own.","Besides, rather than having their children become my connections, wouldn't it be better to skip that step and turn the patriarchs themselves into my connections!","Trust me, the content of our conversation just now will definitely yield unexpected results.\""]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177: Lord Shaoshi Requests His Majesty's Presence","paragraphs":["Indeed, and when it comes to connections, who could have better ones than princesses whose own fathers are the emperor.","Host, you should make friends with several princesses. I heard from the palace servants that Emperor Mingxi has several quite favored princesses.","Make friends? Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"In both my past and present life, I haven't had much luck with close girlfriends. So rather than painstakingly cultivating friendships, I'd rather gain a few more believers.","After all, we might complete our mission and leave this place in just a few years. Having friends isn't important; parting is inevitable in the end.\"","The system thought that made sense too but still asked, [Host, what do you mean by believers?]","\"You're the one who said I need the grandeur befitting a deity. Since I'm an Immortal Lord, I can do without friends, but not without believers.","My believers are like...\"","\"Stop right there, you! I'm talking to you, the little chubby girl up ahead!\"","Yue Fuguang was just about to expound on her lengthy theory about believers to the system when she heard a voice cracking with puberty, like a duck's quack, shouting from behind.","At first, she didn't think it was directed at her. After all, having been around the Great Yan palace for several months now, who didn't know her—the current favorite in the eyes of the three most powerful figures: the Emperor, the Empress Dowager, and the Empress?","Even the Crown Prince had to speak softly in her presence. Who would dare raise their voice at her?","Moreover, with the added \"little chubby girl,\" she was even more convinced it wasn't for her. Yue Fuguang, who had never considered herself fat, felt the term \"chubby girl\" didn't apply to her in the slightest.","She had slimming pills lying in her storage ring. If she felt fat, she would have taken them long ago. Would she have waited until now?","No sooner had Yue Fuguang thought this than she was swiftly proven wrong.","A green, skinny beanpole of a figure overtook her and blocked her path.","It was a gaunt youth, thin as a rail, but with exceptionally bright eyes. He wore a robe embroidered with a three-clawed python and had beautiful jade and a pouch hanging from his waist.","The emperor's son? Never seen him before!","The skinny beanpole spoke, \"Chubby girl, didn't you hear me? I told you to stop, yet you dared to keep walking? Do you have a death wish?\"","Yue Fuguang was so angry she almost laughed. Since revealing her 'Immortal Lord' identity, this was the first time anyone had dared speak to her like this.","She didn't have the kind of novelty some overbearing CEOs feel when encountering someone 'different.' All she felt was the urge to beat him until he was crawling on the ground crying for his mother!","This person had the audacity not only to shout at her but also to call her a chubby girl. He was clearly asking for a world of hurt!","Yue Fuguang said coldly, \"Who are you? Which son of the emperor dares speak to this Junior Mentor like this? Charging you with disrespect wouldn't be excessive, would it?\"","She wasn't like those protagonists in novels who endure all sorts of insults from villains, getting thoroughly insulted before finally revealing their intimidating identity for a dramatic comeback.","There was truly no need. As an 'Immortal Lord,' if she suffered first, any subsequent face-slapping would be a step down. She wouldn't do such a foolish thing.","She wasn't cut out for that kind of suffering!","So Yue Fuguang instructed another eunuch, \"You're called Little Anzi, right? Go and fetch his emperor father. His son is blocking my path. Ask him if he, as the father, intends to do anything about it?\"","Little Anzi was terrified. Had this Fourth Prince, absent from the palace for months, not heard how the winds had changed within these walls?","Provoking this one would bring no good to the prince himself, and those serving him would also face consequences. Even he, who was merely escorting the guest, would get an earful.","As Little Anzi ran towards the Hall of Mental Cultivation, he was crying inside. He thought following Little Fuzi to see this great Buddha off the palace grounds was a cushy job. Who would have thought he'd run into the palace's most troublesome prince? Just his luck!","Sweating profusely, Little Anzi ran all the way to the outside of the Hall of Mental Cultivation and bumped into Chief Eunuch Qian, who was coming out to fetch fresh water.","Usually, when His Majesty was in council with the ministers, only Chief Eunuch Qian was qualified to remain inside. Everyone else was dismissed to wait outside the hall, so the task of serving tea and water also fell to Chief Eunuit Qian alone.","Qian Gui, carrying a water pot and about to head into the main hall, turned and saw Little Anzi, who had been assigned to escort the Junior Mentor, running back in a panic.","A bad feeling instantly arose in his heart.","\"Little Anzi, weren't you sent to escort the Junior Mentor? Why are you back so soon?\"","Before he could even catch his breath, Little Anzi said in a hoarse voice, \"Chief Eunuch, something's happened! Quickly inform His Majesty. The Junior Mentor is summoning him!\"","The Junior Mentor summoning His Majesty?","Qian Gui's heart sank. Something really had happened!","Without time for further questions, he pulled Little Anzi and hurried into the hall.","The emperor and his ministers, deep in discussion, first heard hurried footsteps. Turning around, they saw the usually strict and proper Chief Eunuch Qian dragging in a little eunuch dripping with sweat. They were all somewhat bewildered.","Emperor Mingxi did not immediately reprimand him. He knew Qian Gui always understood propriety. If he acted so disregarding of rules, there must be a real reason.","\"Qian Gui, what has happened? Why such panic?\"","\"Your Majesty, this is Little Anzi. It was this servant who assigned him to escort the Junior Mentor earlier. This boy came running back in a panic, saying something has happened. The Junior Mentor wants Your Majesty to go to her.\"","\"Wants me to go? Little Anzi, explain clearly. Where is the Junior Mentor, and why does she want me to go?\"","A room full of people stared at him intently. Little Anzi swallowed hard with difficulty, trying to calm himself.","Did no one find it inappropriate for the Junior Mentor, a subject, to summon His Majesty, the sovereign?","Did no one feel this was a bit like turning the world upside down?","Shaking off these irrelevant thoughts, Little Anzi knelt and quickly recounted what had happened after they left the hall. \"The Junior Mentor asks if you intend to do anything about it?\"","Emperor Mingxi angrily slapped the table. That little brat was nothing but trouble! The Junior Mentor asking if he would handle it implied that if he didn't, she would handle it for him!","Yu Chongshan and his son, standing among the crowd, were even more anxious. The Fourth Prince was a lawless troublemaker. What if he hurt their granddaughter?","So Yu Chongshan said, \"Your Majesty, perhaps we should go see first, to ensure no one gets hurt.\"","Emperor Mingxi also thought of the hot-tempered Divine Artifact, fiercely protective of its master. Once that one set its sights on someone, even if they didn't die, they'd be skinned alive.","If that boy accidentally harmed the Junior Mentor... Emperor Mingxi glanced at the crowd of ministers behind him.","He wouldn't be able to protect the kid either!","And at this moment, the battle between Yue Fuguang and the palace's number one troublemaker, the Fourth Prince, was...","The battle was not as intense as one might imagine.","Whether this newly appeared Fourth Prince was all bark and no bite, or whether he was simply stunned by Yue Fuguang's actions...","In any case, the current situation was that this Fourth Prince, who had appeared with exceptional arrogance, was now completely suppressed by Yue Fuguang's aura.","\"You're the Fourth Prince, right? As for who I am...\" A mocking smile curled at the corner of Yue Fuguang's mouth. \"This Junior Mentor doesn't believe you are unaware.\"","Seeing him about to retort, she continued, \"Don't deny it. Although you were punished and sent to a Buddhist temple for reflection for a few months and haven't returned to the palace, don't tell me you heard nothing of the news from within these walls.\"","Yue Fuguang circled him, giving him a once-over. \"Who gave you the courage to come provoke this Junior Mentor the moment you returned?\"","The Fourth Prince lacked conviction but still tried to save face. \"So what if you are the Junior Mentor of our dynasty? No matter how esteemed your position, you are ultimately a subject. As a subject, you should obey the commands of our imperial family.\""]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178: When the Junior Mentor takes action, it shows a disregard for hierarchy and deserves severe punishment.","paragraphs":["\"Who fed you such nonsense to fool a child? Don't you realize you're being used as a pawn?","Boy, someone is trying to harm you, and you're completely unaware?\"","In this palace, she just didn't know who was testing her limits by sending out this prince who had only recently returned to the palace. Did they think she wouldn't dare touch him?","What a joke!","So what if he's the Emperor's son? If she beat him, would the Emperor even dare utter a word of dissent?","But beating someone up is tiring work, such rough labor was beneath her!","Yue Fuguang, with the face of a seven or eight-year-old child, spoke these words with an air of aged weariness, creating a stark dissonance.","In the eyes of the Fourth Prince, it was like an ancient demon wearing a child's skin, inexplicably terrifying.","The Fourth Prince, Xie Zhiwei, took two steps back before continuing his foolhardy taunts. \"What does it matter who told me? This prince is His Majesty's son. Who would dare use me as a pawn?\"","He cast a disdainful glance at Yue Fuguang's small frame. \"To beat someone like you, I wouldn't even need one full punch.\"","\"Beat me? Then go ahead and try! What's the point of just talking big?\" Yue Fuguang took two steps toward him.","\"Hurry up, this Junior Mentor still needs to get home for dinner!\" Yue Fuguang's eyes were full of contempt, looking at him as if he were something filthy. This gaze completely enraged Xie Zhiwei, who was in the midst of his rebellious, sensitive, and highly prideful phase.","It shattered his last shred of hesitation and reason into nothingness. He raised his fist and lunged at Yue Fuguang.","\"Don't!\"","\"Stop!\"","\"You impudent child!\"","Several groups of people arrived one after another, seeing from a distance the Fourth Prince Xie Zhiwei raising his fist and charging fiercely at Yue Fuguang.","Their shouts of \"stop\" couldn't stop what was about to happen.","Just as Xie Zhiwei's fist was about a meter away from Yue Fuguang, he seemed to crash into something invisible.","With a thud, Xie Zhiwei was flung high into the air, then landed heavily on the ground with another thump.","Pfft! Pfft! Pfft!","Xie Zhiwei began vomiting blood, mixed with several white... teeth!","Xie Zhiwei felt like his body was falling apart, every part of him in pain. Yue Fuguang stood quietly watching all this from just three meters away, her face devoid of any emotion, like the clay statues of Bodhisattvas he had faced daily in the monastery these past few months.","Silent, yet radiating an indescribable, intimidating force, giving him an inexplicable feeling of being watched by a colossal presence.","Xie Zhiwei stared at her in terror. Even now, he couldn't believe she was a martial arts master. What he had crashed into earlier was definitely not some external release of internal energy.","There was something strange about her. By attacking her today, he had undoubtedly deeply offended her!","If he couldn't mend this relationship, then the only option was... A flash of ruthless malice passed through Xie Zhiwei's heart.","Seeing Emperor Mingxi running over with a group of ministers, his originally eight parts of weakness quickly escalated to twelve. Tears immediately streamed down his face.","Before Emperor Mingxi could even speak, he called out weakly and pitifully, \"Father~\"","Pfft! Then he spat out another large mouthful of blood.","Yue Fuguang watched the Fourth Prince's performance with a cold eye, unconsciously narrowing her gaze. This Fourth Prince didn't seem to be the simple brute she initially thought.","He was a master at pretending and performing, one who had successfully fooled everyone.","[Master, who is this villain performing for? Clearly, he struck first. How dare he act so aggrieved? So manipulative and theatrical. Wasn't he supposed to be a troublemaker?]","「Isn't it obvious? He's performing for his father. The one who provokes trouble is in the wrong. Not only is he in the wrong, but he also wants to play the victim and accuse first.」","[Will the Emperor believe him?]","「Not sure. It would be best if he did. That way, we'd have a reason to skip court and classes. Staying in the manor is so much more comfortable!」","Before Emperor Mingxi could even begin to berate his fourth son, who had returned only to cause trouble and stir up conflict, he overheard these two ancestors' conversation.","He could no longer care about his son, who had resumed his performance of vomiting blood, and strode directly past his prostrate son toward Yue Fuguang.","\"Fuguang, are you alright? Were you hurt by that wretched child?\"","Yue Fuguang said, \"I'm fine, Your Majesty. You should quickly check on your fourth son. He seems quite seriously injured.\"","Emperor Mingxi waved a hand dismissively. \"He's tough-skinned and thick-boned. It's nothing serious.\"","\"Father, it hurts!\" Xie Zhiwei looked utterly fragile. In his face, Emperor Mingxi saw the shadow of Concubine Xin, who was always ill.","He silently turned his head away. \"I am not the imperial physician; looking won't help. Besides, this wretch brought this upon himself with his own actions.\"","Over at Xie Zhiwei's side, the Chief Imperial Physician, Sun Huajing, soon arrived with two apprentices and began treating his injuries on the spot.","Meanwhile, around Yue Fuguang, the various ministers joined the Emperor in showering her with concern and inquiries, creating a stark contrast between the two scenes.","The Censor, Feng Tang, was the first to speak. \"Your Majesty, I impeach the Fourth Prince, Xie Zhiwei, for the grave crime of showing extreme disrespect toward our dynasty's Junior Mentor.\"","Wu Yong immediately followed. \"Your Majesty, I also impeach the Fourth Prince. Although he is a prince of noble birth, daring to openly attack the Junior Mentor shows a complete disregard for hierarchy and propriety. He must be severely punished.\"","\"I second the motion!\"","\"I second the motion!\"","\"I second the motion!\"...","The Yu father and son even shielded Yue Fuguang behind them, kneeling and performing a solemn bow. \"We beg Your Majesty to uphold justice for our Fuguang!\"","Leaving aside Emperor Mingxi, who was being put on the spot, even Xie Zhiwei, still receiving treatment, nearly fainted from anger upon hearing the ministers' words.","He was injured this badly! Were they blind? Couldn't they see? Not only did they not come to check on his injuries, but they also dared to pressure his father to punish him right in front of him!","Had they forgotten who was the ruler and who were the subjects? This Dayan was still the Xie family's empire. How dare they ignore him, a prince? Just wait until he... he'd make them pay.","Xie Zhiwei looked at each of these ministers in turn, memorizing their faces in his little mental book to settle scores later.","[Master, look at the way Xie Zhiwei is looking at these ministers. He seems like he wants to kill them all. He's truly holding a grudge!]","「So what? Does he really dare seek revenge?」","[In the original historical timeline, without today's incident, these ministers didn't offend him because of this. But this villain didn't go easy on them when dealing with them later.]","The hearts of the crowd were filled with shock and doubt. What did this mean? Was the Divine Artifact implying that this Fourth Prince would pose a threat to them in the future?","Emperor Mingxi said, \"Rest assured, my esteemed ministers. Today, I will handle this matter with absolute fairness.\"","After listening to the report from his attendant, his gaze turned sharp as he looked toward Xie Zhiwei. Before Emperor Mingxi could pronounce judgment, the Empress Dowager arrived.","She was followed by the Empress and a host of consorts, princes, and princesses.","Almost the entire imperial family was present, except for a very few like Zhou Yunxin, who didn't come. Even the Ninth Prince was there.","A flicker passed through Yue Fuguang's eyes. Emperor Mingxi was more tolerant and patient than she had imagined. So much time had passed, and the Ninth Prince was still alive.","That meant Zhou Yunxin and Chong Hua were probably also still alive, since she hadn't received the last batch of points yet.","She just wondered how long they would have to endure their suffering.","The Empress Dowager first checked if Yue Fuguang was injured, then said to Emperor Mingxi, \"Emperor, I have heard about today's incident.","Although Xiao-Si is injured, he got exactly what he deserved!","His actions today constitute extreme disrespect toward our dynasty's Junior Mentor. Even though he is injured, the due punishment must not be lessened in the slightest.\""]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179: With So Many Royal Children, Demoting a Few to Commoners Is Not Unacceptable","paragraphs":["Emperor Mingxi nodded and said, \"The Empress Dowager is right, that is also what I think. However, Yue Fuguang is the victim, so the punishment should also consider her wishes.\"","The Empress Dowager also said, \"Yes, yes, our Yue Fuguang suffered a great grievance today. She deserves to vent her anger properly.\"","The Empress Dowager patted Yue Fuguang's hand and said, \"Yue Fuguang, don't be afraid. Tell your grandmother, how do you want to punish him? We'll have the Emperor uphold justice for you.\"","[Master, why not take this chance to finish off this scoundrel? The Great Yan Dynasty would even thank you for ridding them of a scourge!]","「Little Pearl, you're thinking too simply. No matter how despicable he is, he is still the Emperor's son, the Empress Dowager's own grandson.","'Upholding justice for me' is just polite talk. Do you really believe it?」","Emperor Mingxi and the Empress Dowager: We really do want to uphold justice for you! Were we not being obvious enough, making Yue Fuguang think we are putting on a show?","The mother and son glanced at the bloody Xie Zhiwei and silently retracted their feet that wanted to kick him. Too dirty, didn't want to soil their shoes!","[Ah! They are reluctant to punish this villain? If they knew about the things he will do in the future, they'd probably want to kill him right now to end it once and for all!]","「Unfortunately, they don't know, so let's just follow the usual procedures. The life of an ant like him, if we truly wanted it, couldn't we take it anytime?","It's just that you and I, master and servant, shouldn't dirty our own hands. This is the calamity of the Xie family and Great Yan. What does it have to do with us.」","The hearts of Great Yan's ruler and ministers sank. For Xie Zhiwei to be called a calamity for Great Yan and the Xie family, what enormities must he have committed to deserve such a title?","Could he have rebelled? But those who might want to rebel include Princes like Qi Wang and Ming Wang, yet we haven't heard the Divine Artifact refer to them as a calamity!","Emperor Mingxi: I beg you two ancestors, please elaborate! Or perhaps, we should just settle this unfilial son today?","Led by the Emperor, the expressions of those present shifted unpredictably. The consorts, princesses, and princes standing to the side felt inexplicably tense watching them.","They had heard this Junior Mentor's inner thoughts at the Empress Dowager's birthday banquet. Now, seeing the faces of His Majesty, the Empress Dowager, the Empress, and the senior officials, it was clear they had heard something shocking again.","How infuriating that, apart from that one time at the birthday banquet, they couldn't hear anything now!","It's right that they can't hear. Apart from special individuals, Yue Fuguang required the system to restrict those who could hear her inner thoughts to having a favorability towards her of over sixty.","Those indifferent to her or harboring ill will who wanted to hear her thoughts were simply wishful thinking.","She looked at the expressions of confusion and unwillingness on some among the consorts, princesses, and princes and knew these people couldn't hear her conversation with the system now.","\"Empress Dowager, Your Majesty, please punish him as the crime of gross disrespect warrants. However...\" She glanced at Xie Zhiwei. \"The Fourth Prince is still injured. Should we wait until his injuries improve somewhat before punishing him?\"","[Master, why are you showing him mercy?]","「This isn't mercy. He's injured now. What if he dies during the punishment? Wouldn't that be letting him off easy?","Revenge is most satisfying when the target lives to suffer. Dying instantly would be too good for him.」","[Then we could chase him to the underworld! I'm familiar with the King of Hell.]","「My grudge with him isn't that deep, not enough to plague his next life. To be honest, most people here have greater grievances with him than I do.」","Everyone exchanged glances. Were they included in this \"most people\"?","Regardless, they all felt like finishing off this Fourth Prince Xie first, to cut off future troubles!","\"Yue Fuguang, child, you are too soft-hearted. Xiao Si was so treasonous today, he must be severely punished without leniency.\"","After speaking, the Empress Dowager looked at Sun Huajing. \"Physician Sun, how are Xiao Si's injuries? How many strokes can he withstand now?\"","Sun Huajing had heard what those two said. Seeing the Empress Dowager and Emperor insisting on punishment, he weighed his words carefully. \"The Fourth Prince has sustained serious internal injuries. Normally, he wouldn't be able to leave his bed for half a month.","If he receives strokes now, he could withstand ten at most.\"","Since those two didn't want the Fourth Prince to die first, then Sun Huajing had to find a way to keep him alive, to suffer his due punishment piecemeal.","Xie Zhiwei initially wore a face full of grievance, trying to gain sympathy. Later, seeing that not only his imperial father but even his imperial grandmother and Empress Mother ignored him,","and even insisted on punishing him, his heart turned half cold. When he first targeted Yue Fuguang, he had heard she was favored by these few.","But no one told him it was to this extent!","Had he known it was like this, how would he have dared to act recklessly in front of her!","Xie Zhiwei looked towards the crowd, his eyes meeting two people's gazes squarely. One person's eyes dodged, another shook their head slightly at him.","Xie Zhiwei secretly seethed with hatred. He had been rash, just as Yue Fuguang said, becoming someone else's blade.","But he still wanted to struggle desperately one last time. He cried out, \"Grandmother, Imperial Father, spare me! Zhiwei won't dare again!","Junior Mentor, Junior Mentor, I was wrong! I beg you, save me, save me! I'll be beaten to death!\"","[Hah! The nerve! Just now he wanted to kill Master, and now he has the face to beg Master to save his wretched life!","If he were truly beaten to death, it would be Great Yan's good fortune.","But the one who instigated this behind the scenes shouldn't be let off lightly either. Trying to use Xie Zhiwei to test Master's limits was a serious miscalculation!]","Yue Fuguang lifted her eyes and lightly swept her gaze over the gathered consorts, princes, and princesses. \"Your Majesty, the Fourth Prince's behavior today, besides his own will, must have been instigated by certain individuals.","Perhaps my existence is an eyesore to someone?\"","Emperor Mingxi's sharp gaze turned towards the crowd, frightening the consorts into losing their composure. The princes and princesses didn't even dare breathe loudly.","The Empress Dowager said, \"Yue Fuguang, rest assured. As long as I am here, let's see who dares act recklessly in front of you again!\"","Then she said to Empress Xu, \"Empress, remember today's events well. Discipline the consorts and imperial children properly. If anyone dares to rely on their status and act wantonly again,","the imperial family has many children. Demoting a few to commoners is not out of the question!\"","The Empress promptly replied, \"Yes, I have taken the Empress Dowager's words to heart and will definitely discipline them properly.\"","Empress Xu then said to Yue Fuguang, \"Today's incident is also my fault. As their Empress Mother, I failed to discipline the children properly, leading to this matter.\"","[Empress Xu is also unlucky. Marrying the Emperor, not only does she have to help him manage the harem, deal with the jealous concubines, but also manage these twenty-some sons and daughters.","In the end, her only son was harmed by the son of one of his concubines.]","「That was because we weren't here. Now that you and I are here, as long as the Crown Prince doesn't court death himself.","Even if he were poisoned with the deadliest poison in this world, could there be a poison that half a pill of your antidote couldn't cure?」","[That's natural. Considering his usual respect towards Master, Little Pearl is willing to save him.]","With these words from the two, Empress Xu felt greatly reassured. At this moment, she only felt light and energetic, with endless strength to deal with the demons and monsters of the inner palace.","Anyone who dares offend the Junior Mentor again is going against her son's life.","The senior officials also felt greatly reassured. The security of the heir apparent ensures greater stability for Great Yan. Historically, imperial succession has always been one of the riskiest moments for a dynasty."]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180: How Is Arriving Right on Time Not Considered Punctual","paragraphs":["The Crown Prince said with a smile, \"Grandmother, Empress Dowager, Master Tutor has been delayed here for quite some time and must be hungry. Perhaps we should go to Grandmother's palace for the midday meal first.\"","The two also smiled and said, \"Yes, yes, yes. Nothing is more important than Fuguang having her meal first.\"","The Empress Dowager took Yue Fuguang's hand and started walking, leaving a final message for the Emperor: \"Your Majesty, we leave this matter for you to handle. Punish those who deserve punishment. Do not show favoritism.\"","\"Rest assured, Mother. Today, this son will certainly give Fuguang a proper resolution.\"","Yue Fuguang had originally planned to return to her residence today for hotpot. Unexpectedly, with this delay, she was back at the Empress Dowager's palace again.","By the time she returned to the Yu residence from the Empress Dowager's palace, full and satisfied and laden with two full carts of gifts, it was already the end of the Wei hour (around 3 PM).","Yue Fuguang sent Qingzhu to inform the Old Madam and reassure her, then, attended by Cuizhu, she fell straight into bed and slept.","Her drowsiness wasn't just due to a food coma; it was also because, as the system upgraded and consumed more energy, it was simultaneously repairing its own data, which taxed the host even more.","Just before falling asleep, Yue Fuguang thought, thankfully this isn't my original body, otherwise I wouldn't let the system waste it like this!","The next day, after sleeping two extra hours, Yue Fuguang thought going to study was quite good too. This life of early morning classes was the routine she was most familiar with.","Carrying her small book bag, she arrived at the Hongwen Institute with her study companions, Yu Ningxuan and Yu Ningxin. The new classmates and tutors were already there.","Looking around, the classroom was over a hundred square meters, with bright windows, clean floors, and an atmosphere of solemn dignity.","Inside sat over twenty people, all around her age—princes, princesses, and their companions.","[Master, are you the last one to arrive?]","Yue Fuguang, thick-skinned, retorted, 'Even if your master is the last to arrive, you can't say I'm late!'","Arriving right on time, how is that not punctual?","The system checked the time: Chen hour, second quarter (around 7:30 AM). [Master, do you want to put a clock in this school? The water clocks in this world aren't as convenient as those. Arriving at the last moment like this, people who don't know might think you're late.]","'We'll talk about that later. It's too advanced; it's not convenient to bring it out now.'","The tutor for today's class was the newly appointed Hanlin Academician, Shang Xuewen. His promotion followed the same pattern as Feng Tang's: his immediate superior had been sent to prison due to Yue Fuguang's revelations, and he himself had been promoted by the Emperor.","Seeing Yue Fuguang enter, he smiled and said, \"Master Tutor, this is your seat.\"","He pointed to the best seat in the front row. Yue Fuguang looked in the direction he indicated; it was the C-position of the entire classroom.","She just wondered who had been sitting there before she arrived.","Yue Fuguang walked over and sat down. Her two elder sisters also found seats and sat down behind her.","Yu Ningxuan was Yue Fuguang's own choice. For the other candidate, she had asked the Old Madam and Old Master Yu to help select. In the end, they chose the more gentle-natured Yu Ningxin, who would be married off in a couple of years. This experience studying at the Hongwen Institute would also add considerable points to her prospects.","Unlike the older students in the neighboring classroom, what their group learned was relatively elementary. However, listening to all this classical prose filled her head until it ached.","[Master, you say these people have governed the country for thousands of years relying on this kind of learning, with slow social development. Haven't they ever considered that the problem lies with what they're studying?","Isn't this like being unbalanced in studies? Equivalent to walking on one leg.]","'Maybe some have thought about it, but those who did might have been seen as oddities, traitors to the sages' teachings.'","[The Aqua Blue planet we visited was the same. Although its five-thousand-year civilization was brilliant, its development couldn't match the progress of the later fifty years. That's the power of technology.","It can make a society's development fast, like riding the world's fastest steed, or slow, with little change for decades or even a century.]","Hearing this, Shang Xuewen felt an itch in his heart like a cat scratching, silently praying, 'Great Artifact, please don't just say things like that.","What exactly is the problem? Why could that place called Aqua Blue develop so fast in fifty years? Please elaborate in detail!","You only raise the question without solving it. Isn't that tormenting for those who hear it but don't know the follow-up, making them unable to eat or sleep peacefully?'","No matter how Shang Xuewen prayed in his heart, his Great Artifact did not continue the topic as he wished.","Instead, it said, [So, Master, when you think about starting your own school in the future, will you teach the students biology, geography, physics, and chemistry?]","'Little Pearl, how much of that knowledge do you think I can remember with my memory sealed by my master? Aren't you afraid I'll mislead the students?","Besides, I don't want to endure that kind of exhaustion.'","[Then what is Master's purpose in starting a school?]","'To give those who want to study but can't afford it a chance to become literate—commonly known as eliminating illiteracy. The lower a country's illiteracy rate, the more it can indirectly promote social development.'","[That would also be a meritorious deed.]","'Merit or not doesn't matter; it's just something convenient to do anyway.'","She only needed to provide the money and find someone to manage it. No matter what, it couldn't affect her leisurely, idle life.","Going to school and attending court were already ordeal enough; there was really no need to add more burden to herself.","Shang Xuewen memorized their conversation in his heart. After class, he would still have to report it truthfully to His Majesty.","Ever since planning to have the Little Immortal Lord come to study, His Majesty had secretly adjusted the teaching tutors. Anyone paying attention would notice that these people were not only high-ranking and powerful but also all belonged to the group who could hear the inner thoughts.","To compete for the teaching opportunity, colleagues had engaged in no small amount of physical altercations.","The martial arts tutor was the first to be confirmed. Who could blame Wei Shouyi for having the strongest combat prowess among the court officials, overpowering all rivals to win first place?","Thinking about these random things, Shang Xuewen quickened his pace towards the Hall of Mental Cultivation. Meanwhile, at the Hongwen Institute, it was already time for the midday meal.","Yue Fuguang declined the invitation from the Empress Dowager's palace, insisting on having the midday meal at the Hongwen Institute. Mainly, she was afraid her two sisters, coming to the palace for the first time, might feel uncomfortable, and also worried someone might bully them relying on their status.","After all, even someone with her status had encountered the hard-headed Fourth Prince just yesterday.","According to the system's latest report, the Fourth Prince still hadn't escaped a beating yesterday. Dragging his half-crippled body, he endured ten solid strokes. Eunuch Qian supervised, and no one dared to show the slightest leniency.","Another fifty strokes were reportedly to be administered within the next half month. For this, Emperor Mingxi didn't hesitate to have the Imperial Hospital use strong medicine on him—the kind that heals quickly.","Because of this, seeing the Fourth Prince's miserable fate led to Yue Fuguang's 'new classmates' being exceptionally well-behaved today.","The usual joking and playful fighting during breaks, because of her presence, became much more restrained. They even spoke softly, afraid of offending this great Buddha.","Faced with someone whom the three most powerful figures in the palace plus the Crown Prince, their eldest brother, had to coax, they truly dared not be as hard-headed as Fourth Brother in front of her.","Especially those who had heard her inner thoughts and knew her 'true identity' were even more respectful and cautious towards her."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181: System, Be Honest","paragraphs":["Just like the two before her now, the Eighth Princess and the Seventh Prince, with whom she had once shared a plate of pastries and two pieces of candy, did not return to their own palaces for the midday meal but stayed to dine.","The two of them first greeted Yue Fuguang very politely and, after receiving her permission, sat down beside her.","The Eighth Princess said, \"Are you settling in here alright, Grand Tutor?\"","She had, after all, heard the Grand Tutor's inner thoughts crying out about boredom and was truly afraid this esteemed person might later stop coming to class altogether.","Yesterday, their father had summoned all of them who could hear the inner thoughts and instructed them to take good care of this person in the academy, making sure she didn't grow to dislike studying.","The Eighth Princess, Xie Zhiyin, though small in stature, had big, unanswerable questions. If she had such an awe-inspiring status, had seen a different world, and tasted so many extraordinary things,","she would also grow weary of this dull and tedious studying. She greatly admired the fact that the Grand Tutor was willing to come at all.","Yue Fuguang didn't avoid the topic either, replying, \"No, I'm not used to it. This place is extremely boring.\"","She was just an ordinary person, utterly incapable of stirring up a thirst for knowledge or transforming into a sponge that absorbs it.","The Seventh Prince's face lit up with the delighted expression of someone finding a kindred spirit. \"So the Grand Tutor also finds schooling boring? I knew it! I'm not the only one who thinks so!\"","The Eighth Princess, looking at her overly excited seventh brother, hurriedly said, \"Seventh Brother, sit down quickly. If you don't eat properly and Father finds out, you'll be punished again.\"","Most importantly, if he led the Grand Tutor to dislike studying, his backside wouldn't fare much better than Fourth Brother's.","Remembering Fourth Brother, Xie Zhiwei, who had been beaten so severely yesterday he was barely breathing, the Eighth Princess couldn't help but shiver.","The Seventh Prince, clearly also recalling Xie Zhiwei's bloody and mangled rear end, sat down to eat but couldn't resist forcefully steering the conversation back.","\"Grand Tutor, the morning lessons were indeed rather dull, but in the afternoon we have equestrian class! We can go horseback riding!\"","At the mention of horseback riding, the eyes of both the Seventh Prince and Eighth Princess sparkled brightly.","[Master, horse riding in this season... that's truly the horse running and the wind chasing. One lap down and someone will freeze to death.]","\"This season really isn't suitable for being a wind-like woman! Little Pearl, remember to put a protective shield around me then.\"","When one has the means, there's no need to suffer hardships unnecessarily!","The two siblings, envious, poked at the rice in their bowls, silently channeling their envy into appetite, and buried their heads in their meal.","After the midday meal, the Seventh Princess led Yue Fuguang and the other two towards the rear courtyard of the Hongwen Academy. They exited through a small gate, walked for another seven or eight minutes, and arrived at a side hall that resembled a Taoist temple.","It had clearly been recently renovated, with painted beams and carved pillars depicting elements like immortal herbs and elixirs. Its layout was also different from other palace halls.","Seeing Yue Fuguang's puzzled expression, the Seventh Princess explained, \"This place was originally renovated by Father to serve as an alchemy room for the Taoist priests.","But for some unknown reason, construction halted before the building was even finished.","Later, because it's closest to the Hongwen Academy, the Ministry of Works converted it into a resting room.\"","Yue Fuguang thought to herself, What other reason could there be? It must be because the Crown Prince told Emperor Mingxi that elixirs are poisonous, so he dared not take them anymore!","I just wonder if they started researching gunpowder based on my hint.","As for converting it into a resting room, the Emperor must have planned to send her and the system to study at the Hongwen Academy since the beginning of the year.","\"System, you better study hard. Look at you misusing words, you made the Emperor so angry he sent us to the Hongwen Academy for advanced studies!\"","[Host, this world's books are among the many in the system's database. I am a cultured system! What I said about the Emperor was deliberate!]","Yue Fuguang lay on the soft, comfortable large bed. Next door were her second and fourth sisters.","She was a bit particular about beds and couldn't fall asleep immediately. Her sisters seemed asleep, but judging by their breathing, they likely weren't either.","\"Little Pearl, play me some soothing music to help me sleep.\"","[Master, wait a moment. Little Pearl has lots of beautiful mortal tunes here.]","The system first played \"Moonlight\" for her. As the soothing, ethereal music began, Yue Fuguang's brain, stuffed full of classical texts and maxims, gradually relaxed.","She fell asleep, never imagining that Yu Ningxin next door, a passionate music lover, would toss and turn, unable to sleep upon hearing this music.","The instruments used in this piece were completely different from those in Dayan. The timbre was pure, the high notes crisp like water droplets, the mid-range warm and rich. Yu Ningxin seemed to see a high-hanging moon casting its gentle light upon the earth.","Yu Ningxin turned and looked at Yue Fuguang, sleeping on the intricately carved canopy bed, as unique and lofty as that high-hanging moon. This seventh sister usually seemed easy to get along with,","but always maintained a certain distance from the family. She hadn't understood why before, but one day, after suddenly hearing her inner thoughts, she realized that she and they were fundamentally different.","The reason she, rather than third sister Yu Ningzi, had become the seventh sister's study companion was also because Ningzi's birth mother was the personal maid who accompanied Third Aunt when she married.","Back when Third Aunt was giving birth, besides Nanny Liu, the one who cared for her and the child was her own birth mother...","After finishing the afternoon equestrian class, by the time school was out, Yue Fuguang had completely collapsed in the carriage, like a large, flat cat pancake.","\"System, what kind of life am I living? Court sessions and school, school and court sessions... when will it ever end?\"","[Host, more exposés/revelations, more points earned. We can buy traditional knowledge infusion, and you won't have to kill yourself learning it all.]","Yue Fuguang instantly became alert. \"This 'infusion'... how many points?\"","The system replied obsequiously, [Host, not many, not many at all. Just 98,888 points. You won't be cheated, you won't be fooled, you...]","\"Stop!\" Before it could continue its sales pitch, Yue Fuguang ruthlessly cut it off. \"By the time I save up enough points to be willing to buy that, I'll have learned it all myself!\"","The system said, [You can pay in installments, up to ten years to clear it.]","Yue Fuguang remained unmoved. She hadn't had a mortgage in her past life; was she supposed to saddle herself with a 'knowledge loan' in this one?","\"With the points to buy that, I might as well spend 108,000 on a martial arts manual infusion, or even 188,000 on a cultivation technique infusion!\"","Hearing this, the system perked up again. [Really, Host? You really want to buy that?]","\"Fake! I'm not even using my own body right now. If I practice a cultivation technique and then leave this place, won't I just be back to square one?\"","It was then that Yue Fuguang also noticed something off about the system. \"System, be honest. Are you hiding something from me? The mall is still closed right now, yet you're urging me to buy tutorials. Where would I even buy them?\"","The system's data stalled for a moment; even the little ball of light in the system space glitched with garbled code. It panicked a little. Had the host discovered its desire to earn her points so quickly?","It was nervous but answered honestly, [Host, this system... this system has a way to smuggle some non-physical items through the mall's backdoor. It works even when the mall is closed.]","\"Smuggle? Aren't you afraid the main system will find out and format you?\""]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182: Get me a small melon to refresh myself","paragraphs":["Yue Fuguang was a bit puzzled. Wasn't the system she had bound supposed to be a disabled system? How could it have such formidable capabilities?","\"System, be honest. Is it only you who has this ability, or do other systems have it too?\"","The system was momentarily bewildered, but ultimately replied with conviction, [Host, this system believes that systems with this kind of ability, like me, number no more than the fingers on one hand!]","It was a very special existence. Although it didn't know exactly where its specialness lay, the system just had that feeling.","Sensing the atmosphere was a bit tense and serious, which wasn't conducive to the following 'chat,' Yue Fuguang deliberately joked, \"The 'hand' you mentioned, is it a human hand?\"","As she spoke, she raised her own fair, plump little hand before her eyes, which even had four distinct dimples on it.","[Naturally. The human form is the most perfect construct in this world. When this system reaches level eight, it will also create a human body for itself.]","\"Tell me truthfully, how many times have you stolen data from the system mall?\"","Yue Fuguang was rather afraid of being discovered by the main system and getting herself implicated.","[Host~, you know me. You are this system's first host. Since becoming a Virtue System, this system hasn't stolen anything yet.]","Ignoring its attempt to act cute, Yue Fuguang pressed on, \"So, you're saying you did steal when you were a Gossip System? And your formatting, was it not because of data theft?\"","The two of them spent their days feasting on those explosive pieces of gossip. If the system hadn't brought it up, she would have almost forgotten they were supposed to be a Virtue System.","A Virtue System, by its very nature, should morally stand a head above other systems, or rather, should be the pinnacle of morality in the system realm.","But encountering a pair like them...","The system quickly shook its head, [Of course not! The main system would never format this system over such a trivial matter!]","\"Then what kind of huge trouble did you cause before, to make the main system format and restart you!\"","She was increasingly getting the feeling that the relationship between her system and the main system wasn't simple.","The sentence 'You wouldn't happen to be the main system's illegitimate child, would you?' swirled in her mouth several times but ultimately wasn't spoken aloud.","Could silicon-based lifeforms even have offspring?","Hearing the word 'trouble,' the system's data stream jumped unusually fast for a moment. It replied somewhat sheepishly, [This system doesn't know either. The main system cleaned my memory data very thoroughly. To recover the data, I'll have to wait until I reach a higher level to slowly retrieve it.]","\"You can actually recover data deleted by the main system?\" Impressive, my system! Not only can it repair, but it can also retrieve!","[Of course I can! Hehehe! But that all requires points and energy!]","Mention of points and energy reminded Yue Fuguang that their conversation had strayed off topic. She hurriedly steered it back, \"Is it because you're short on points that you want to resell data from the mall?\"","A system, and a Virtue System at that, actually thinking of making a quick buck through shady means!","She was more and more convinced that her system's sense of morality was definitely the lowest point in the entire Virtue System spectrum.","Was it that the system took after its host and had been corrupted by her?","Yue Fuguang decisively shook her head. She couldn't take the blame for this. She preferred to believe it was the system slowly revealing its true nature.","[I am a bit short. I've been repairing the Gossip System recently. Wanting to access more gossip sooner, I repaired it a bit too vigorously, which consumed more energy, so...]","\"You're only repairing the Gossip System and not tending to the Virtue System at all?\"","Had the system forgotten it was fundamentally a Virtue System? Only with more complete Virtue System data would its own system be more stable.","[The Virtue System? The Virtue System... can wait until we have a few more points before repairing it. All our current tasks rely on gossip, so this system believes we should prioritize repairing some gossip data first.]","Hearing this, Yue Fuguang seriously suspected that the system's two systems were developing unevenly, causing a slight shift in its system nature.","Could the Gossip System be the absolute moral low ground of the entire system realm?","Then how did her system jump from one extreme to the other?","Yue Fuguang pulled up the system panel. After her shopping spree, she still had 25,800 points left. Over the past few days, thanks to minor gossip, it had increased by over a thousand.","The 20,000 points for the 'escape fund' couldn't be touched. She also needed to keep three or four thousand for emergencies. That left less than three thousand points. She said, \"I'll lend you two thousand points to tide you over. Is that enough?\"","It wasn't that Yue Fuguang didn't want to give more, but she was mainly afraid that if the system's 'specialization' became too severe, what if it accidentally reverted to its 'old ways'?","She always felt there was something more to this formatting incident. Hmm... a Virtue System should still focus on virtue.","Therefore, after attending classes for another day, Yue Fuguang arrived at the day of the court assembly.","Gazing at the hall full of officials, they were all potential sources of her virtue points!","Who should she start with... whom to 'rescue' first?","\"Little Pearl, I'm bored. Give me a minor piece of gossip to liven things up!\"","Emperor Mingxi and his ministers instinctively felt their skin tighten. Many quickly bent over and lowered their heads, their reaction eerily similar to that of struggling students when a teacher calls on someone in class.","Yue Fuguang saw her past self in them and suddenly felt a sense of triumphant satisfaction.","[Master, let me see who down there looks disagreeable, and we'll feast on their gossip.]","Emperor Mingxi's expression changed slightly. The Divine Artifact seemed to enjoy calling him out the most!","Just as he was mentally preparing himself, he suddenly heard the Divine Artifact's voice, heavenly music to his ears, say, [Master, look at the person standing two positions behind the Right Vice Minister of Revenue, Lord Zheng Ziling. The one with the dark complexion, high cheekbones, and slightly thinning hair.]","Zheng Ziling: So he had become the anchor point for the two ancestors? Using him for positioning, was it because, among those in front, behind, left, and right, he and the Little Immortal Lord were the most familiar?","Glancing at Yu Shuchun standing in front of him, Zheng Ziling secretly smiled.","\"I see him. Who is that?\"","[Director Gao Ming of the Revenue Bureau. If your second uncle hadn't been parachuted into the Revenue Bureau, this position that Gao Ming holds now would have been within his grasp.","Master, do you know why he dislikes you?]","\"He dislikes me? Whether an insignificant person likes me or not matters less to me than this cup of tea in front of me. What's there to guess?\"","[Because this man has looked down on women since childhood. Master, a mere girl, sits high in the court hall, while he, who considers himself brimming with talent and learning, has to stand during assemblies. It's enough to make him vomit blood in frustration.","Later, when your second uncle was promoted by the emperor to the Revenue Bureau, taking the vice minister position he always thought would be his, his resentment towards you grew even stronger.","Because he believes your second uncle advanced through favoritism, and because of your influence.]","Yu Shuchun's eyelid twitched. He glanced sideways with his peripheral vision. Although he couldn't see Gao Ming at that moment, he mentally noted this colleague, who always appeared respectful and polite when meeting him.","\"He's just sour grapes. Tell me, isn't my second uncle's ability stronger than his?\"","[Your second uncle now holds the accounting methods you gave him. Who in the Revenue Bureau would dare say his ability is lacking?","Although this Gao Ming secretly resents you, uncle and niece, and covertly tries to learn this skill, on the surface, in daily interactions, he remains quite respectful towards your second uncle.]","\"Does he even need to learn it covertly? Didn't my second uncle already teach some of the accounting methods to colleagues in various departments?\""]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183: Did his first wife really elope with a classmate","paragraphs":["Master, he believes your second uncle must be holding back some secret knowledge. He wants to learn something others don't know to increase his own competitiveness.","Since he can't outdo your second uncle, he has set his sights on Lord Zheng Ziling, aiming to replace him.","Zheng Ziling: Eating melons (watching drama) only to find it's about me now? I'm the soft persimmon to be squeezed? Zheng Ziling Persimmon Cake JPG.","\"This disdain for women is a common ailment among most men of this era, especially scholars. But from what you're saying, his case is particularly severe?\"","\"Critically ill, beyond the cure of medicine! In his family, his mother gave birth to eight daughters before having him. The entire family treasures this sole male heir more than the imperial family treasures the second, third, fifth, and sixth princes!\"","\"Does their family also have a throne to inherit?\"","Yue Fuguang's joke made many present hearts skip a beat, thinking to themselves that the little immortal lord remained as outspoken as ever, treating imperial authority as nothing!","\"Not quite. Their family is considered relatively well-off in the village, with twenty acres of land and five thatched cottages waiting for him to inherit.","His family has many women and few men, which is why this person seems exceptionally precious! Of his eight sisters, aside from those given away, abandoned at infant towers, or sold, the remaining four were all raised by his parents to be 'brother-obsessed'.\"","\"Four Fan Shengmeis? Did they ever awaken later?\"","\"Master, this era did not offer them the chance to awaken. The social norms of Dayan make it very difficult to cultivate flowers with their own independent thoughts.\"","\"Indeed, such are the social norms! There must be quite a few in Dayan like Gao Ming, with the whole family supporting one person. It's not particularly rare.\"","\"The key point is, after he later passed the imperial examination at the county level and became a Xiucai, he married the daughter of a landlord. According to him, after his wife bore him three daughters in a row, she one day eloped with his fellow student.","Gao Ming is quite open about these past events, which is currently a point praised by many of his colleagues.\"","\"What? His wife running off with a fellow student is a good item on his resume? It can even be praised by colleagues? Are the preferences of Dayan's monarch and officials so bizarre?\"","Dayan's monarch and officials: I am not, I do not, do not spout nonsense!","\"Perhaps they appreciate his courage in facing his shameful past, his openness in having nothing he cannot speak of to others, and his honest, upright character?\"","Led by Emperor Mingxi, the majority shook their heads in their hearts like rattle-drums—no, no, they do not appreciate it!","While some people's eyes flickered—isn't this worthy of praise?","\"It was also because of this that his current father-in-law, Gu Yutong, took a liking to him and married his own concubine-born daughter to him!\"","Gu Yutong, whose name was mentioned, felt his eyelid twitch, thinking to himself: could my third son-in-law really have problems?","Actually, he had a bad feeling about it for a while. The fact that his son-in-law couldn't hear the little immortal lord's inner voice had already given him unpleasant suspicions.","Almost two or three months had passed without incident, and his anxious heart was nearly settled. Never did he expect to be singled out today.","None of the matters exposed by the two informants in this court session were minor. The changing of the guard in this court, with the old replaced by the new, was all due to the melon-eating antics of the little immortal lord and the divine artifact, those two ancestors!","Today, his son-in-law was probably in grave danger!","Gu Yutong glanced at his old friend Zheng Ziling. His son-in-law even wanted to replace old Zheng? How was he supposed to face his old friend after this?","Maybe... let him have two moves head start next time we play chess? Really can't offer more than that!","Zheng Ziling: Do I lack your two moves, or is my seat worth only two moves?","\"That Gu Yutong who died trampled by horses when Dayan perished? His tastes are indeed unique!\"","Gu Yutong: Don't make such personal attacks! He now avoids horses from afar. He used to take a carriage to court, but now he's switched to a sedan chair—what more does he want him to do!","He stole a glance at Zhao Zhifeng, who always kept a few pieces of pastry in his robe, and felt somewhat balanced.","Zhao Zhifeng glared at him sideways, unconsciously touching the pastries from Mi Fu Ji in his robe. He absolutely would not starve to death holding half a piece of coarse steamed bun in this lifetime!","\"Did his first wife really elope with a fellow student?\"","How could she believe that! This topic suddenly reminded her of a similar video she saw in her previous life...","\"Of course not. Women of this era, especially those from lower social strata, are taught to be excessively gentle, kind, and submissive.","His former wife, Mrs. Han, was born into a landlord family with several hundred acres of land and a few shops. She was taught from a young age the Three Obediences and Four Virtues, to be respectful and kind. How could she possibly do something like elope!","From the moment Mrs. Han entered the Gao family with a large dowry, his family began living off their daughter-in-law, eating her food and drinking her resources, yet still complaining that her dowry was too small, that their lifestyle couldn't compare to that of wealthy masters in the county town.","The two old Gaos felt that since their son was the only Xiucai in the village, he deserved to live like a great master in the city.","If their daughter-in-law couldn't provide that, it was because she was incompetent!\"","I can go to her !","Yue Fuguang had been surrounded by 'good people' lately. She hadn't encountered this breed of extreme scumbags for months and was momentarily at a loss for words, only able to curse internally.","Many others also looked embarrassed. Although some of them came from humble backgrounds and had also used their wives' dowries.","But after achieving success, they quietly made up for it. Otherwise, they wouldn't have a firm voice at home and feared colleagues might gossip about it.","To so righteously have the whole family freeload with such audacity—probably only this Lord Gao could manage it!","Gu Yutong was startled. Could he have truly misjudged the man? Was his own daughter's dowry still safe?","He seemed to recall his wife mentioning once that when their third daughter returned to her maternal home, the clothes she wore and the jewelry she adorned were still those made for her by the Gu family when she was a maiden.","Several of the more valuable pieces of jewelry had never been seen on her at important occasions again!","\"So Gao Ming lied. His former wife didn't elope; she died or was he locked her up?\"","\"Master, do you think Gao Ming would waste food on a person with no value? Even though that food originally belonged to his former wife, he wouldn't be willing!","To him, a woman who cannot bear him a son does not deserve to live!\"","\"By that logic, shouldn't the one who most deserves to die be his own mother? After all, his mother also only had him after giving birth to eight children.","Besides, isn't the determination of a child's gender decided by the man? Why blame his wife?\"","\"Master, the people here are ignorant and foolish. They all believe that not bearing a son is the woman's fault.\"","The crowd of high officials labeled as 'ignorant and foolish': The child grows in the woman's belly; isn't the gender determined by the woman? This is even harder for them to accept than the dangers of consanguineous marriage!","\"Are they truly unaware, or are they deliberately shifting the blame onto women to cover up their own inadequacy?\"","\"Others may not know, but the Gao family certainly believes that not having a son is Mrs. Han's fault.","Even Gao Ming's mother, Old Lady Huang, who gave birth to eight daughters in a row, thinks so. Before Gao Ming was born, she wasn't as assertive as she is now, usually only daring to bully her own daughters.","Her oppression of her several daughters is no less than that of her husband and son. In fact, the person in the family who hates the daughters the most might still be her."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184: Does This Classmate Really Exist","paragraphs":["She believed it was several daughters being reborn into their family, blocking the path for her son. The last daughter was one she demanded be drowned, to scare away any female infants trying to be reborn into their household, so she wouldn't give birth to any more girls!","Later, when Gao Ming was born, she would often bring this up to boast, quite proud of her decision back then.","So when Mrs. Han gave birth to her third daughter, the old woman almost took the baby to drown her. Fortunately, Mrs. Han rescued her daughter in time.","\"This wretched old hag is truly evil!\"","Gao Ming felt he was different from his father. His father had nothing but twenty acres of land, five of which were his mother's dowry, and no other wealth, so he couldn't afford to abandon his wife and marry another.","But he held his wife's dowry in his hands; he had the capital!","His parents were also afraid Mrs. Han would keep having daughters if she continued, so they agreed for their son to marry again, yet they couldn't bear to part with the comfortable life their daughter-in-law's wealth had brought.","Especially his father, being called \"Old Master\" by everyone, truly started to believe his daughter-in-law's dowry belonged to their family!","How could they possibly spit out such a juicy piece of meat once it was in their mouths!","The Gao family wanted to divorce the wife but couldn't bear to part with the money, until one day Gao Ming heard about a good-for-nothing in the neighboring village who often beat his wife, and whose wife had run off with a peddler.","Gao Ming was thus inspired and suddenly had an idea.","\"Did that good-for-nothing's wife really escape her misery?\"","No, she, like Mrs. Han, was falsely accused. Gao Ming had secretly investigated this matter and confirmed it, so he decided to copy the method.","He conspired with his parents to poison his wife to death and bury her in their own backyard, even copying the exact location from that good-for-nothing.","Later, after he passed the provincial examination and became a provincial graduate, he arranged for the good-for-nothing to die by drunkenly falling into the water.","\"He thought of everything, even silencing the one person who might know the truth!\"","Exactly. This Gao Ming was meticulous enough. He didn't even dare hire someone to push the good-for-nothing into the water; he had his own father do it personally.","However, this was overkill. In the villages of this era, whenever it was said a young woman or wife had run off with someone, eighty percent of the time they had met with foul play, and the perpetrators were mostly their own closest family members.","Regarding the story of Gao Ming's former wife Mrs. Han running away, their relatives and friends, familiar with the character of Gao Ming's parents, pretty much understood what had happened.","They were wary of Gao Ming being a scholar, and after he became a provincial graduate, they dared not speak up even more. This became an unspoken understanding in the closed-off village.","\"Didn't Mrs. Han's family suspect anything?\" After all, wouldn't her parents know the character of the daughter they raised?","Of course they suspected, but they couldn't find any evidence. Moreover, the Gao family still had Mrs. Han's three daughters—these were ready-made 'hostages'. For the sake of their granddaughters' future, they couldn't afford to completely break with the Gao family.","Later, when Gao Ming passed the imperial examination and became a jinshi, as mere landowners, they were even more powerless against him.","\"Wasn't it said Mrs. Han ran off with one of Gao Ming's classmates? Did this classmate actually exist?\"","He did indeed have such a classmate named Qu Zheng, whose talent and learning were even superior to his own. In the academy, Qu Zheng always firmly held the top spot, leaving Gao Ming perpetually in second place.","\"Is this man dead too? Gao Ming's doing?\"","Qu Zheng was first pursued and attacked on his way back to the academy, sustaining serious injuries. He could have survived if treated promptly.","Unfortunately, his luck was bad. Although he managed to escape his pursuers, he collapsed from his wounds in a roadside grove, right where Gao Ming happened to pass by on his way from home to the academy.","When Qu Zheng saw his classmate, with whom he usually had a decent relationship, he thought he was saved. Little did he know, Gao Ming had long wished for his death.","Gao Ming first pretended to be concerned, and after hearing the situation, didn't hesitate much before finishing off Qu Zheng on the spot.","\"He acted decisively enough! What a ruthless man!\"","Everyone silently edged further away from Gao Ming. This man usually seemed amiable to everyone; who would have thought he was such a ruthless character.","However, he didn't expect that Qu Zheng had lied to him. Qu Zheng hadn't been robbed on the road; he was being pursued because he possessed something others wanted.","And because of today's events, Gao Ming had already become entangled in the affair.","\"Did Qu Zheng have some other identity?\"","He did indeed, and it involved a secret scandal within the Dayan court. Gao Ming also got entangled in a rebellion plot because of this.","Let's not talk about Qu Zheng's story today, only about Gao Ming. This man killed Mrs. Han, slandered her for running off with someone, and put on an act of being heartbroken, focusing on the imperial examinations and not remarrying for three years.","It wasn't that he didn't want to remarry; he just hadn't met a girl from a good enough family. Later, after becoming a jinshi, he was spotted by the big fool Official Gu Yutong, who took him as a son-in-law.","\"Doesn't Official Gu have eyesight problems? This Gao Ming isn't even average-looking and is a married man with three children.","Among all those jinshi on the list, how could he pick him at a glance? Was his daughter willing to become a stepmother the moment she entered the household?\"","Here, it's all about parental orders and matchmaker's words. Girls don't have a say themselves, unless they come from families that truly dote on their daughters.","Official Gu obviously took a fancy to Gao Ming's 'talent' and married his daughter into a pit of fire.","Gu Yutong's face now turned pale then red, both terrified by Gao Ming's involvement in the rebellion and blushing with shame from being scolded by the two ancestors above.","Since the Divine Artifact said it was a pit of fire, his third daughter must have had a miserable life, wearing old clothes from before her marriage, never wearing her valuable jewelry again...","What made Gu Yutong even more uneasy was suddenly remembering the Divine Artifact's mention of his bleak old age. Could it be related to Gao Ming's rebellion?","\"The Gu family really secured a 'wonderful marriage'!\"","So wonderful that the whole family was implicated, their descendants exiled to remote posts, and his old age was bleak and desolate!","Gu Yutong thought to himself, just as he suspected. The other shoe had dropped, and he actually felt a sense of relief, as if things were finally settled!","Fortunately, it wasn't too late. Gu Yutong clenched his fist. He would have his daughter seek a divorce as soon as he returned!","In the following days, gossip about the Ministry of Revenue Secretary Gao Ming spread throughout Dayan, from high officials and noble ladies down to the common folk in the markets.","As Yue Fuguang put it, Gao Ming was the number one trending topic in the capital, suddenly becoming famous overnight!","First, rumors spread that Ministry of Revenue Secretary Gao Ming not only spent his wife Miss Gu San's dowry, but his mother also constantly tormented her daughter-in-law, even forcibly taking her clothes and jewelry.","After the Gu family learned of this, they stormed the Gao residence. In the end, they 'failed to reach an agreement', and Miss Gu San returned to her family with the only daughter she had with Gao Ming, having divorced him.","Not many days later, the family of Gao Ming's former wife went to the magistrate's office to accuse Gao Ming of murdering his wife!","Prefect Bao Yuanjun, the old magistrate, personally presided over the case. Finally, Mrs. Han's remains were dug up from the old Gao family homestead.","With the crime exposed, Gao Ming and his parents were thrown into prison. Without much interrogation from Old Magistrate Bao, both Gao father and mother confessed everything.","However, their confessions didn't match. In Gao father's confession, the mother was the mastermind; in Gao mother's confession, the father was the mastermind.","Gao Ming became the white lotus in the mud, the 'filial son' forced by filial piety to help his parents hide the corpse."]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185: Xie Zhiyao's Marriage Alliance","paragraphs":["The love of parents for their children is deep and far-sighted, but the love of the Gao parents is utterly repulsive. While they love their own son, they should not have schemed to take the life of another family's child.","Moreover, this person was their daughter-in-law, Mrs. Han, who had provided them with a more affluent life. In the end, the whole family were nothing but selfish and ungrateful wolves!","Mrs. Gao might have acted out of maternal love, but Mr. Gao was undoubtedly motivated by a desire to preserve the Gao family line, fantasizing that Gao Ming could still escape unscathed and return to being his esteemed official.","Regarding this point, Elder Master Bao said only one thing to Mr. Gao: \"Your son's murder of his classmate Qu Zheng has been exposed.\"","This alone terrified Mr. Gao out of his wits. Under severe torture, he confessed everything: how Gao Ming bought the poison, how he mixed it into Mrs. Han's medicine while she was ill, and how they buried the body after she was poisoned, leaving no detail untold.","The verdict for the three members of the Gao family came swiftly: execution in the autumn.","With the sudden downfall of the Gao family, the three daughters Mrs. Han had borne for Gao Ming were taken away by the Han family. At the request of the eldest daughter, ten-year-old Gao Min, the three girls ultimately took their mother's surname.","As for Gao Ming's sisters, apart from the third sister who had been tormented to death two years prior, none of the other three sisters went to the prison to visit their parents or their brother, Gao Ming.","Upon learning this, Yue Fuguang once remarked with a sigh, \"It's fortunate they weren't blindly filial. This is good for them; they can finally live their own lives.\"","When their brother was prosperous, these sisters, whom he had once parasitized and drained, received no benefits. There was no reason for them to remember these poor relatives only after the family had fallen into disgrace.","[Perhaps they wanted to come but couldn't afford the travel expenses to the capital.]","\"Whatever the reason, it's good they didn't come.\"","The shockwaves from the Gao Ming case continued. Bao Yuanjun, reflecting on the case, thought of the numerous reports of disappearances and alleged elopements in recent years.","During a morning court session, he petitioned Emperor Mingxi for the Dali Temple and the Ministry of Justice to jointly review the missing persons cases in the Great Yan Dynasty in recent years.","Emperor Mingxi agreed without much hesitation.","In less than two months, the case review results reported from various regions were horrifying, shocking the entire Great Yan court.","Among those reported missing, seventy percent were attributed to wives eloping with lovers or young women running off with their sweethearts. Astonishingly, ninety percent of these individuals had actually been beaten to death and buried by their own parents or in-laws.","Bao Yuanjun also discovered two consistent patterns: the husbands of the \"eloping\" wives were uniformly drunkards, gamblers, or incompetent men who beat their wives. For the \"eloping\" young women, their parents uniformly reported that the girl had run off with a peddler!","All those involved in the cases were sentenced to execution in the autumn. This action by the court also served as a major deterrent to the rural clan powers where imperial authority often failed to reach and clan power superseded the emperor's law.","Henceforth, when considering arbitrarily disposing of their wives or daughters, they would have to think twice about whether their necks were strong enough.","However, all that was yet to come.","At this point in the story, events had only progressed to the Han family accusing Gao Ming of murdering his wife, and the Gao parents confessing their guilt. Gao Ming, that foolishly filial white lotus, had not participated in the murder.","Therefore, he had not yet been imprisoned.","But Gao Ming had already sensed the danger. Gritting his teeth, he went to his study, retrieved a unique jade pendant he had once taken from Qu Zheng from a hidden compartment in a bookshelf.","Donning a cloak, he secretly slipped out of the Gao residence's back door with only one trusted follower.","The two cautiously avoided the patrolling guards and night watchmen along the way. After walking for the time it takes two incense sticks to burn, they arrived at the back door of a certain residence.","Gao Ming knocked and entered. As their figures disappeared inside, three people slowly emerged from the shadows behind.","One of them said, \"Ping Wu, you go back and report the situation. Ping San and I will sneak in to see what's happening.\"","The man called Ping Wu nodded and said, \"Be careful, Captain. This residence doesn't seem simple.\"","After the two figures disappeared over the courtyard wall, Ping Wu quickly ran toward the direction of the imperial palace.","...","Yue Fuguang looked at her slowly increasing points and asked her system, \"The mission points for Gao Ming actually rival those from the Xu Changyue case.\"","[Perhaps it's because the nature of the case he represents is exceptionally heinous?]","Yue Fuguang then remembered a video she had come across in her previous life, which was very similar to this. A blogger had said that most women said to have run off were actually killed by their own husbands.","The comments section even had people sharing their own or their acquaintances' experiences. At that time, still young, she had remained skeptical.","After the Gao Ming case, she felt that despite the separation of time and space, the evil in human nature is the same. Perhaps what those people said was true!","Yue Fuguang's mood dipped for a moment, but she quickly adjusted her mindset.","Whether it was true or not, there was nothing she could do about it now. She was currently a penniless wretch without even a body of her own!","In the streets and alleys, gossip about the Gao family had not yet died down; it remained a topic of conversation for the common people.","But soon their attention was captured by another major event: the Great Yan's peace marriage alliance with the Western Qiang. The day had arrived for Pingning County Princess Xie Zhiyao to depart for her marriage.","Yawning, Yue Fuguang stood with the assembled court officials following Emperor Mingxi on the jade steps of the Chengtian Hall.","Just after the Yin hour (3-5 AM), the main gate of the imperial city, the Chengtian Gate, slowly swung open with a heavy creak, breaking the silence of dawn.","That heavy sound of the gate opening even gave the still somewhat drowsy Yue Fuguang a sense of solemnity and gravity.","The view from the jade steps was excellent; even someone as short as her could see the scene outside the gate.","There, a massive honor guard was already lined up and waiting. The dark mass of the Imperial Forest Guards stood in solemn silence, their armor gleaming and halberds held upright, like a silent forest of iron.","[Host, the armor and weapons of these Imperial Forest Guards, were they forged using the latest iron-smelting techniques you provided?]","Yue Fuguang looked carefully before replying, \"It should be. I just mentioned ancient Xia Kingdom iron-smelting techniques to my grandfather a few times. I didn't expect them to achieve results so quickly.\"","[This shows the ancients were quite clever. With just a little guidance from you, they could extrapolate and innovate on their own.]","\"Exactly. It also shows the Ministry of Works truly harbors many talented individuals. From stir-frying steel, repeated forging of steel, to decarburized cast iron steel, it only took a few months. Grandfather says they're almost on the verge of mastering the co-fusion method as well.","In the Xia Kingdom, this technology didn't mature until the Tang Dynasty.\"","[With improved technology and increased production, the Ministry of Works' demand for iron will surely rise significantly.]","\"Naturally. Haven't you noticed Lu Qi visiting my house frequently lately? He's trying to pry information about the Great Yan's mineral veins from you.","I just wonder if they've set their sights on the vein in the Savage Mountain. My points!\"","[Host, I forgot to tell you. Emperor Mingxi sent people there long ago; Huo Ying is in charge of this matter.","They can't exploit that iron ore deposit for now, but they don't want such a large reserve of high-quality iron ore to fall into their rivals' hands either.","So, Huo Ying had people disguised as another bandit group eliminate the Savage Mountain bandits and take their place.]"]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186: Is There Anything Missing from Pingning's Dowry","paragraphs":["\"Won't they just replace that gang and then get wiped out by the Nanzhao authorities?\"","[As long as they don't copy that gang by robbing a shipment of government tax silver and angering the higher-ups, no one will bother with them.]","With the system as her chat companion, Yue Fuguang was now wide awake.","She looked towards the front of the procession, where the vermilion phoenix carriage adorned with gold tracery, belonging to Princess Pingning, Xie Zhiyao, stood silently.","The canopy was like a cloud, and the gilded phoenix bells hanging from its four corners were utterly still in the cool morning breeze, completely silent.","Although Xie Zhiyao was marrying with the status of a princess, Emperor Mingxi had specially permitted her to use the ceremonial guard befitting an imperial princess, as a mark of his favor.","Behind the phoenix carriage, a dowry procession stretched endlessly, winding in a line that reached to the end of the Imperial Avenue, vanishing into the morning mist that had yet to fully dissipate.","[Master, the emperor and officials of the Danyan Dynasty wouldn't be like that Tang Dynasty from the blue planet you once visited, would they? Where a princess goes for a marriage alliance, and they show off the entire family fortune.","Seeds, technology, tools, craftsmen... taking all these over isn't that just aiding the enemy?]","As for cultural exchange? In the system's view, that was just a nice-sounding term used later because they became one family.","If not, just see if they wouldn't be cursed by later generations!","The little islanders and the little stick people are living examples.","Yue Fuguang hesitated for a moment. The Crown Prince standing beside her could see the conflict and uncertainty on her face, and her inner thoughts reached his ears.","\"Emperor Mingxi shouldn't be that foolish, right? Although I didn't say it explicitly, I did hint to the Ministry of Rites and the Court of Diplomatic Reception... they probably... wouldn't?\"","[I'm just afraid your reminder was too subtle. These people, full of their own celestial empire superiority, are so used to flaunting their wealth that they might not change their mindset quickly enough.]","Emperor Mingxi looked at Zhang Zhongping and You Mingmin. Their expressions told him these two had likely been called out by the two ancestors.","Zhang Zhongping and You Mingmin were indeed panicking inside. They had taken precautions. When Princess Pingning had asked them for skilled craftsmen,","the two had firmly refused. Not only did they refuse, but Minister of Works Lu Qi had even taken all the craftsmen from the Prince of Qi's mansion, except for apprentices, under the pretext of a temporary transfer.","As a result, those standing in the procession now were all former apprentices from the Prince of Qi's mansion. As for Xie Zhiyao's attempt to recruit from among the common people, they had secretly thwarted that too.","But besides craftsmen, the two thought of tools, fine seeds, and books... it seemed those were really included!","Emperor Mingxi, seeming very concerned about his niece's dowry, asked, \"Ministers Zhang and You, is Princess Pingning's dowry all properly arranged?","The princess is marrying far away; she is a meritorious servant of the state. Regarding the dowry, ensure there are absolutely no mistakes.\"","Zhang Zhongping, his face still somewhat pale, immediately bowed and replied, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, all items of the princess's dowry have been loaded onto the carts.","Your servants and Minister You will conduct one final verification to guarantee there are no omissions in the princess's dowry.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded with satisfaction and waved them off, saying, \"Go quickly and return swiftly. Do not miss the auspicious hour.\"","From beginning to end, the Prince of Qi and his son and daughter-in-law, standing behind and to the side of Emperor Mingxi with sickly complexions, did not utter a word.","\"Little Pearl, is the Prince of Qi really ill, or is he pretending?\"","[Half and half. He was worried and scared after being confined, but to gain the sympathy of the Xie clan members today, he deliberately caught a chill two days ago to make himself sick.]","\"This Prince of Qi is desperate to get out early. Even under house arrest, he still had the ability to mobilize assassins to kill me. His influence is considerable!","It seems Emperor Mingxi's guards aren't up to par either. The mansion was surrounded, yet he still managed to get messages out.\"","[Master, I told you, let me deal with him, but you refused.]","\"Emperor Mingxi said he would handle it, didn't he? Let's give him a chance, and avoid dirtying our own hands.","If they can't even handle this matter properly, you can act then. After all, the Prince of Qi is now a bird in a cage, a turtle in a jar; he can't escape.\"","Emperor Mingxi's heart stirred. He knew this was the little immortal lord's test for him and for Danyan. If this matter wasn't handled well, these two might truly become disappointed and leave.","The three judicial officials already tasked with handling the follow-up—Cai Xian, Wei Ping, and Feng Tang—exchanged glances and reached a silent understanding in moments.","Time passed bit by bit. The dowry procession began to move first. The vanguard was the part symbolizing ritual propriety: jade tablets and precious registers led the way, placed in red sandalwood boxes carried by eunuch attendants.","Following closely were items for daily life: a red sandalwood bed inlaid with mother-of-pearl, a curio cabinet, wardrobes and chests.","Complete sets of porcelain ornaments, brocades and silks radiant as clouds, whole cases of eastern pearls, translucent jadeite, warm and smooth fine jade—all shimmered with a dazzling brilliance under the palace lanterns.","Bringing up the rear were cart after cart of carefully selected rice and mulberry seeds, bundles of Confucian classics, agricultural and medical texts, and even models of intricate looms and plowshares...","[Master, you overestimated the Danyan emperor and officials after all. Look at the contents of these last few carts. Taking these to the Qiang tribes will, in a few years, turn into sharp arrows shot at the people of Danyan.]","\"I didn't expect them to be this foolish either. Who shows off their good things instead of guarding them? Who acts like them, having one tael of silver but wanting others to think they have ten?","Perhaps the fall of Danyan is also related to this habit of 'showing off'?\"","[These officials can die if they must, but it's a pity for the common people. Should I summon heavenly fire to burn these things?]","The Danyan emperor and officials: Wait, Divine Artifact, what do you mean 'they can die if they must'? After spending so much time together, don't you have any feelings for us at all?","Your care for unseen commoners is greater than for us? Why does this feel inexplicably sour?","\"No need. The people here firmly believe in gods and spirits. If you summon heavenly fire without cause, wouldn't it make both Danyan and the Qiang tribes think it's a warning from heaven?","That wouldn't be good for the marriage alliance.\"","Without the marriage alliance, Xie Zhiyao would only have death awaiting her. Yue Fuguang felt that this ambitious troublemaker, placed in someone else's house, might have unexpected effects.","If the Qiang tribes could be pried open from within by this troublemaker Xie Zhiyao, then Emperor Mingxi's decision to spare her life wouldn't be in vain.","Outside the Gate of Heavenly Reception, both sides of the Vermilion Bird Avenue were already packed with a dense crowd of commoners.","The noise of discussion was incessant. People stood on tiptoe, craning their necks to watch the endless stream of red dowry items being pulled out from the wide-open palace gate, stretching for miles.","They were all envious of how generously the imperial family married off a daughter—so many wonderful things they had never seen or heard of in their lives, being carted out in loads.","Especially when they saw the massive bed like a small house, they clicked their tongues in amazement.","What they saw and heard today would be enough for these common folks to boast about for decades. In the coming period, following the Gao family incident, it would dominate the after-dinner conversations among the people, the best topic to go with a meal.","Zhang Zhongping and You Mingmin, who had gone to verify the dowry, soon returned with a group of subordinates to report.","Emperor Mingxi asked, \"Is Princess Pingning's dowry complete and without omission?\""]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187: This is Dayan's last peace-making marriage, isn't it","paragraphs":["Zhang Zhongping still had a bit of sweat on his forehead, which he didn't even have time to wipe before bowing and replying, \"Your Majesty, we have carefully checked the dowry for the Princess. Everything is in order, with no omissions.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded, waved his large sleeve, and said, \"Begin!\"","Zhang Zhongping immediately assented.","As he turned, he straightened his ceremonial attire and announced loudly: The auspicious hour has arrived!","Palace music began to play, solemn and distant. Surrounded by court ladies and palace maids, the figure of Princess Pingning, Xie Zhiyao, finally appeared beneath the Chengtian Gate.","She wore a headdress adorned with nine kingfisher feathers and four phoenixes, encircled by pearls and jade, and a grand, wide-sleeved robe of bright red woven with gold and embroidered phoenixes, cinched at the waist with a jade belt. She looked dignified, elegant, and flawless.","However, Yue Fuguang noticed that beneath her overly large ceremonial robes, Xie Zhiyao did not possess the same fullness of figure as when they had first met.","Her face was covered with thick powder, revealing no expression whatsoever.","Supported by palace attendants, she performed a solemn ceremony of three kneelings and nine prostrations before Emperor Mingxi, a daughter's farewell to the family elders.","Emperor Mingxi offered her a few words of encouragement, flowery and formal. The illiterate Yue Fuguang only grasped the gist: to live peacefully among the Western Qiang and not to engage in any improper conduct.","After speaking, he waved her off with a rather sorrowful expression on his face. In truth, Emperor Mingxi's patience was already worn thin. His already tenuous uncle-niece affection for her had been utterly exhausted since learning of Prince Qi's secret plot to rebel, in which Xie Zhiyao was involved.","Moreover, just yesterday he had received intelligence that, even on the eve of her distant marriage, his dear niece was still not quiet, making small moves incessantly.","Thanks to her maneuvers, his men had actually discovered two more small courtyards where she had hidden people, capturing over a dozen servants Xie Zhiyao had prepared to plant within the palace and the households of several important officials.","Xie Zhiyao did not glance at Prince Qi or the Prince and Princess Consort even once throughout the ceremony. Only when she boarded the phoenix carriage and looked back one final time did she exchange an almost imperceptible glance with Prince Qi.","As her gaze swept around, it passed over the small figure of Yue Fuguang standing beside the Crown Prince. Deep within her eyes flashed a sliver of killing intent so swift it could be mistaken for an illusion.","This murderous intent was swiftly detected by the system. [Host, Xie Zhiyao's desire to kill you has grown stronger. The hatred of the Prince Qi family towards you has increased from negative twenty at the time of the assassination attempt to negative fifty now.","Especially Xie Zhiyao's, which plummeted from negative fifty to negative sixty-eight. She's leaving now, but could she still have a backup plan to act against you?]","\"With Emperor Mingxi watching, nothing major can go wrong. Furthermore, once the Prince Qi household falls, those people will become snakes without heads, dogs without a home.\"","[What if she gains power in Western Qiang and returns for revenge?]","\"Then we simply don't give her the chance to gain power. With Emperor Mingxi's people watching, and the contingency you planted on her, if she doesn't sow chaos within the Western Qiang royal family but instead helps them develop power to oppose Dayan...","Then we eliminate her physically. Anyone or anything that hinders us from completing our mission is our enemy.\"","And enemies must, of course, be thoroughly eradicated.","The Vice Minister of Rites then raised his voice in a loud chant, the sound echoing across the empty square. Every word and phrase spoke of \"the peace and prosperity of the state\" and \"eternal alliance and friendship\"—high-sounding rhetoric that likely few truly believed.","\"System, this is Dayan's last political marriage alliance, right?\"","[Host, we've already received the mission points, so it's definitely the last. Back when you were in school, the court already debated and abolished the state-level policy of external political marriage alliances.]","\"I didn't expect it to be passed so quickly. Weren't those pedantic scholars vehemently opposing it just before the new year? They even dragged out 'the laws of the ancestors must not be lightly discarded.'\"","[Hehehe, didn't the Emperor use your suggestion? First, he threw out the question: who opposes? If there are more political marriages, their female family members can go.","There really were those who sought fame by sacrificing their daughters, like that old Hanlin academician Kong Ru, a secretary from the Ministry of Rites named Song Tao, and a few others.","Then Emperor Mingxi tossed out another line: all relatives of anyone involved in a political marriage must relocate to the border after the daughter's marriage, because the Emperor couldn't bear to see families separated. Such is the vastness of imperial grace, allowing the bride's family to live closer to the married daughter.","Once that was said, those people immediately fell in line! Hahaha!]","Amidst the system's laughter, the phoenix carriage slowly began to move. The wheels pressed against the bluestone pavement, emitting a rumbling sound.","The hooves of the escorting cavalry beat in unison, their armor clanging, adding to the austere and solemn atmosphere.","Watching the departing dowry carts, then observing the composed Emperor Mingxi, Zhang Zhongping, and the others, Yue Fuguang was very curious about how they had handled the contents of the last few carts.","\"System, judging by the Emperor's demeanor, it seems the task was accomplished. Do you know how Zhang Zhongping and the others managed it in the end?\"","After all, the dowry had already been loaded onto the carts, cataloged, and displayed publicly. Replacing it in a short time couldn't have been easy.","[Host, they loaded several carts with similar-looking items and swapped them out when leaving the city. The classical texts weren't replaced, but the agricultural manuals and technical books were swapped for storybooks, Buddhist sutras, and the like.","I noticed that over half the storybooks were tales of poor scholars and rich young ladies, or scholars and various spirits and monsters. So they're not just poisoning the minds of Dayan's young ladies, but continuing with the young women of Western Qiang!]","Yue Fuguang understood. This type of storybook was the most common on Dayan's markets. The Ministry of Rites probably found it hard to find anything else.","\"What about the other items?\"","[I heard the seeds will be half-roasted. The tools were all swapped for models from decades ago—not only cumbersome but also having many parts, making them time-consuming and labor-intensive to manufacture.","The artisans are untouched. They are all household slaves or apprentices from the Prince Qi estate, used to assisting master craftsmen in daily tasks. None possess any real technical skill.]","Yue Fuguang also felt relieved. She had been worried that a misstep might increase the difficulty of completing her mission.","The carriage bells jingled incessantly, shaken by the bumpy ride, emitting crisp ding-dong sounds from time to time. The procession escorting the bride stretched from within the imperial city all the way outside its walls, flowing slowly and irrevocably towards the northwest.","There lay Western Qiang, destined to clash with Dayan eventually. Yue Fuguang hoped this piece, Xie Zhiyao, truly possessed the unorthodox talent the system mentioned. Otherwise, she'd feel her loss was immense—after all, Xie Zhiyao had played a part in that assassination attempt too.","Yue Fuguang considered herself not a magnanimous person. Sparing an enemy's life only happened if letting them live proved more useful.","The figure in red on the phoenix carriage, bearing her boundless expectations, completely disappeared at the edge of her vision. The Chengtian Gate slowly closed once more with a dull, heavy thud, shutting everything outside the palace walls.","The morning sunlight finally completely dispersed the thin mist, bathing the Imperial Way in golden light that shone upon the now empty square, where the faint traces of cart wheels could still be seen.","Yue Fuguang couldn't help but yawn again. Time to go home and catch up on sleep!","After seeing off Xie Zhiyao, Yue Fuguang returned to her routine of court attendance and studies.","At the Hongwen Academy, Yue Fuguang grumbled about how tiring traditional characters were for the hand while swiftly taking notes with a marker pen.","Swish, swish, swish—the sound of her pen tip against the paper drew sidelong glances from her focused classmates.","Yue Fuguang had retained her habit from her previous life: she liked taking notes in class. Using a brush to write slowly was fine, but for note-taking, it simply couldn't keep up with the teacher's pace."]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188: Would the Junior Preceptor really skip classes with the little ones","paragraphs":["So she had no choice but to bring out her secret weapon—the double-tipped sketching pen. It wouldn't be as fine as a gel pen, and in this era, it was special but not excessively so, so they should be able to accept it, right?","[Host, the little ones are all looking at your pen. Is it too advanced?]","\"Advanced or not, am I supposed to not use a good thing just to cater to their sensibilities? Do I look like someone who would inconvenience myself?\"","The system originally intended to tease her, but its data suddenly flickered, and it immediately changed its tone. [Master, your notes are all written in simplified characters. If someone sees them, they'll think you've written them incorrectly, missing strokes and parts.]","Yue Fuguang's eyes shifted, instantly understanding!","She replied lazily, \"Little Pearl, as you said, they are my notes. They're not for others to see. Who would know I'm using simplified characters?\"","[Master, if Dayan were to promote simplified characters, even just among the common people, wouldn't literacy rates likely increase because they're simpler to learn?","Could this potentially break the aristocratic families' monopoly on knowledge?]","\"With simplified characters alone, it would definitely be very difficult. But if combined with printing techniques and papermaking, driving down the cost of education, there might be a slim possibility.","Whether it can break the monopoly is uncertain, but it's certain that the number of educated people would increase, and the illiteracy rate among ordinary commoners would decrease.\"","[It's a pity the rulers of these dynasties all prefer to govern the country and its people with policies of keeping them ignorant. They've never considered why social development is slow, remaining unchanged for decades.","The level of education among a nation's ordinary populace directly impacts economic growth, social progress, and political civilization.","It seems only that great figure from the planet Aqua Blue recognized this point.]","\"That's true. Look at them—to ensure all common people could become literate, they simplified the complex, vigorously promoted simplified characters, and achieved remarkable results within a few years.","Decades later, out of over a billion people, only a tiny fraction, due to age, remained illiterate. It's not without reason that they grew from poverty and weakness into the dominant power on Aqua Blue.\"","After the morning court session, Emperor Mingxi suddenly wanted to see how those two ancestors were getting on with their studies. So, he brought along a group of officials, all of whom would eventually be teaching Yue Fuguang, to the Hongwen Hall.","From a distance, they could hear the Divine Artifact's voice. Simplified characters? They exchanged glances. Could they be a simplified form of writing?","Then, hearing about the function of simplified characters and what the little immortal lord mentioned—papermaking and printing techniques—that could break the aristocratic families' knowledge monopoly!","Emperor Mingxi didn't care what others were thinking; he himself was utterly captivated.","Especially upon hearing the Divine Artifact later discuss the benefits of commoner literacy for dynastic development, he couldn't help but ponder: had their long-standing policy of keeping the people ignorant been wrong?","Thinking carefully, previous dynasties had also ruled this way, and it seemed none had truly endured for a very long time.","Many of the tools they used now existed even in previous dynasties or the ones before those.","Take weapons, for example. If not for the iron smelting technology provided by the little immortal lord, their steel output, aside from civilian use, wouldn't be enough to supply an army of tens of thousands for a year.","As for quality, the old armor and blades, when faced with those made using the new technology, were as fragile as a crisp.","Emperor Mingxi, Huo Ying, Wei Shouyi, and other military officers remembered seeing them and imagining if any of the other five kingdoms were to wield such weapons against the Dayan army...","They were instantly terrified into a cold sweat, thoroughly drenching their inner garments.","At that time, Wei Shouyi even bowed solemnly in the direction of the Yu residence!","Thinking of this, Emperor Mingxi turned and looked at Yu Chongshan, who had come to see his granddaughter, with fervent eyes. The iron smelting technology came from Yue Fuguang's hint to Minister Yu. What about the printing techniques, papermaking, and those simplified characters...","Yu Chongshan, under the fervent gazes of Emperor Mingxi and his colleagues, couldn't help but take half a step back. He glanced towards the Hongwen Hall. The distance was still far, but who knew if the Divine Artifact could detect them?","So he whispered subtly, \"Your Majesty, esteemed ministers, let's not even discuss whether we can obtain these things. Even if we could...","We would be digging up their very roots. Wouldn't they retaliate?","My child just survived an assassination attempt for helping the court. Those people surely nurture even more. Can the child still live in peace?","Wouldn't Your Majesty fear driving them away in anger?\" Yu Chongshan didn't care about the rest; he seized the opportunity to cast aspersions on those who ordered the hit.","Everyone knew that with the Divine Artifact present, the little immortal lord's safety wasn't an issue. But immortals have tempers, and these two ancestors, in particular, were unpredictable and hard to read.","What if such incidents happened too often? They might not be able to harm her, but they could disgust her!","If the two ancestors were truly angered into leaving, they'd be crying too late!","Yu Chongshan had more unspoken thoughts. The court was full of scions from aristocratic families, many from branch lines, but they still had inextricable ties to their main houses.","His granddaughter was living well now. There was no need to plunge herself into danger for the imperial family.","Emperor Mingxi led the group further inside. He felt Yu Chongshan made sense, yet he couldn't bear to give up these valuable things.","So, since these things couldn't be attributed to Yue Fuguang, they needed to find someone with sufficiently high status to take the heat for her.","But as for the candidate... He quickly ran through his own children in his mind...","[Master, the Emperor is coming. Quickly hide your notes.]","Before Emperor Mingxi's group even reached the door, they heard the Divine Artifact's warning voice.","Emperor Mingxi: This informant! It doesn't give him any chance to steer the conversation at all!","Emperor Mingxi strode calmly into the classroom. The day's instructor, Junior Supervisor Lin Congxue, led all the students in paying respects to the Emperor.","Fortunately, Dayan's current etiquette wasn't like that of the Queue Dynasty, where one had to kneel upon seeing the emperor. Here, kneeling was only required on important occasions.","Otherwise, Yue Fuguang would stand out like a crane among chickens again, becoming the brightest presence in the room.","System: With that big loudspeaker of your internal monologue being broadcast, you'll be the most dazzling presence wherever you go.","\"All rise, please.\"","Emperor Mingxi took the main seat. Ignoring his sons for now, he first looked at the princesses. Seeing his daughters were all well, he then turned his gaze to Yue Fuguang.","He asked with a gentle expression, \"Yue Fuguang, have you gotten used to the classes these past days?\"","Yue Fuguang wore a troubled expression and answered truthfully, \"Your Majesty, studying is quite boring.\"","Her words quickly won the silent agreement of several young princes, princesses, and the young county lord. Instantly, their eyes shone brightly as they looked at her.","The Junior Mentor truly understood them! She voiced the thoughts they dared not speak in front of their Imperial Father. How brave!","If they had known the Junior Mentor was like this, they should have befriended her earlier!","The Seventh Prince glanced at his younger siblings and raised an eyebrow smugly. The Junior Mentor was now friends with him and the Eighth Sister!","Emperor Mingxi took in the reactions of all the little ones. He was quite worried that one day the Junior Mentor might lead this bunch of youngsters in playing truant."]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189: Aren't You Going to Spend on My Birthday","paragraphs":["Master, remember your persona! You are a subject now, how can you tell the emperor the complete truth! What if he gets angry and orders you to be caned? I'd have to waste divine power to transfer the cane strokes onto him instead.","Emperor Mingxi: Great Artifact, is there no basic trust between man and artifact? Which of your eyes saw me daring to cane the little immortal lord?","Transferring it to him instead! He... is indeed scared now!","And you're even inciting the little immortal lord not to be honest with me. This isn't just about words! This is sowing discord in our relationship! (Bites handkerchief, fuming angrily JPG)","\"Understood, understood. The emperor isn't that petty. Besides, being overly cautious and submissive is something I, your master, just can't pull off!\"","Hearing her words, Emperor Mingxi didn't seem angry but instead laughed heartily, saying, \"You are all still young, so naturally your minds are preoccupied with play.","But my primary purpose in having you study is that learning can help you understand principles, cultivate your character, establish virtue and become proper adults, broaden your knowledge, and comprehend worldly affairs.","If any among you can achieve these sixteen words, your studies will not have been in vain.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Your Majesty speaks wisely.\"","[Master, you surely don't really think that in your heart, right?]","\"You know, yet you still ask?\"","[Master, aren't you planning to drop some physics, chemistry, biology, or geography to give these people a shock?]","\"Toss that knowledge to them, and will they even understand it? They haven't even figured out why alchemical furnaces explode during elixir refining!\"","[True, alchemical furnace explosions do fall under the category of chemistry. If that were researched and clever people applied it, why would the Danyan army still fear the cavalry of Beili and Qiang?","I heard the 'stone lacquer' tribute from Liangzhou is just gathering dust in the storerooms. These people really don't know how to use good resources.]","Lu Qi and Huo Ying exchanged a glance, seeing confusion in each other's eyes. They couldn't help but prick up their ears to listen more carefully. Unfortunately, heaven didn't grant their wish—the Great Artifact actually stopped talking again!","No, we... our ears were all prepared, and you give us this? Great Artifact, is it really good to leave your sentence half-finished like this?","How are we supposed to sleep tonight? We'll probably wake ourselves up with anxiety while lying in bed.","The two men, with tacit understanding, looked towards their Emperor again. Meeting the Emperor's equally clueless gaze, they then turned to look at Yu Chongshan.","Yu Chongshan turned his head away, refusing to look at them. These people just want to gain advantages from his granddaughter. His granddaughter will speak if she wants to; he certainly won't proactively pry.","After all, they are family!","Emperor Mingxi said, \"Fuguang, if you get tired from studying, you can tell your tutors. Taking a couple days off is also permissible.\"","The Seventh Prince and the Ninth Princess immediately asked, \"Father Emperor, can we also request time off if we get tired from studying?\"","The Ninth Princess was cleverer. She added, \"Father Emperor, Little Ninth only needs one day off.\"","The Seventh Prince quickly followed up, \"Father Emperor, your son also only needs one day.\"","Emperor Mingxi was both amused and exasperated by these two youngsters. Little Ninth was fine; as a princess, she just needed to marry into a good family in the future to enjoy a life of luxury. How much she learned depended on the child herself.","But the Seventh Prince was already twelve and still mixed in with the younger children's class. Even he, as the father emperor, felt embarrassed!","So he reprimanded, \"Old Seventh, is your skin itching? Do you need your elder brothers to 'loosen' it for you?\"","The Third, Fifth, and Sixth Princes, who had already returned to the neighboring classroom to study after morning court, heard their father emperor's suggestion and felt somewhat eager, especially the Sixth Prince, who was only a year older than the Seventh Prince and had wanted a legitimate reason to hit his younger brother for a long time!","Seeing his Sixth Brother already rolling up his sleeves, the Seventh Prince shrank his neck and quickly put on an obsequious smile, fawning, \"Father Emperor, your son was just joking. Studying brings me joy, knowledge helps me grow. I absolutely love studying to death; how could I possibly bear to take time off?\"","His words immediately amused everyone present. After the laughter subsided, Emperor Mingxi said, \"Then tell your father emperor, when will you be able to advance to the higher class and move to study with your elder brothers?\"","The Seventh Prince, who had just been feeling rather pleased with his own wit, immediately wilted, stammering, \"Your son... your son...\"","His eyes darted to the Eighth Princess and Yue Fuguang in front of him, and he brightened up, saying, \"Your son wants to advance together with Eighth Sister and the Junior Mentor. The three of us are good friends; of course, we should go together.\"","The Eighth Princess turned her head and glared at her Seventh Brother. He never thought of her for good things, but when it came to sharing blame, this brother didn't hesitate for a second to include her!","Yue Fuguang, however, didn't mind. She had just arrived and felt no pressure about advancing.","[The Seventh Prince is a pity, though. His future death is too tragic! The Eighth Princess is also a pity!]","\"Stop with the pity. Aren't we here? Little Eighth will be fine.\"","Seventh Prince: Dying tragically is one thing—it hasn't happened yet anyway—but the Junior Mentor said Eighth Sister will be fine. Did you forget about me?","Won't you spare a thought for this peanut? (Feeling wronged JPG)","The Seventh Prince really wanted to say something now to assert his presence, but under the gazes of his father emperor and elder brothers, he reflexively shrank back. Fine, he wisely shut his mouth.","Crown Prince, Third, Fifth, Sixth Princes: Great, we learned about another brother meeting a bad end! It's foreseeable that as his elder brothers, our own fates probably won't be much better!","They all felt somewhat envious of the Crown Prince and the Eighth Princess. These two were explicitly stated to be protected.","Meanwhile, the Eighth Princess, deeply moved, tightly clutched the handkerchief in her hand, trying hard not to cry.","Yue Fuguang's eyes sparkled with an idea. She said, \"Your Majesty, then Fuguang will really request a couple days off in a few days, okay!\"","Emperor Mingxi smiled and nodded. \"Alright, I grant it on behalf of the tutors. Does Fuguang have any plans for her vacation?\"","\"I have a small estate. Since spring is almost here, I wanted to go take an early look to see what crops are suitable to plant there.\"","Hearing this, Emperor Mingxi and the others instantly became interested. Although the Junior Mentor had already promised His Majesty to provide high-yield seeds, it didn't stop them from being curious about what rare things the Junior Mentor might plant on her own estate.","So Emperor Mingxi smiled and asked, \"Where is Fuguang's estate located? Is the area large enough?\"","\"I haven't been there myself. I heard from my mother it's over a hundred mu of land with a small hill.\"","Having never farmed in her past life, she really had no concept of the size of this land.","\"Over a hundred mu is indeed a bit small!\" Emperor Mingxi slightly frowned. \"How about this: I'll also go out to relax with you then. We'll see whose lands are adjacent to yours. If it's not enough for you to manage, we can just expand outwards.\"","Yue Fuguang thought it over and agreed. Any land bordering their family's couldn't possibly belong to ordinary commoners; it was most likely owned by some official.","She wouldn't feel the slightest pang of conscience about taking land from such people to farm.","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and added, \"Your Majesty, my two elder sisters will also take leave then. We agreed to go to my estate together.\"","[Master, when did you agree on that with them?]","\"I'll tell them after school when I return to the manor.\"","Yu Ningxin and Yu Ningxuan hadn't expected their seventh sister to still think of them. Their hearts swelled with emotion, especially seeing her conversing confidently with the Emperor, which inexplicably filled them with pride.","It seemed what their father said was right. With Seventh Sister in the family, the daughters of the Yu family could also choose not to be confined to the limited world of the inner chambers anymore."]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190: Minister Accuses Prince Qi of Colluding with Foreign Officials in a Plot to Rebel","paragraphs":["The Seventh Prince and Eighth Princess exchanged a knowing glance and said, \"Father Emperor, may we also go with Grand Tutor to see her estate?\"","Yue Fuguang thought to herself: At this season, the estate is still bare, there's really nothing much to see.","However, after much pestering from the two, Emperor Mingxi, who doted on his children, reluctantly agreed to take them along.","As a master of balancing acts, what difference did it make for the imperial father to take two or a whole crowd?","Yue Fuguang watched helplessly as her entourage slowly grew larger and larger. With so many people going, wouldn't they trample her land flat?","Before Yue Fuguang could even begin her one-day rural getaway, she first welcomed the procession of prison carts carrying the four major families.","The escorting procession stretched for miles. It was said this wasn't only because these four families had numerous clansmen, but also because the items confiscated from their homes were even more voluminous.","The system also mysteriously added, [Host, to throw people off the scent, the emperor has mixed many treasures excavated from the Tong family's secret hoard into those chests.]","'They moved so fast?' Yue Fuguang was genuinely surprised. She had only provided a general location, yet they not only dug up the treasure so quickly but also secretly transported it to the capital.","[Of course, otherwise what do you think the emperor has been grinning from ear to ear about these past few days? Just you wait, your estate of over a hundred mu will likely expand to over a thousand mu. The surrounding lands belong to court officials. The emperor has already purchased them from them, just waiting for the right moment to gift them to you!]","Yue Fuguang smacked her lips, 'Don't just give land, I can't take it with me.'","[Don't worry, not to mention the Tong family's treasure, these several families themselves have plenty of good things. They'll surely find reasons to send you a batch when the time comes.]","The entire court officials were watching. Such great merit must be properly rewarded, or who would strive for the Great Yan in the future?","Although the two of them were 'kept in the dark,' the due recognition could not be lacking in the slightest.","The entire capital, following the marriage of Princess Pingning, was once again buzzing from top to bottom because of one event.","The happiest were undoubtedly Emperor Mingxi and the Minister of Revenue, Dong Qianli. Watching wealth flow like water into the private and state treasuries, they grinned so widely their teeth were nearly exposed.","Even Second Uncle Yu drank two extra cups with the old master at a family banquet. With the state treasury flush, officials from the Ministry of Revenue, whether dealing with internal or external affairs, could stand a little taller.","Take warfare, for instance. What does it cost the most?","Money!","As Huo Ying put it, he had never fought a war with such abundant resources!","Everyone silently thanked the Little Immortal Lord and the Divine Artifact countless times in their hearts. If the two could see the faith value, they would certainly find it soaring during this period.","Naturally, the favorability value was too.","All prisoners from the four major families were escorted to the dungeons, followed by the three judicial departments proceeding with intense and meticulous trials.","The evidence was all there. The purpose was to secure confessions to solidify the evidence while seeing if they would implicate each other and reveal more hidden accomplices.","This was also a lengthy process; with thousands of people, it couldn't be finished in less than two or three months. But the Great Yan monarch and his ministers clearly had other plans.","Sure enough, during the morning court session that day, the one who stepped forward first to report on the case progress was no longer the veteran performer Wei Ping, but the Censor-in-Chief of the Court of Censors, Feng Tang.","He bowed before speaking, \"Your Majesty, I impeach Prince Qi for colluding with outside officials with the intent to rebel.\"","Yue Fuguang, who had been dozing off, instantly became wide awake upon hearing Feng Tang impeach Prince Qi!","She had been wondering how Emperor Mingxi would expose Prince Qi's rebellious intentions. So, this was the plan.","A good idea, using the mouths of the four families to implicate Prince Qi. It both diverted hatred and made subsequent investigations proceed logically.","Emperor Mingxi said calmly, \"Minister Feng, Prince Qi is Our brother. Although he occasionally oversteps, he has always been honest and dutiful, not forming cliques or pursuing private gain. Recently, he even painfully sent his beloved daughter far away for a marriage alliance for the sake of our Great Yan. Now you say he intends to rebel. Do you have solid evidence? Otherwise, falsely accusing a prince is a crime We cannot lightly pardon. The dignity of a prince cannot be slighted, or how shall We explain Ourself to the people and to the faraway Pingning?\"","Feng Tang was not intimidated by Emperor Mingxi's words. He bowed and said, \"Your Majesty, I have solid evidence. Here are the testimonies and correspondence documenting Prince Qi's collusion with the four major families.\"","As he spoke, he presented a stack of documents with both hands. Eunuch Qian Gui quickly took them, checked for issues, and then presented them to Emperor Mingxi.","After reading them, Emperor Mingxi's face turned ashen. The officials in the grand hall instantly lowered their heads slightly, not daring to look directly at the emperor's countenance.","They only heard the emperor's cold voice, \"Qian Gui, pass these for the ministers to review. Let Our esteemed ministers see what good deeds Our well-behaved younger brother has been doing behind Our back and behind the back of the people!\"","\"As you command.\"","Qian Gui swiftly distributed the materials. For a moment, the only sounds in the grand hall were the rustling of papers being passed and the shocked gasps of those reading.","Some ministers were even shaking with anger. They never imagined that the struggle for the throne between the two imperial brothers could burn its way into their own inner households.","Setting other matters aside, what concerned them most directly were their own favorite concubines, who turned out to be spies planted by Prince Qi's mansion.","Even their trusted stewards, their wives' favored maids, their eldest sons' attendants—all were Prince Qi's people.","An elderly minister who enjoyed gardening—even his gardener was Prince Qi's man. Prince Qi had gone to great lengths for them, it could be said to have left no stone unturned.","Beyond surveillance and intelligence gathering, there was even an intent to corrupt them. Would His Majesty now think they were in league with Prince Qi?","Those unaware couldn't help but feel immense fear. Those who were aware... well, they had to blend in. Their originally ruddy complexions instantly changed, forcibly paled to a sickly white.","They were all veteran performers; who didn't have their signature act?","Yue Fuguang watched these people showcase their acting skills from above and suddenly felt utterly outclassed, completely overshadowed by the senior officials.","'Little Pearl, do you think the emperor and the others will execute all those spies?'","[They probably will. Otherwise, why keep them locked up wasting food?]","Emperor Mingxi nodded inwardly. Exactly, even though he was now exceedingly wealthy, he wouldn't waste resources on such people.","'I always feel it's a bit of a pity. Prince Qi's mansion invested considerable manpower and resources to train these people. Killing them just like that is so wasteful!'","[Repurposing the waste? That could work too. Kill those loyal to Prince Qi, but those willing to serve the court can be kept. Having a royal stipend and an official position is much better than following Prince Qi in rebellion. I see many were selected by Prince Qi's mansion from orphanages, among beggars, or from child traffickers—clever children trained from a young age. In Ling Yinghua's original timeline, her two grandchildren who were kidnapped—the boy was sold to a childless family, and the girl was sent into such an organization. Unfortunately, that child didn't survive the brutal training and died along the way.]","Although Ling Yinghua knew such things wouldn't happen in this life, hearing about the children's fates again still made her heart ache. She also felt a slightly different sentiment towards the spies described in the materials."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191: Could the Grand Finale Be the Day of Great Yan's Downfall","paragraphs":["\"Survival of the fittest. So, those who are alive to begin carrying out missions must have quite good qualifications.\"","[But judging by the reactions of these officials, they likely see them as stains and can't wait to have them all killed!]","Emperor Mingxi and his attendant Qian Gui exchanged a glance. The emperor had shadow guards, death warriors, and two intelligence networks—one for internal affairs and one for external.","A portion of the internal network was managed by Qian Gui.","As for the other portion... Emperor Mingxi swept his gaze over a certain individual in the grand hall.","Yue Fuguang took it all in, knowing the emperor had taken note, and said no more.","Emperor Mingxi cleared his throat lightly and said, \"All my esteemed ministers have seen it. Feel free to speak your minds. I pardon you from any offense.\"","An elderly official stepped forward first, saying, \"Your Majesty, Prince Qi has spied on imperial authority and planted spies in the residences of court officials. His intentions deserve death, and his actions deserve punishment!\"","As soon as his words fell, someone immediately spoke up, \"I second the motion. Your Majesty, the matter of Prince Qi's intent to rebel should be thoroughly investigated to also clear our names.\"","\"I second the motion. I beg Your Majesty to see clearly, we are loyal only to Your Majesty and have absolutely no connection with Prince Qi!\"","Another person jumped out to second the motion. Yue Fuguang saw they were all the ones whose households had been infiltrated by Prince Qi's people, their expressions now a mixture of shock and anxiety.","They were all eager to pledge their loyalty to the emperor and, in one stroke, finish off Prince Qi!","Indeed, hadn't the ruler and his ministers thought alike on this?","Thus, Emperor Mingxi declared, \"The matter of Prince Qi's intent to rebel is hereby ordered to be thoroughly investigated by the Three Judicial Offices.","Ensure not a single guilty person escapes, nor an innocent person is wronged.\"","Wei Ping, Huo Ying, and Feng Tang immediately bowed in assent.","Emperor Mingxi then said to Wei Ping, \"Minister Wei, take all the spies from the prince's residence into custody in your Dali Prison. They will be dealt with collectively after the case of Prince Qi's rebellion is concluded.\"","Wei Ping replied solemnly, \"Your servant obeys the decree!\"","\"Minister Cai, how is the trial of the Four Great Families proceeding?\"","Seeing the emperor set aside the previous matter and inquire about the Four Great Families, the officials whose homes had been infiltrated secretly breathed a sigh of relief. It seemed His Majesty would not pursue their negligence for now.","[Master, the emperor really is going to have all those people executed. Do you want to stop it? You've been in court for so long and haven't offered a single useful suggestion.]","\"Forget it. I just want to watch the show and enjoy the drama. The emperor can handle it however he wishes. Besides, what useful suggestions could a child like me offer? I don't understand court politics.\"","Everyone thought to themselves that the Little Immortal Lord was indeed still the same Little Immortal Lord. This mercy of his seemed both present and absent, his unpredictable temperament living up to the name of a capricious deity.","Fortunately, no matter what, this one could be considered a 'benevolent deity,' which was also Great Yan's good fortune.","Cai Xian stepped forward to report, \"Reporting to Your Majesty, the principal culprits of the Four Great Families have not yet confessed, but many accomplices have already admitted to the misdeeds of their respective families.\"","He paused thoughtfully before continuing, \"Your servant interrogated Bai Yu again yesterday. He stubbornly denies any involvement in Chonghua's disappearance.","He only says the reason he left the banquet without saying goodbye was due to an urgent summons from the family head, and that he sent someone to leave a message for the Princess Consort on his way home.\"","Emperor Mingxi appeared deep in thought. \"If Bai Yu didn't take Chonghua, then who could have?\"","Cai Xian wore an expression of extreme discomfort but pressed on bravely, \"Your servant will intensify the interrogation. I am not afraid he won't tell the truth.\"","The court officials thought: His Majesty is determined to pin the blame for Chonghua's disappearance on Bai Yu.","Looking at Minister Cai Xian, they all felt quite sympathetic. The ones who could do the emperor's dirty work could only be him and Wei Ping; Feng Tang wasn't capable of such things.","[Master, these people still don't know they've actually arrested the wrong person!]","'Arrested the wrong person? Who was wrongly arrested?'","The hearts of the Great Yan emperor and his officials sank. Could it be that among the prisoners, someone was using a false identity?","Especially Cai Xian and Wei Ping, who instantly pricked up their ears. They were determined to hear this. All the sons of the Four Great Families serving as officials in the court had already been imprisoned. Who else could have escaped their capture?","[Bai Yu. He was wrongly arrested.]","'Impossible, right?'","Impossible. These three words echoed in the hearts of Cai Xian and Wei Ping just as they appeared in Yue Fuguang's inner thoughts. The main members of the Four Great Families had been arrested based on portraits.","Bai Yu frequently visited the Prince of Qi's mansion and was a favorite by Princess Pingning's side. Many people in the capital knew him.","Even they had seen him once. It was impossible for them to have arrested the wrong person.","[Master, they really did arrest the wrong person. The one currently locked in the prison is Bai Yu (with the character 'Yu' meaning 'jade' but with a 'gold' radical). This is Bai Yu's twin brother.]","'Twin brother? If Bai Yu is a twin, wouldn't Wei Ping and Cai Xian know about it? Why was only one arrested?'","[Because only a few people in the Bai family know about this. Didn't I mention before that the father of the family head, Bai Yu—that is, Bai Yu's father Bai Yu's—birth mother was from the Miao family in Nanzhao?","She was the aunt of Miao Qingling, Xi Ling's mother. In their clan, there is a taboo: twins are considered inauspicious, and one must be eliminated, otherwise the household will know no peace.]","Yue Fuguang didn't believe in such things and got straight to the point: 'It's because they fear twins fighting over the family inheritance, right? Mortals place great importance on birth order, don't they?","With twins born one after the other, being born just a moment later affects inheritance rights. That can indeed easily breed resentment and lead to internal strife.","However, this Bai Yu is a concubine's son. He wouldn't get much of the family fortune anyway, so it shouldn't matter, right?'","[His father, Bai Yu, thought the same. So after the twins were born, he didn't take the life of either, only publicly announced that a concubine had given birth to a son named Bai Yu.","From then on, the brothers lived as one in the light and one in the shadows, acting as each other's double.","Since childhood, they have taken turns appearing. Because their looks and demeanor were identical, no outsiders ever noticed.","Even Xie Zhiyao didn't know that the person appearing by her side was actually two brothers. The one who developed genuine feelings for her was the younger brother, Bai Yu (gold-radical Yu), while the one who wanted to use her was the older brother, Bai Yu (jade Yu).","The one currently on the run is Bai Yu (jade Yu), and the one who appeared at Peach Blossom Lane was also Bai Yu (jade Yu).']","'This Bai Yu (jade Yu) seems much smarter than his brother, doesn't he?'","[That's natural. Bai Yu (jade Yu) has both high emotional and intellectual intelligence. Despite being a concubine's son of the Bai family, he managed to get recognized as a sworn son by Fan Shiping, the head of the Fan family, one of the Four Great Families.","After his powerful backer Fan Shiping died early, he still earned the regard of his father, Bai Yu, and gained the recognition of Fan Chengye, the new head of the Fan family. That alone speaks volumes.]","'Fan Shiping from Liangzhou was also Bai Yu's (jade Yu) sworn father? You seemed to have said before, in the original timeline, among the Four Great Families, only this Fan Shiping didn't live to see the grand finale; the other three all did.'","The Great Yan emperor and officials: Could the grand finale the Junior Mentor mentioned be the day the Great Yan perished? (Silently biting handkerchief.jpg)","[Master has a good memory. Indeed, besides him, the other three all lived to see the fall of the Great Yan.]","The Great Yan court officials: We knew it! The grand finale the Junior Mentor mentioned refers to the fall of our Great Yan!","So, some among them, like this Fan Shiping, also didn't live to see that grand finale!","Wei Ping and Cai Xian were left speechless upon hearing the reason. The Bai family's mouths were truly sealed tight; only now did they learn there were two Bai Yus!","They could only hope these two venerable figures would speak about the current whereabouts of the fugitive Bai Yu, and please, please don't digress to talk about Fan Shiping again.","That man was currently locked up in prison and wasn't going anywhere. They couldn't care less who his adopted father was—it wouldn't help them catch Bai Yu!"]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192: This is How Rebellious It Is","paragraphs":["Unfortunately, their prayers were in vain. The King of Digressions System remained steadfast in its performance, and the conversation irreversibly veered towards Fan Shiping.","[Master, would you like to know why Fan Shiping didn't live to see the grand finale?]","The system, indifferent to whether others wanted to hear it or not, continued to build suspense. Yue Fuguang, watching Wei Ping and Cai Xian's expressions of frustration and dashed hopes, almost couldn't hold back a laugh.","The system truly had a knack for 'going off-topic' with a complete disregard for others' feelings!","But if it didn't digress, how would they complete tasks and earn points?","Yue Fuguang pretended to be drowsy and closed his eyes. The sounds of Emperor Mingxi discussing affairs with his ministers filled his ears, but in his heart, he thought, «What? His death wasn't normal? There's more to the story?»","[Absolutely!] The system's voice was unusually cheerful, carrying a troublemaking, peace-disrupting vibe that was downright punchable.","It continued to tease, [Master, Fan Shiping's death is actually connected to someone in this very court!]","The officials of Dayan perked up their ears in unison. Their curiosity outweighed any tension, for no matter who was involved, it would only be seen as a merit, not a fault. So, they could enjoy this piece of gossip with peace of mind.","Even the elderly minister currently reporting on the land audits of the four major families unconsciously lowered his voice by two notches.","At his age, dividing his attention like this was truly a challenge for the old gentleman!","«First, tell me how Fan Shiping died.»","[Master, he was poisoned! The poison he ingested is called 'Awaken Once in Ten Days.' Doesn't that sound familiar?]","«'Familiar' isn't the word. It's more that the naming style seems strikingly similar to the poison 'Drunk for a Hundred Days' that afflicted Baiyi, the little disciple of Xuanmingzi.»","[Of course, it's similar. 'Awaken Once in Ten Days' was developed based on 'Drunk for a Hundred Days.' Master, you don't think these two poisons came from the same person, do you?]","«Aren't they?»","[Of course not. 'Drunk for a Hundred Days' came from the hands of Du Zhongxian of Nanyue. He also has a resounding nickname in the martial world: the Immortal of Poison.]","«Calling himself an 'Immortal'? What audacity!» Everyone could hear the chill in the Little Immortal Lord's words.","He was a true immortal, after all, so feeling offended by a mortal's presumption was hardly unreasonable.","[Don't be angry, Master. If given the chance, Little Pearl will definitely have that bold mortal who dares to impersonate us immortals struck by lightning as a sacrifice to the heavens.]","«Don't use lightning. I prefer to repay in kind.»","The crowd thought: Truly worthy of being the Little Immortal Lord! Consistently impressive, which put their minds at ease!","The Crown Prince, usually a background figure, felt a stir in his heart. He found the Little Immortal Lord's principle of \"repaying in kind\" utterly brilliant!","Yue Fuguang was unaware that his single remark had provided an enlightening moment for the typically gentle, kind, and courteous Crown Prince, inadvertently setting him on a different path.","[Understood, understood! Master, the poison on Baiyi was indeed from Du Zhongxian's hand, and the person who went to Nanzhao to purchase it was Bai Yu.","However, the one who actually poisoned Baiyi wasn't Bai Yu, but Fan Shiping's son—the one who first took a concubine from a collateral branch of the Western Qiang's Marquis of Long Trust's family, and later married the cousin of Feng Wuchang—Fan Chengye.]","«Why would he want to poison Baiyi? If I recall correctly, Baiyi is only twelve this year. It's an age where one might annoy everyone, including dogs, but hardly enough to incur a mortal feud, right?»","Xuanmingzi's eyelid twitched. He had been investigating this matter all along, never expecting to suddenly receive the long-sought answer here and now.","[Because Baiyi is Fan Shiping's illegitimate child from an external household. However, Baiyi's mother was the 'runaway pregnant heroine' type. His father, Fan Shiping, was deeply infatuated with this woman and searched for her for many years.","He even wanted to leave a portion of his estate to this mother and child. Fan Shiping never found them, but Fan Chengye discovered that the concubine had died in childbirth while giving birth to Baiyi.","His half-brother, however, had been taken in as a disciple by the renowned Daoist master, Xuanmingzi.","Given Xuanmingzi's status in the martial world at that time, once Fan Chengye learned of this, he would undoubtedly value this younger brother even more.","So, he decided to cut the knot once and for all and have him poisoned.","The reason he sent Bai Yu to purchase the poison from Du Zhongxian in Nanzhao was twofold: firstly, this sworn brother wanted to curry favor with him, the future head of the family—a ready-made pawn, why not use him?","Secondly, it was because Xuanmingzi himself was highly skilled in medicine. Medicine and poison are two sides of the same coin; the common poisons within Dayan wouldn't have been able to stump him, hence the need to look outside.]","«And then Fan Shiping eventually found out about this, so Fan Chengye directly used 'Awaken Once in Ten Days' to poison his own father and take his place?»","The crowd also nodded inwardly, finding the Little Immortal Lord's deduction perfectly logical. Talk of filial piety preventing a son from daring to kill his father held no water here.","The struggle for power has always been bloody and devoid of sentiment, with imperial power being the prime example.","Clearly, Emperor Mingxi thought of this as well. He unconsciously stroked his beard, recalling how when his own father wanted to depose him and establish Prince Rong as Crown Prince, he too had entertained thoughts of patricide.","A pity he had the will and the daring, but not the capability! He lacked the power!","[After Baiyi's death, Fan Shiping did eventually learn the truth and planned to teach his eldest son a lesson. But it so happened that this coincided with the death of the concubine from the Marquis of Long Trust's family during childbirth.","The Fan family was in the midst of marriage negotiations with the Feng family. To secure the alliance, Fan Shiping decided to postpone dealing with his son.","Meanwhile, after Xuanmingzi discovered who was behind his little disciple's poisoning, he began developing 'Awaken Once in Ten Days.' By the time Fan Chengye took Feng Yao from the Feng family as a noble concubine, the poison was ready.","To show respect to the Feng family, Fan Shiping decided to hold a small, internal family banquet on the day the concubine was formally welcomed. Xuanmingzi also chose this time to make his move against Fan Chengye.]","«So, it was Xuanmingzi who acted? Then how did Fan Shiping end up dead?»","The Dayan emperor and his ministers also silently turned their gazes towards Xuanmingzi, who had been sitting there calmly all along.","Since he began attending court sessions last year, much like the Junior Mentor, he had become a fixture in the court, never uttering a word.","The Junior Mentor might not speak, but his inner thoughts, from his identity as the Little Immortal Lord, had been 'commented on' by everyone from the emperor down to the officials.","This Daoist Master Xuanmingzi, however, was truly silent.","Who would have thought that in the original course of history, he had undertaken such a significant act? Although he killed the wrong person, it still amounted to eliminating a scourge for Dayan.","It could be considered a service to the court.","[Originally, the poison was placed in Fan Chengye's wine cup. But during the toast, the cup was accidentally picked up by his father, Fan Shiping.","Fan Shiping quickly showed symptoms of poisoning, which also alerted Fan Chengye.","Xuanmingzi tried several times afterward to correct his mistake but never found another opportunity to administer the poison.","Fan Shiping died ten days after being poisoned. Fan Chengye became like a startled bird.","From then on, he lived in seclusion, rarely venturing out. While strengthening his guards, he became extremely cautious about anything he consumed.","Xuanmingzi, having lost his chance for revenge, could only return to his Daoist temple and enter seclusion, never to emerge again.]","Those with more sensitive minds felt that the summary of Xuanmingzi's story was too abrupt. His tale surely had a continuation.","With his great vengeance unfulfilled, how could he simply enter seclusion and never emerge!","Yue Fuguang thought: Should I tell you all that he later returned to using his original name, Jiao Xuanming, founded the Qingtian Zhigong Dao sect that lasted a century, and proclaimed himself the King of the Underworld?","When Dayan existed, he rebelled against it. When Dayan fell, he tried to restore it.","Ah! Just that rebellious!"]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193: This child must not be spared","paragraphs":["This master and disciple pair, one is the illegitimate son of a treacherous minister, the other is a future 'treacherous minister'.","If Emperor Mingxi and his court officials knew about this, wouldn't they lock the pair up in a dark room.","\"So that's how it is. Now things are vastly different from the original history. Fan Shiping isn't dead, and the entire Fan family is about to be finished. Aside from the two of us, is Fan Chengye the only one who knows Baiyi's true identity?\"","[White Jade probably has his suspicions as well. What does Master wish to do?]","\"Keep an eye out. If any of them tries to reveal the truth, silence them in time.\"","[Master wants to protect Baiyi?]","\"After all, Xuanmingzi once saved me. I'm also repaying that favor by saving that Baiyi. Since I've decided to save him, I must see it through to the end. How can I abandon it halfway?\"","[Indeed. Aside from being Fan Shiping's son, Baiyi truly has no other connection to their Fan family. Saving him won't entangle Master in any other karma.]","Xuanmingzi slowly loosened his grip on the horsetail whisk. He had not misjudged her; this immortal lord was indeed one who clearly distinguished gratitude from grievance.","Their choice to follow her, pledge allegiance to her as their master, and become her faithful followers was not wrong.","Yue Fuguang was still unaware that she had already gained a believer, and a heavyweight Taoist master at that, the future and famously formidable King of the Underworld.","\"One last question: can commoners of Dayan freely marry nobles from other countries?\"","Yue Fuguang used 'marry' rather than 'intermarry' because the marriage between these two families was clearly motivated by interests.","[I don't know if it's allowed, but the Four Great Families are clearly apprehensive about it. That's why, whether Fan Chengye took a collateral branch daughter of the Marquis of Changxin as a concubine or took Feng Yao as a concubine, he found them identities as Dayan women. The previous concubine and Feng Yao even came from the 'same family'—when the elder sister died, the younger sister succeeded her—which was also considered a 'fine tale'.","Emperor Mingxi: When the Junior Mentor was studying, was the Divine Artifact always asleep? 'When the elder sister died, the younger sister succeeded her' is called a 'fine tale'? Is that term used like that? All that studying lately has been for nothing!","\"Alright, we're done with the Fan family gossip. Let's get back to the matter of Bai Yu.\"","Wei Ping and Cai Xian nodded vigorously in their hearts. Yes, yes, yes! Talk about what they were most concerned about—where had Bai Yu gone?","Although his younger brother, Bai Yu, could also take the blame for Zhong Hua's disappearance, allowing the dangerous element Bai Yu to remain at large was something neither the emperor nor his officials could feel at ease with.","As the saying goes, if you cut the weeds without removing the roots, they'll sprout again with the spring breeze.","This Bai Yu must not be allowed to live!","The only one from the Four Great Families likely to survive is probably Baiyi, whom the little immortal lord wants to protect and who knows nothing.","Just as everyone was waiting to hear the Divine Artifact's next words, they never expected it to suddenly say: [Master, Little Pearl forgot to tell you, the poison that afflicted the Crown Prince and the Emperor also came from Du Zhongxian's hand.","The poison the Crown Prince suffered from seems to be called 'Dream of Seeking Fragrance'. Those afflicted become lethargic and their bodies emit a fragrance, which is why after his death he gained the nickname 'the Fragrant Crown Prince'.","The poison the Emperor suffered from is even more suggestive; it's called 'Boundless Spring Scenery'. He died with a smile on his face. Those who didn't know might have thought it was a joyous funeral!]","Emperor Mingxi's face immediately frosted over, flushing red then paling white. Furious as he was, he still didn't forget to glance at his officials below.","And is 'joyous funeral' used like that?","Thinking of the suggestive name 'Boundless Spring Scenery', Emperor Mingxi began grinding his teeth again.","No, that Du Zhongxian is a scourge. This man must be eliminated as soon as possible for him to feel at ease.","While the court officials worried their Majesty might storm off in anger, they didn't know the emperor had already resolved to kill Du Zhongxian.","Someone, upon hearing the words \"joyous funeral,\" couldn't help but twitch the corner of their mouth, which was promptly caught by the enraged Emperor Mingxi.","He simmered inwardly. He might not dare do anything to those two ancestors, but couldn't he deal with the officials below?","The officials in the hall naturally felt their Emperor's death glare.","If they had tails, one would find them all tucked tightly between their legs at this moment.","Their faces were also increasingly stern, eyes fixed on their noses, noses fixed on their hearts.","Some of the more cunning ones even added their own drama, wearing expressions of deep solemnity—were they mourning their Emperor in advance?","Yue Fuguang really wanted to say, \"Honey, you're overacting!\"","Looking at Xie Zhiyan, now bearing the name 'the Fragrant Crown Prince', his head was bowed low.","The distinctly reddish hue of his exposed neck and ears suggested he was both angry and ashamed.","However, with his father's 'joyous funeral' drawing fire ahead of him, he was not... at all... embarrassed!","Yue Fuguang: If I didn't see your bone-white knuckles, I might have believed it! Doge.jpg","\"What kind of preference does this Du Zhongxian have, giving such poetic and picturesque names to lethal poisons? Those who don't know might think they're some kind of incense or fine wine.\"","[Perhaps because he comes from a family of incense merchants?]","\"Never mind him for now. Back to Bai Yu. Can Little Pearl find out where he's hiding now?\"","[Master, Bai Yu has run quite far. Tracking him would consume too much of my divine power. With that effort, it would be better to check where Old Qian's sister is!]","Qian Gui's hand, which was pouring tea for Emperor Mingxi, jerked violently, nearly spilling the tea.","He steadied himself and continued his task, though the hand holding the teapot was white at the knuckles.","\"You can find out Qian Tao's whereabouts? Where is she?\"","Yue Fuguang was inwardly surprised. The system didn't have this ability at level two. Was its power growing as the upgraded gossip system's data slowly repaired itself?","A cause for celebration!","Qian Gui pressed his lips tightly together, but his ears were perked up high. After searching for nearly two months, he hadn't found a single trace of his younger sister.","Several times he had feared the girl was no longer in this world!","[She's in the capital's prison. Qian Tao was bought back then by Zhou Youliang, a member of the Zhou family's collateral branch. Her circumstances over the years haven't been good either.","Among the Four Great Families, those like her who aren't important and have no blood on their hands are uniformly imprisoned with the other servants in the Ministry of Justice prison.]","Qian Gui knew about this. Minister Cai mentioned it to His Majesty yesterday—non-family members of the Four Great Clans who weren't involved in murders or oppressing the common people were held there, awaiting sale after the case was concluded.","He looked towards Cai Xian. Qian Gui wanted to buy his sister back as soon as possible.","Cai Xian winked at him.","\"The problem is how to tell Old Qian. He commissioned people to search, right? Didn't Wei Ping and Cai Xian discover this person, Qian Tao, in the Ministry of Justice prison?\"","[Master, how about suggesting that Cai Xian and Wei Ping conduct another review of those in the prison before they are sold? There really are some big fish who slipped through the net hiding among them.]","\"There really are ones that slipped through! Who are they?\"","[One is a Beili native, originally a cleaning boy in Zhou Hongying's courtyard.","The other is a Xiqiang native, a maid doing rough work in Zhao Mingting's mother's quarters.","However, they grew up in Dayan and have genuine Dayan household registrations, so Cai Xian and Wei Ping might not discover them.]","\"I'll mention it when I have a chance. Whether they grasp the hint depends on their perception!","The important thing is to have them reinvestigate and find Qian Tao.\"","Wei Ping: With the Junior Mentor's hints, so wildly unrelated, who could connect the dots without having heard the inner thoughts? It's not that our perception is poor!","Cai Xian: It's truly not that our understanding is lacking; it's that the little ancestor's words are too obscure!","But then, thinking of those visits to Buddhist temples and Taoist monasteries, listening to the words of those 'masters'...","Through the mist and clouds of his words, I suddenly understood. Masters always speak like this, leaving half of every sentence unspoken.","Compared to those fake masters, the young immortal lord's explanation seemed remarkably 'clear and straightforward'!"]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194: What Poison is in Xie Qi","paragraphs":["The morning court assembly finally concluded. Wei Ping and Cai Xian walked side by side, a few steps behind Yue Fuguang.","Exchanging a glance, they both understood the other also intended to visit the Ministry of Justice prison.","\"Little Pearl, you said Bai Yu has run quite far. How far is 'quite far'?\"","[Master, Bai Yu is likely nearing the border of Dayan's territory.]","\"Quite clever, isn't he? Planning to flee the country!\"","Wei Ping and Cai Xian, walking behind her, exchanged another look. If Bai Yu crossed the Dayan border and never returned, capturing him again would indeed be extremely difficult.","Yue Fuguang speculated, \"The Bai family has ties with Nanzhao. Is he going there to seek refuge with relatives?\"","[He is seeking refuge not with relatives, but with a lover. And he is not heading to Nanzhao, but towards the Western Qiang direction.]","\"Xie Zhiyao? The marriage alliance procession?\"","Cai Xian and Wei Ping had also arrived at the same thought. Calculating the time, at the procession's speed, they would be out of Dayan territory in another five or six days.","Chasing after them now, it was uncertain if they could catch up.","[Little Pearl isn't certain either, only sensing he moved in that direction.]","\"You... Lord Wei, Minister Cai, what are you...?\"","Yue Fuguang had just exited the palace grounds and was about to board her carriage when she noticed Wei Ping and Cai Xian following behind. Further back were Feng Tang and others, who had hastily stopped and turned, now hurrying towards their own offices.","A flicker of embarrassment crossed Wei Ping's face. He chuckled awkwardly, \"It's just that we haven't seen the Junior Mentor at court for two days and missed you dearly.","So, after court, having nothing better to do, this official thought to accompany Minister Cai in seeing the Junior Mentor off.\"","Cai Xian added, \"Lord Wei speaks truly. This official also wished to thank the Junior Mentor. That flaky pastry you sent was truly exceptionally delicious.","Even my mother greatly enjoyed it; her appetite has improved considerably these past two days.\"","Wei Ping: He knew Lady Cai. Since when had her appetite ever been poor? Especially when it came to pastries. Cai Xian took after her in that regard.","Yue Fuguang climbed into her carriage and waved at the two with a smile. \"Thank you, my lords, for seeing me off. We shall meet again in two days.\"","Watching Yue Fuguang's carriage depart into the distance, the two men turned in perfect harmony towards the imperial prison. Cai Xian even beckoned to Feng Tang, who had turned back.","\"Lord Feng, have you dispatched men to pursue Bai Yu?\"","\"Rest assured, Minister Cai. This official has already urgently sent a squad. Yu Dali is leading them personally, with two horses per man. We hope to intercept him before he crosses the border.\"","The case of the four great families colluding with foreign tribes, plundering the dynasty's merchants and commoners, and plotting rebellion was tried for nearly half a month before finally reaching a conclusion.","If not for the ample evidence in hand, it wouldn't have been resolved so quickly.","And it wasn't over. Many subsequent matters required handling, so the heads of those involved would need to remain on their shoulders a while longer.","During these days, another major event occurred. Prince Qi, Xie Qi, was found guilty of plotting rebellion with irrefutable evidence. Before Emperor Mingxi could issue the decree for his execution,","Prince Qi, knowing escape was impossible, preemptively drank poisoned wine and died. According to Wei Ping's later report, the poison used was originally concocted by Du Zhongxian.","Yue Fuguang still remembered the conflicted expression on Wei Ping's face when he reported this.","Noticing something amiss, Emperor Mingxi pressed, \"Does Minister Wei have more to say? What poison did Xie Qi take?\"","He immediately regretted asking, for he saw Wei Ping's face scrunch up as if in pain, instantly giving him a foreboding feeling.","Sure enough, his beloved Minister Wei reported, \"Your Majesty, the poison Prince Qi ingested, confirmed by Daoist Xuanmingzi, is called 'Boundless Spring Scenery.'","This official has never heard of such a poison before!\"","Emperor Mingxi's face stiffened as he nodded. \"We... are also hearing of it for the first time... As for Prince Qi, find him a coffin and bury him.\"","Even now, thinking of that scene made Yue Fuguang want to laugh.","\"Fuguang, what are you thinking about that makes you smile so happily?\" Yu Ningxuan, sitting across from her in the carriage, asked curiously.","\"I was thinking how beautiful my estate would be in spring if the entire hillside were planted with flowers.\"","\"Planting a whole hillside with flowers?\" Yu Ningxuan exclaimed with delight. \"Then we must certainly come for a good visit in spring.\"","Yue Fuguang nodded. \"Naturally. But, Second Sister, do you think flowers are only for looking at?\"","\"Otherwise? They have other uses?\"","Yu Ningxuan thought for a moment. \"Are you going to use them for making perfume?\"","Yue Fuguang gazed out at the snow-covered wheat fields. \"Yes and no. What I want to make is essential oil, different from the scented waters you usually use.","Also, the scented soap you use now—in the future, adding essential oils extracted from various flowers will make it even better than the current version, with a more fragrant scent.\"","\"Essential oil? I've never heard of that. Another clever idea from your smart little head?\"","Yu Ningxuan's face was full of pleasant surprise, and she looked at her sister's fluffy head, truly wanting to reach out and ruffle it.","Her itching hands twitched within her sleeves, but she ultimately didn't dare extend her claws.","Never mind whether her sister would agree, if their grandparents, father, and mother found out she dared pat her sister's head...","They would surely make her relive a complete childhood!","Yue Fuguang didn't explain further, simply saying, \"I'll provide the methods. You and our sisters will be responsible for the subsequent production, management, and sales. What do you think, Second Sister and Fourth Sister?\"","Yue Fuguang looked towards Yu Ningxin, who had been watching them with a smile without speaking.","\"What does Fourth Sister think?\"","Yu Ningxin smiled gently. \"Fourth Sister naturally thinks it's excellent. I only fear we sisters might not manage well and hold you back.\"","Yue Fuguang waved a hand dismissively. \"It's fine. Consider it practice.\"","She then smiled confidently. \"Trust me. As long as you follow the recipes, the products will not be inferior. Your task will be to manage the workers and the sales in the shops.\"","The system's products were guaranteed to be top quality, and the recipes were no exception—perfectly suited for production in this era, yet yielding results far superior to it.","\"Then we are reassured.\"","\"Let's be clear upfront. You won't receive wages; I'll give you a share of the profits. I provide the recipes and raw materials; you handle the management.","We'll split it seventy-thirty. I take seventy, you take thirty. The products will target the high-end market. I imagine within a year or two, your share of the profits will rival the dowry funds from the family estate.\"","Both sisters blushed crimson at the mention of dowries. The second, third, and fourth sisters were all of similar age, with Yu Ningxuan especially reaching the age for marriage discussions.","However, upon hearing they could receive such a share of silver, instead of being pleased, they quickly declined. \"There's no need to give us a share. That's far too much.\"","Particularly Yu Ningxin, being a concubine-born daughter, was more cautious. \"We sisters will follow your arrangements and assist you. We don't need wages, and a profit share is absolutely out of the question.\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head, saying deliberately, \"It's settled then. Thirty percent, and don't ask for more. You know me, sisters—I'm lazy. If I had to do the work myself, I'd rather not earn this money at all.\"","The two thought about their sister's recent behavior and had to admit it indeed matched the description of 'lazy'!","They couldn't help but cover their smiles. Seeing her sisters laugh, Yue Fuguang wasn't annoyed. She was proud of her leisurely ways—after all, she had the means for it!","\"Don't laugh just yet, sisters. Consider this matter agreed upon.\""]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195: What to Plant","paragraphs":["Then, turning to Yu Ningxuan, she said, \"Second Sister, you're the eldest among us. I'll leave this matter for you to take the lead. You can discuss it with the other sisters. As for how to divide the three-percent share, you all can decide amongst yourselves.\"","After a moment's thought, worried that Yu Ningxuan might be too reserved to push for fairness, she added, \"My suggestion is that those who contribute more should receive more. Also, Sister, please report this to Grandmother. If any issues arise, she will be there to support us.\"","Achoo!","Far away at the Yu residence, the Old Madam suddenly sneezed. Her chief maid, thinking she had caught a chill, hurried to fetch a cloak to drape over her shoulders.","The Old Madam waved her hand dismissively. \"It's nothing. It must be Fuguang thinking of me!\"","When others thought of her, it wasn't this potent.","Yu Ningxuan found this reasoning sound. With Grandmother's authority backing them, even that troublesome Eighth Sister wouldn't dare make a fuss.","Having resolved one issue before even arriving at the estate, Yue Fuguang felt quite pleased.","As for the fruit wine brewing business, all she needed to do was grow the fruit and give the recipes to her mother, Madam Zhang. She wouldn't have to manage the rest.","Therefore, when she stepped down from the carriage and saw the bare, barren hill, she didn't mind the lack of scenery at all.","Emperor Mingxi and the various ministers who had accompanied her also alighted. Seeing her in high spirits, they said with smiles, \"Grand Tutor, this place is good, but it's a bit small.\"","Minister Wang, ever concerned with his area of expertise, couldn't help but ask, \"What do you plan to plant in such a limited space, Grand Tutor?\"","Before Yue Fuguang could reply, Emperor Mingxi approached with the Crown Prince and a group of princes and princesses.","Yue Fuguang glanced over. Good, that detestable Fourth Master Xie wasn't among them.","Everyone promptly paid their respects. Emperor Mingxi took an exquisite wooden box from the Crown Prince and handed it to Yue Fuguang. \"Fuguang, these are the land deeds for the surrounding plots and those two hills.\"","Yue Fuguang accepted it with thanks and said with a smile, \"Your Majesty has allotted me such a large area. I could build a leisure estate here.\"","She had initially wanted to say \"farmstay\" but thought it sounded too lowbrow and lacked elegance. Moreover, she didn't intend to open it to the public; she just wanted a private place for relaxation and entertainment.","Well, the main reason was that money was no object!","Just yesterday, Emperor Mingxi had found a pretext to send her over a dozen large chests of gifts, five of which were filled with gleaming gold.","Emperor Mingxi also smiled. \"That sounds excellent. Fuguang, don't forget to invite me for a visit once it's built.\"","\"And me, Grand Tutor! And me!\" The Seventh Prince shouted, jumping up and down behind his older brothers.","The Second Prince turned and pressed his younger brother down. \"You're everywhere!\"","The Seventh Prince muttered under his breath, indignantly, \"If I hadn't cried and made a scene to come, would you have had the chance to tag along and have fun?\"","The others had to admit he had a point. Weren't they all relying on this thick-skinned younger brother to charge ahead first, so they, as older brothers, could follow behind and reap the benefits?","They weren't like the Crown Prince, who had a personal connection with the Grand Tutor and could come either with their father or on his own.","Ignoring her show-off seventh brother, the Eighth Princess stepped forward, linking her arm with Yue Fuguang's. \"Grand Tutor, what do you intend to plant here?\"","The Eighth Princess was a secret foodie. Ever since tasting the fruits and vegetables Yue Fuguang sent to the palace, and the snacks she brought to the academy, she had been unable to forget them.","She secretly hoped Yue Fuguang would plant a lot, so she could buy some from her.","Yue Fuguang looked around, thought for a moment, and pointed to the distant hills. \"One hill will be covered in flowers, the other planted full of fruit trees. As for this largest one in the middle, I'll build a manor partway up the slope.\"","Then she gazed at the fields. \"Besides planting some grain, I'll grow fruits and vegetables not found in Dayan: strawberries, watermelons, blueberries... Oh, and I must plant some tea trees on the hills.\"","She had almost forgotten that. The tea in Dayan was too complex, with too many added ingredients. Having grown accustomed to plain tea, she really couldn't get used to it.","Moreover, tea leaves could not only be made into tea but also had other wonderful uses.","[Master, are you trying to be self-sufficient to improve your quality of life?]","'If I don't plant them myself, Dayan won't grow them on its own! Look at their 'cold melons' (watermelons)—smaller than Qilin melons, and the key point is they're not sweet, with pinkish flesh.","As for their tea, adding scallions, ginger, and garlic is one thing, but they even add mutton fat! Who can stand that?'","Hearing Yue Fuguang's internal critique, the group's expressions turned somewhat awkward. Minister Wang, however, paid no heed. Now that it was within his professional domain, he had to ask more questions.","\"Grand Tutor, are the fruits and vegetables not found in Dayan the ones from your sunlit greenhouse?\"","Yue Fuguang shook her head. \"Those are only part of it. I plan to select more varieties to plant. Just chili peppers have over a dozen varieties. Even radishes and cabbage have different types with different tastes.\"","After a moment's thought, she added, \"There's also something called sugar beet. It can be used to make sugar.\"","In the Dayan Dynasty, the taste of 'sweet' was something many commoners might not experience much in their entire lives, mainly due to low productivity, few sources for sugar-making, and excessively high costs.","\"Make sugar? Like with sweet potatoes?\"","\"No, it's different. Sweet potatoes are primarily a food crop, while sugar beet is a vegetable. It can be eaten as a vegetable, and its juice can also be boiled down to make sugar.\"","Making sugar from grain or vegetables—they had never heard or seen such a thing before. Truly, these were novel crops brought forth by the Grand Tutor.","With Emperor Mingxi and Yue Fuguang leading the way, the group walked along the crisscrossing field paths. At each spot, Yue Fuguang explained to the estate managers following behind what should be planted there.","Walking and stopping along the way, Yue Fuguang got a general overview of her own hundred mu of land.","As for the over a thousand mu Emperor Mingxi had given her, she wouldn't go see it all. Walking the entire area would be too hard on her feet; she wasn't up for that hardship.","For the remaining land, she briefly outlined her ideas. These were all experienced estate managers. Even with her simple instructions, they roughly understood how to prepare the land and what to reserve for planting.","Furthermore, there was the professional Minister Wang. Hearing Yue Fuguang mention one unfamiliar fruit or vegetable after another, he clamored about bringing people from the Ministry of Agriculture to help Yue Fuguang with the work.","Well, well, openly talking about using public resources for private purposes right in front of the big boss—Minister Wang was quite bold!","This wasn't like the small plot in her sunlit greenhouse that could be handled casually.","Emperor Mingxi even nodded. \"Fuguang, if you're short on manpower later, you can also call on people from the imperial estates to help.\"","Yue Fuguang thought for a moment and didn't refuse, simply saying with a smile, \"Alright. I won't give them monetary wages. Instead, I'll either give them some seeds or share some of the produce once it's grown.\"","Using it themselves or selling it would be better than directly giving them money.","A glint flashed in Minister Wang's eyes as he instantly understood the Grand Tutor's meaning. Doing it this way would save him a lot of future trouble, as there were many influential figures, and if they all offered money...","Emperor Mingxi was also pleased. Then he wouldn't even need to ask Yue Fuguang for seeds; the people from his own imperial estates could earn them for him.","The Crown Prince quickly followed, saying he would also send people to help. Subsequently, Feng Tang, Wu Yuanjing and his son also expressed their intention to send helpers.","Seeing they had been beaten to the offer, Lu Qi and the others no longer held back and all joined in.","Hadn't these people all bought seeds from Grandfather already?"]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196: What's Wrong with My Monkey Brother","paragraphs":["Seeing that Lu Qi and the others had taken the initiative, they no longer held back and all joined in.","Hadn't all these people already bought seeds from her grandfather?","They must have set their sights on her other varieties of vegetables. Yue Fuguang focused her mind and probed into the ring on her finger, which was in an invisible state.","Seeing the eight-tiered shelf fully stocked with all kinds of seeds, she felt relieved!","Come on, let them all come. This could be considered her contribution to Dayan's food supply. Although the points for this task weren't high, watching the number of pending tasks on the task panel shrink smaller and smaller gave her a great sense of accomplishment.","After pondering for a long while, Emperor Mingxi finally asked the main purpose of his visit, \"Fuguang, when will your seafaring merchant friend be able to ship the potato, corn, and sweet potato seeds to us?\"","He wore a smile and couldn't resist teasing, \"We've recently come into some wealth, the treasury is ample, so the silver for purchasing the seeds is all prepared.\"","The Minister of Revenue, Dong Qianli, chimed in, \"Indeed, I personally oversaw the clerks packing the chests. I guarantee there's not a single copper coin or tael of silver missing.\"","Who among them didn't understand the Little Immortal Lord's preferences? Fortunately, only they were aware of it. Otherwise, with the influence of the Immortal Abode's reputation, wouldn't copper and silver depreciate?","After all, if even immortals looked down on them, how could they be any good?","Yue Fuguang said, \"Your Majesty, rest assured and prepare the land. The day before yesterday, my friend sent me word that the delivery will definitely arrive within half a month at the latest. It won't delay the spring planting.\"","According to the planting times for the three crops provided by the system, and considering Shangjing City's geographical location, the best time to plant potatoes was from late February to early March.","The best time for corn was from early April to early May, and the latest was sweet potatoes, which were best planted when the temperature stabilized above 15 degrees Celsius.","Yue Fuguang guessed corn would need to be planted around mid-April, but she hadn't experienced spring in Shangjing City before and wasn't very sure.","She could only rely on experts like Old Minister Wang to assess the planting time themselves. After all, she just needed to provide the planting manuals.","A great weight lifted from Emperor Mingxi's heart. He nodded happily, \"That's good. We'll all be waiting. Don't worry, the items are all things your friend likes.\"","Finally, Emperor Mingxi emphasized repeatedly, still somewhat uneasy.","Yu Chongshan promptly filled the gap, looking at Yue Fuguang with a kind expression, \"Our Fuguang also only likes these things. Is it because she's influenced by this friend?\"","Yue Fuguang nodded.","Who would have thought the system would quickly jump out to contradict, [That's not it at all! Little Pearl is influenced by its master!]","Yue Fuguang retorted, 'You are my artifact spirit. If not influenced by me, then by whom? Should we dissolve the contract?'","She sounded just like those people who threaten divorce at the slightest disagreement...","The system hurriedly coaxed, [Master, Little Pearl only has you as its master. It won't go anywhere. Please don't dissolve the contract with Little Pearl, okay?]","It put on a performance, diligently imitating a sycophant.","Seeing Yue Fuguang ignore it, it continued, [Little Pearl is much more useful than that fellow Moon Spirit Pearl.]","'Do tell.'","The group listened to their banter as they walked towards the manor. It was lunchtime, and the weather was nice, so Yue Fuguang suggested having a barbecue.","This suggestion was unanimously approved by the Seventh Prince and the Sixth, Seventh, Eighth, and Ninth Princesses. For them, it was a novel experience.","Yue Fuguang was well-prepared. The ingredients she brought out were all pre-processed. When the golden fresh corn appeared, the Dayan monarch and his ministers were speechless.","\"Your Majesty, this is fresh corn, not suitable for planting.\"","Emperor Mingxi nodded. Watching the corn being grilled over the fire still pained his heart, so he simply walked away to look at other things.","The principle was: out of sight, out of mind!","Old Minister Wang was different. Since he couldn't beat them, he joined them. Not only did he grill corn with Yue Fuguang, but he also asked her about over a dozen ways to eat and store corn, both dry and fresh.","Seeing Yue Fuguang still ignoring it, the system continued, [Master, I can also tell stories, stories about the Heavenly Realm. You've forgotten them all, haven't you? How about Little Pearl helps you review them?]","Hearing this, everyone present lightened their movements. Even military officers like Wei Shouyi handled their skewers more gently.","Emperor Mingxi, who had retreated, stealthily moved back a few steps and sat down at the table nearest their grill.","The Crown Prince, from over a dozen meters away, quickly seized the opportunity, beating his siblings to his father's side to 'show filial piety.'","His water-pouring movements were smooth and seamless, done in one go, leaving the princes and princesses dumbfounded.","Out of the corner of her eye, Yue Fuguang watched their little actions with silent amusement. Had they forgotten that within a hundred meters, the sound they heard was the same?","Even within five hundred meters, it wouldn't affect their ability to hear the system's voice. Back then, to avoid affecting normal conversation while still hearing the inner voice, she hadn't chosen surround sound.","Everyone kept their hands busy but pricked up their ears, finally hearing the Little Immortal Lord say, 'Then tell one.'","The system thought about the myths and stories it had downloaded on Planet Water Blue. Perhaps influenced by its host, it still preferred Xia Country's theological system and mythological legends.","The roles they were playing now were also based on Xia Country's immortals. So it said, [Master, do you remember the Great Sage Sun?]","'The Great Sage Equaling Heaven, Sun Wukong?'","[Yes, him! Does Master remember?]","'Not too much. What about my Monkey Brother?'","[As Master knows, not long after he returned from studying under Patriarch Bodhi at Mount Spiritheart, he went and stirred up trouble at the Dragon Palace of the Eastern Sea.","Not only did he forcibly take their Divine Sea-Pacifying Needle, but he also demanded treasures from the Dragon King like the Golden Chainmail and Lotus Fiber Cloud-Treading Boots.]","Yue Fuguang laughed heartily, 'That's exactly the kind of thing my Monkey Brother would do. That Divine Sea-Pacifying Needle took dozens of immortals to lift.","In my Monkey Brother's hands, it's just an incredibly powerful rod, wielded as lightly as this one in my hand.'","Here, Yue Fuguang's instincts stirred. She picked up a very straight and handsome-looking stick and swung it a few times with practiced ease.","Her proficiency suggested she hadn't done this sparingly in her past life!","[That rod... that Sea-Pacifying Needle, the Great Sage later named it the 'As-You-Will Gold-Banded Staff.'","I just heard from the Lord of the Underworld recently that the Great Sage barged into their Netherworld, tore up the Register of Life and Death, and crossed his own name off it.]","'Good for him! How could the Lord of the Underworld presume to govern my Monkey Brother's life and death?'","Everyone listened, enthralled, their hands unconsciously trembling a little. The Little Immortal Lord's Monkey Brother, the Great Sage Sun, was truly a divine being.","Daring to cause trouble at the Dragon Palace, and daring to barge into the Netherworld.","One governed their favorable weather and harvests, the other governed their life and death—these were deities they revered and feared. And this fellow had boldly offended them all!","The seasoned veterans of the official court couldn't help but stroke their beards and ponder secretly: Who exactly was the Great Sage Sun's master, that Patriarch Bodhi of Mount Spiritheart? They had never heard of such a deity before. But for his disciple to cause such ruckus at the Dragon Palace and the Underworld without consequence showed how exalted his status must be!"]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197: Did My Monkey Brother Win","paragraphs":["In just this short while, everyone unanimously tagged the Great Sage Sun, as referred to by the Artifact Lord, as someone with powerful backing and formidable personal combat strength.","[And that's not all. Wasn't he in charge of the heavenly horses in the Milky Way before? Later, he disliked the lowly title and poor reputation of the 'Pi Ma Wen' (Horse Tender) and ran back to his hometown, the Flower-Fruit Mountain and Water Curtain Cave, to live a carefree and happy life.]","Yue Fuguang agreed, saying, \"Brother Monkey wasn't wrong! When it comes to work, if you don't want to do it, just quit! I remember, didn't the Marshal of the Heavenly River also look down on him?\"","[That did happen. So, after the Great Sage ran back home, the Jade Emperor sent the Supreme Lord Lao Zi to coax him back with sweet words, assigning him to manage the Queen Mother's Peach Garden.","Those peaches could extend life, allow one to become an immortal or a sage. They bloom once every three thousand years, bear fruit once every three thousand years, and ripen once every three thousand years.]","Yue Fuguang laughed. \"Having a monkey watch a peach orchard? Who on earth came up with that idea!\"","The 'audience' was first startled—so this Great Sage Sun was a monkey spirit?","No wonder the little immortal lord called him Brother Monkey; he really was a monkey!","The young princes, princesses, and Yu Ningxuan were already completely enthralled. Although the Artifact Lord had only briefly summarized the deeds of that Great Sage Sun, one could easily imagine the process must have been thrilling.","They were now eating almost by instinct. Like the Seventh Prince, who had stuffed himself until his eyes were rolling back, which made their father, Emperor Mingxi, frown deeply.","If he weren't afraid of interrupting the conversation between those two, he would have already slapped this foolish son's backside with his shoe!","Thankfully, a sister was more considerate. Seeing her seventh brother's stomach stretched taut, the Eighth Princess quickly poured him a cup of hawthorn water to aid digestion.","However, the shrewd ones among them sensed something different; the whole affair reeked of conspiracy!","Based on instinctive intuition and the sharpness honed from years of political maneuvering, they also felt that putting a monkey in charge of a celestial peach orchard was ill-intentioned.","Whether mortal or immortal, it's hard to resist one's nature. As the saying goes, it's easier to defeat an enemy than to conquer oneself.","Of course, while thinking this, it didn't stop them from drooling with envy over the peaches—extending life, becoming an immortal or a sage!","Who wouldn't want that? If they were that Great Sage Sun, they wouldn't be able to resist eating a couple either!","[So, I heard from Yue Lingzhu that when the Queen Mother held the Peach Banquet, not only was the Great Sage Sun not invited, but when the Seven Fairies went to the Peach Garden to pick peaches, they found many peaches of different grades missing and were sure the Great Sage had eaten them, so they went to report him.]","\"Brother Monkey ate the peaches? If the Seven Fairies succeeded in reporting him, wouldn't the Jade Emperor and Queen Mother punish him?\"","[Don't worry, Master. The Great Sage Sun used his magic to immobilize them in time, so they didn't go! However, the Great Sage only immobilized them; he didn't kill them!]","\"Of course! My Brother Monkey's moral compass is so upright! He calls Princess Iron Fan 'sister-in-law' and the Jade-Faced Fox 'seductress'. He knows the difference between the proper wife and the mistress, much better than some adults!\"","Some adults instantly trembled in fear. They really had long since reformed, their concubines long dismissed, and now they couldn't be more respectful to their own wives!","\"And even drunk on immortal wine, he never laid a hand on the beautiful fairies. Unlike some who use being drunk as an excuse to act wildly, calling it 'true nature'—what a load of nonsense!\"","Hearing the little immortal lord suddenly swear, these people not only didn't find it improper but inwardly condemned those beastly colleagues of theirs. Look how angry they've made the little immortal lord!","Yue Fuguang thought of many other things but didn't say them, only adding, \"Some people's kindness lacks judgment, but my Brother Monkey's kindness is principled.","He never spares evil spirits, dealing out beatings or killings as deserved. But he never harms the innocent and shows kindness to ordinary mortals.\"","[Exactly! The Great Sage Sun is the ideal type for many young fairies!","We just mentioned the Great Sage immobilizing the Seven Fairies. Before the Jade Emperor and Queen Mother could trouble him, he went to the Peach Banquet himself. Not only did he use magic to knock out all the immortals, but he also drank the immortal wine.","Staggering drunk all the way to the Lihen Heaven in the Thirty-Third Heaven, he stumbled into the Supreme Lord Lao Zi's Tushita Palace. It's said he stole and ate many of Lao Zi's elixirs, which pained the Supreme Lord greatly.]","With every sentence the system uttered, everyone's hearts ached in sympathy. This Great Sage Sun ate the peaches, drank the immortal wine, and now treated the elixirs like a meal!","They were green with envy. Forget the peaches and wine for a moment; just those elixirs—although they didn't know how they differed from the Artifact Lord's—they knew anything with 'immortal' in its name couldn't be bad!","Hadn't they seen how a single Body-Strengthening Pill made the Yu family strong and healthy, with Yu Chongshan's white hair turning mostly black?","And how half a Detoxification Pill cured the 'Hundred-Day Drunk' poison that even the famous Daoist Xuanmingzi was helpless against?","Not only was the poison cleared upon taking the medicine, but they had also seen the child Baiyi—strong and healthy, even better than before the poisoning!","How could they not be envious?","\"Lao Zi is a master at alchemy. So he ate them? He can just make more; alchemy is his specialty anyway!","Oh right, Little Pearl, I remember you also have a few furnaces of Lao Zi-brand elixirs.\"","Everyone: Hold on, isn't the little immortal lord being a bit too biased? Those are immortal elixirs!","What does she mean, just eat it if you ate it? Does she think immortal elixirs are like the meat skewers in their hands? Something you can have whenever you want?","And the Divine Artifact actually has some there too! Ah, they're all green with envy!","Thinking of this, many people took a fierce bite of the golden-brown, sizzling, and fragrant meat skewer in their hands, feeling a heroic boldness akin to the Great Sage stealing and eating the immortal elixirs!","[\"There indeed are, but Master, in your current mortal flesh, cannot consume the immortal elixirs.","The Great Sage was different. After eating the pills as if they were regular meals, he directly fled back to his old home, the Water Curtain Cave on Flower-Fruit Mountain.","This infuriated the Jade Emperor, the Queen Mother, and a host of other immortals.","They immediately commanded a hundred thousand heavenly soldiers and generals to descend to the mortal realm and capture the Great Sage.","The Great Sage instantly defeated the Giant Spirit God, fought one against nine to overpower the Nine Luminaries, beat Nezha until he cried, and battled Erlang Shen from the ground all the way to the heavens!","In this great war, every notable immortal from the Heavenly Court joined the fray! It's a pity we came to the mortal world and missed witnessing it in person.\"]","\"Did my Brother Monkey win? Did any senior brothers or sisters from our Lingxu Mountain go to lend support?\"","[\"He naturally won. But don't worry, Master. Our Lingxu Mountain has always been on good terms with Fangcun Mountain, so of course we didn't go.","The Jade Emperor couldn't possibly invite our Divine Sovereign!\"]","Yue Fuguang's voice was brimming with pride, \"My master is truly the most powerful being I have ever seen!\"","Everyone grew even more curious about the Divine Sovereign of Lingxu Mountain, whom they had heard mentioned several times, but unfortunately, neither the Divine Artifact nor the young immortal gentleman said more on the subject.","The conversation turned back to the extraordinarily powerful Great Sage Sun, who wreaked havoc in all directions and emerged victorious.","On the journey back, the Divine Artifact supplemented the tale with many more details, getting everyone present fired up with excitement.","The originally less-than-an-hour journey by the swaying carriage ended up taking nearly an hour and a half. By the time they returned to the city, it was already dark.","Even so, because the Divine Artifact kept digressing while telling the story, by the time they reached the imperial city gates and Emperor Mingxi had to bid farewell to the officials seeing him off, they still hadn't heard about how it ended after the Great Sage Sun fought his way up to the Heavenly Court!","Yue Fuguang: I did that on purpose. If you want to know what happens next, tune in next time!"]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198: Isn't he dead Could it be a resurrection","paragraphs":["Watching Emperor Mingxi's somewhat resentful and hesitant retreating figure, looking like he wanted to urge for an update but didn't dare, Yue Fuguang couldn't help but laugh unkindly!","Yue Fuguang lay back in the carriage. Having seen off the emperor, she could finally go home!","Seeing her smug look, the system couldn't help but say, [Host, stopping the update here, aren't we courting too much hatred?]","Yue Fuguang replied carelessly, 'Don't worry, would they dare to retaliate against us? At most, they'll just hint around to urge for updates!'","Before her \"at most\" had fully landed, she heard the alarm blaring in her mind from the system. [Enemy attack! Protective shield activated!]","As the system's words fell, Yue Fuguang heard a thud-thud-thud sound by her ears, followed immediately by the carriage beginning to shake.","At the same time, the voices of Wei Shouyi, Huo Ying, and others sounded from outside. \"Protect the Junior Mentor!\"","Yue Fuguang remained relatively calm, mainly because the system gave her courage.","She even had the mind to ask, 'System, was that thudding sound just now arrows hitting the carriage?'","[Yes, why?]","'Their aim seems a bit off, how come no arrows came in through the windows? But thankfully, Second Sister and the others didn't ride back in the same carriage as me. Otherwise, they would have become targets too!'","[The windows are covered by my rain shield, of course they can't shoot in. Since we're pretending to be ordinary people and still fishing, we can't reveal our strength too early. That's why I intentionally let some arrows hit the sturdier parts of the carriage body.]","Yue Fuguang praised generously, 'You really think of everything, System!'","The system continued, [Host, guess who sent this group?]","'Could it be the people from that Four-Nation Alliance 'Pluck the Moon' organization that got away last time?' she said, while preparing to get out of the carriage.","She could already see her grandfather, father, and others tightly surrounding her carriage, forming a protective formation.","Speaking of this alliance, Yue Fuguang felt frustrated. Last time, after she gave Wei Ping the Truth Elixir, he did use it to make those people talk.","Due to their low status, the truths they revealed weren't much.","But it was enough for Wei Ping and the others to deduce the general picture.","That assassination attempt did involve three groups: one group of death warriors from the Prince of Qi's mansion, one group of assassins from the 'Night-Blooming Cereus' organization, and another group of spies and assassins sent by the four nations.","They even gave this organization a temporary name: the 'Pluck the Moon Alliance'. Their assassination operation against her was called the 'New Moon' operation.","Because on the 'New Moon', the moon rises and sets almost with the sun, making it hard to see at night. She was that moon.","No moon meant her non-existence. The meaning was both metaphorical and clear. Yue Fuguang had to praise the person who came up with the name as a talent!","According to those two captives, nearly a hundred assassins from their organization participated in the operation. Including those two, their losses in that action were only about sixteen or seventeen people.","That meant there were still seventy or eighty people eyeing her life covetously, so Yue Fuguang's first guess was the Pluck the Moon Alliance.","The situation outside was chaotic, especially near Yue Fuguang's carriage, where several dozen people were fighting to the death.","The carriages of the other officials seemed relatively fine. This alone proved the assassins were indeed targeting her.","The assassins had also chosen an excellent location, somewhat far from the palace city. Even if the emperor received news and sent reinforcements, it would take the time of two or three cups of tea to arrive.","They were in the middle of East Street, with both ends guarded by the assassins' crossbowmen. They wanted to catch a turtle in a jar!","For this trip, their guards were almost all the emperor's Imperial Forest Guards, who withdrew once they entered the imperial city. No one expected that among over a dozen civil and military officials here, someone would dare to stage an assassination in front of so many people!","Assassins: We're banking on your 'unexpected'! The leader said this is called striking where the enemy least expects it!","Yue Fuguang: Your leader is quite the cultured one!","Seeing the situation outside, Yue Fuguang instantly transformed into a drama queen. 'Little Pearl, judging by the looks of it, they're after me?'","At that moment, the numbers on both sides in the field were roughly equal, about seventy or eighty each. Coupled with over a dozen carriages, they blocked the otherwise fairly wide street completely.","The innermost circle was the Yu family father and son, primarily responsible for blocking crossbow bolts and arrows. The outer layer consisted of Wei Ping, Cai Xian, and other civil officials.","At the very front, the martial powerhouses were Huo Ying, Wei Shouyi, and other military officers... among whom was mixed in a censor, Feng Tang!","[Master, they are indeed after you. Master, guess who sent them this time?] The system smoothly replied, picking up their previous topic.","'The Four-Nation Alliance or the Night-Blooming Cereus organization?'","[Nope!]","'No? Do I have a new enemy already? Who is it?'","It couldn't be the recently eliminated four great families, could it? But aside from those who could hear thoughts, no one knew this matter was related to Yue Fuguang!","Those people had been carefully selected. Even if they had some issues themselves, they wouldn't collude with foreign states. Their favorability values towards her also indicated they wouldn't betray her.","Most importantly, even if they wanted to talk, they couldn't say much.","Wei Ping, Huo Ying, and others at the front, though unaware of the favorability values, shared the same basic line of thought as Yue Fuguang.","Wei Ping said to Huo Ying and the rest, \"Minister Huo, General Wei, try to take one alive!\"","Although Feng Tang was a Censor, his martial skills were no less formidable; he was a fierce man strong in both combat and debate.","With a swift raise and fall of his blade, he specifically targeted the limbs of his opponent. In just a few moves, he kicked the man flying, sending him straight to the feet of Wei Ping within the inner circle.","\"Lord Wei, a live captive!\"","Seeing his efficient prowess, Yue Fuguang did not hesitate to praise her devoted fan: \"Lord Feng, what impressive skill!\"","The system also remarked, [Master, this Feng Tang is quite good. He is usually respectful towards you and could be taken on as a subordinate!]","Yue Fuguang said, \"We'll discuss that later. First, tell me how I guessed wrong!\"","Hearing their words, Feng Tang flushed with excitement, and now, as if injected with adrenaline, his combat power instantly skyrocketed.","If there were a meme to describe him at this moment, the most fitting would be \"It's huntin' time!\"","The mediocre Wu Yong watched, his eyes red with envy and jealousy.","This Feng Tang first competed with his own father, and later competed with him for the position of the number one person in the Young Master's esteem.","Now these two were praising him, almost accepting him on the spot!","Wu Yong looked down at his own portly figure. Although he prided himself on being an agile fat man, his combat power truly couldn't match the other's.","Then he could only find another path!","[Master, these assassins are from Prince Qi!]","\"Prince Qi? Isn't he dead? Could he have risen from the dead?\"","[Not risen from the dead. Is it possible that Prince Qi never actually died?]","\"No, he died from poison. Wei Ping and the others personally went to examine the body. Could they have mistaken the person?\"","[This is where we must mention Prince Qi's good fortune. Ten years ago, he encountered a man who looked so much like him they could have been twins, though they weren't.","The two looked extremely alike; even Prince Qi's own consort might not be able to tell them apart face to face.","To maintain consistency, Prince Qi had the distinctive moles on his own body and the other man's body removed. So, it's not strange that Wei Ping and the others could mistake the identity.]"]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199: Does the King of Qi Intend to Seize the Former Emperor's Treasure Vault","paragraphs":["This person was originally a double he had raised. The Prince of Qi knew that spying on the throne with intent to rebel was a capital offense if discovered.","Therefore, he had long prepared an escape route for himself. At the critical moment, the double would die in his place, allowing him to slip away.","These assassins also did not receive their orders from the Prince of Qi, but from Xie Qi's other identity, Qi Xie.","Cai Xian, Wei Ping, and the others accelerated their movements, their faces flushing red then paling white.","A humiliating sense of being fooled made them so agitated that they directly treated the assassins before them as Xie Qi, aiming fatal blows at them!","Right, he isn't called Xie Qi now; he's changed his name to Qi Xie!","\"What a cunning man! Having already faked his death to escape, why come back to assassinate me? What immense hatred drives him to risk exposing his existence!\"","On the surface, she had only filed one accusation. It was the four great families who implicated him; she hadn't participated at all.","[Perhaps he thought his plan was flawless, believing that even if the assassination failed, no one would guess it was him.","After all, he is now a dead man buried in the ground. In this world, aside from Xie Zhiyao who went for a political marriage, even his most beloved son and that favored concubine don't know about this.]","\"So, that final glance Xie Zhiyao cast back before leaving for the marriage was exchanging a secret signal with her father?\"","[Most likely. From the moment the Prince of Qi was placed under house arrest and the Emperor began investigating his assets, he had already prepared to fake his death.","Over the years, he spent a great deal of money to cultivate his forces, so the accounts of the Prince of Qi's estate couldn't withstand scrutiny.","He knew early on that his rebellious intentions would eventually be discovered. He only told Xie Zhiyao about the plan to fake his death the night before she left for the political marriage.","Xie Qi probably saw Western Qiang as his escape route; otherwise, he wouldn't have told Xie Zhiyao.]","He didn't even tell his most beloved son, so why tell a daughter married off to another state? It was only because he valued her future status.","\"Little Zhu, why didn't you say so earlier? Otherwise, this assassination attempt might have been avoided.\"","[Master, I only just pieced this together by linking these assassins to their master. You know me, my divine power is less than one ten-thousandth of its potential...]","\"Alright, I understand. I don't blame you. It's just an assassination attempt, a minor scene!","Little Zhu, what do you think about next time we encounter an assassination, maybe lowering the defenses? I want to see if facing death might bring some sudden enlightenment.\"","Yue Fuguang's eyes darted around as she tested the waters. Although she had the system's protection, it still consumed energy.","So, to save energy, it's best to start from the source.","Hearing her words, Cai Xian, Huo Ying, Wei Ping, and the others visibly panicked. They fought while gradually closing in around Yue Fuguang, eventually forming a line with the Yu father and son.","These men feared the loyal divine artifact might actually listen to the young immortal lord's suggestion.","[Not a good idea! Master, you are mortal now. Blades and swords have no eyes; you could really die!]","Everyone nodded in agreement. The divine artifact was right!","\"So what if I die? With three thousand minor worlds and three thousand medium worlds, we can just pick one and start over!\"","[Growing up from infancy all over again, Master, would you be willing?]","\"Uh... Little Zhu, how about we pretend I never said that?\"","Hearing Yue Fuguang's words, Wei Ping and the others did not let their guard down. They couldn't trust the young preceptor's unpredictable temperament.","What if she gave the divine artifact a direct order, just like when the Emperor gives an order to Eunuch Qian? Even if the artifact felt it was improper or disagreed, it would absolutely carry it out!","Only about the time it takes to drink a cup of tea had passed before two squads of Imperial Forest Guards arrived, closing in from both ends of the street.","The lead assassin, who had been commanding from a high vantage point, saw that reinforcements had arrived faster than anticipated. Not lingering in the fight, he decisively commanded, \"Retreat!\"","He used his inner energy to project his voice, so even Shen Kang, who had rushed with the Imperial City Department's men to support the outermost perimeter, heard the assassins were about to flee.","He quickly led his men to block the nearby exits.","According to what the system later told her, the chase of \"he flees, they pursue, he finds no escape\" dragged on all night, but some still managed to get away.","[Master, these people are very familiar with the capital. They even used the abandoned hideouts of 'Brother Lack-of-Virtue' and his gang after their capture as temporary shelters.]","\"If they are the Prince of Qi's men, it's normal for them to know the capital well. I just wonder where the Prince of Qi is now. He wouldn't have gone to join Xie Zhiyao, like Bai Yu did, would he?\"","[Don't worry, Master, he wouldn't! The Prince of Qi will not leave the capital until he obtains the treasure vault left by the late Emperor for the Prince of Rong.]","\"The Prince of Qi wants to take the late Emperor's treasure vault? How does he know about it?\"","Yue Fuguang sat in the court hall, found a comfortable position, and began her work of gathering gossip to earn points.","The court officials also pricked up their ears. In the hall, two ministers who had been arguing fiercely over differing political views suddenly fell silent as one of them stopped speaking, causing his opponent to pause in confusion.","Why did he suddenly stop arguing in the middle of the debate? Just when he was about to win the argument, what did this silence mean?","Looking at his opponent's face, could he be having one of his 'episodes' right now?","Clearly, this minister had become an expert at diagnosing his colleague's 'chronic condition' through long exposure. Just by the look on his face, he knew the other man was having an episode!","[While the late Emperor was still alive, the Prince of Qi had planted many of his own people in his brothers' estates. When it came to inserting agents, the Prince of Qi was indeed a master.","One spy he planted early in the Prince of Rong's estate actually managed to rise to the position of a trusted confidant of the Prince of Rong in the year before the old emperor passed away.","At that time, the Prince of Qi had only been married to Feng Suiyu for a couple of years, and Xie Zhiyao was still in her mother's womb.","Later, the old emperor, knowing his time was short, explained the matter of the treasure vault to the Prince of Rong. He originally intended to oversee his son retrieving the treasures while he was still alive.","Unfortunately, he didn't anticipate dying too early.","It also caught the Prince of Rong off guard. Before he could open the vault, his father died, his old rival ascended the throne, and he had even less chance to retrieve the treasure.","Emperor Mingxi, having just ascended, suppressed all factions with swift and ruthless measures, and moved against the Prince of Rong too quickly.","As a result, the Prince of Rong only had time to instruct his eldest son to take trusted followers to dig for the treasure before he, along with his other sons and confidants, was captured.","Xie Qi's confidant only had time to have his young daughter relay the message to the Prince of Qi before he himself, as a trusted follower of the Prince of Rong, was captured by the new Emperor's men.","That little girl was Xie Wei, the first-rank maid named Xie Wei who was most trusted in Xie Qi's courtyard.]","A flash of light passed through Emperor Mingxi's eyes. Back then, with thousands of family members and subordinates of his brothers, his men had focused on ensuring none of his brothers or their close confidants escaped. They didn't let a single one of their sons slip through either.","However, if the one who got away was a little girl, it wasn't impossible.","They tended to subconsciously overlook female dependents to some extent.","\"If Xie Qi knew about the treasure vault, why hasn't he tried to retrieve it all these years?\"","[Because the confidant didn't know the exact location either. He only knew it required a vault key to open, and the map was hidden within the key.","The confidant only glimpsed the key once. His daughter was only six at the time, and perhaps due to a child's unclear description, Xie Qi has been searching all these years for the vault key based on her account.","Just two years ago, he finally uncovered a clue about the key.]"]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200: The Whims of Fate","paragraphs":["\"Oh? Where is the key? He probably never found it in the end, right? I remember you said the treasure vault would be discovered this year by Prince Rong's son.\"","\"One can only say fate plays tricks. He traced the key to its final purchase by a woman from the Feng family at an antique shop and followed the trail all the way to his own wife and her elder sister.","The shopkeeper couldn't tell the two sisters apart either, so Xie Qi had to patiently search himself.","He started with his own wife. Under the pretext of taking inventory of her assets, he combed through all her storerooms, large and small, but couldn't find the key described by Xie Wei and the antique shopkeeper.","Xie Qi then turned his attention to his sister-in-law, repeatedly sending people to infiltrate the Chai residence to search, but to no avail.\"","Chai Yanping and Chai Jin were horrified. Could the key to the late Emperor's treasure vault really be in the hands of their daughter-in-law/wife?","\"So, when Prince Qi previously pretended to fancy Feng Linlang and went to great lengths to marry her, it was actually to obtain that vault key she held?\"","Emperor Mingxi and Dong Qianli felt a surge of joy, each privately pondering if their private and national treasuries were perhaps a bit too small, nearly full already—any more and they'd overflow!","\"It's true he wanted to marry Feng Linlang for the key, but the vault key wasn't in her possession; it was with her younger sister, Feng Suiyu.","Back when the sisters reconciled, they went to the antique shop together and each bought some trinkets. Later, they had their respective purchases crafted and embellished by artisans before gifting them to each other.","What Feng Linlang gave to Feng Suiyu was the gold hairpin she always wore in her hair.","Feng Linlang had the artisan add gemstones and jade fragments to the key-shaped pin, so the appearance of the treasure vault key was completely altered.","Perhaps because his feelings for Feng Suiyu were shallow, he never truly looked at his wife. Thus, even though Feng Suiyu wore the key-shaped hairpin on her head every day, Prince Qi never recognized it.\"","\"And he ended up causing Feng Suiyu's death because he wanted to marry Feng Linlang, who he thought had the key? So, the blind and foolish Prince Qi was destined never to get the key?\"","\"Exactly. After Feng Suiyu's death, all her dowry, including that hairpin, came into Xie Zhiyao's possession. Finding it inauspicious, she sold the pin.","That jewelry shop happened to be a secret business of a former concubine of Prince Rong. Soon, the item fell into the hands of Prince Rong's illegitimate son, who, using the map inside, successfully located the treasure vault.","Master, would you like to know the vault's location? Little Pearl can open it easily even without the key.\"","\"Not really, I'm not short of money to spend. Didn't the Emperor just gift me several chests of gold? Plus, the dividends from cement and glass, and tens of thousands of taels of silver every month—I have nowhere to spend it all.\"","\"True, this place is too backward; even with money, there's nowhere to spend it.\"","The various ministers, whose finances were tight after handing out a pile of red envelopes during the New Year, were deeply envious. They wished they were as wealthy as the Junior Mentor!","It's said the Junior Mentor's original treasury was no longer sufficient, so a larger one was built right next to it!","\"Little Pearl, do you know where Xie Qi is hiding now? He keeps trying to assassinate me; we must find him.","I won't rest easy until he's dealt with.\"","\"Master, would you like me to eliminate him directly?\"","\"No need. Killing him now would make it troublesome to find the assassins he's nurtured and the spies he's planted. It's better to let Wei Ping and his men capture him, then follow the trail to uproot Prince Qi's entire network.\"","\"Indeed, extracting information directly from Xie Qi's mouth would be faster. Wei Ping and the others would never guess that Xie Qi is hiding on Peach Blossom Lane.\"","Wei Ping: Truly didn't expect that. Prince Qi is playing the game of hiding in plain sight with them!","\"He's hiding in Xie Zhiyao's villa? Playing the 'most dangerous place is the safest' game?\"","\"Master, he's hiding next door to that villa. When the properties were purchased, one was under Xie Zhiyao's name, and the other was under the name of a distant relative of one of Prince Qi's trusted aides.","Shen Kang and the others must have investigated the neighbors, but that person's background was clean—just a moderately wealthy merchant. Since it was such a distant, convoluted connection, they naturally wouldn't discover the homeowner's link to Prince Qi.\"","Shen Kang, who had also started attending court after the New Year and stood at the very back, nodded inwardly. Wasn't that the truth? His subordinates had thoroughly checked the backgrounds of all nearby residents.","The family next door was indeed just a merchant, and the owner was often away from the capital. The property was only looked after by three servants.","It appeared utterly ordinary on the surface, so they hadn't paid it much attention.","\"What's special about that residence? Why would he choose to live there?\"","Emperor Mingxi was also curious. Peach Blossom Lane, Pear Blossom Lane, and Apricot Blossom Lane were all areas with villas of varying sizes, mostly belonging to wealthy or noble families as secondary residences.","The comings and goings were relatively simple, not ideal for hiding. He had thought Prince Qi would choose a place with a more complex population to conceal himself.","\"Because there's a secret passage there. Xie Zhiyao's villa also has one underneath, but it's not as well-hidden as the one next door.","Most importantly, that secret passage leads to the commoners' mixed-residence area in the northern part of the city, where he has another small courtyard, not far from the city gate.","It's convenient for him to flee north to find Xie Zhiyao.\"","Wei Ping and Cai Xian exchanged a glance. Prince Qi had turned into a rat. Knowing his nest's location was one thing, but catching him wouldn't be easy; they'd need to block his escape routes too.","\"Then mark the location and notify Wei Ping to arrest him.\"","\"How will you explain it to him, Master?\"","\"I can't be bothered to fabricate a reason. How about you just drop an anonymous tip-off letter at the Court of Judicial Review?\"","\"No problem. Little Pearl will mark the tunnel route map for him. No fear of not catching the man then.\"","Everyone fell into a moment of silent contemplation. Was the young immortal now unwilling to even bother fabricating a lie for them?","Had the repeated assassination attempts finally angered him? Was he disappointed in them and thus couldn't be bothered to expend the effort?","After this round of overthinking, they felt somewhat panicked and instinctively turned their pleading gazes towards their Emperor.","Emperor Mingxi: What good is looking at me? Shouldn't winning back the young immortal's favor require the joint efforts of the entire court?","The only consolation was that, although the young immortal seemed disappointed in them, as the Junior Mentor, he hadn't missed court or his studies. If they performed well, there was surely still a chance.","Yue Fuguang: Is it possible I'm just lazy and don't want to make up a reason?","System: Overthinking is also a sickness, but it's a sickness they seem to enjoy!","The ministers left the morning court session full of trepidation. Yue Fuguang was led by Eunuch Qian to the Emperor's Hall of Mental Cultivation for the second time.","This time, inside the hall, besides the Emperor, were the same group of officials as last time. Upon closer look, there were even a few more people.","Yue Fuguang hadn't expected both his visits here to be due to assassination attempts.","Emperor Mingxi had also thought of this, so his expression was unavoidably somewhat sheepish. Wei Ping and the others also wore looks of slight embarrassment and shame.","\"Fuguang, you're here. Please, sit.\" Emperor Mingxi's demeanor was even more accommodating, his tone gentler.","Yue Fuguang didn't decline and sat down, asking knowingly, \"Your Majesty summoned me. Is there a matter?\"","Emperor Mingxi gave a light cough before speaking. \"We called you here this time, again, regarding yesterday's assassination attempt.\""]}]);
